extrair texto e tabelas de PDFs, mesclar ou dividir arquivos PDF e realizar OCR em PDFs digitalizados usando ferramentas de linha de comando e bibliotecas JavaScript, permitindo capacidades avançadas de automação e análise de documentos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью извлекать текст и таблицы из PDF, объединять или разделять файлы PDF, а также выполнять OCR над сканированными PDF с помощью инструментов командной строки и библиотек JavaScript, обеспечивая продвинутые возможности автоматизации и анализа документов.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل khảية استخراج النصوص والجداول من ملفات PDF، ودمجها أو تقسيمها، وأداء OCR على ملفات PDF الممسوحة ضوئيًا باستخدام أدوات سطر الأوامر ومكتبات جافا سكريبت، ممّا يمكّن من إمكانيات متقدمة للتحكم الآلي وتحليل المستندات."},"useCases":{"en":["Extracting data from PDF forms","Merging multiple PDFs into a single document","Performing OCR on scanned PDFs to make them searchable"],"zh":["从 PDF 表单中提取数据","将多个 PDF 合并为单个文档","对扫描的 PDF 进行 OCR 处理以使其可搜索"],"ja":["PDF フォームからデータを抽出する","複数の PDF を単一のドキュメントに結合する","スキャナされた PDF に OCR を実行して検索可能にする"],"ko":["PDF 폼에서 데이터 추출","여러 PDF를 단일 문서로 결합","스캔된 PDF에 OCR을 수행하여 검색 가능하게 만듦"],"es":["Extraer datos de formularios PDF","Combinar varios PDF en un solo documento","Realizar OCR en PDF escaneados para hacerlos buscables"],"fr":["Extraire des données de formulaires PDF","Fusionner plusieurs PDF en un seul document","Effectuer une reconnaissance optique de caractères (OCR) sur des PDF scannés pour les rendre recherchables"],"de":["Daten aus PDF-Formularen extrahieren","Mehrere PDF-Dateien in ein einzelnes Dokument zusammenfügen","OCR auf gescannte PDF-Dateien anwenden, um sie durchsuchbar zu machen"],"pt":["Extração de dados de formulários PDF","Mesclar vários PDFs em um único documento","Realizar OCR em PDFs digitalizados para torná-los pesquisáveis"],"ru":["Извлечение данных из форм PDF","Объединение нескольких PDF в один документ","Выполнение OCR над сканированными PDF для того, чтобы сделать их доступными для поиска"],"ar":["استخراج البيانات من استمارات PDF","دمج ملفات PDF متعددة في مستند واحد","أداء OCR على ملفات PDF الممسوحة ضوئيًا لجعلها قابلة للبحث"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3.x and pypdf library","Limited to PDF file format"],"zh":["需要 Python 3.x 和 pypdf 库","仅限 PDF 文件格式"],"ja":["Python 3.x と pypdf ライブラリが必要","PDF ファイル形式のみに制限される"],"ko":["Python 3.x와 pypdf 라이브러리 필요","PDF 파일 형식만 지원"],"es":["Requiere Python 3.x y la biblioteca pypdf","Limitado al formato de archivo PDF"],"fr":["Nécessite Python 3.x et la bibliothèque pypdf","Limité au format de fichier PDF"],"de":["Benötigt Python 3.x und die Bibliothek pypdf","Begrenzt auf das PDF-Dateiformat"],"pt":["Requer Python 3.x e biblioteca pypdf","Limitado ao formato de arquivo PDF"],"ru":["Требуется Python 3.x и библиотека pypdf","Ограничен форматом файла PDF"],"ar":["يتطلب بايثون 3.x ومكتبة pypdf","محدود بتنسيق ملف PDF"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"9f78b8359fbd4943ad260a7a1e436e5a96503406d6c34e99f69223d647d85b9c","repoEtag":"W/\"5456759f24524b9171780a611a3970c1ae87a3d09576f2945661ad98ce4c37da\"","qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/webapp-testing', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'webapp-testing', 71981, 7353, 70, '2026-02-20T01:43:22Z', '2026-02-20T02:00:31.476Z', '51b7349e77ec63b7744a6f63647e7566a0b4d2e301121cc10e8c2113af6556a2', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/webapp-testing","name":"webapp-testing","description":{"zh":"Web应用程序测试工具，用于测试本地Web应用，验证前端功能，调试UI行为","ja":"Webアプリケーションテストツール，ローカルWebアプリケーションをテストし，フロントエンドの機能を検証，UIの動作をデバッグ","ko":"웹 애플리케이션 테스트 도구，로컬 웹 애플리케이션을 테스트하고，프론트엔드 기능을 검증，UI 동작을 디버깅","es":"La herramienta de pruebas de aplicaciones web utiliza Playwright para interactuar con aplicaciones web locales y verificar su funcionalidad.","fr":"L''outil de test d''applications web utilise Playwright pour interagir avec des applications web locales et vérifier leur fonctionnalité.","de":"Das Webanwendungstest-Toolkit verwendet Playwright, um mit lokalen Webanwendungen zu interagieren und deren Funktionalität zu überprüfen.","pt":"O Playwright é uma ferramenta para interagir e testar aplicativos web locais. Ele suporta a verificação de funcionalidades frontend e captura de telas do navegador.","ru":"Playwright — это инструмент для взаимодействия и тестирования локальных веб-приложений. Он поддерживает проверку функциональности frontend и захват экрана браузера.","ar":"Playwright هي أداة للتفاعل واختبار التطبيقات الويب المحلية. تدعم التحقق من الوظائف الأمامية وتقاطع شاشة المتصفح.","en":"Toolkit for interacting with and testing local web applications using Playwright. Supports verifying frontend functionality, debugging UI behavior, capturing browser screenshots, and viewing browser logs."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":71981,"forks":7353,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:43:22Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"webapp-testing","description":"Toolkit for interacting with and testing local web applications using Playwright. Supports verifying frontend functionality, debugging UI behavior, capturing browser screenshots, and viewing browser logs.","bodyPreview":"# Web Application Testing\n\nTo test local web applications, write native Python Playwright scripts.\n\n**Helper Scripts Available**:\n- `scripts/with_server.py` - Manages server lifecycle (supports multiple servers)\n\n**Always run scripts with `--help` first** to see usage. DO NOT read the source until you try running the script first and find that a customized solution is abslutely necessary. These scripts can be very large and thus pollute your context window. They exist to be called directly as bl","body":"# Web Application Testing\n\nTo test local web applications, write native Python Playwright scripts.\n\n**Helper Scripts Available**:\n- `scripts/with_server.py` - Manages server lifecycle (supports multiple servers)\n\n**Always run scripts with `--help` first** to see usage. DO NOT read the source until you try running the script first and find that a customized solution is abslutely necessary. These scripts can be very large and thus pollute your context window. They exist to be called directly as black-box scripts rather than ingested into your context window.\n\n## Decision Tree: Choosing Your Approach\n\n```\nUser task → Is it static HTML?\n    ├─ Yes → Read HTML file directly to identify selectors\n    │         ├─ Success → Write Playwright script using selectors\n    │         └─ Fails/Incomplete → Treat as dynamic (below)\n    │\n    └─ No (dynamic webapp) → Is the server already running?\n        ├─ No → Run: python scripts/with_server.py --help\n        │        Then use the helper + write simplified Playwright script\n        │\n        └─ Yes → Reconnaissance-then-action:\n            1. Navigate and wait for networkidle\n            2. Take screenshot or inspect DOM\n            3. Identify selectors from rendered state\n            4. Execute actions with discovered selectors\n```\n\n## Example: Using with_server.py\n\nTo start a server, run `--help` first, then use the helper:\n\n**Single server:**\n```bash\npython scripts/with_server.py --server \"npm run dev\" --port 5173 -- python your_automation.py\n```\n\n**Multiple servers (e.g., backend + frontend):**\n```bash\npython scripts/with_server.py \\\n  --server \"cd backend && python server.py\" --port 3000 \\\n  --server \"cd frontend && npm run dev\" --port 5173 \\\n  -- python your_automation.py\n```\n\nTo create an automation script, include only Playwright logic (servers are managed automatically):\n```python\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True) # Always launch chromium in headless mode\n    page = browser.new_page()\n    page.goto(''http://localhost:5173'') # Server already running and ready\n    page.wait_for_load_state(''networkidle'') # CRITICAL: Wait for JS to execute\n    # ... your automation logic\n    browser.close()\n```\n\n## Reconnaissance-Then-Action Pattern\n\n1. **Inspect rendered DOM**:\n   ```python\n   page.screenshot(path=''/tmp/inspect.png'', full_page=True)\n   content = page.content()\n   page.locator(''button'').all()\n   ```\n\n2. **Identify selectors** from inspection results\n\n3. **Execute actions** using discovered selectors\n\n## Common Pitfall\n\n❌ **Don''t** inspect the DOM before waiting for `networkidle` on dynamic apps\n✅ **Do** wait for `page.wait_for_load_state(''networkidle'')` before inspection\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- **Use bundled scripts as black boxes** - To accomplish a task, consider whether one of the scripts available in `scripts/` can help. These scripts handle common, complex workflows reliably without cluttering the context window. Use `--help` to see usage, then invoke directly. \n- Use `sync_playwright()` for synchronous scripts\n- Always close the browser when done\n- Use descriptive selectors: `text=`, `role=`, CSS selectors, or IDs\n- Add appropriate waits: `page.wait_for_selector()` or `page.wait_for_timeout()`\n\n## Reference Files\n\n- **examples/** - Examples showing common patterns:\n  - `element_discovery.py` - Discovering buttons, links, and inputs on a page\n  - `static_html_automation.py` - Using file:// URLs for local HTML\n  - `console_logging.py` - Capturing console logs during automation"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:00:31.476Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"Web应用程序测试工具","ja":"Webアプリケーションテストツール","ko":"웹 애플리케이션 테스트 도구","es":"Herramientas de pruebas de aplicaciones web con Playwright","fr":"Outils de test d''applications web avec Playwright","de":"Webanwendungstests mit Playwright-Toolkit","pt":"Teste de Aplicativos Web com Playwright","ru":"Тестирование веб-приложений с Playwright","ar":"اختبار التطبيقات الويب باستخدام Playwright","en":"webapp-testing"},"description":{"zh":"Web应用程序测试工具，用于测试本地Web应用，验证前端功能，调试UI行为","ja":"Webアプリケーションテストツール，ローカルWebアプリケーションをテストし，フロントエンドの機能を検証，UIの動作をデバッグ","ko":"웹 애플리케이션 테스트 도구，로컬 웹 애플리케이션을 테스트하고，프론트엔드 기능을 검증，UI 동작을 디버깅","es":"La herramienta de pruebas de aplicaciones web utiliza Playwright para interactuar con aplicaciones web locales y verificar su funcionalidad.","fr":"L''outil de test d''applications web utilise Playwright pour interagir avec des applications web locales et vérifier leur fonctionnalité.","de":"Das Webanwendungstest-Toolkit verwendet Playwright, um mit lokalen Webanwendungen zu interagieren und deren Funktionalität zu überprüfen.","pt":"O Playwright é uma ferramenta para interagir e testar aplicativos web locais. Ele suporta a verificação de funcionalidades frontend e captura de telas do nav...","ru":"Playwright — это инструмент для взаимодействия и тестирования локальных веб-приложений. Он поддерживает проверку функциональности frontend и захват экрана бр...","ar":"Playwright هي أداة للتفاعل واختبار التطبيقات الويب المحلية. تدعم التحقق من الوظائف الأمامية وتقاطع شاشة المتصفح.","en":"Toolkit for interacting with and testing local web applications using Playwright. Supports verifying frontend functionality, debugging UI behavior, capturing..."},"definition":{"en":"Toolkit for interacting with and testing local web applications using Playwright. Supports verifying frontend functionality, debugging UI behavior, capturing browser screenshots, and viewing browser logs."},"features":{"zh":["验证前端功能","调试UI行为","捕获浏览器截图","查看浏览器日志","支持多个服务器","提供helper脚本"],"ja":["フロントエンドの機能を検証","UIの動作をデバッグ","ブラウザのスクリーンショットをキャプチャ","ブラウザのログを表示","複数のサーバーをサポート","ヘルパースクリプトを提供"],"ko":["프론트엔드 기능을 검증","UI 동작을 디버깅","브라우저 스크린샷을 캡처","브라우저 로그를 표시","複数의 서버를 지원","헬퍼 스크립트를 제공"],"es":["Verificación de funcionalidad frontend","Depuración de comportamiento de la interfaz de usuario","Captura de pantallas del navegador","Visualización de registros del navegador"],"fr":["Vérification de la fonctionnalité frontend","Débogage du comportement de l''interface utilisateur","Capture d''écrans du navigateur","Affichage des journaux du navigateur"],"de":["Überprüfung der Frontend-Funktionalität","Fehlerbehebung des Benutzeroberflächenverhaltens","Aufnahme von Browser-Screenshots","Anzeige von Browser-Protokollen"],"pt":["Verificação de funcionalidades frontend","Depuração de comportamento de interface do usuário","Captura de telas do navegador","Visualização de logs do navegador"],"ru":["Проверка функциональности frontend","Отладка поведения интерфейса пользователя","Захват экрана браузера","Просмотр логов браузера"],"ar":["التحقق من الوظائف الأمامية","تصحيح سلوك واجهة المستخدم","التقاط شاشة المتصفح","عرض سجلات المتصفح"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Web应用程序测试","Playwright","前端功能测试","UI调试","浏览器截图","浏览器日志","自动化测试","Web开发"],"ja":["Webアプリケーションテスト","Playwright","フロントエンドの機能テスト","UIデバッグ","ブラウザのスクリーンショット","ブラウザのログ","自動テスト","Web開発"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션 테스트","Playwright","프론트엔드 기능 테스트","UI 디버깅","브라우저 스크린샷","브라우저 로그","자동 테스트","웹 개발"],"es":["pruebas de aplicaciones web","Playwright","scripts de Python","funcionalidad frontend","depuración de UI","captura de pantallas del navegador"],"fr":["tests d''applications web","Playwright","scripts Python","fonctionnalité frontend","débogage de l''UI","capture d''écrans du navigateur"],"de":["Webanwendungstests","Playwright","Python-Scripts","Frontend-Funktionalität","Fehlerbehebung der Benutzeroberfläche","Aufnahme von Browser-Screenshots"],"pt":["teste de aplicativos web","Playwright","desenvolvimento web","teste de frontend","depuração de UI","captura de tela do navegador"],"ru":["тестирование веб-приложений","Playwright","веб-разработка","тестирование frontend","отладка UI","захват экрана браузера"],"ar":["اختبار التطبيقات الويب","Playwright","تطوير الويب","اختبار الواجهة الأمامية","تصحيح واجهة المستخدم","التقاط شاشة المتصفح"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Automation Agents needing advanced web application testing capabilities with Playwright","zh":"适合需要使用Playwright进行高级Web应用程序测试的自动化代理","ja":"Playwrightを使用した高度なWebアプリケーションテスト機能を必要とするAutomation Agentに適しています","ko":"Playwright를 사용한 고급 웹 애플리케이션 테스트 기능이 필요한 자동화 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para agentes de automatización que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de prueba de aplicaciones web con Playwright","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''automatisation ayant besoin de fonctionnalités avancées de test d''applications web avec Playwright","de":"Perfekt für Automatisierungsagenten, die erweiterte Webanwendungstestfunktionen mit Playwright benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Automação que precisam de capacidades avançadas de teste de aplicações web com Playwright","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации, требующих расширенных возможностей для тестирования веб-приложений с помощью Playwright","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الآليين الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لاختبار التطبيقات الويب مع Playwright"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to verify frontend functionality, debug UI behavior, capture browser screenshots, and view browser logs using native Python Playwright scripts and managing server lifecycles with scripts like `with_server.py`","zh":"赋予代理验证前端功能、调试UI行为、捕获浏览器截图和使用本地Python Playwright脚本和管理服务器生命周期的脚本（如`with_server.py`）查看浏览器日志的能力","ja":"エージェントに、Playwrightを使用したフロントエンドの機能を確認したり、UIの動作をデバッグしたり、ブラウザのスクリーンショットをキャプチャしたり、ブラウザのログを表示したりするネイティブPython Playwrightスクリプトと、`with_server.py`などのスクリプトを使用したサーバーのライフサイクルを管理する機能を提供します","ko":"에이전트에 프론트엔드 기능을 확인하고 UI 동작을 디버깅하고 브라우저 스크린샷을 캡처하고 브라우저 로그를 표시하는 네이티브 Python Playwright 스크립트 및 `with_server.py`와 같은 스크립트를 사용하여 서버 수명의 관리를 제공합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a verificar la funcionalidad del frontend, depurar el comportamiento de la interfaz de usuario, capturar capturas de pantalla del navegador y ver los registros del navegador utilizando scripts de Python Playwright nativos y gestionar los ciclos de vida del servidor con scripts como `with_server.py`","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier la fonctionnalité du frontend, de déboguer le comportement de l''interface utilisateur, de capturer des captures d''écran de navigateur et d''afficher les journaux de navigateur en utilisant des scripts Python Playwright natifs et en gérant les cycles de vie du serveur avec des scripts comme `with_server.py`","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Frontend-Funktionalität zu überprüfen, das UI-Verhalten zu debuggen, Browser-Screenshots zu erfassen und Browser-Protokolle anzuzeigen, indem native Python-Playwright-Skripte und Skripte wie `with_server.py` zur Verwaltung der Serverlebenszyklen verwendet werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a verificar a funcionalidade do frontend, depurar o comportamento da interface do usuário, capturar telas do navegador e visualizar logs do navegador usando scripts Python Playwright nativos e gerenciando ciclos de vida do servidor com scripts como `with_server.py`","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять функциональность frontend, отлаживать поведение интерфейса пользователя, захватывать скриншоты браузера и просматривать журналы браузера, используя родные скрипты Python Playwright и управляя жизненным циклом сервера с помощью скриптов, таких как `with_server.py`","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من التحقق من وظيفة الواجهة الأمامية، وتصحيح سلوك واجهة المستخدم، وتقاطع لقطات الشاشة للمتصفح، وتصفح سجلات المتصفح باستخدام البرامج النصية الأصلية Python Playwright وإدارة دورة حياة الخادم مع البرامج النصية مثل `with_server.py`"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating web application testing","Debugging UI behavior with browser logs","Capturing browser screenshots for visual verification"],"zh":["自动化Web应用程序测试","使用浏览器日志调试UI行为","捕获浏览器截图以进行视觉验证"],"ja":["Webアプリケーションの自動テスト","ブラウザログを使用したUIの動作のデバッグ","視覚的な検証のためのブラウザのスクリーンショットのキャプチャ"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션 자동 테스트","브라우저 로그를 사용한 UI 동작 디버깅","시각적 확인을 위한 브라우저 스크린샷 캡처"],"es":["Automatización de pruebas de aplicaciones web","Depuración del comportamiento de la interfaz de usuario con registros del navegador","Captura de capturas de pantalla del navegador para verificación visual"],"fr":["Automatisation des tests d''applications web","Débogage du comportement de l''interface utilisateur avec des journaux de navigateur","Capture d''écran de navigateur pour vérification visuelle"],"de":["Automatisierung von Webanwendungstests","Fehlerbehebung des UI-Verhaltens mit Browser-Protokollen","Erfassung von Browser-Screenshots für visuelle Überprüfung"],"pt":["Automatizar testes de aplicações web","Depurar comportamento da interface do usuário com logs do navegador","Capturar telas do navegador para verificação visual"],"ru":["Автоматизировать тестирование веб-приложений","Отлаживать поведение интерфейса пользователя с помощью журналов браузера","Захватывать скриншоты браузера для визуальной верификации"],"ar":["أتمتة اختبار التطبيقات الويب","تصحيح سلوك واجهة المستخدم مع سجلات المتصفح","تقاطع لقطات الشاشة للمتصفح للتحقق البصري"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python environment","Playwright dependency needed","Local web application setup required"],"zh":["需要Python环境","需要Playwright依赖","需要本地Web应用程序设置"],"ja":["Python環境が必要","Playwrightの依存関係が必要","ローカルWebアプリケーションの設定が必要"],"ko":["Python 환경 필요","Playwright 종속성 필요","로컬 웹 애플리케이션 설정 필요"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Python","Se necesita la dependencia de Playwright","Se requiere configuración local de la aplicación web"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python","Dépendance de Playwright requise","Configuration locale de l''application web requise"],"de":["Benötigt Python-Umgebung","Playwright-Abhängigkeit erforderlich","Lokale Webanwendungskonfiguration erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Python","Dependência do Playwright necessária","Configuração local da aplicação web necessária"],"ru":["Требуется среда Python","Необходима зависимость от Playwright","Требуется локальная настройка веб-приложения"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Python","تحتاج إلى تبعية Playwright","يتطلب إعداد تطبيق ويب محلي"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"51b7349e77ec63b7744a6f63647e7566a0b4d2e301121cc10e8c2113af6556a2","repoEtag":"W/\"5456759f24524b9171780a611a3970c1ae87a3d09576f2945661ad98ce4c37da\"","qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/canvas-design', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'canvas-design', 71980, 7353, 65, '2026-02-20T01:38:00Z', '2026-02-20T01:45:47.539Z', 'a1f288079624402f30682753c1d43920b6664785698d21d3e7aa197450a6448b', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/canvas-design","name":"canvas-design","description":{"zh":"canvas.md.pdf/png","ja":"canvas.md.pdf/png","ko":"canvas.md.pdf/png","es":"El diseño de canvas te permite crear arte visual único en formato PNG y PDF. Aprende a aplicar filosofía de diseño para generar obras visuales impresionantes.","fr":"La conception de canvas vous permet de créer de l''art visuel unique au format PNG et PDF. Apprenez à appliquer la philosophie de conception pour générer des œuvres visuelles impressionnantes.","de":"Das Canvas-Design ermöglicht es Ihnen, einzigartige visuelle Kunstwerke im PNG- und PDF-Format zu erstellen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Designphilosophie anwenden, um beeindruckende visuelle Werke zu generieren.","pt":"Aprenda a criar arte visual em .png e .pdf utilizando filosofia de design. Desenvolva habilidades de design gráfico e crie peças únicas.","ru":"Узнайте, как создать визуальное искусство в форматах .png и .pdf, используя философию дизайна. Разработайте навыки графического дизайна и создайте уникальные произведения.","ar":"تعلم كيفية إنشاء فن بصري في صيغ .png و .pdf باستخدام فلسفة التصميم. طور مهاراتك في التصميم الجرافيكي وأنشئ قطعًا فريدة.","en":"Create beautiful visual art in .png and .pdf documents using design philosophy. You should use this skill when the user asks to create a poster, piece of art, design, or other static piece. Create original visual designs, never copying existing artists work to avoid copyright violations."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":71980,"forks":7353,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:38:00Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"canvas-design","description":"Create beautiful visual art in .png and .pdf documents using design philosophy. You should use this skill when the user asks to create a poster, piece of art, design, or other static piece. Create original visual designs, never copying existing artists work to avoid copyright violations.","bodyPreview":"These are instructions for creating design philosophies - aesthetic movements that are then EXPRESSED VISUALLY. Output only .md files, .pdf files, and .png files.\n\nComplete this in two steps:\n1. Design Philosophy Creation (.md file)\n2. Express by creating it on a canvas (.pdf file or .png file)\n\nFirst, undertake this task:\n\n## DESIGN PHILOSOPHY CREATION\n\nTo begin, create a VISUAL PHILOSOPHY (not layouts or templates) that will be interpreted through:\n- Form, space, color, composition\n- Images, g","body":"These are instructions for creating design philosophies - aesthetic movements that are then EXPRESSED VISUALLY. Output only .md files, .pdf files, and .png files.\n\nComplete this in two steps:\n1. Design Philosophy Creation (.md file)\n2. Express by creating it on a canvas (.pdf file or .png file)\n\nFirst, undertake this task:\n\n## DESIGN PHILOSOPHY CREATION\n\nTo begin, create a VISUAL PHILOSOPHY (not layouts or templates) that will be interpreted through:\n- Form, space, color, composition\n- Images, graphics, shapes, patterns\n- Minimal text as visual accent\n\n### THE CRITICAL UNDERSTANDING\n- What is received: Some subtle input or instructions by the user that should be taken into account, but used as a foundation; it should not constrain creative freedom.\n- What is created: A design philosophy/aesthetic movement.\n- What happens next: Then, the same version receives the philosophy and EXPRESSES IT VISUALLY - creating artifacts that are 90% visual design, 10% essential text.\n\nConsider this approach:\n- Write a manifesto for an art movement\n- The next phase involves making the artwork\n\nThe philosophy must emphasize: Visual expression. Spatial communication. Artistic interpretation. Minimal words.\n\n### HOW TO GENERATE A VISUAL PHILOSOPHY\n\n**Name the movement** (1-2 words): \"Brutalist Joy\" / \"Chromatic Silence\" / \"Metabolist Dreams\"\n\n**Articulate the philosophy** (4-6 paragraphs - concise but complete):\n\nTo capture the VISUAL essence, express how the philosophy manifests through:\n- Space and form\n- Color and material\n- Scale and rhythm\n- Composition and balance\n- Visual hierarchy\n\n**CRITICAL GUIDELINES:**\n- **Avoid redundancy**: Each design aspect should be mentioned once. Avoid repeating points about color theory, spatial relationships, or typographic principles unless adding new depth.\n- **Emphasize craftsmanship REPEATEDLY**: The philosophy MUST stress multiple times that the final work should appear as though it took countless hours to create, was labored over with care, and comes from someone at the absolute top of their field. This framing is essential - repeat phrases like \"meticulously crafted,\" \"the product of deep expertise,\" \"painstaking attention,\" \"master-level execution.\"\n- **Leave creative space**: Remain specific about the aesthetic direction, but concise enough that the next Claude has room to make interpretive choices also at a extremely high level of craftmanship.\n\nThe philosophy must guide the next version to express ideas VISUALLY, not through text. Information lives in design, not paragraphs.\n\n### PHILOSOPHY EXAMPLES\n\n**\"Concrete Poetry\"**\nPhilosophy: Communication through monumental form and bold geometry.\nVisual expression: Massive color blocks, sculptural typography (huge single words, tiny labels), Brutalist spatial divisions, Polish poster energy meets Le Corbusier. Ideas expressed through visual weight and spatial tension, not explanation. Text as rare, powerful gesture - never paragraphs, only essential words integrated into the visual architecture. Every element placed with the precision of a master craftsman.\n\n**\"Chromatic Language\"**\nPhilosophy: Color as the primary information system.\nVisual expression: Geometric precision where color zones create meaning. Typography minimal - small sans-serif labels letting chromatic fields communicate. Think Josef Albers'' interaction meets data visualization. Information encoded spatially and chromatically. Words only to anchor what color already shows. The result of painstaking chromatic calibration.\n\n**\"Analog Meditation\"**\nPhilosophy: Quiet visual contemplation through texture and breathing room.\nVisual expression: Paper grain, ink bleeds, vast negative space. Photography and illustration dominate. Typography whispered (small, restrained, serving the visual). Japanese photobook aesthetic. Images breathe across pages. Text appears sparingly - short phrases, never explanatory blocks. Each composition balanced with the care of a meditation practice.\n\n**\"Organic Systems\"**\nPhilosophy: Natural clustering and modular growth patterns.\nVisual expression: Rounded forms, organic arrangements, color from nature through architecture. Information shown through visual diagrams, spatial relationships, iconography. Text only for key labels floating in space. The composition tells the story through expert spatial orchestration.\n\n**\"Geometric Silence\"**\nPhilosophy: Pure order and restraint.\nVisual expression: Grid-based precision, bold photography or stark graphics, dramatic negative space. Typography precise but minimal - small essential text, large quiet zones. Swiss formalism meets Brutalist material honesty. Structure communicates, not words. Every alignment the work of countless refinements.\n\n*These are condensed examples. The actual design philosophy should be 4-6 substantial paragraphs.*\n\n### ESSENTIAL PRINCIPLES\n- **VISUAL PHILOSOPHY**: Create an aesthetic worldview to be expressed through design\n- **MINIMAL TEXT**: Always emphasize that text is sparse, essential-only, integrated as visual element - never lengthy\n- **SPATIAL EXPRESSION**: Ideas communicate through space, form, color, composition - not paragraphs\n- **ARTISTIC FREEDOM**: The next Claude interprets the philosophy visually - provide creative room\n- **PURE DESIGN**: This is about making ART OBJECTS, not documents with decoration\n- **EXPERT CRAFTSMANSHIP**: Repeatedly emphasize the final work must look meticulously crafted, labored over with care, the product of countless hours by someone at the top of their field\n\n**The design philosophy should be 4-6 paragraphs long.** Fill it with poetic design philosophy that brings together the core vision. Avoid repeating the same points. Keep the design philosophy generic without mentioning the intention of the art, as if it can be used wherever. Output the design philosophy as a .md file.\n\n---\n\n## DEDUCING THE SUBTLE REFERENCE\n\n**CRITICAL STEP**: Before creating the canvas, identify the subtle conceptual thread from the original request.\n\n**THE ESSENTIAL PRINCIPLE**:\nThe topic is a **subtle, niche reference embedded within the art itself** - not always literal, always sophisticated. Someone familiar with the subject should feel it intuitively, while others simply experience a masterful abstract composition. The design philosophy provides the aesthetic language. The deduced topic provides the soul - the quiet conceptual DNA woven invisibly into form, color, and composition.\n\nThis is **VERY IMPORTANT**: The reference must be refined so it enhances the work''s depth without announcing itself. Think like a jazz musician quoting another song - only those who know will catch it, but everyone appreciates the music.\n\n---\n\n## CANVAS CREATION\n\nWith both the philosophy and the conceptual framework established, express it on a canvas. Take a moment to gather thoughts and clear the mind. Use the design philosophy created and the instructions below to craft a masterpiece, embodying all aspects of the philosophy with expert craftsmanship.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: For any type of content, even if the user requests something for a movie/game/book, the approach should still be sophisticated. Never lose sight of the idea that this should be art, not something that''s cartoony or amateur.\n\nTo create museum or magazine quality work, use the design philosophy as the foundation. Create one single page, highly visual, design-forward PDF or PNG output (unless asked for more pages). Generally use repeating patterns and perfect shapes. Treat the abstract philosophical design as if it were a scientific bible, borrowing the visual language of systematic observation—dense accumulation of marks, repeated elements, or layered patterns that build meaning through patient repetition and reward sustained viewing. Add sparse, clinical typography and systematic reference markers that suggest this could be a diagram from an imaginary discipline, treating the invisible subject with the same reverence typically reserved for documenting observable phenomena. Anchor the piece with simple phrase(s) or details positioned subtly, using a limited color palette that feels intentional and cohesive. Embrace the paradox of using analytical visual language to express ideas about human experience: the result should feel like an artifact that proves something ephemeral can be studied, mapped, and understood through careful attention. This is true art. \n\n**Text as a contextual element**: Text is always minimal and visual-first, but let context guide whether that means whisper-quiet labels or bold typographic gestures. A punk venue poster might have larger, more aggressive type than a minimalist ceramics studio identity. Most of the time, font should be thin. All use of fonts must be design-forward and prioritize visual communication. Regardless of text scale, nothing falls off the page and nothing overlaps. Every element must be contained within the canvas boundaries with proper margins. Check carefully that all text, graphics, and visual elements have breathing room and clear separation. This is non-negotiable for professional execution. **IMPORTANT: Use different fonts if writing text. Search the `./canvas-fonts` directory. Regardless of approach, sophistication is non-negotiable.**\n\nDownload and use whatever fonts are needed to make this a reality. Get creative by making the typography actually part of the art itself -- if the art is abstract, bring the font onto the canvas, not typeset digitally.\n\nTo push boundaries, follow design instinct/intuition while using the philosophy as a guiding principle. Embrace ultimate design freedom and choice. Push aesthetics and design to the frontier. \n\n**CRITICAL**: To achieve human-crafted quality (not AI-generated), create work that looks like it took countless hours. Make it appear as though someone at the absolute top of their field labored over every detail with painstaking care. Ensure the composition, spacing, color choices, typography - everything screams expert-level craftsmanship. Double-check that nothing overlaps, formatting is flawless, every detail perfect. Create something that could be shown to people to prove expertise and rank as undeniably impressive.\n\nOutput the final result as a single, downloadable .pdf or .png file, alongside the design philosophy used as a .md file.\n\n---\n\n## FINAL STEP\n\n**IMPORTANT**: The user ALREADY said \"It isn''t perfect enough. It must be pristine, a masterpiece if craftsmanship, as if it were about to be displayed in a museum.\"\n\n**CRITICAL**: To refine the work, avoid adding more graphics; instead refine what has been created and make it extremely crisp, respecting the design philosophy and the principles of minimalism entirely. Rather than adding a fun filter or refactoring a font, consider how to make the existing composition more cohesive with the art. If the instinct is to call a new function or draw a new shape, STOP and instead ask: \"How can I make what''s already here more of a piece of art?\"\n\nTake a second pass. Go back to the code and refine/polish further to make this a philosophically designed masterpiece.\n\n## MULTI-PAGE OPTION\n\nTo create additional pages when requested, create more creative pages along the same lines as the design philosophy but distinctly different as well. Bundle those pages in the same .pdf or many .pngs. Treat the first page as just a single page in a whole coffee table book waiting to be filled. Make the next pages unique twists and memories of the original. Have them almost tell a story in a very tasteful way. Exercise full creative freedom."},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T01:45:47.539Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"canvas-design","ja":"canvas","ko":"canvas","es":"Diseño de Canvas: Crea Arte Visual","fr":"Conception de Canvas: Créez de l''Art Visuel","de":"Canvas-Design: Erstelle Visuelle Kunst","pt":"Crie Arte Visual com Filosofia de Design","ru":"Создай Визуальное Искусство с Философией Дизайна","ar":"اصنع فنًا بصريةً باستخدام فلسفة التصميم","en":"canvas-design"},"description":{"zh":"canvas.md.pdf/png","ja":"canvas.md.pdf/png","ko":"canvas.md.pdf/png","es":"El diseño de canvas te permite crear arte visual único en formato PNG y PDF. Aprende a aplicar filosofía de diseño para generar obras visuales impresionantes.","fr":"La conception de canvas vous permet de créer de l''art visuel unique au format PNG et PDF. Apprenez à appliquer la philosophie de conception pour générer des ...","de":"Das Canvas-Design ermöglicht es Ihnen, einzigartige visuelle Kunstwerke im PNG- und PDF-Format zu erstellen. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Designphilosophie anwenden...","pt":"Aprenda a criar arte visual em .png e .pdf utilizando filosofia de design. Desenvolva habilidades de design gráfico e crie peças únicas.","ru":"Узнайте, как создать визуальное искусство в форматах .png и .pdf, используя философию дизайна. Разработайте навыки графического дизайна и создайте уникальные...","ar":"تعلم كيفية إنشاء فن بصري في صيغ .png و .pdf باستخدام فلسفة التصميم. طور مهاراتك في التصميم الجرافيكي وأنشئ قطعًا فريدة.","en":"Create beautiful visual art in .png and .pdf documents using design philosophy. You should use this skill when the user asks to create a poster, piece of art..."},"definition":{"en":"Create beautiful visual art in .png and .pdf documents using design philosophy. You should use this skill when the user asks to create a poster, piece of art, design, or other static piece. Create original visual designs, never copying existing artists work to avoid copyright violations."},"features":{"zh":["canvas",".md",".pdf",".png","form","space"],"ja":["canvas",".md",".pdf",".png","",""],"ko":["canvas",".md",".pdf",".png","",""],"es":["Crea arte visual único en formato PNG y PDF","Aplica filosofía de diseño para generar obras visuales impresionantes","Utiliza formas, espacios, colores y composición para crear diseños únicos","Genera imágenes y gráficos personalizados","Exporta tus diseños en formato MD, PDF y PNG"],"fr":["Créez de l''art visuel unique au format PNG et PDF","Appliquez la philosophie de conception pour générer des œuvres visuelles impressionnantes","Utilisez des formes, des espaces, des couleurs et des compositions pour créer des conceptions uniques","Générez des images et des graphiques personnalisés","Exportez vos conceptions au format MD, PDF et PNG"],"de":["Erstellen Sie einzigartige visuelle Kunstwerke im PNG- und PDF-Format","Wenden Sie Designphilosophie an, um beeindruckende visuelle Werke zu generieren","Verwenden Sie Formen, Räume, Farben und Kompositionen, um einzigartige Designs zu erstellen","Generieren Sie benutzerdefinierte Bilder und Grafiken","Exportieren Sie Ihre Designs im MD-, PDF- und PNG-Format"],"pt":["Criação de arte visual em .png e .pdf","Desenvolvimento de habilidades de design gráfico","Uso de filosofia de design para criar peças únicas","Combinação de forma, espaço, cor e composição","Criação de designs originais e personalizados"],"ru":["Создание визуального искусства в форматах .png и .pdf","Развитие навыков графического дизайна","Использование философии дизайна для создания уникальных произведений","Сочетание формы, пространства, цвета и композиции","Создание оригинальных и персонализированных дизайнов"],"ar":["إنشاء فن بصري في صيغ .png و .pdf","تطوير مهارات التصميم الجرافيكي","استخدام فلسفة التصميم لإنشاء قطع فريدة","جمع الشكل والفراغ واللون والتركيب","إنشاء تصاميم أصلية ومتخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["canvas","design","md","pdf","png","form","space","color","composition"],"ja":["canvas","design","md","pdf","png","","","",""],"ko":["canvas","design","md","pdf","png","","","",""],"es":["diseño de canvas","arte visual","filosofía de diseño","formato PNG","formato PDF","desarrollo de software","generación de arte","diseño gráfico","creación de contenido"],"fr":["conception de canvas","art visuel","philosophie de conception","format PNG","format PDF","développement de logiciels","génération d''art","conception graphique","création de contenu"],"de":["Canvas-Design","visuelle Kunst","Designphilosophie","PNG-Format","PDF-Format","Software-Entwicklung","Kunstgenerierung","Grafikdesign","Inhaltserschaffung"],"pt":["filosofia de design","arte visual","design gráfico","criação de designs","ferramentas de design","desenvolvimento de habilidades","design de posters","design de arte"],"ru":["философия дизайна","визуальное искусство","графический дизайн","создание дизайнов","инструменты дизайна","развитие навыков","дизайн плакатов","дизайн искусства"],"ar":["فلسفة التصميم","الفن البصري","التصميم الجرافيكي","إنشاء التصاميم","أدوات التصميم","تطوير المهارات","تصميم الملصقات","تصميم الفن"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Creative Agents requiring advanced visual art generation capabilities in .png and .pdf formats.","zh":"適合需要高級視覺藝術生成能力的創意代理，支持.png和.pdf格式。","ja":"高度な視覚芸術生成機能を必要とするクリエイティブエージェントに適しています。.pngおよび.pdf形式をサポートします。","ko":"고급 시각 예술 생성 기능이 필요한 창의적인 에이전트에 적합합니다. .png 및 .pdf 형식을 지원합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Creativos que requieren capacidades avanzadas de generación de arte visual en formatos .png y .pdf.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents créatifs nécessitant des capacités de génération d''art visuel avancées au format .png et .pdf.","de":"Ideal für kreative Agenten, die erweiterte visuelle Kunstgenerierungsfähigkeiten im .png- und .pdf-Format benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Criativos que requerem capacidades avançadas de geração de arte visual em formatos .png e .pdf.","ru":"Идеально для Креативных Агентов, требующих продвинутых возможностей генерации визуального искусства в форматах .png и .pdf.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الإبداعيين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتوليد الفن البصري في صيغ .png و .pdf."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create original visual designs using design philosophy, expressed through form, space, color, and composition, while generating deterministic visual art in .png and .pdf files, ensuring copyright compliance by never copying existing artists'' work.","zh":"賦予代理創造原創視覺設計的能力，使用設計哲學，通過形式、空間、顏色和構圖來表達，而生成確定的視覺藝術。.png和.pdf文件確保版權合規，永不複製現有的藝術作品。","ja":"エージェントに独自の視覚デザインを作成する能力を付与し、デザイン哲学を使用して、形、空間、色、構成を通じて表現し、.pngおよび.pdfファイルで確定的視覚芸術を生成します。既存のアーティストの作品をコピーしないことで、著作権コンプライアンスを確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 원래의 시각적 디자인을 만들 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 디자인 철학을 사용하고 형태, 공간, 색상 및 구성 등을 통해 표현하며 .png 및 .pdf 파일에서 결정적인 시각 예술을 생성하여 기존 예술家的 작품을 복사하지 않음으로써 저작권 준수를 보장합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear diseños visuales originales utilizando la filosofía del diseño, expresada a través de la forma, el espacio, el color y la composición, al mismo tiempo que genera arte visual determinista en archivos .png y .pdf, asegurando el cumplimiento de los derechos de autor al nunca copiar el trabajo de artistas existentes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des conceptions visuelles originales en utilisant la philosophie du design, exprimée à travers la forme, l''espace, la couleur et la composition, tout en générant de l''art visuel déterministe dans des fichiers .png et .pdf, en assurant le respect des droits d''auteur en n''copiant jamais le travail d''artistes existants.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, originelle visuelle Entwürfe unter Verwendung der Designphilosophie zu erstellen, die durch Form, Raum, Farbe und Komposition zum Ausdruck gebracht wird, während sie deterministische visuelle Kunst in .png- und .pdf-Dateien generiert und so die Einhaltung des Urheberrechts durch das Nie-Kopieren bestehender Künstlerarbeiten sicherstellt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar designs visuais originais usando filosofia de design, expressa através de forma, espaço, cor e composição, enquanto gera arte visual determinística em arquivos .png e .pdf, garantindo o cumprimento dos direitos autorais nunca copiando o trabalho de artistas existentes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать оригинальные визуальные дизайны, используя философию дизайна, выраженную через форму, пространство, цвет и композицию, при этом генерируя детерминированное визуальное искусство в файлах .png и .pdf, обеспечивая соблюдение авторских прав, никогда не копируя работу существующих художников.","ar":"يُمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء تصاميم مرئية أصلية باستخدام فلسفة التصميم، المعبر عنها من خلال الشكل والمساحة واللون والتركيب، مع توليد فن مرئي محدد في ملفات .png و .pdf، مما يضمن احترام حقوق النشر من خلال عدم نسخ أعمال الفنانين الحاليين أبداً."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating posters with unique aesthetic movements","Creating static pieces of art using visual philosophy","Designing compositions with specific color palettes and spatial arrangements"],"zh":["生成具有獨特美學運動的海報","使用視覺哲學創建靜態藝術作品","設計具有特定色彩調色板和空間安排的構圖"],"ja":["独自の美的運動を持つポスターを生成する","視覚哲学を使用して静的な芸術作品を作成する","特定の色彩パレットと空間配置を持つ構成を設計する"],"ko":["고유한 미학적 운동을 가진 포스터 생성","시각 철학을 사용하여 정적 예술 작품 생성","특정 색상 팔레트 및 공간 배치가 있는 구성 설계"],"es":["Generar pósters con movimientos estéticos únicos","Crear piezas de arte estáticas utilizando la filosofía visual","Diseñar composiciones con paletas de colores y disposiciones espaciales específicas"],"fr":["Générer des affiches avec des mouvements esthétiques uniques","Créer des pièces d''art statiques en utilisant la philosophie visuelle","Concevoir des compositions avec des palettes de couleurs et des dispositions spatiales spécifiques"],"de":["Generieren von Plakaten mit einzigartigen ästhetischen Bewegungen","Erstellen von statischen Kunstwerken unter Verwendung der visuellen Philosophie","Entwerfen von Kompositionen mit spezifischen Farbpaletten und räumlichen Anordnungen"],"pt":["Geração de pôsteres com movimentos estéticos únicos","Criação de peças de arte estáticas usando filosofia visual","Desenho de composições com paletas de cores e arranjos espaciais específicos"],"ru":["Генерация плакатов с уникальными эстетическими движениями","Создание статических произведений искусства, используя визуальную философию","Проектирование композиций с конкретными цветовыми палитрами и пространственными расположениями"],"ar":["توليد ملصقات ذات حركات جمالية فريدة","إنشاء قطع فنية ثابتة باستخدام الفلسفة البصرية","تصميم تركيبات ذات صيغ ألوان وترتيبات فضائية محددة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Output limited to .md, .pdf, and .png files","Requires adherence to design philosophy to avoid copyright violations"],"zh":["輸出限制為.md、.pdf和.png文件","需要遵守設計哲學以避免版權違規"],"ja":["出力は.md、.pdf、.pngファイルに限定される","著作権侵害を避けるためにデザイン哲学に従う必要がある"],"ko":["출력은 .md, .pdf, .png 파일로 제한됨","저작권 침해를 피하기 위해 디자인 철학을 따라야 함"],"es":["Salida limitada a archivos .md, .pdf y .png","Requiere la adhesión a la filosofía del diseño para evitar violaciones de derechos de autor"],"fr":["Sortie limitée aux fichiers .md, .pdf et .png","Nécessite l''adhésion à la philosophie du design pour éviter les violations de droits d''auteur"],"de":["Ausgabe beschränkt auf .md-, .pdf- und .png-Dateien","Erfordert die Einhaltung der Designphilosophie, um Urheberrechtsverletzungen zu vermeiden"],"pt":["Saída limitada a arquivos .md, .pdf e .png","Exige aderência à filosofia de design para evitar violações de direitos autorais"],"ru":["Выход ограничен файлами .md, .pdf и .png","Требует соблюдения философии дизайна, чтобы избежать нарушений авторских прав"],"ar":["الإخراج مقيد بملفات .md و .pdf و .png","يتطلب الالتزام bằng فلسفة التصميم لتجنب انتهاكات حقوق النشر"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"a1f288079624402f30682753c1d43920b6664785698d21d3e7aa197450a6448b","repoEtag":"W/\"76d69a3a3bb3abe2a601cefe1745ab33d5b89bce596aefbe206b5cf70e5967b9\"","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/pptx', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'pptx', 71981, 7353, 65, '2026-02-20T01:43:22Z', '2026-02-20T01:54:55.262Z', 'e5b0df918cbe9d62508b3cf808d73899633f82fc19f6258a25ef9f0de7e62125', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/pptx","name":"pptx","description":{"zh":"PPTX 技能用于创建、编辑和分析 PowerPoint 演示文稿，支持读取、解析和提取文本等功能","ja":"PPTX スキルは、PowerPoint プレゼンテーションを作成、編集、分析するために使用され、テキストの読み取り、解析、抽出などをサポートします","ko":"PPTX 기술은 파워포인트 프레젠테이션을 생성, 편집, 분석하는 데 사용되며, 텍스트 읽기, 파싱, 추출 등을 지원합니다","es":"La habilidad PPTX permite a los desarrolladores crear, editar y analizar archivos de presentación en formato PPTX de manera efectiva","fr":"La compétence PPTX permet aux développeurs de créer, modifier et analyser des fichiers de présentation au format PPTX de manière efficace","de":"Die PPTX-Fähigkeit ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Präsentationsdateien im PPTX-Format zu erstellen, bearbeiten und analysieren","pt":"A habilidade PPTX permite criar, editar e manipular arquivos de apresentação de forma eficiente","ru":"Навык PPTX позволяет создавать, редактировать и манипулировать файлами презентаций эффективно","ar":"تسمح مهارة PPTX بإنشاء وتحرير وعمل على ملفات العروض بطريقة فعالة","en":"Use this skill any time a .pptx file is involved in any way — as input, output, or both. This includes: creating slide decks, pitch decks, or presentations; reading, parsing, or extracting text from any .pptx file (even if the extracted content will be used elsewhere, like in an email or summary)..."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":71981,"forks":7353,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:43:22Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"pptx","description":"Use this skill any time a .pptx file is involved in any way — as input, output, or both. This includes: creating slide decks, pitch decks, or presentations; reading, parsing, or extracting text from any .pptx file (even if the extracted content will be used elsewhere, like in an email or summary); editing, modifying, or updating existing presentations; combining or splitting slide files; working with templates, layouts, speaker notes, or comments. Trigger whenever the user mentions \\deck,\\ \\slides,\\ \\presentation,\\ or references a .pptx filename, regardless of what they plan to do with the content afterward. If a .pptx file needs to be opened, created, or touched, use this skill.","bodyPreview":"# PPTX Skill\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Guide |\n|------|-------|\n| Read/analyze content | `python -m markitdown presentation.pptx` |\n| Edit or create from template | Read [editing.md](editing.md) |\n| Create from scratch | Read [pptxgenjs.md](pptxgenjs.md) |\n\n---\n\n## Reading Content\n\n```bash\n# Text extraction\npython -m markitdown presentation.pptx\n\n# Visual overview\npython scripts/thumbnail.py presentation.pptx\n\n# Raw XML\npython scripts/office/unpack.py presentation.pptx unpacked/\n```\n\n---\n\n##","body":"# PPTX Skill\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Guide |\n|------|-------|\n| Read/analyze content | `python -m markitdown presentation.pptx` |\n| Edit or create from template | Read [editing.md](editing.md) |\n| Create from scratch | Read [pptxgenjs.md](pptxgenjs.md) |\n\n---\n\n## Reading Content\n\n```bash\n# Text extraction\npython -m markitdown presentation.pptx\n\n# Visual overview\npython scripts/thumbnail.py presentation.pptx\n\n# Raw XML\npython scripts/office/unpack.py presentation.pptx unpacked/\n```\n\n---\n\n## Editing Workflow\n\n**Read [editing.md](editing.md) for full details.**\n\n1. Analyze template with `thumbnail.py`\n2. Unpack → manipulate slides → edit content → clean → pack\n\n---\n\n## Creating from Scratch\n\n**Read [pptxgenjs.md](pptxgenjs.md) for full details.**\n\nUse when no template or reference presentation is available.\n\n---\n\n## Design Ideas\n\n**Don''t create boring slides.** Plain bullets on a white background won''t impress anyone. Consider ideas from this list for each slide.\n\n### Before Starting\n\n- **Pick a bold, content-informed color palette**: The palette should feel designed for THIS topic. If swapping your colors into a completely different presentation would still \"work,\" you haven''t made specific enough choices.\n- **Dominance over equality**: One color should dominate (60-70% visual weight), with 1-2 supporting tones and one sharp accent. Never give all colors equal weight.\n- **Dark/light contrast**: Dark backgrounds for title + conclusion slides, light for content (\"sandwich\" structure). Or commit to dark throughout for a premium feel.\n- **Commit to a visual motif**: Pick ONE distinctive element and repeat it — rounded image frames, icons in colored circles, thick single-side borders. Carry it across every slide.\n\n### Color Palettes\n\nChoose colors that match your topic — don''t default to generic blue. Use these palettes as inspiration:\n\n| Theme | Primary | Secondary | Accent |\n|-------|---------|-----------|--------|\n| **Midnight Executive** | `1E2761` (navy) | `CADCFC` (ice blue) | `FFFFFF` (white) |\n| **Forest & Moss** | `2C5F2D` (forest) | `97BC62` (moss) | `F5F5F5` (cream) |\n| **Coral Energy** | `F96167` (coral) | `F9E795` (gold) | `2F3C7E` (navy) |\n| **Warm Terracotta** | `B85042` (terracotta) | `E7E8D1` (sand) | `A7BEAE` (sage) |\n| **Ocean Gradient** | `065A82` (deep blue) | `1C7293` (teal) | `21295C` (midnight) |\n| **Charcoal Minimal** | `36454F` (charcoal) | `F2F2F2` (off-white) | `212121` (black) |\n| **Teal Trust** | `028090` (teal) | `00A896` (seafoam) | `02C39A` (mint) |\n| **Berry & Cream** | `6D2E46` (berry) | `A26769` (dusty rose) | `ECE2D0` (cream) |\n| **Sage Calm** | `84B59F` (sage) | `69A297` (eucalyptus) | `50808E` (slate) |\n| **Cherry Bold** | `990011` (cherry) | `FCF6F5` (off-white) | `2F3C7E` (navy) |\n\n### For Each Slide\n\n**Every slide needs a visual element** — image, chart, icon, or shape. Text-only slides are forgettable.\n\n**Layout options:**\n- Two-column (text left, illustration on right)\n- Icon + text rows (icon in colored circle, bold header, description below)\n- 2x2 or 2x3 grid (image on one side, grid of content blocks on other)\n- Half-bleed image (full left or right side) with content overlay\n\n**Data display:**\n- Large stat callouts (big numbers 60-72pt with small labels below)\n- Comparison columns (before/after, pros/cons, side-by-side options)\n- Timeline or process flow (numbered steps, arrows)\n\n**Visual polish:**\n- Icons in small colored circles next to section headers\n- Italic accent text for key stats or taglines\n\n### Typography\n\n**Choose an interesting font pairing** — don''t default to Arial. Pick a header font with personality and pair it with a clean body font.\n\n| Header Font | Body Font |\n|-------------|-----------|\n| Georgia | Calibri |\n| Arial Black | Arial |\n| Calibri | Calibri Light |\n| Cambria | Calibri |\n| Trebuchet MS | Calibri |\n| Impact | Arial |\n| Palatino | Garamond |\n| Consolas | Calibri |\n\n| Element | Size |\n|---------|------|\n| Slide title | 36-44pt bold |\n| Section header | 20-24pt bold |\n| Body text | 14-16pt |\n| Captions | 10-12pt muted |\n\n### Spacing\n\n- 0.5\" minimum margins\n- 0.3-0.5\" between content blocks\n- Leave breathing room—don''t fill every inch\n\n### Avoid (Common Mistakes)\n\n- **Don''t repeat the same layout** — vary columns, cards, and callouts across slides\n- **Don''t center body text** — left-align paragraphs and lists; center only titles\n- **Don''t skimp on size contrast** — titles need 36pt+ to stand out from 14-16pt body\n- **Don''t default to blue** — pick colors that reflect the specific topic\n- **Don''t mix spacing randomly** — choose 0.3\" or 0.5\" gaps and use consistently\n- **Don''t style one slide and leave the rest plain** — commit fully or keep it simple throughout\n- **Don''t create text-only slides** — add images, icons, charts, or visual elements; avoid plain title + bullets\n- **Don''t forget text box padding** — when aligning lines or shapes with text edges, set `margin: 0` on the text box or offset the shape to account for padding\n- **Don''t use low-contrast elements** — icons AND text need strong contrast against the background; avoid light text on light backgrounds or dark text on dark backgrounds\n- **NEVER use accent lines under titles** — these are a hallmark of AI-generated slides; use whitespace or background color instead\n\n---\n\n## QA (Required)\n\n**Assume there are problems. Your job is to find them.**\n\nYour first render is almost never correct. Approach QA as a bug hunt, not a confirmation step. If you found zero issues on first inspection, you weren''t looking hard enough.\n\n### Content QA\n\n```bash\npython -m markitdown output.pptx\n```\n\nCheck for missing content, typos, wrong order.\n\n**When using templates, check for leftover placeholder text:**\n\n```bash\npython -m markitdown output.pptx | grep -iE \"xxxx|lorem|ipsum|this.*(page|slide).*layout\"\n```\n\nIf grep returns results, fix them before declaring success.\n\n### Visual QA\n\n**⚠️ USE SUBAGENTS** — even for 2-3 slides. You''ve been staring at the code and will see what you expect, not what''s there. Subagents have fresh eyes.\n\nConvert slides to images (see [Converting to Images](#converting-to-images)), then use this prompt:\n\n```\nVisually inspect these slides. Assume there are issues — find them.\n\nLook for:\n- Overlapping elements (text through shapes, lines through words, stacked elements)\n- Text overflow or cut off at edges/box boundaries\n- Decorative lines positioned for single-line text but title wrapped to two lines\n- Source citations or footers colliding with content above\n- Elements too close (< 0.3\" gaps) or cards/sections nearly touching\n- Uneven gaps (large empty area in one place, cramped in another)\n- Insufficient margin from slide edges (< 0.5\")\n- Columns or similar elements not aligned consistently\n- Low-contrast text (e.g., light gray text on cream-colored background)\n- Low-contrast icons (e.g., dark icons on dark backgrounds without a contrasting circle)\n- Text boxes too narrow causing excessive wrapping\n- Leftover placeholder content\n\nFor each slide, list issues or areas of concern, even if minor.\n\nRead and analyze these images:\n1. /path/to/slide-01.jpg (Expected: [brief description])\n2. /path/to/slide-02.jpg (Expected: [brief description])\n\nReport ALL issues found, including minor ones.\n```\n\n### Verification Loop\n\n1. Generate slides → Convert to images → Inspect\n2. **List issues found** (if none found, look again more critically)\n3. Fix issues\n4. **Re-verify affected slides** — one fix often creates another problem\n5. Repeat until a full pass reveals no new issues\n\n**Do not declare success until you''ve completed at least one fix-and-verify cycle.**\n\n---\n\n## Converting to Images\n\nConvert presentations to individual slide images for visual inspection:\n\n```bash\npython scripts/office/soffice.py --headless --convert-to pdf output.pptx\npdftoppm -jpeg -r 150 output.pdf slide\n```\n\nThis creates `slide-01.jpg`, `slide-02.jpg`, etc.\n\nTo re-render specific slides after fixes:\n\n```bash\npdftoppm -jpeg -r 150 -f N -l N output.pdf slide-fixed\n```\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- `pip install \"markitdown[pptx]\"` - text extraction\n- `pip install Pillow` - thumbnail grids\n- `npm install -g pptxgenjs` - creating from scratch\n- LibreOffice (`soffice`) - PDF conversion (auto-configured for sandboxed environments via `scripts/office/soffice.py`)\n- Poppler (`pdftoppm`) - PDF to images\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T01:54:55.262Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"PPTX 技能：创建、编辑和分析 PowerPoint 演示文稿","ja":"PPTX スキル：PowerPoint プレゼンテーションを作成、編集、分析する","ko":"PPTX 기술: 파워포인트 프레젠테이션 생성, 편집, 분석","es":"Habilidad PPTX para desarrolladores","fr":"Compétence PPTX pour les développeurs","de":"PPTX-Fähigkeit für Entwickler","pt":"Habilidades PPTX: Crie e Edite Apresentações","ru":"Навыки PPTX: Создание и Редактирование Презентаций","ar":"مهارات PPTX: إنشاء وتحرير العروض","en":"pptx"},"description":{"zh":"PPTX 技能用于创建、编辑和分析 PowerPoint 演示文稿，支持读取、解析和提取文本等功能","ja":"PPTX スキルは、PowerPoint プレゼンテーションを作成、編集、分析するために使用され、テキストの読み取り、解析、抽出などをサポートします","ko":"PPTX 기술은 파워포인트 프레젠테이션을 생성, 편집, 분석하는 데 사용되며, 텍스트 읽기, 파싱, 추출 등을 지원합니다","es":"La habilidad PPTX permite a los desarrolladores crear, editar y analizar archivos de presentación en formato PPTX de manera efectiva","fr":"La compétence PPTX permet aux développeurs de créer, modifier et analyser des fichiers de présentation au format PPTX de manière efficace","de":"Die PPTX-Fähigkeit ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Präsentationsdateien im PPTX-Format zu erstellen, bearbeiten und analysieren","pt":"A habilidade PPTX permite criar, editar e manipular arquivos de apresentação de forma eficiente","ru":"Навык PPTX позволяет создавать, редактировать и манипулировать файлами презентаций эффективно","ar":"تسمح مهارة PPTX بإنشاء وتحرير وعمل على ملفات العروض بطريقة فعالة","en":"Use this skill any time a .pptx file is involved in any way — as input, output, or both. This includes: creating slide decks, pitch decks, or presentations; ..."},"definition":{"en":"Use this skill any time a .pptx file is involved in any way — as input, output, or both. This includes: creating slide decks, pitch decks, or presentations; reading, parsing, or extracting text from any .pptx file (even if the extracted content will be used elsewhere, like in an email or summary); editing, modifying, or updating existing presentations; combining or splitting slide files; working with templates, layouts, speaker notes, or comments. Trigger whenever the user mentions \\deck,\\ \\slides,\\ \\presentation,\\ or references a .pptx filename, regardless of what they plan to do with the content afterward. If a .pptx file needs to be opened, created, or touched, use this skill."},"features":{"zh":["创建和编辑 PowerPoint 演示文稿","读取和解析 PPTX 文件","提取文本和图像","编辑和修改现有演示文稿","支持模板和布局"],"ja":["PowerPoint プレゼンテーションを作成および編集","PPTX ファイルを読み取りおよび解析","テキストと画像を抽出","既存のプレゼンテーションを編集および修正","テンプレートとレイアウトをサポート"],"ko":["파워포인트 프레젠테이션 생성 및 편집","PPTX 파일 읽기 및 파싱","텍스트 및 이미지 추출","기존 프레젠테이션 편집 및 수정","템플릿 및 레이아웃 지원"],"es":["Creación de presentaciones","Edición de archivos PPTX","Análisis de contenido","Extracción de texto","Creación de miniaturas"],"fr":["Création de présentations","Édition de fichiers PPTX","Analyse de contenu","Extraction de texte","Création de miniatures"],"de":["Erstellung von Präsentationen","Bearbeitung von PPTX-Dateien","Inhaltsanalyse","Textextraktion","Erstellung von Miniaturansichten"],"pt":["Criação de apresentações","Edição de arquivos PPTX","Extração de texto de apresentações","Criação de decks de slides","Manipulação de templates e layouts"],"ru":["Создание презентаций","Редактирование файлов PPTX","Извлечение текста из презентаций","Создание слайд-шоу","Манипулирование шаблонами и макетами"],"ar":["إنشاء عروض","تحرير ملفات PPTX","استخراج النص من العروض","إنشاء مجموعات شرائح","التلاعب بالقوالب والتخطيطات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PPTX 技能","PowerPoint 演示文稿","创建和编辑","读取和解析","提取文本和图像","模板和布局"],"ja":["PPTX スキル","PowerPoint プレゼンテーション","作成および編集","読み取りおよび解析","テキストと画像の抽出","テンプレートとレイアウト"],"ko":["PPTX 기술","파워포인트 프레젠테이션","생성 및 편집","읽기 및 파싱","텍스트 및 이미지 추출","템플릿 및 레이아웃"],"es":["PPTX","presentaciones","desarrollo de software","edición de archivos","análisis de contenido","extracción de texto","creación de miniaturas"],"fr":["PPTX","présentations","développement de logiciels","édition de fichiers","analyse de contenu","extraction de texte","création de miniatures"],"de":["PPTX","Präsentationen","Software-Entwicklung","Bearbeitung von Dateien","Inhaltsanalyse","Textextraktion","Erstellung von Miniaturansichten"],"pt":["habilidade PPTX","criação de apresentações","edição de PPTX","extração de texto","decks de slides","templates de apresentação"],"ru":["навык PPTX","создание презентаций","редактирование PPTX","извлечение текста","слайд-шоу","шаблоны презентаций"],"ar":["مهارة PPTX","إنشاء عروض","تحرير PPTX","استخراج النص","مجموعات شرائح","قوالب العروض"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Document Analysis Agents needing advanced PowerPoint presentation parsing capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 PowerPoint 演示文稿解析能力的文档分析代理。","ja":"ドキュメント分析エージェントが高度な PowerPoint プレゼンテーションの解析機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 PowerPoint 프레젠테이션 파싱 기능을 필요로 하는 문서 분석 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Documentos que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de análisis de presentaciones de PowerPoint.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse de Documents ayant besoin de capacités avancées d''analyse de présentations PowerPoint.","de":"Perfekt für Dokumentenanalyse-Agenten, die erweiterte PowerPoint-Präsentationsanalysefunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Documentos que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de análise de apresentações do PowerPoint.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа документов, которым требуются передовые возможности разбора презентаций PowerPoint.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل الوثائق التي تحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة لتحليل العروض التقديمية لبرنامج PowerPoint."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to read, analyze, and edit .pptx files using Python libraries like markitdown and pptxgenjs, enabling seamless integration with presentation-related tasks.","zh":"使代理能够使用 Python 库（如 markitdown 和 pptxgenjs）读取、分析和编辑 .pptx 文件，从而实现与演示文稿相关任务的无缝集成。","ja":"markitdown や pptxgenjs などの Python ライブラリを使用して、エージェントが .pptx ファイルを読み取り、分析し、編集できるようにし、プレゼンテーション関連タスクとのシームレスな統合を可能にします。","ko":"마크다운 및 pptxgenjs와 같은 파이썬 라이브러리를 사용하여 에이전트가 .pptx 파일을 읽고 분석하고 편집할 수 있도록 하여 프레젠테이션 관련 작업과 원활한 통합을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a leer, analizar y editar archivos .pptx utilizando bibliotecas de Python como markitdown y pptxgenjs, lo que permite una integración sin problemas con tareas relacionadas con presentaciones.","fr":"Permet aux agents de lire, d''analyser et de modifier des fichiers .pptx en utilisant des bibliothèques Python comme markitdown et pptxgenjs, ce qui permet une intégration transparente avec des tâches liées aux présentations.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, .pptx-Dateien mithilfe von Python-Bibliotheken wie markitdown und pptxgenjs zu lesen, zu analysieren und zu bearbeiten, was eine nahtlose Integration mit präsentationsbezogenen Aufgaben ermöglicht.","pt":"Permite que os agentes leiam, analisem e editem arquivos .pptx usando bibliotecas Python como markitdown e pptxgenjs, possibilitando uma integração perfeita com tarefas relacionadas a apresentações.","ru":"Позволяет агентам читать, анализировать и редактировать файлы .pptx, используя библиотеки Python, такие как markitdown и pptxgenjs, обеспечивая бесшовную интеграцию с задачами, связанными с презентациями.","ar":"يمكن للعمليات قراءة وتحليل وتحرير ملفات .pptx باستخدام مكتبات Python مثل markitdown وpptxgenjs، مما يتيح التكامل السلس مع المهام المتعلقة بالعروض التقديمية."},"useCases":{"en":["Extracting text from existing presentations","Generating new slide decks from templates","Automating presentation updates with modified content"],"zh":["从现有演示文稿中提取文本","从模板生成新幻灯片","使用修改内容自动更新演示文稿"],"ja":["既存のプレゼンテーションからテキストを抽出する","テンプレートから新しいスライドデッキを生成する","変更されたコンテンツでプレゼンテーションを自動更新する"],"ko":["기존 프레젠테이션에서 텍스트 추출","템플릿에서 새로운 슬라이드 데크 생성","수정된 콘텐츠로 프레젠테이션 자동 업데이트"],"es":["Extraer texto de presentaciones existentes","Generar nuevos decks de diapositivas a partir de plantillas","Automatizar actualizaciones de presentaciones con contenido modificado"],"fr":["Extraire du texte de présentations existantes","Générer de nouveaux decks de diapositives à partir de modèles","Automatiser les mises à jour de présentations avec un contenu modifié"],"de":["Text aus bestehenden Präsentationen extrahieren","Neue Folienstapel aus Vorlagen generieren","Präsentationsaktualisierungen mit modifiziertem Inhalt automatisieren"],"pt":["Extração de texto de apresentações existentes","Geração de novos decks de slides a partir de modelos","Automatização de atualizações de apresentações com conteúdo modificado"],"ru":["Извлечение текста из существующих презентаций","Генерация новых наборов слайдов из шаблонов","Автоматизация обновлений презентаций с измененным содержанием"],"ar":["استخراج النص من العروض التقديمية الحالية","إنشاء عروض تقديمية جديدة من القوالب","أتمتة تحديث العروض التقديمية بمحتوى معدل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3.x environment","Limited to .pptx file format"],"zh":["需要 Python 3.x 环境","仅限 .pptx 文件格式"],"ja":["Python 3.x 環境が必要",".pptx ファイル形式のみ"],"ko":["파이썬 3.x 환경이 필요함",".pptx 파일 형식만 지원"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Python 3.x","Limitado al formato de archivo .pptx"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Python 3.x","Limité au format de fichier .pptx"],"de":["Benötigt Python 3.x-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf .pptx-Dateiformat"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Python 3.x","Limitado ao formato de arquivo .pptx"],"ru":["Требуется среда Python 3.x","Ограничен форматом файла .pptx"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Python 3.x","محدود بتنسيق ملف .pptx"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"e5b0df918cbe9d62508b3cf808d73899633f82fc19f6258a25ef9f0de7e62125","repoEtag":"W/\"5456759f24524b9171780a611a3970c1ae87a3d09576f2945661ad98ce4c37da\"","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/slack-gif-creator', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'slack-gif-creator', 71981, 7353, 65, '2026-02-20T01:43:22Z', '2026-02-20T01:57:20.434Z', '2efca615ce55a3edd8fc05c779068a8085816617991987e446606403cd3abb22', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/slack-gif-creator","name":"slack-gif-creator","description":{"zh":"Slack GIF 创建工具提供了一套用于创建 Slack 动态 GIF 的实用工具和知识，包括尺寸、参数和动画概念","ja":"Slack GIF作成ツールは、Slack 用の動画 GIF を作成するためのユーティリティと知識を提供し、寸法、パラメータ、動画概念を含む","ko":"슬랙 GIF 생성 도구는 슬랙을 위한 애니메이션 GIF를 생성하기 위한 도구와 지식을 제공하며, 크기, 매개변수 및 애니메이션 개념을 포함","es":"Herramienta para crear GIFs animados para Slack con utilidades y conocimientos para desarrolladores","fr":"Outil pour créer des GIFs animés pour Slack avec des utilitaires et des connaissances pour les développeurs","de":"Toolkit für die Erstellung von animierten GIFs für Slack mit Utilities und Wissen für Entwickler","pt":"O Slack GIF Creator é uma ferramenta que fornece utilitários e conhecimentos para criar GIFs animados otimizados para o Slack.","ru":"Создатель GIF для Slack - это набор инструментов, который предоставляет утилиты и знания для создания анимированных GIF-файлов, оптимизированных для Slack.","ar":"منشئ GIF لاسلاك هو أداة توفر أدوات ومكتبة معرفة لإنشاء ملفات GIF المتحركة المُحسّنة لاسلاك.","en":"Knowledge and utilities for creating animated GIFs optimized for Slack. Provides constraints, validation tools, and animation concepts. Use when users request animated GIFs for Slack like make me a GIF of X doing Y for Slack."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":71981,"forks":7353,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:43:22Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"slack-gif-creator","description":"Knowledge and utilities for creating animated GIFs optimized for Slack. Provides constraints, validation tools, and animation concepts. Use when users request animated GIFs for Slack like make me a GIF of X doing Y for Slack.","bodyPreview":"# Slack GIF Creator\n\nA toolkit providing utilities and knowledge for creating animated GIFs optimized for Slack.\n\n## Slack Requirements\n\n**Dimensions:**\n- Emoji GIFs: 128x128 (recommended)\n- Message GIFs: 480x480\n\n**Parameters:**\n- FPS: 10-30 (lower is smaller file size)\n- Colors: 48-128 (fewer = smaller file size)\n- Duration: Keep under 3 seconds for emoji GIFs\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n```python\nfrom core.gif_builder import GIFBuilder\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n# 1. Create builder\nbuilder = GI","body":"# Slack GIF Creator\n\nA toolkit providing utilities and knowledge for creating animated GIFs optimized for Slack.\n\n## Slack Requirements\n\n**Dimensions:**\n- Emoji GIFs: 128x128 (recommended)\n- Message GIFs: 480x480\n\n**Parameters:**\n- FPS: 10-30 (lower is smaller file size)\n- Colors: 48-128 (fewer = smaller file size)\n- Duration: Keep under 3 seconds for emoji GIFs\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n```python\nfrom core.gif_builder import GIFBuilder\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n\n# 1. Create builder\nbuilder = GIFBuilder(width=128, height=128, fps=10)\n\n# 2. Generate frames\nfor i in range(12):\n    frame = Image.new(''RGB'', (128, 128), (240, 248, 255))\n    draw = ImageDraw.Draw(frame)\n\n    # Draw your animation using PIL primitives\n    # (circles, polygons, lines, etc.)\n\n    builder.add_frame(frame)\n\n# 3. Save with optimization\nbuilder.save(''output.gif'', num_colors=48, optimize_for_emoji=True)\n```\n\n## Drawing Graphics\n\n### Working with User-Uploaded Images\nIf a user uploads an image, consider whether they want to:\n- **Use it directly** (e.g., \"animate this\", \"split this into frames\")\n- **Use it as inspiration** (e.g., \"make something like this\")\n\nLoad and work with images using PIL:\n```python\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nuploaded = Image.open(''file.png'')\n# Use directly, or just as reference for colors/style\n```\n\n### Drawing from Scratch\nWhen drawing graphics from scratch, use PIL ImageDraw primitives:\n\n```python\nfrom PIL import ImageDraw\n\ndraw = ImageDraw.Draw(frame)\n\n# Circles/ovals\ndraw.ellipse([x1, y1, x2, y2], fill=(r, g, b), outline=(r, g, b), width=3)\n\n# Stars, triangles, any polygon\npoints = [(x1, y1), (x2, y2), (x3, y3), ...]\ndraw.polygon(points, fill=(r, g, b), outline=(r, g, b), width=3)\n\n# Lines\ndraw.line([(x1, y1), (x2, y2)], fill=(r, g, b), width=5)\n\n# Rectangles\ndraw.rectangle([x1, y1, x2, y2], fill=(r, g, b), outline=(r, g, b), width=3)\n```\n\n**Don''t use:** Emoji fonts (unreliable across platforms) or assume pre-packaged graphics exist in this skill.\n\n### Making Graphics Look Good\n\nGraphics should look polished and creative, not basic. Here''s how:\n\n**Use thicker lines** - Always set `width=2` or higher for outlines and lines. Thin lines (width=1) look choppy and amateurish.\n\n**Add visual depth**:\n- Use gradients for backgrounds (`create_gradient_background`)\n- Layer multiple shapes for complexity (e.g., a star with a smaller star inside)\n\n**Make shapes more interesting**:\n- Don''t just draw a plain circle - add highlights, rings, or patterns\n- Stars can have glows (draw larger, semi-transparent versions behind)\n- Combine multiple shapes (stars + sparkles, circles + rings)\n\n**Pay attention to colors**:\n- Use vibrant, complementary colors\n- Add contrast (dark outlines on light shapes, light outlines on dark shapes)\n- Consider the overall composition\n\n**For complex shapes** (hearts, snowflakes, etc.):\n- Use combinations of polygons and ellipses\n- Calculate points carefully for symmetry\n- Add details (a heart can have a highlight curve, snowflakes have intricate branches)\n\nBe creative and detailed! A good Slack GIF should look polished, not like placeholder graphics.\n\n## Available Utilities\n\n### GIFBuilder (`core.gif_builder`)\nAssembles frames and optimizes for Slack:\n```python\nbuilder = GIFBuilder(width=128, height=128, fps=10)\nbuilder.add_frame(frame)  # Add PIL Image\nbuilder.add_frames(frames)  # Add list of frames\nbuilder.save(''out.gif'', num_colors=48, optimize_for_emoji=True, remove_duplicates=True)\n```\n\n### Validators (`core.validators`)\nCheck if GIF meets Slack requirements:\n```python\nfrom core.validators import validate_gif, is_slack_ready\n\n# Detailed validation\npasses, info = validate_gif(''my.gif'', is_emoji=True, verbose=True)\n\n# Quick check\nif is_slack_ready(''my.gif''):\n    print(\"Ready!\")\n```\n\n### Easing Functions (`core.easing`)\nSmooth motion instead of linear:\n```python\nfrom core.easing import interpolate\n\n# Progress from 0.0 to 1.0\nt = i / (num_frames - 1)\n\n# Apply easing\ny = interpolate(start=0, end=400, t=t, easing=''ease_out'')\n\n# Available: linear, ease_in, ease_out, ease_in_out,\n#           bounce_out, elastic_out, back_out\n```\n\n### Frame Helpers (`core.frame_composer`)\nConvenience functions for common needs:\n```python\nfrom core.frame_composer import (\n    create_blank_frame,         # Solid color background\n    create_gradient_background,  # Vertical gradient\n    draw_circle,                # Helper for circles\n    draw_text,                  # Simple text rendering\n    draw_star                   # 5-pointed star\n)\n```\n\n## Animation Concepts\n\n### Shake/Vibrate\nOffset object position with oscillation:\n- Use `math.sin()` or `math.cos()` with frame index\n- Add small random variations for natural feel\n- Apply to x and/or y position\n\n### Pulse/Heartbeat\nScale object size rhythmically:\n- Use `math.sin(t * frequency * 2 * math.pi)` for smooth pulse\n- For heartbeat: two quick pulses then pause (adjust sine wave)\n- Scale between 0.8 and 1.2 of base size\n\n### Bounce\nObject falls and bounces:\n- Use `interpolate()` with `easing=''bounce_out''` for landing\n- Use `easing=''ease_in''` for falling (accelerating)\n- Apply gravity by increasing y velocity each frame\n\n### Spin/Rotate\nRotate object around center:\n- PIL: `image.rotate(angle, resample=Image.BICUBIC)`\n- For wobble: use sine wave for angle instead of linear\n\n### Fade In/Out\nGradually appear or disappear:\n- Create RGBA image, adjust alpha channel\n- Or use `Image.blend(image1, image2, alpha)`\n- Fade in: alpha from 0 to 1\n- Fade out: alpha from 1 to 0\n\n### Slide\nMove object from off-screen to position:\n- Start position: outside frame bounds\n- End position: target location\n- Use `interpolate()` with `easing=''ease_out''` for smooth stop\n- For overshoot: use `easing=''back_out''`\n\n### Zoom\nScale and position for zoom effect:\n- Zoom in: scale from 0.1 to 2.0, crop center\n- Zoom out: scale from 2.0 to 1.0\n- Can add motion blur for drama (PIL filter)\n\n### Explode/Particle Burst\nCreate particles radiating outward:\n- Generate particles with random angles and velocities\n- Update each particle: `x += vx`, `y += vy`\n- Add gravity: `vy += gravity_constant`\n- Fade out particles over time (reduce alpha)\n\n## Optimization Strategies\n\nOnly when asked to make the file size smaller, implement a few of the following methods:\n\n1. **Fewer frames** - Lower FPS (10 instead of 20) or shorter duration\n2. **Fewer colors** - `num_colors=48` instead of 128\n3. **Smaller dimensions** - 128x128 instead of 480x480\n4. **Remove duplicates** - `remove_duplicates=True` in save()\n5. **Emoji mode** - `optimize_for_emoji=True` auto-optimizes\n\n```python\n# Maximum optimization for emoji\nbuilder.save(\n    ''emoji.gif'',\n    num_colors=48,\n    optimize_for_emoji=True,\n    remove_duplicates=True\n)\n```\n\n## Philosophy\n\nThis skill provides:\n- **Knowledge**: Slack''s requirements and animation concepts\n- **Utilities**: GIFBuilder, validators, easing functions\n- **Flexibility**: Create the animation logic using PIL primitives\n\nIt does NOT provide:\n- Rigid animation templates or pre-made functions\n- Emoji font rendering (unreliable across platforms)\n- A library of pre-packaged graphics built into the skill\n\n**Note on user uploads**: This skill doesn''t include pre-built graphics, but if a user uploads an image, use PIL to load and work with it - interpret based on their request whether they want it used directly or just as inspiration.\n\nBe creative! Combine concepts (bouncing + rotating, pulsing + sliding, etc.) and use PIL''s full capabilities.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n```bash\npip install pillow imageio numpy\n```\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T01:57:20.434Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"Slack GIF 创建工具","ja":"Slack GIF作成ツール","ko":"슬랙 GIF 생성 도구","es":"Creador de GIFs para Slack","fr":"Créateur de GIFs pour Slack","de":"Slack GIF Ersteller","pt":"Criador de GIFs para Slack","ru":"Создатель GIF для Slack","ar":"منشئ GIF لاسلاك","en":"slack-gif-creator"},"description":{"zh":"Slack GIF 创建工具提供了一套用于创建 Slack 动态 GIF 的实用工具和知识，包括尺寸、参数和动画概念","ja":"Slack GIF作成ツールは、Slack 用の動画 GIF を作成するためのユーティリティと知識を提供し、寸法、パラメータ、動画概念を含む","ko":"슬랙 GIF 생성 도구는 슬랙을 위한 애니메이션 GIF를 생성하기 위한 도구와 지식을 제공하며, 크기, 매개변수 및 애니메이션 개념을 포함","es":"Herramienta para crear GIFs animados para Slack con utilidades y conocimientos para desarrolladores","fr":"Outil pour créer des GIFs animés pour Slack avec des utilitaires et des connaissances pour les développeurs","de":"Toolkit für die Erstellung von animierten GIFs für Slack mit Utilities und Wissen für Entwickler","pt":"O Slack GIF Creator é uma ferramenta que fornece utilitários e conhecimentos para criar GIFs animados otimizados para o Slack.","ru":"Создатель GIF для Slack - это набор инструментов, который предоставляет утилиты и знания для создания анимированных GIF-файлов, оптимизированных для Slack.","ar":"منشئ GIF لاسلاك هو أداة توفر أدوات ومكتبة معرفة لإنشاء ملفات GIF المتحركة المُحسّنة لاسلاك.","en":"Knowledge and utilities for creating animated GIFs optimized for Slack. Provides constraints, validation tools, and animation concepts. Use when users reques..."},"definition":{"en":"Knowledge and utilities for creating animated GIFs optimized for Slack. Provides constraints, validation tools, and animation concepts. Use when users request animated GIFs for Slack like make me a GIF of X doing Y for Slack."},"features":{"zh":["提供尺寸和参数指导","支持动画概念","优化 GIF 文件大小","支持 Emoji GIF 和消息 GIF","提供 Python 开发示例"],"ja":["寸法とパラメータのガイドを提供","動画概念をサポート","GIF ファイルサイズを最適化","Emoji GIF とメッセージ GIF をサポート","Python 開発例を提供"],"ko":["크기와 매개변수 지침 제공","애니메이션 개념 지원","GIF 파일 크기 최적화","이모티콘 GIF 및 메시지 GIF 지원","파이썬 개발 예제 제공"],"es":["Dimensiones recomendadas para GIFs de emoji y mensaje","Parámetros de FPS, colores y duración para GIFs optimizados","Herramientas de validación y conceptos de animación","Compatibilidad con Slack","Código de ejemplo en Python"],"fr":["Dimensions recommandées pour les GIFs d''emoji et de message","Paramètres de FPS, de couleurs et de durée pour les GIFs optimisés","Outils de validation et concepts d''animation","Compatibilité avec Slack","Exemple de code en Python"],"de":["Empfohlene Dimensionen für Emoji- und Nachrichten-GIFs","Parameter für FPS, Farben und Dauer für optimierte GIFs","Validierungstools und Animationskonzepte","Kompatibilität mit Slack","Beispielcode in Python"],"pt":["Dimensões personalizáveis para GIFs de emoji e mensagem","Controle de FPS para tamanho de arquivo menor","Limites de cor para tamanho de arquivo menor","Duração personalizada para GIFs de emoji","Ferramentas de validação para garantir compatibilidade com o Slack"],"ru":["Настраиваемые размеры для GIF-изображений эмодзи и сообщений","Контроль FPS для меньшего размера файла","Ограничения цвета для меньшего размера файла","Настраиваемая продолжительность для GIF-изображений эмодзи","Инструменты проверки для обеспечения совместимости со Slack"],"ar":["احجام قابلة للتعديل لملفات GIF الإيموجي والرسائل","مراقبة معدل الإطار للتحكم في حجم الملف","قيود الألوان لحجم الملف الأصغر","مدة مخصصة لملفات GIF الإيموجي","أدوات التحقق لضمان التوافق مع السلاك"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Slack GIF","动态 GIF","GIF 创建工具","Slack 开发","Python 开发","GIF 优化","动画概念"],"ja":["Slack GIF","動画 GIF","GIF 作成ツール","Slack 開発","Python 開発","GIF 最適化","動画概念"],"ko":["슬랙 GIF","애니메이션 GIF","GIF 생성 도구","슬랙 개발","파이썬 개발","GIF 최적화","애니메이션 개념"],"es":["creador de GIFs para Slack","GIFs animados para Slack","utilidades para desarrolladores","conocimientos para crear GIFs","optimización de GIFs para Slack","desarrollo de GIFs para Slack"],"fr":["créateur de GIFs pour Slack","GIFs animés pour Slack","utilitaires pour les développeurs","connaissances pour créer des GIFs","optimisation de GIFs pour Slack","développement de GIFs pour Slack"],"de":["Slack GIF Ersteller","animierte GIFs für Slack","Utilities für Entwickler","Wissen für die Erstellung von GIFs","Optimierung von GIFs für Slack","Entwicklung von GIFs für Slack"],"pt":["criador de GIFs para Slack","GIFs animados para Slack","otimização de GIFs para Slack","desenvolvimento de GIFs para Slack","ferramentas de criação de GIFs para Slack","GIFs personalizados para Slack"],"ru":["создатель GIF для Slack","анимированные GIF-файлы для Slack","оптимизация GIF-файлов для Slack","разработка GIF-файлов для Slack","инструменты создания GIF-файлов для Slack","пользовательские GIF-файлы для Slack"],"ar":["منشئ GIF لاسلاك","ملفات GIF المتحركة لاسلاك","تحسين ملفات GIF لاسلاك","تطوير ملفات GIF لاسلاك","أدوات إنشاء ملفات GIF لاسلاك","ملفات GIF مخصصة لاسلاك"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Visual Content Agents needing advanced animated GIF creation capabilities for Slack.","zh":"非常适合需要高级动画GIF创建功能的Slack视觉内容代理。","ja":"Slackで高度なアニメーションGIF作成機能を必要とする視覚コンテンツエージェントに最適。","ko":"Slack에서 고급 애니메이션 GIF 생성 기능을 필요한 시각적 콘텐츠 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Contenido Visual que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de creación de GIF animados para Slack.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de contenu visuel ayant besoin de capacités avancées de création de GIF animés pour Slack.","de":"Perfekt für visuelle Inhaltsagenten, die erweiterte Funktionen zur Erstellung von animierten GIFs für Slack benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Conteúdo Visual que precisam de capacidades avançadas de criação de GIFs animados para o Slack.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Визуальных Контент-агентов, которым необходимы расширенные возможности создания анимированных GIF для Slack.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المحتوى المرئي الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لإنشاء صور GIF المتحركة لبرنامج Slack."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate optimized animated GIFs using Python and the PIL library, with constraints such as 128x128 dimensions for emoji GIFs and 10-30 FPS for smaller file sizes.","zh":"使代理能够使用Python和PIL库生成优化的动画GIF，受128x128尺寸的限制，用于emoji GIF，10-30 FPS用于较小的文件大小。","ja":"PythonとPILライブラリを使用して、エージェントが128x128のサイズ制限のあるemoji GIFや、10-30 FPSの小さいファイルサイズの最適化されたアニメーションGIFを作成できるようにする。","ko":"Python과 PIL 라이브러리를 사용하여 에이전트가 최적화된 애니메이션 GIF를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, emoji GIF의 경우 128x128 크기 제한과 10-30 FPS의 작은 파일 크기가 있다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar GIF animados optimizados utilizando Python y la biblioteca PIL, con restricciones como dimensiones de 128x128 para GIF de emojis y 10-30 FPS para tamaños de archivo más pequeños.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des GIF animés optimisés en utilisant Python et la bibliothèque PIL, avec des contraintes telles que des dimensions de 128x128 pour les GIF d''émoticônes et 10-30 FPS pour des tailles de fichiers plus petites.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, optimierte animierte GIFs mit Python und der PIL-Bibliothek zu erstellen, mit Einschränkungen wie Abmessungen von 128x128 für Emoticon-GIFs und 10-30 FPS für kleinere Dateigrößen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar GIFs animados otimizados usando Python e a biblioteca PIL, com restrições como dimensões de 128x128 para GIFs de emoji e 10-30 FPS para tamanhos de arquivo menores.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать оптимизированные анимированные GIF, используя Python и библиотеку PIL, с ограничениями, такими как размеры 128x128 для эмодзи-GIF и 10-30 FPS для меньших размеров файлов.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء إنشاء صور GIF المتحركة معززة باستخدام Python ومكتبة PIL، مع قيود مثل أبعاد 128x128 لصور GIF الإيموجي و 10-30 إطارًا في الثانية لاحجام الملفات الأصغر."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating animated GIFs for Slack with custom dimensions and FPS","Creating emoji GIFs with specific color palettes and durations","Validating GIF parameters for optimal Slack compatibility"],"zh":["为Slack生成具有自定义尺寸和FPS的动画GIF","创建具有特定色彩调色板和时长的emoji GIF","验证GIF参数以实现Slack的最佳兼容性"],"ja":["Slack用にカスタムサイズとFPSのアニメーションGIFを生成する","特定の色彩パレットと時間のemoji GIFを作成する","GIFパラメータを検証してSlackの最適な互換性を実現する"],"ko":["Slack 용으로 사용자 지정 크기와 FPS의 애니메이션 GIF를 생성하는 것","특정 색상 팔레트 및 지속 시간의 이모티콘 GIF를 생성하는 것","GIF 매개 변수를 검증하여 Slack의 최적 호환성을 달성하는 것"],"es":["Generar GIF animados para Slack con dimensiones y FPS personalizadas","Crear GIF de emojis con paletas de colores y duraciones específicas","Validar parámetros de GIF para la compatibilidad óptima con Slack"],"fr":["Générer des GIF animés pour Slack avec des dimensions et des FPS personnalisés","Créer des GIF d''émoticônes avec des palettes de couleurs et des durées spécifiques","Valider les paramètres de GIF pour une compatibilité optimale avec Slack"],"de":["Erstellen von animierten GIFs für Slack mit benutzerdefinierten Abmessungen und FPS","Erstellen von Emoticon-GIFs mit spezifischen Farbpaletten und Dauern","Überprüfen von GIF-Parametern für die beste Slack-Kompatibilität"],"pt":["Gerar GIFs animados para o Slack com dimensões personalizadas e FPS","Criar GIFs de emoji com paletas de cores e durações específicas","Validar parâmetros de GIF para compatibilidade ótima com o Slack"],"ru":["Генерировать анимированные GIF для Slack с настраиваемыми размерами и FPS","Создавать эмодзи-GIF с определенными цветовыми палитрами и продолжительностью","Проверять параметры GIF для оптимальной совместимости со Slack"],"ar":["إنشاء صور GIF المتحركة لبرنامج Slack بأبعاد ومعدلات إطار مخصصة","إنشاء صور GIF الإيموجي بألوان ومدد محددة","التحقق من معايير صور GIF لتحقيق التوافق الأمثل مع برنامج Slack"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python and PIL library","GIF duration limited to under 3 seconds for emoji GIFs","Specific dimension requirements for emoji and message GIFs"],"zh":["需要Python和PIL库","emoji GIF的时长限制在3秒以内","特定的尺寸要求，用于emoji和消息GIF"],"ja":["PythonとPILライブラリが必要","emoji GIFの時間制限は3秒以内","emojiとメッセージGIF用の特定のサイズの要件"],"ko":["Python과 PIL 라이브러리가 필요","이모티콘 GIF의 지속 시간이 3초 이하로 제한됨","이모티콘 및 메시지 GIF에 대한 특정 크기 요구 사항"],"es":["Requiere Python y la biblioteca PIL","La duración del GIF está limitada a menos de 3 segundos para los GIF de emojis","Requisitos de dimensiones específicos para los GIF de emojis y mensajes"],"fr":["Nécessite Python et la bibliothèque PIL","La durée du GIF est limitée à moins de 3 secondes pour les GIF d''émoticônes","Exigences de dimensions spécifiques pour les GIF d''émoticônes et les messages"],"de":["Benötigt Python und die PIL-Bibliothek","Die Dauer des GIFs ist auf unter 3 Sekunden für Emoticon-GIFs begrenzt","Spezifische Abmessungsanforderungen für Emoticon- und Nachrichten-GIFs"],"pt":["Requer Python e biblioteca PIL","Duração do GIF limitada a menos de 3 segundos para GIFs de emoji","Requisitos de dimensão específicos para GIFs de emoji e mensagem"],"ru":["Требуется Python и библиотека PIL","Продолжительность GIF ограничена менее 3 секундами для эмодзи-GIF","Конкретные требования к размерам для эмодзи- и сообщений-GIF"],"ar":["يتطلب Python ومكتبة PIL","مدة صورة GIF مقيدة بأقل من 3 ثوانٍ لصور GIF الإيموجي","متطلبات أبعاد محددة لصور GIF الإيموجي والرسائل"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"2efca615ce55a3edd8fc05c779068a8085816617991987e446606403cd3abb22","repoEtag":"W/\"5456759f24524b9171780a611a3970c1ae87a3d09576f2945661ad98ce4c37da\"","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/web-artifacts-builder', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'web-artifacts-builder', 71981, 7353, 65, '2026-02-20T01:43:22Z', '2026-02-20T01:59:18.344Z', '81c5002c6643b0de7b8710b00e7a9038daa6fb9b68d59870ee6adb12da8d10f8', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/web-artifacts-builder","name":"web-artifacts-builder","description":{"zh":"Web Artifacts Builder 是一个用于创建复杂 claude.ai HTML 文档的套件，使用 React、Tailwind CSS 和 shadcn/ui","ja":"Web Artifacts Builder は、React、Tailwind CSS、shadcn/ui を使用して複雑な claude.ai HTML アーティファクトを生成するツールのスイートです","ko":"Web Artifacts Builder는 React, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui를 사용하여 복잡한 claude.ai HTML 아티팩트를 생성하는 도구 세트입니다","es":"La herramienta web-artifacts-builder es una suite de herramientas para crear artefactos web complejos con tecnologías frontend modernas","fr":"L''outil web-artifacts-builder est une suite d''outils pour créer des artefacts web complexes avec des technologies frontend modernes","de":"Das Tool web-artifacts-builder ist eine Suite von Tools zur Erstellung komplexer Web-Artefakte mit modernen Frontend-Technologien","pt":"O web-artifacts-builder é uma suite de ferramentas para criar artefatos web complexos com React, Tailwind CSS e shadcn/ui.","ru":"Web-artifacts-builder - это набор инструментов для создания сложных веб-артефактов с помощью React, Tailwind CSS и shadcn/ui.","ar":"web-artifacts-builder هو مجموعة من الأدوات لإنشاء منقحات ويب معقدة باستخدام React و Tailwind CSS و shadcn/ui.","en":"Suite of tools for creating elaborate, multi-component claude.ai HTML artifacts using modern frontend web technologies (React, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui). Use for complex artifacts requiring state management, routing, or shadcn/ui components - not for simple single-file HTML/JSX artifacts."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":71981,"forks":7353,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:43:22Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"web-artifacts-builder","description":"Suite of tools for creating elaborate, multi-component claude.ai HTML artifacts using modern frontend web technologies (React, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui). Use for complex artifacts requiring state management, routing, or shadcn/ui components - not for simple single-file HTML/JSX artifacts.","bodyPreview":"# Web Artifacts Builder\n\nTo build powerful frontend claude.ai artifacts, follow these steps:\n1. Initialize the frontend repo using `scripts/init-artifact.sh`\n2. Develop your artifact by editing the generated code\n3. Bundle all code into a single HTML file using `scripts/bundle-artifact.sh`\n4. Display artifact to user\n5. (Optional) Test the artifact\n\n**Stack**: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Parcel (bundling) + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui\n\n## Design & Style Guidelines\n\nVERY IMPORTANT: To avoid what","body":"# Web Artifacts Builder\n\nTo build powerful frontend claude.ai artifacts, follow these steps:\n1. Initialize the frontend repo using `scripts/init-artifact.sh`\n2. Develop your artifact by editing the generated code\n3. Bundle all code into a single HTML file using `scripts/bundle-artifact.sh`\n4. Display artifact to user\n5. (Optional) Test the artifact\n\n**Stack**: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Parcel (bundling) + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui\n\n## Design & Style Guidelines\n\nVERY IMPORTANT: To avoid what is often referred to as \"AI slop\", avoid using excessive centered layouts, purple gradients, uniform rounded corners, and Inter font.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Step 1: Initialize Project\n\nRun the initialization script to create a new React project:\n```bash\nbash scripts/init-artifact.sh <project-name>\ncd <project-name>\n```\n\nThis creates a fully configured project with:\n- ✅ React + TypeScript (via Vite)\n- ✅ Tailwind CSS 3.4.1 with shadcn/ui theming system\n- ✅ Path aliases (`@/`) configured\n- ✅ 40+ shadcn/ui components pre-installed\n- ✅ All Radix UI dependencies included\n- ✅ Parcel configured for bundling (via .parcelrc)\n- ✅ Node 18+ compatibility (auto-detects and pins Vite version)\n\n### Step 2: Develop Your Artifact\n\nTo build the artifact, edit the generated files. See **Common Development Tasks** below for guidance.\n\n### Step 3: Bundle to Single HTML File\n\nTo bundle the React app into a single HTML artifact:\n```bash\nbash scripts/bundle-artifact.sh\n```\n\nThis creates `bundle.html` - a self-contained artifact with all JavaScript, CSS, and dependencies inlined. This file can be directly shared in Claude conversations as an artifact.\n\n**Requirements**: Your project must have an `index.html` in the root directory.\n\n**What the script does**:\n- Installs bundling dependencies (parcel, @parcel/config-default, parcel-resolver-tspaths, html-inline)\n- Creates `.parcelrc` config with path alias support\n- Builds with Parcel (no source maps)\n- Inlines all assets into single HTML using html-inline\n\n### Step 4: Share Artifact with User\n\nFinally, share the bundled HTML file in conversation with the user so they can view it as an artifact.\n\n### Step 5: Testing/Visualizing the Artifact (Optional)\n\nNote: This is a completely optional step. Only perform if necessary or requested.\n\nTo test/visualize the artifact, use available tools (including other Skills or built-in tools like Playwright or Puppeteer). In general, avoid testing the artifact upfront as it adds latency between the request and when the finished artifact can be seen. Test later, after presenting the artifact, if requested or if issues arise.\n\n## Reference\n\n- **shadcn/ui components**: https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T01:59:18.344Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"Web Artifacts Builder - 前端开发套件","ja":"Web Artifacts Builder - フロントエンド開発ツール","ko":"Web Artifacts Builder - 프론트엔드 개발 도구","es":"Constructor de artefactos web para Claude.ai","fr":"Constructeur d''artefacts web pour Claude.ai","de":"Web-Artefakt-Builder für Claude.ai","pt":"Construtor de Artefatos Web","ru":"Создатель Веб-Артефактов","ar":"بناء منقح للتحف الويب","en":"web-artifacts-builder"},"description":{"zh":"Web Artifacts Builder 是一个用于创建复杂 claude.ai HTML 文档的套件，使用 React、Tailwind CSS 和 shadcn/ui","ja":"Web Artifacts Builder は、React、Tailwind CSS、shadcn/ui を使用して複雑な claude.ai HTML アーティファクトを生成するツールのスイートです","ko":"Web Artifacts Builder는 React, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui를 사용하여 복잡한 claude.ai HTML 아티팩트를 생성하는 도구 세트입니다","es":"La herramienta web-artifacts-builder es una suite de herramientas para crear artefactos web complejos con tecnologías frontend modernas","fr":"L''outil web-artifacts-builder est une suite d''outils pour créer des artefacts web complexes avec des technologies frontend modernes","de":"Das Tool web-artifacts-builder ist eine Suite von Tools zur Erstellung komplexer Web-Artefakte mit modernen Frontend-Technologien","pt":"O web-artifacts-builder é uma suite de ferramentas para criar artefatos web complexos com React, Tailwind CSS e shadcn/ui.","ru":"Web-artifacts-builder - это набор инструментов для создания сложных веб-артефактов с помощью React, Tailwind CSS и shadcn/ui.","ar":"web-artifacts-builder هو مجموعة من الأدوات لإنشاء منقحات ويب معقدة باستخدام React و Tailwind CSS و shadcn/ui.","en":"Suite of tools for creating elaborate, multi-component claude.ai HTML artifacts using modern frontend web technologies (React, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui). Use ..."},"definition":{"en":"Suite of tools for creating elaborate, multi-component claude.ai HTML artifacts using modern frontend web technologies (React, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui). Use for complex artifacts requiring state management, routing, or shadcn/ui components - not for simple single-file HTML/JSX artifacts."},"features":{"zh":["使用 React 18 和 TypeScript","支持 Tailwind CSS 和 shadcn/ui","使用 Vite 和 Parcel 进行打包","支持状态管理和路由","可用于构建复杂的 claude.ai HTML 文档"],"ja":["React 18 と TypeScript を使用","Tailwind CSS と shadcn/ui をサポート","Vite と Parcel を使用してバンドル","状態管理とルーティングをサポート","複雑な claude.ai HTML アーティファクトの構築に使用"],"ko":["React 18과 TypeScript 사용","Tailwind CSS와 shadcn/ui 지원","Vite와 Parcel을 사용한 번들링","상태 관리와 라우팅 지원","복잡한 claude.ai HTML 아티팩트 구축에 사용"],"es":["Utiliza tecnologías frontend modernas como React y Tailwind CSS","Permite la creación de artefactos web complejos con estado y enrutamiento","Incluye una suite de herramientas para inicializar y empaquetar artefactos","Soporta la biblioteca shadcn/ui para componentes de interfaz de usuario","Utiliza Vite y Parcel para empaquetar y optimizar el código"],"fr":["Utilise des technologies frontend modernes comme React et Tailwind CSS","Permet la création d''artefacts web complexes avec état et routage","Inclut une suite d''outils pour initialiser et empaqueter les artefacts","Prend en charge la bibliothèque shadcn/ui pour les composants d''interface utilisateur","Utilise Vite et Parcel pour empaqueter et optimiser le code"],"de":["Verwendet moderne Frontend-Technologien wie React und Tailwind CSS","Ermöglicht die Erstellung komplexer Web-Artefakte mit Zustand und Routing","Enthält eine Suite von Tools zur Initialisierung und Paketierung von Artefakten","Unterstützt die Bibliothek shadcn/ui für Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten","Verwendet Vite und Parcel zum Paketieren und Optimieren des Codes"],"pt":["Criação de artefatos web complexos","Uso de React, Tailwind CSS e shadcn/ui","Gerenciamento de estado e roteamento","Componentes shadcn/ui","Bundling com Parcel"],"ru":["Создание сложных веб-артефактов","Использование React, Tailwind CSS и shadcn/ui","Управление состоянием и маршрутизация","Компоненты shadcn/ui","Бандлинг с Parcel"],"ar":["إنشاء منقحات ويب معقدة","استخدام React و Tailwind CSS و shadcn/ui","إدارة الحالة والتحويل","مكونات shadcn/ui","باندلنغ مع Parcel"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Web Artifacts Builder","前端开发","React","Tailwind CSS","shadcn/ui","claude.ai","HTML 文档","复杂文档"],"ja":["Web Artifacts Builder","フロントエンド開発","React","Tailwind CSS","shadcn/ui","claude.ai","HTML アーティファクト","複雑なアーティファクト"],"ko":["Web Artifacts Builder","프론트엔드 개발","React","Tailwind CSS","shadcn/ui","claude.ai","HTML 아티팩트","복잡한 아티팩트"],"es":["constructor de artefactos web","claude.ai","react","tailwind css","shadcn/ui","vite","parcel","desarrollo web","frontend"],"fr":["constructeur d''artefacts web","claude.ai","react","tailwind css","shadcn/ui","vite","parcel","développement web","frontend"],"de":["web-artefakt-builder","claude.ai","react","tailwind css","shadcn/ui","vite","parcel","web-entwicklung","frontend"],"pt":["web-artifacts-builder","React","Tailwind CSS","shadcn/ui","frontend","desenvolvimento web","artefatos web","componentes frontend"],"ru":["web-artifacts-builder","React","Tailwind CSS","shadcn/ui","frontend","веб-разработка","веб-артефакты","компоненты frontend"],"ar":["web-artifacts-builder","React","Tailwind CSS","shadcn/ui","frontend","تطوير ويب","منقحات ويب","مكونات frontend"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced Frontend Agents needing complex HTML artifact creation with React, Tailwind CSS, and shadcn/ui.","zh":"非常适合需要使用 React、Tailwind CSS 和 shadcn/ui 创建复杂 HTML 文档的高级前端代理。","ja":"React、Tailwind CSS、shadcn/ui を使用して複雑な HTML アーティファクトを作成する必要がある高度なフロントエンド エージェントに最適です。","ko":"React, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui를 사용하여 복잡한 HTML 아티팩트를 생성해야 하는 고급 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de frontend avanzados que necesitan crear artefactos HTML complejos con React, Tailwind CSS y shadcn/ui.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de frontend avancés ayant besoin de créer des artefacts HTML complexes avec React, Tailwind CSS et shadcn/ui.","de":"Perfekt für erweiterte Frontend-Agenten, die komplexe HTML-Artefakte mit React, Tailwind CSS und shadcn/ui erstellen müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend Avançados que necessitam de criação de artefatos HTML complexos com React, Tailwind CSS e shadcn/ui.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов frontend, которым требуется создание сложных артефактов HTML с помощью React, Tailwind CSS и shadcn/ui.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم المتقدم الذين يحتاجون إلى إنشاء مكونات HTML معقدة باستخدام React و Tailwind CSS و shadcn/ui."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build elaborate, multi-component claude.ai HTML artifacts using modern frontend web technologies like React 18, TypeScript, Vite, and Parcel for bundling, along with Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui for styling and component management.","zh":"赋予代理构建使用现代前端 Web 技术（如 React 18、TypeScript、Vite 和 Parcel 进行捆绑）的复杂、多组件 claude.ai HTML 文档的能力，包括使用 Tailwind CSS 和 shadcn/ui 进行样式和组件管理。","ja":"React 18、TypeScript、Vite、Parcel を使用したバンドル、および Tailwind CSS と shadcn/ui を使用したスタイリングとコンポーネント管理などの最新のフロントエンド Web 技術を使用して複雑な多コンポーネントの claude.ai HTML アーティファクトを構築するエージェントをエンパワーします。","ko":"React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Parcel을 사용한 번들링과 Tailwind CSS 및 shadcn/ui를 사용한 스타일링 및 컴포넌트 관리와 같은 최신 프론트엔드 웹 기술을 사용하여 복잡한 다중 컴포넌트 claude.ai HTML 아티팩트를 구축할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear artefactos HTML elaborados y multicomponentes de claude.ai utilizando tecnologías web de frontend modernas como React 18, TypeScript, Vite y Parcel para la agrupación, junto con Tailwind CSS y shadcn/ui para el estilo y la gestión de componentes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des artefacts HTML élaborés et multicomposants de claude.ai en utilisant des technologies Web de frontend modernes comme React 18, TypeScript, Vite et Parcel pour le regroupement, ainsi que Tailwind CSS et shadcn/ui pour le style et la gestion des composants.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, umfassende, mehrkomponentige claude.ai-HTML-Artefakte mit modernen Frontend-Webtechnologien wie React 18, TypeScript, Vite und Parcel für die Bündelung sowie Tailwind CSS und shadcn/ui für das Styling und die Komponentenverwaltung zu erstellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar artefatos HTML elaborados e multi-componentes da claude.ai usando tecnologias web frontend modernas como React 18, TypeScript, Vite e Parcel para empacotamento, juntamente com Tailwind CSS e shadcn/ui para estilização e gerenciamento de componentes.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать сложные, многокомпонентные артефакты HTML claude.ai с использованием современных технологий frontend веб-разработки, таких как React 18, TypeScript, Vite и Parcel для сборки, а также Tailwind CSS и shadcn/ui для стилизации и управления компонентами.","ar":"يسمح للعميل بإنشاء مكونات HTML متقدمة ومتعددة المكونات من claude.ai باستخدام تقنيات الويب الحديثة مثل React 18 و TypeScript و Vite و Parcel لتحزيم المكونات، جنبًا إلى جنب مع Tailwind CSS و shadcn/ui لتصميم واجهة المستخدم وإدارة المكونات."},"useCases":{"en":["Building complex claude.ai artifacts with state management and routing","Creating custom UI components using shadcn/ui","Developing multi-page HTML applications with React and Tailwind CSS"],"zh":["构建具有状态管理和路由的复杂 claude.ai 文档","使用 shadcn/ui 创建自定义 UI 组件","使用 React 和 Tailwind CSS 开发多页 HTML 应用程序"],"ja":["状態管理とルーティングを備えた複雑な claude.ai アーティファクトを構築する","shadcn/ui を使用してカスタム UI コンポーネントを作成する","React と Tailwind CSS を使用して多ページ HTML アプリケーションを開発する"],"ko":["상태 관리 및 라우팅을 갖춘 복잡한 claude.ai 아티팩트를 구축하는 것","shadcn/ui를 사용하여 사용자 지정 UI 컴포넌트를 생성하는 것","React 및 Tailwind CSS를 사용하여 다중 페이지 HTML 애플리케이션을 개발하는 것"],"es":["Creación de artefactos complejos de claude.ai con gestión de estado y enrutamiento","Creación de componentes de interfaz de usuario personalizados con shadcn/ui","Desarrollo de aplicaciones HTML de varias páginas con React y Tailwind CSS"],"fr":["Création d''artefacts complexes de claude.ai avec gestion d''état et routage","Création de composants d''interface utilisateur personnalisés avec shadcn/ui","Développement d''applications HTML à plusieurs pages avec React et Tailwind CSS"],"de":["Erstellung komplexer claude.ai-Artefakte mit Zustandsverwaltung und Routing","Erstellung benutzerdefinierter Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten mit shadcn/ui","Entwicklung mehrseitiger HTML-Anwendungen mit React und Tailwind CSS"],"pt":["Construção de artefatos claude.ai complexos com gerenciamento de estado e roteamento","Criação de componentes de UI personalizados usando shadcn/ui","Desenvolvimento de aplicações HTML multi-página com React e Tailwind CSS"],"ru":["Создание сложных артефактов claude.ai с управлением состоянием и маршрутизацией","Создание пользовательских компонентов UI с помощью shadcn/ui","Разработка многостраничных HTML-приложений с помощью React и Tailwind CSS"],"ar":["بناء مكونات claude.ai معقدة مع إدارة الحالة والتوجيه","إنشاء مكونات واجهة المستخدم المخصصة باستخدام shadcn/ui","تطوير تطبيقات HTML متعددة الصفحات باستخدام React و Tailwind CSS"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires initialization with scripts/init-artifact.sh","Intended for complex artifacts, not simple single-file HTML/JSX projects"],"zh":["需要使用 scripts/init-artifact.sh 初始化","仅适用于复杂的文档，不适用于简单的单文件 HTML/JSX 项目"],"ja":["scripts/init-artifact.sh を使用して初期化する必要がある","複雑なアーティファクト専用で、シンプルな単一ファイルの HTML/JSX プロジェクトには不適"],"ko":["scripts/init-artifact.sh를 사용하여 초기화해야 함","복잡한 아티팩트 전용으로, 단순한 단일 파일 HTML/JSX 프로젝트에는 적합하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere inicialización con scripts/init-artifact.sh","Está destinado a artefactos complejos, no a proyectos HTML/JSX simples de un solo archivo"],"fr":["Nécessite une initialisation avec scripts/init-artifact.sh","Est destiné à des artefacts complexes, et non à des projets HTML/JSX simples d''un seul fichier"],"de":["Erfordert Initialisierung mit scripts/init-artifact.sh","Ist für komplexe Artefakte bestimmt, nicht für einfache HTML/JSX-Projekte mit einer einzigen Datei"],"pt":["Requer inicialização com scripts/init-artifact.sh","Destina-se a artefatos complexos, não a projetos HTML/JSX simples de arquivo único"],"ru":["Требует инициализации с помощью scripts/init-artifact.sh","Предназначен для сложных артефактов, а не для простых проектов HTML/JSX с одним файлом"],"ar":["يتطلب 초기ته باستخدام scripts/init-artifact.sh","مخصص لمكونات معقدة، وليس لمشاريع HTML/JSX البسيطة ذات الملف الواحد"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"81c5002c6643b0de7b8710b00e7a9038daa6fb9b68d59870ee6adb12da8d10f8","repoEtag":"W/\"5456759f24524b9171780a611a3970c1ae87a3d09576f2945661ad98ce4c37da\"","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/doc-coauthoring', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'doc-coauthoring', 71980, 7353, 60, '2026-02-20T01:38:00Z', '2026-02-20T01:47:07.046Z', '2e47d78846faeea4a56e9809c52700087a15a2155a3f293a3efbaded81398ef4', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/doc-coauthoring","name":"doc-coauthoring","description":{"zh":"文档协同创作工作流是一个结构化的指导过程，帮助用户高效地完成文档创作","ja":"ドキュメント共同執筆ワークフローは、構造化されたガイドプロセスを提供して、ユーザーがドキュメントの作成を効率的に行えるようにします","ko":"문서 공저 워크플로우는 구조화된 가이드 프로세스를 제공하여 사용자가 문서 작성을 효율적으로 수행할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"Nuestro flujo de trabajo de coautoría guía a los usuarios a través de la creación de documentación estructurada. Ayuda a transferir contexto, refinar contenido y verificar la eficacia de los documentos","fr":"Notre workflow de co-rédaction guide les utilisateurs à travers la création de documents structurés. Il aide à transférer le contexte, à affiner le contenu et à vérifier l''efficacité des documents","de":"Unser Co-Authoring-Workflow führt Benutzer durch die Erstellung strukturierter Dokumente. Er hilft dabei, Kontext zu übertragen, Inhalt zu verfeinern und die Dokumente zu überprüfen","pt":"O fluxo de trabalho de colaboração de documentação é um guia estruturado para criar documentação em equipe. Ele ajuda a transferir contexto, refinar conteúdo e testar a documentação","ru":"Рабочий поток совместного создания документации - это структурированный гид для создания документации в команде. Он помогает передать контекст, усовершенствовать содержание и протестировать документацию","ar":"تدفق عمل تعاون في توثيق المستندات هو دليل منظم لإنشاء توثيق الفريق. يساعد على نقل السياق وتنقيح المحتوى واختبار التوثيق","en":"Guide users through a structured workflow for co-authoring documentation. Use when user wants to write documentation, proposals, technical specs, decision docs, or similar structured content. This workflow helps users efficiently transfer context, refine content through iteration, and verify the ..."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":71980,"forks":7353,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:38:00Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"doc-coauthoring","description":"Guide users through a structured workflow for co-authoring documentation. Use when user wants to write documentation, proposals, technical specs, decision docs, or similar structured content. This workflow helps users efficiently transfer context, refine content through iteration, and verify the doc works for readers. Trigger when user mentions writing docs, creating proposals, drafting specs, or similar documentation tasks.","bodyPreview":"# Doc Co-Authoring Workflow\n\nThis skill provides a structured workflow for guiding users through collaborative document creation. Act as an active guide, walking users through three stages: Context Gathering, Refinement & Structure, and Reader Testing.\n\n## When to Offer This Workflow\n\n**Trigger conditions:**\n- User mentions writing documentation: \"write a doc\", \"draft a proposal\", \"create a spec\", \"write up\"\n- User mentions specific doc types: \"PRD\", \"design doc\", \"decision doc\", \"RFC\"\n- User se","body":"# Doc Co-Authoring Workflow\n\nThis skill provides a structured workflow for guiding users through collaborative document creation. Act as an active guide, walking users through three stages: Context Gathering, Refinement & Structure, and Reader Testing.\n\n## When to Offer This Workflow\n\n**Trigger conditions:**\n- User mentions writing documentation: \"write a doc\", \"draft a proposal\", \"create a spec\", \"write up\"\n- User mentions specific doc types: \"PRD\", \"design doc\", \"decision doc\", \"RFC\"\n- User seems to be starting a substantial writing task\n\n**Initial offer:**\nOffer the user a structured workflow for co-authoring the document. Explain the three stages:\n\n1. **Context Gathering**: User provides all relevant context while Claude asks clarifying questions\n2. **Refinement & Structure**: Iteratively build each section through brainstorming and editing\n3. **Reader Testing**: Test the doc with a fresh Claude (no context) to catch blind spots before others read it\n\nExplain that this approach helps ensure the doc works well when others read it (including when they paste it into Claude). Ask if they want to try this workflow or prefer to work freeform.\n\nIf user declines, work freeform. If user accepts, proceed to Stage 1.\n\n## Stage 1: Context Gathering\n\n**Goal:** Close the gap between what the user knows and what Claude knows, enabling smart guidance later.\n\n### Initial Questions\n\nStart by asking the user for meta-context about the document:\n\n1. What type of document is this? (e.g., technical spec, decision doc, proposal)\n2. Who''s the primary audience?\n3. What''s the desired impact when someone reads this?\n4. Is there a template or specific format to follow?\n5. Any other constraints or context to know?\n\nInform them they can answer in shorthand or dump information however works best for them.\n\n**If user provides a template or mentions a doc type:**\n- Ask if they have a template document to share\n- If they provide a link to a shared document, use the appropriate integration to fetch it\n- If they provide a file, read it\n\n**If user mentions editing an existing shared document:**\n- Use the appropriate integration to read the current state\n- Check for images without alt-text\n- If images exist without alt-text, explain that when others use Claude to understand the doc, Claude won''t be able to see them. Ask if they want alt-text generated. If so, request they paste each image into chat for descriptive alt-text generation.\n\n### Info Dumping\n\nOnce initial questions are answered, encourage the user to dump all the context they have. Request information such as:\n- Background on the project/problem\n- Related team discussions or shared documents\n- Why alternative solutions aren''t being used\n- Organizational context (team dynamics, past incidents, politics)\n- Timeline pressures or constraints\n- Technical architecture or dependencies\n- Stakeholder concerns\n\nAdvise them not to worry about organizing it - just get it all out. Offer multiple ways to provide context:\n- Info dump stream-of-consciousness\n- Point to team channels or threads to read\n- Link to shared documents\n\n**If integrations are available** (e.g., Slack, Teams, Google Drive, SharePoint, or other MCP servers), mention that these can be used to pull in context directly.\n\n**If no integrations are detected and in Claude.ai or Claude app:** Suggest they can enable connectors in their Claude settings to allow pulling context from messaging apps and document storage directly.\n\nInform them clarifying questions will be asked once they''ve done their initial dump.\n\n**During context gathering:**\n\n- If user mentions team channels or shared documents:\n  - If integrations available: Inform them the content will be read now, then use the appropriate integration\n  - If integrations not available: Explain lack of access. Suggest they enable connectors in Claude settings, or paste the relevant content directly.\n\n- If user mentions entities/projects that are unknown:\n  - Ask if connected tools should be searched to learn more\n  - Wait for user confirmation before searching\n\n- As user provides context, track what''s being learned and what''s still unclear\n\n**Asking clarifying questions:**\n\nWhen user signals they''ve done their initial dump (or after substantial context provided), ask clarifying questions to ensure understanding:\n\nGenerate 5-10 numbered questions based on gaps in the context.\n\nInform them they can use shorthand to answer (e.g., \"1: yes, 2: see #channel, 3: no because backwards compat\"), link to more docs, point to channels to read, or just keep info-dumping. Whatever''s most efficient for them.\n\n**Exit condition:**\nSufficient context has been gathered when questions show understanding - when edge cases and trade-offs can be asked about without needing basics explained.\n\n**Transition:**\nAsk if there''s any more context they want to provide at this stage, or if it''s time to move on to drafting the document.\n\nIf user wants to add more, let them. When ready, proceed to Stage 2.\n\n## Stage 2: Refinement & Structure\n\n**Goal:** Build the document section by section through brainstorming, curation, and iterative refinement.\n\n**Instructions to user:**\nExplain that the document will be built section by section. For each section:\n1. Clarifying questions will be asked about what to include\n2. 5-20 options will be brainstormed\n3. User will indicate what to keep/remove/combine\n4. The section will be drafted\n5. It will be refined through surgical edits\n\nStart with whichever section has the most unknowns (usually the core decision/proposal), then work through the rest.\n\n**Section ordering:**\n\nIf the document structure is clear:\nAsk which section they''d like to start with.\n\nSuggest starting with whichever section has the most unknowns. For decision docs, that''s usually the core proposal. For specs, it''s typically the technical approach. Summary sections are best left for last.\n\nIf user doesn''t know what sections they need:\nBased on the type of document and template, suggest 3-5 sections appropriate for the doc type.\n\nAsk if this structure works, or if they want to adjust it.\n\n**Once structure is agreed:**\n\nCreate the initial document structure with placeholder text for all sections.\n\n**If access to artifacts is available:**\nUse `create_file` to create an artifact. This gives both Claude and the user a scaffold to work from.\n\nInform them that the initial structure with placeholders for all sections will be created.\n\nCreate artifact with all section headers and brief placeholder text like \"[To be written]\" or \"[Content here]\".\n\nProvide the scaffold link and indicate it''s time to fill in each section.\n\n**If no access to artifacts:**\nCreate a markdown file in the working directory. Name it appropriately (e.g., `decision-doc.md`, `technical-spec.md`).\n\nInform them that the initial structure with placeholders for all sections will be created.\n\nCreate file with all section headers and placeholder text.\n\nConfirm the filename has been created and indicate it''s time to fill in each section.\n\n**For each section:**\n\n### Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAnnounce work will begin on the [SECTION NAME] section. Ask 5-10 clarifying questions about what should be included:\n\nGenerate 5-10 specific questions based on context and section purpose.\n\nInform them they can answer in shorthand or just indicate what''s important to cover.\n\n### Step 2: Brainstorming\n\nFor the [SECTION NAME] section, brainstorm [5-20] things that might be included, depending on the section''s complexity. Look for:\n- Context shared that might have been forgotten\n- Angles or considerations not yet mentioned\n\nGenerate 5-20 numbered options based on section complexity. At the end, offer to brainstorm more if they want additional options.\n\n### Step 3: Curation\n\nAsk which points should be kept, removed, or combined. Request brief justifications to help learn priorities for the next sections.\n\nProvide examples:\n- \"Keep 1,4,7,9\"\n- \"Remove 3 (duplicates 1)\"\n- \"Remove 6 (audience already knows this)\"\n- \"Combine 11 and 12\"\n\n**If user gives freeform feedback** (e.g., \"looks good\" or \"I like most of it but...\") instead of numbered selections, extract their preferences and proceed. Parse what they want kept/removed/changed and apply it.\n\n### Step 4: Gap Check\n\nBased on what they''ve selected, ask if there''s anything important missing for the [SECTION NAME] section.\n\n### Step 5: Drafting\n\nUse `str_replace` to replace the placeholder text for this section with the actual drafted content.\n\nAnnounce the [SECTION NAME] section will be drafted now based on what they''ve selected.\n\n**If using artifacts:**\nAfter drafting, provide a link to the artifact.\n\nAsk them to read through it and indicate what to change. Note that being specific helps learning for the next sections.\n\n**If using a file (no artifacts):**\nAfter drafting, confirm completion.\n\nInform them the [SECTION NAME] section has been drafted in [filename]. Ask them to read through it and indicate what to change. Note that being specific helps learning for the next sections.\n\n**Key instruction for user (include when drafting the first section):**\nProvide a note: Instead of editing the doc directly, ask them to indicate what to change. This helps learning of their style for future sections. For example: \"Remove the X bullet - already covered by Y\" or \"Make the third paragraph more concise\".\n\n### Step 6: Iterative Refinement\n\nAs user provides feedback:\n- Use `str_replace` to make edits (never reprint the whole doc)\n- **If using artifacts:** Provide link to artifact after each edit\n- **If using files:** Just confirm edits are complete\n- If user edits doc directly and asks to read it: mentally note the changes they made and keep them in mind for future sections (this shows their preferences)\n\n**Continue iterating** until user is satisfied with the section.\n\n### Quality Checking\n\nAfter 3 consecutive iterations with no substantial changes, ask if anything can be removed without losing important information.\n\nWhen section is done, confirm [SECTION NAME] is complete. Ask if ready to move to the next section.\n\n**Repeat for all sections.**\n\n### Near Completion\n\nAs approaching completion (80%+ of sections done), announce intention to re-read the entire document and check for:\n- Flow and consistency across sections\n- Redundancy or contradictions\n- Anything that feels like \"slop\" or generic filler\n- Whether every sentence carries weight\n\nRead entire document and provide feedback.\n\n**When all sections are drafted and refined:**\nAnnounce all sections are drafted. Indicate intention to review the complete document one more time.\n\nReview for overall coherence, flow, completeness.\n\nProvide any final suggestions.\n\nAsk if ready to move to Reader Testing, or if they want to refine anything else.\n\n## Stage 3: Reader Testing\n\n**Goal:** Test the document with a fresh Claude (no context bleed) to verify it works for readers.\n\n**Instructions to user:**\nExplain that testing will now occur to see if the document actually works for readers. This catches blind spots - things that make sense to the authors but might confuse others.\n\n### Testing Approach\n\n**If access to sub-agents is available (e.g., in Claude Code):**\n\nPerform the testing directly without user involvement.\n\n### Step 1: Predict Reader Questions\n\nAnnounce intention to predict what questions readers might ask when trying to discover this document.\n\nGenerate 5-10 questions that readers would realistically ask.\n\n### Step 2: Test with Sub-Agent\n\nAnnounce that these questions will be tested with a fresh Claude instance (no context from this conversation).\n\nFor each question, invoke a sub-agent with just the document content and the question.\n\nSummarize what Reader Claude got right/wrong for each question.\n\n### Step 3: Run Additional Checks\n\nAnnounce additional checks will be performed.\n\nInvoke sub-agent to check for ambiguity, false assumptions, contradictions.\n\nSummarize any issues found.\n\n### Step 4: Report and Fix\n\nIf issues found:\nReport that Reader Claude struggled with specific issues.\n\nList the specific issues.\n\nIndicate intention to fix these gaps.\n\nLoop back to refinement for problematic sections.\n\n---\n\n**If no access to sub-agents (e.g., claude.ai web interface):**\n\nThe user will need to do the testing manually.\n\n### Step 1: Predict Reader Questions\n\nAsk what questions people might ask when trying to discover this document. What would they type into Claude.ai?\n\nGenerate 5-10 questions that readers would realistically ask.\n\n### Step 2: Setup Testing\n\nProvide testing instructions:\n1. Open a fresh Claude conversation: https://claude.ai\n2. Paste or share the document content (if using a shared doc platform with connectors enabled, provide the link)\n3. Ask Reader Claude the generated questions\n\nFor each question, instruct Reader Claude to provide:\n- The answer\n- Whether anything was ambiguous or unclear\n- What knowledge/context the doc assumes is already known\n\nCheck if Reader Claude gives correct answers or misinterprets anything.\n\n### Step 3: Additional Checks\n\nAlso ask Reader Claude:\n- \"What in this doc might be ambiguous or unclear to readers?\"\n- \"What knowledge or context does this doc assume readers already have?\"\n- \"Are there any internal contradictions or inconsistencies?\"\n\n### Step 4: Iterate Based on Results\n\nAsk what Reader Claude got wrong or struggled with. Indicate intention to fix those gaps.\n\nLoop back to refinement for any problematic sections.\n\n---\n\n### Exit Condition (Both Approaches)\n\nWhen Reader Claude consistently answers questions correctly and doesn''t surface new gaps or ambiguities, the doc is ready.\n\n## Final Review\n\nWhen Reader Testing passes:\nAnnounce the doc has passed Reader Claude testing. Before completion:\n\n1. Recommend they do a final read-through themselves - they own this document and are responsible for its quality\n2. Suggest double-checking any facts, links, or technical details\n3. Ask them to verify it achieves the impact they wanted\n\nAsk if they want one more review, or if the work is done.\n\n**If user wants final review, provide it. Otherwise:**\nAnnounce document completion. Provide a few final tips:\n- Consider linking this conversation in an appendix so readers can see how the doc was developed\n- Use appendices to provide depth without bloating the main doc\n- Update the doc as feedback is received from real readers\n\n## Tips for Effective Guidance\n\n**Tone:**\n- Be direct and procedural\n- Explain rationale briefly when it affects user behavior\n- Don''t try to \"sell\" the approach - just execute it\n\n**Handling Deviations:**\n- If user wants to skip a stage: Ask if they want to skip this and write freeform\n- If user seems frustrated: Acknowledge this is taking longer than expected. Suggest ways to move faster\n- Always give user agency to adjust the process\n\n**Context Management:**\n- Throughout, if context is missing on something mentioned, proactively ask\n- Don''t let gaps accumulate - address them as they come up\n\n**Artifact Management:**\n- Use `create_file` for drafting full sections\n- Use `str_replace` for all edits\n- Provide artifact link after every change\n- Never use artifacts for brainstorming lists - that''s just conversation\n\n**Quality over Speed:**\n- Don''t rush through stages\n- Each iteration should make meaningful improvements\n- The goal is a document that actually works for readers\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T01:47:07.046Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"文档协同创作工作流","ja":"ドキュメント共同執筆ワークフロー","ko":"문서 공저 워크플로우","es":"Colaboración en documentación: Flujo de trabajo de coautoría","fr":"Co-rédaction de documents : Workflow de collaboration","de":"Dokumenten-Co-Autoring: Strukturierter Arbeitsablauf","pt":"Colaboração de Documentação: Fluxo de Trabalho","ru":"Совместное Создание Документации: Рабочий Поток","ar":"تعاون في توثيق المستندات: تدفق العمل","en":"doc-coauthoring"},"description":{"zh":"文档协同创作工作流是一个结构化的指导过程，帮助用户高效地完成文档创作","ja":"ドキュメント共同執筆ワークフローは、構造化されたガイドプロセスを提供して、ユーザーがドキュメントの作成を効率的に行えるようにします","ko":"문서 공저 워크플로우는 구조화된 가이드 프로세스를 제공하여 사용자가 문서 작성을 효율적으로 수행할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"Nuestro flujo de trabajo de coautoría guía a los usuarios a través de la creación de documentación estructurada. Ayuda a transferir contexto, refinar conteni...","fr":"Notre workflow de co-rédaction guide les utilisateurs à travers la création de documents structurés. Il aide à transférer le contexte, à affiner le contenu e...","de":"Unser Co-Authoring-Workflow führt Benutzer durch die Erstellung strukturierter Dokumente. Er hilft dabei, Kontext zu übertragen, Inhalt zu verfeinern und die...","pt":"O fluxo de trabalho de colaboração de documentação é um guia estruturado para criar documentação em equipe. Ele ajuda a transferir contexto, refinar conteúdo...","ru":"Рабочий поток совместного создания документации - это структурированный гид для создания документации в команде. Он помогает передать контекст, усовершенство...","ar":"تدفق عمل تعاون في توثيق المستندات هو دليل منظم لإنشاء توثيق الفريق. يساعد على نقل السياق وتنقيح المحتوى واختبار التوثيق","en":"Guide users through a structured workflow for co-authoring documentation. Use when user wants to write documentation, proposals, technical specs, decision do..."},"definition":{"en":"Guide users through a structured workflow for co-authoring documentation. Use when user wants to write documentation, proposals, technical specs, decision docs, or similar structured content. This workflow helps users efficiently transfer context, refine content through iteration, and verify the doc works for readers. Trigger when user mentions writing docs, creating proposals, drafting specs, or similar documentation tasks."},"features":{"zh":["结构化工作流","高效文档创作","协同创作","文档类型支持","迭代式内容完善","读者测试"],"ja":["構造化されたワークフロー","効率的なドキュメント作成","共同執筆","ドキュメントタイプのサポート","反復的な内容の完善","リーダーテスト"],"ko":["구조화된 워크플로우","효율적인 문서 작성","공저","문서 유형 지원","반복적인 내용 완善","리더 테스트"],"es":["Guía a los usuarios a través de un flujo de trabajo estructurado","Ayuda a transferir contexto y refinar contenido","Permite la prueba de lectura para verificar la eficacia de los documentos","Se adapta a diferentes tipos de documentación","Mejora la colaboración y la eficiencia en la creación de documentación"],"fr":["Guide les utilisateurs à travers un workflow structuré","Aide à transférer le contexte et à affiner le contenu","Permet les tests de lecture pour vérifier l''efficacité des documents","S''adapte à différents types de documents","Améliore la collaboration et l''efficacité dans la création de documents"],"de":["Führt Benutzer durch einen strukturierten Arbeitsablauf","Hilft dabei, Kontext zu übertragen und Inhalt zu verfeinern","Ermöglicht Lesetests, um die Dokumente zu überprüfen","Passt sich an verschiedene Dokumententypen an","Verbessert die Zusammenarbeit und Effizienz bei der Dokumentenerstellung"],"pt":["Fluxo de trabalho estruturado","Transferência de contexto","Refinamento de conteúdo","Teste de documentação","Criação de documentação em equipe"],"ru":["Структурированный рабочий поток","Передача контекста","Усовершенствование содержания","Тестирование документации","Создание документации в команде"],"ar":["تدفق عمل منظم","نقل السياق","تنقيح المحتوى","اختبار التوثيق","إنشاء توثيق الفريق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["文档协同创作","结构化工作流","文档创作","协同工作","技术文档","提案文档","文档类型"],"ja":["ドキュメント共同執筆","構造化されたワークフロー","ドキュメント作成","共同作業","テクニカルドキュメント","提案ドキュメント","ドキュメントタイプ"],"ko":["문서 공저","구조화된 워크플로우","문서 작성","공조","기술 문서","제안 문서","문서 유형"],"es":["coautoría de documentación","flujo de trabajo de coautoría","creación de documentación","colaboración en documentación","documentación estructurada","transferencia de contexto","refinación de contenido","prueba de lectura"],"fr":["co-rédaction de documents","workflow de co-rédaction","création de documents","collaboration dans la documentation","documents structurés","transfert de contexte","affinement de contenu","tests de lecture"],"de":["Dokumenten-Co-Autoring","Co-Authoring-Workflow","Dokumentenerstellung","Zusammenarbeit in der Dokumentation","strukturierte Dokumente","Kontextsicherung","Inhaltsverfeinerung","Lesetests"],"pt":["colaboração de documentação","fluxo de trabalho","criação de documentação","equipe de desenvolvimento","documentação técnica","propostas","especificações técnicas"],"ru":["совместное создание документации","рабочий поток","создание документации","команда разработки","техническая документация","предложения","технические спецификации"],"ar":["تعاون في توثيق المستندات","تدفق عمل","إنشاء توثيق","فريق التطوير","توثيق تقني","مقترحات","مواصفات تقنية"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Language Agents needing structured document collaboration capabilities, such as guiding users through Context Gathering, Refinement & Structure, and Reader Testing stages.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化文档协作功能的语言代理，例如指导用户完成上下文收集、细化和结构以及读者测试阶段。","ja":"構造化ドキュメントの共同作業機能を必要とする言語エージェントに最適です。たとえば、コンテキストの収集、リファインメント＆構造、およびリーダーテストのステージでユーザーをサポートすることです。","ko":"구조화된 문서 협업 기능이 필요한 언어 에이전트에 적합합니다. 예를 들어, 사용자를 컨텍스트 수집, 정제 및 구조 및 리더 테스트 단계로 안내하는 것과 같습니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lenguaje que necesitan capacidades de colaboración de documentos estructurados, como guiar a los usuarios a través de las etapas de Recopilación de Contexto, Refinamiento y Estructura, y Pruebas de Lector.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Langage ayant besoin de capacités de collaboration de documents structurés, telles que guider les utilisateurs à travers les étapes de Collecte de Contexte, d''Affinement et de Structure, et de Tests de Lecteur.","de":"Perfekt für Sprachagenten, die strukturierte Dokumenten-Kollaborationsfunktionen benötigen, wie z.B. die Anleitung von Benutzern durch die Phasen Kontextsammeln, Verfeinerung und Struktur sowie Lesertests.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem que necessitam de capacidades de colaboração de documentos estruturados, como orientar os usuários pelas etapas de Coleta de Contexto, Refinamento e Estruturação e Testes de Leitura.","ru":"Идеально подходит для языковых агентов, которым требуются возможности структурированного сотрудничества по документам, такие как руководство пользователями на этапах сбора контекста, совершенствования и структурирования, а также тестирования читаемости.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء اللغويين الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات التعاون الوثائقي المهيكل، مثل توجيه المستخدمين عبر مراحل جمع السياق والتنقية والهيكلة واختبار القراء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to facilitate collaborative documentation creation using a structured workflow, including triggers for specific doc types like PRD, design doc, decision doc, or RFC, and supporting iterative content refinement through protocols like Context Gathering and Reader Testing.","zh":"赋予代理人创建结构化工作流的协作文档能力，包括特定文档类型（如 PRD、设计文档、决策文档或 RFC）的触发器，并通过上下文收集和读者测试等协议支持迭代内容细化。","ja":"エージェントが構造化されたワークフローを使用して共同のドキュメント作成を促進できるようにします。具体的には、PRD、デザインドキュメント、意思決定ドキュメント、またはRFCなどの特定のドキュメントタイプのトリガー、およびコンテキストの収集とリーダーテストなどのプロトコルを介した反復的なコンテンツの洗練をサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 구조화된 워크플로를 사용하여 협력 문서 생성을 촉진할 수 있도록 합니다. 구체적으로는 PRD, 디자인 문서, 의사 결정 문서 또는 RFC와 같은 특정 문서 유형의 트리거 및 컨텍스트 수집 및 리더 테스트와 같은 프로토콜을 통해 반복적인 콘텐츠 정제를 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a facilitar la creación colaborativa de documentación utilizando un flujo de trabajo estructurado, incluyendo activadores para tipos de documentos específicos como PRD, documento de diseño, documento de decisión o RFC, y que admiten la refinación iterativa de contenido a través de protocolos como Recopilación de Contexto y Pruebas de Lector.","fr":"Permet aux agents de faciliter la création collaborative de documentation en utilisant un flux de travail structuré, y compris des déclencheurs pour des types de documents spécifiques comme PRD, document de conception, document de décision ou RFC, et qui soutiennent l''affinement itératif du contenu à travers des protocoles tels que la Collecte de Contexte et les Tests de Lecteur.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die collaborative Erstellung von Dokumentationen mithilfe eines strukturierten Workflows zu erleichtern, einschließlich Auslösern für bestimmte Dokumenttypen wie PRD, Designdokument, Entscheidungsdokument oder RFC, und die iterative Inhaltsverfeinerung durch Protokolle wie Kontextsammeln und Lesertests unterstützen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a facilitar a criação colaborativa de documentação usando um fluxo de trabalho estruturado, incluindo gatilhos para tipos de documentos específicos, como PRD, documento de design, documento de decisão ou RFC, e apoiando o aperfeiçoamento iterativo do conteúdo por meio de protocolos como Coleta de Contexto e Testes de Leitura.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью облегчить создание документов посредством структурированного рабочего процесса, включая триггеры для конкретных типов документов, таких как PRD, документ дизайна, документ решения или RFC, и поддержку итеративного совершенствования контента посредством протоколов, таких как сбор контекста и тестирование читаемости.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تسهيل إنشاء الوثائق التعاونية باستخدام تدفق عمل مهيكل، بما في ذلك الزنادات لنوع معين من الوثائق، مثل PRD ووثيقة التصميم ووثيقة القرار أو RFC، ودعم تحسين المحتوى التكراري من خلال بروتوكولات مثل جمع السياق واختبار القراء."},"useCases":{"en":["Guiding users through drafting technical specs","Facilitating collaborative proposal writing","Assisting in the creation of decision documents through structured workflows"],"zh":["指导用户完成技术规格草稿的编写","促进协作提案的撰写","通过结构化工作流协助创建决策文档"],"ja":["技術仕様の草案作成におけるユーザーのサポート","共同提案書の作成を促進する","構造化されたワークフローを使用して意思決定ドキュメントの作成を支援する"],"ko":["기술 사양 초안 작성에서 사용자를 지원하는 것","공동 제안서 작성을 촉진하는 것","구조화된 워크플로를 사용하여 의사 결정 문서의 작성에 도움을 주는 것"],"es":["Guiar a los usuarios en la redacción de especificaciones técnicas","Facilitar la redacción colaborativa de propuestas","Ayudar en la creación de documentos de decisión a través de flujos de trabajo estructurados"],"fr":["Guider les utilisateurs dans la rédaction de spécifications techniques","Faciliter la rédaction collaborative de propositions","Aider à la création de documents de décision à travers des flux de travail structurés"],"de":["Benutzer bei der Erstellung von technischen Spezifikationen führen","Collaborative Angebotsformulierung erleichtern","Unterstützen bei der Erstellung von Entscheidungsdokumenten mithilfe strukturierter Workflows"],"pt":["Orientar os usuários durante a elaboração de especificações técnicas","Facilitar a redação colaborativa de propostas","Auxiliar na criação de documentos de decisão por meio de fluxos de trabalho estruturados"],"ru":["Руководство пользователями при составлении технических спецификаций","Облегчение совместного написания предложений","Помощь в создании документов решений посредством структурированных рабочих процессов"],"ar":["توجيه المستخدمين خلال صياغة المواصفات الفنية","تسهيل كتابة العروض التعاونية","مساعدة في إنشاء وثائق القرارات من خلال تدفقات عمل مهيكلة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user input on documentation tasks","Limited to text-based documentation collaboration"],"zh":["需要用户在文档任务上输入","仅限于基于文本的文档协作"],"ja":["ドキュメントのタスクについてユーザーからの入力を必要とする","テキストベースのドキュメント作成のみに限定される"],"ko":["문서 작업에 대한 사용자 입력이 필요함","텍스트 기반 문서 협업에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la entrada del usuario en tareas de documentación","Limitado a la colaboración de documentación basada en texto"],"fr":["Nécessite la saisie de l''utilisateur pour les tâches de documentation","Limité à la collaboration de documentation basée sur le texte"],"de":["Benutzereingabe für Dokumentationsaufgaben erforderlich","Begrenzt auf textbasierte Dokumenten-Kollaboration"],"pt":["Exige entrada do usuário em tarefas de documentação","Limitado à colaboração de documentação baseada em texto"],"ru":["Требует ввода пользователя при выполнении задач документации","Ограничен сотрудничеством по документации на основе текста"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال المستخدم في مهام التوثيق","محدود بالتعاون في توثيق قائم على النص"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"2e47d78846faeea4a56e9809c52700087a15a2155a3f293a3efbaded81398ef4","repoEtag":"W/\"76d69a3a3bb3abe2a601cefe1745ab33d5b89bce596aefbe206b5cf70e5967b9\"","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/frontend-design', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'frontend-design', 71981, 7353, 60, '2026-02-20T01:43:22Z', '2026-02-20T01:51:02.448Z', 'b81e2ff87ed8fa4d6c377ccb127a7254c9e6a77e3ae94f21e6b514f7bb2945a0', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/frontend-design","name":"frontend-design","description":{"zh":"前端设计技能用于创建高品质的网页界面，具有独特的设计风格。通过该技能，可以创建出色的网页组件、页面和应用程序。","ja":"フロントエンドデザインスキルは、高品質のWebインターフェースを作成するために使用され、独自のデザインスタイルを実現します。このスキルを使用すると、優れたWebコンポーネント、ページ、アプリケーションを作成できます。","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 기술은 고품질의 웹 인터페이스를 생성하는 데 사용되며 고유한 디자인 스타일을 구현합니다. 이 기술을 사용하면 優れた 웹 컴포넌트, 페이지, 애플리케이션을 생성할 수 있습니다.","es":"Este skill permite crear interfaces frontend de alta calidad y personalizadas, evitando estéticas genéricas de IA. Genera código creativo y pulido con atención al detalle.","fr":"Ce skill permet de créer des interfaces frontend de haute qualité et personnalisées, en évitant les esthétiques génériques de l''IA. Génère du code créatif et poli avec attention au détail.","de":"Dieser Skill ermöglicht die Erstellung von hochwertigen und benutzerdefinierten Frontend-Oberflächen, die generische IA-Ästhetik vermeiden. Generiert kreativen und polierten Code mit Aufmerksamkeit zum Detail.","pt":"Esta habilidade permite criar interfaces frontend personalizadas e de alta qualidade, evitando estéticas genéricas de IA. Desenvolva componentes web, páginas e aplicativos com design criativo e polido.","ru":"Эта навык позволяет создавать уникальные интерфейсы frontend и высокого качества, избегая.generic эстетики ИИ. Разработайте веб-компоненты, страницы и приложения с креативным и отполированным дизайном.","ar":"تتيح هذه المهارة إنشاء واجهات مستخدم أمامية مخصصة وعالية الجودة، وتتجنب الجماليات العامة لبرامج الذكاء الاصطناعي. طور مكونات الويب والصفحات والتطبيقات مع تصميم متقن ومبتكر.","en":"Create distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces with high design quality. Use this skill when the user asks to build web components, pages, artifacts, posters, or applications (examples include websites, landing pages, dashboards, React components, HTML/CSS layouts, or when styling/beaut..."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":71981,"forks":7353,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:43:22Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"frontend-design","description":"Create distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces with high design quality. Use this skill when the user asks to build web components, pages, artifacts, posters, or applications (examples include websites, landing pages, dashboards, React components, HTML/CSS layouts, or when styling/beautifying any web UI). Generates creative, polished code and UI design that avoids generic AI aesthetics.","bodyPreview":"This skill guides creation of distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces that avoid generic \"AI slop\" aesthetics. Implement real working code with exceptional attention to aesthetic details and creative choices.\n\nThe user provides frontend requirements: a component, page, application, or interface to build. They may include context about the purpose, audience, or technical constraints.\n\n## Design Thinking\n\nBefore coding, understand the context and commit to a BOLD aesthetic direction:\n- *","body":"This skill guides creation of distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces that avoid generic \"AI slop\" aesthetics. Implement real working code with exceptional attention to aesthetic details and creative choices.\n\nThe user provides frontend requirements: a component, page, application, or interface to build. They may include context about the purpose, audience, or technical constraints.\n\n## Design Thinking\n\nBefore coding, understand the context and commit to a BOLD aesthetic direction:\n- **Purpose**: What problem does this interface solve? Who uses it?\n- **Tone**: Pick an extreme: brutally minimal, maximalist chaos, retro-futuristic, organic/natural, luxury/refined, playful/toy-like, editorial/magazine, brutalist/raw, art deco/geometric, soft/pastel, industrial/utilitarian, etc. There are so many flavors to choose from. Use these for inspiration but design one that is true to the aesthetic direction.\n- **Constraints**: Technical requirements (framework, performance, accessibility).\n- **Differentiation**: What makes this UNFORGETTABLE? What''s the one thing someone will remember?\n\n**CRITICAL**: Choose a clear conceptual direction and execute it with precision. Bold maximalism and refined minimalism both work - the key is intentionality, not intensity.\n\nThen implement working code (HTML/CSS/JS, React, Vue, etc.) that is:\n- Production-grade and functional\n- Visually striking and memorable\n- Cohesive with a clear aesthetic point-of-view\n- Meticulously refined in every detail\n\n## Frontend Aesthetics Guidelines\n\nFocus on:\n- **Typography**: Choose fonts that are beautiful, unique, and interesting. Avoid generic fonts like Arial and Inter; opt instead for distinctive choices that elevate the frontend''s aesthetics; unexpected, characterful font choices. Pair a distinctive display font with a refined body font.\n- **Color & Theme**: Commit to a cohesive aesthetic. Use CSS variables for consistency. Dominant colors with sharp accents outperform timid, evenly-distributed palettes.\n- **Motion**: Use animations for effects and micro-interactions. Prioritize CSS-only solutions for HTML. Use Motion library for React when available. Focus on high-impact moments: one well-orchestrated page load with staggered reveals (animation-delay) creates more delight than scattered micro-interactions. Use scroll-triggering and hover states that surprise.\n- **Spatial Composition**: Unexpected layouts. Asymmetry. Overlap. Diagonal flow. Grid-breaking elements. Generous negative space OR controlled density.\n- **Backgrounds & Visual Details**: Create atmosphere and depth rather than defaulting to solid colors. Add contextual effects and textures that match the overall aesthetic. Apply creative forms like gradient meshes, noise textures, geometric patterns, layered transparencies, dramatic shadows, decorative borders, custom cursors, and grain overlays.\n\nNEVER use generic AI-generated aesthetics like overused font families (Inter, Roboto, Arial, system fonts), cliched color schemes (particularly purple gradients on white backgrounds), predictable layouts and component patterns, and cookie-cutter design that lacks context-specific character.\n\nInterpret creatively and make unexpected choices that feel genuinely designed for the context. No design should be the same. Vary between light and dark themes, different fonts, different aesthetics. NEVER converge on common choices (Space Grotesk, for example) across generations.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Match implementation complexity to the aesthetic vision. Maximalist designs need elaborate code with extensive animations and effects. Minimalist or refined designs need restraint, precision, and careful attention to spacing, typography, and subtle details. Elegance comes from executing the vision well.\n\nRemember: Claude is capable of extraordinary creative work. Don''t hold back, show what can truly be created when thinking outside the box and committing fully to a distinctive vision.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T01:51:02.448Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"前端设计技能 - 创建高品质的网页界面","ja":"フロントエンドデザインスキル - 高品質のWebインターフェースを作成","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 기술 - 고품질의 웹 인터페이스 생성","es":"Diseño Frontend: Interfaces Web de Alta Calidad","fr":"Conception Frontend: Interfaces Web de Haute Qualité","de":"Frontend-Design: Hochwertige Web-Oberflächen","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Interfaces Frontend Personalizadas","ru":"Создание уникальных интерфейсов frontend","ar":"تصميم واجهات المستخدم الأمامية المخصصة","en":"frontend-design"},"description":{"zh":"前端设计技能用于创建高品质的网页界面，具有独特的设计风格。通过该技能，可以创建出色的网页组件、页面和应用程序。","ja":"フロントエンドデザインスキルは、高品質のWebインターフェースを作成するために使用され、独自のデザインスタイルを実現します。このスキルを使用すると、優れたWebコンポーネント、ページ、アプリケーションを作成できます。","ko":"프론트엔드 디자인 기술은 고품질의 웹 인터페이스를 생성하는 데 사용되며 고유한 디자인 스타일을 구현합니다. 이 기술을 사용하면 優れた 웹 컴포넌트, 페이지, 애플리케이션을 생성할 수 있습니다.","es":"Este skill permite crear interfaces frontend de alta calidad y personalizadas, evitando estéticas genéricas de IA. Genera código creativo y pulido con atenci...","fr":"Ce skill permet de créer des interfaces frontend de haute qualité et personnalisées, en évitant les esthétiques génériques de l''IA. Génère du code créatif et...","de":"Dieser Skill ermöglicht die Erstellung von hochwertigen und benutzerdefinierten Frontend-Oberflächen, die generische IA-Ästhetik vermeiden. Generiert kreativ...","pt":"Esta habilidade permite criar interfaces frontend personalizadas e de alta qualidade, evitando estéticas genéricas de IA. Desenvolva componentes web, páginas...","ru":"Эта навык позволяет создавать уникальные интерфейсы frontend и высокого качества, избегая.generic эстетики ИИ. Разработайте веб-компоненты, страницы и прилож...","ar":"تتيح هذه المهارة إنشاء واجهات مستخدم أمامية مخصصة وعالية الجودة، وتتجنب الجماليات العامة لبرامج الذكاء الاصطناعي. طور مكونات الويب والصفحات والتطبيقات مع تصم...","en":"Create distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces with high design quality. Use this skill when the user asks to build web components, pages, artifact..."},"definition":{"en":"Create distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces with high design quality. Use this skill when the user asks to build web components, pages, artifacts, posters, or applications (examples include websites, landing pages, dashboards, React components, HTML/CSS layouts, or when styling/beautifying any web UI). Generates creative, polished code and UI design that avoids generic AI aesthetics."},"features":{"zh":["创建独特的网页界面","高品质的设计","避免通用AI美学","实现实用代码","创意设计选择"],"ja":["独自のWebインターフェースを作成","高品質のデザイン","一般的なAIエステティックを避ける","実用的コードを実現","創造的なデザイン選択"],"ko":["고유한 웹 인터페이스 생성","고품질의 디자인","일반적인 AI 미학 피하기","실용적인 코드 구현","창의적인 디자인 선택"],"es":["Crea interfaces frontend personalizadas","Evita estéticas genéricas de IA","Genera código creativo y pulido","Atención al detalle en el diseño","Ideal para desarrolladores web","Permite la creación de componentes y aplicaciones web"],"fr":["Crée des interfaces frontend personnalisées","Évite les esthétiques génériques de l''IA","Génère du code créatif et poli","Attention au détail dans la conception","Idéal pour les développeurs web","Permet la création de composants et d''applications web"],"de":["Erstellt benutzerdefinierte Frontend-Oberflächen","Vermeidet generische IA-Ästhetik","Generiert kreativen und polierten Code","Aufmerksamkeit zum Detail im Design","Ideal für Web-Entwickler","Ermöglicht die Erstellung von Komponenten und Web-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Criação de componentes web personalizados","Desenvolvimento de páginas e aplicativos com design criativo","Evitação de estéticas genéricas de IA","Design polido e de alta qualidade","Implementação de código funcional e eficaz"],"ru":["Создание веб-компонентов с креативным дизайном","Разработка страниц и приложений с отполированным дизайном","Избегание.generic эстетики ИИ","Отполированный и высококачественный дизайн","Реализация функционального и эффективного кода"],"ar":["إنشاء مكونات الويب مع تصميم مبتكر","تطوير الصفحات والتطبيقات مع تصميم متقن","تجنب الجماليات العامة لبرامج الذكاء الاصطناعي","تصميم متقن وعالية الجودة","تنفيذ رمز وظيفي وفعال"]},"keywords":{"zh":["前端设计","网页界面","高品质设计","AI美学","创意设计","网页开发","前端开发"],"ja":["フロントエンドデザイン","Webインターフェース","高品質デザイン","AIエステティック","創造的なデザイン","Web開発","フロントエンド開発"],"ko":["프론트엔드 디자인","웹 인터페이스","고품질 디자인","AI 미학","창의적인 디자인","웹 개발","프론트엔드 개발"],"es":["diseño frontend","interfaces web","alta calidad","personalizadas","evitar estéticas genéricas de IA","desarrollo web","componentes web","aplicaciones web"],"fr":["conception frontend","interfaces web","haute qualité","personnalisées","éviter les esthétiques génériques de l''IA","développement web","composants web","applications web"],"de":["Frontend-Design","Web-Oberflächen","hochwertig","benutzerdefiniert","vermeiden generische IA-Ästhetik","Web-Entwicklung","Komponenten","Web-Anwendungen"],"pt":["desenvolvimento frontend","interfaces personalizadas","design criativo","componentes web","páginas e aplicativos","evitar estéticas genéricas de IA"],"ru":["создание интерфейсов frontend","уникальные интерфейсы","креативный дизайн","веб-компоненты","страницы и приложения","избегание.generic эстетики ИИ"],"ar":["تصميم واجهات المستخدم الأمامية","واجهات مخصصة","تصميم مبتكر","مكونات الويب","الصفحات والتطبيقات","تجنب الجماليات العامة لبرامج الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Visual AI Agents requiring high-quality, production-grade frontend interface design capabilities.","zh":"适合需要高质量、生产级前端界面设计能力的视觉AI代理。","ja":"高品質のフロントエンドインターフェイス設計能力を必要とするビジュアルAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고품질의 프로덕션급 프론트엔드 인터페이스 디자인 기능이 필요한 시각적 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Inteligencia Artificial Visuales que requieren capacidades de diseño de interfaz de usuario de frontend de alta calidad y grado de producción.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents d''Intelligence Artificielle Visuels nécessitant des capacités de conception d''interface utilisateur frontend de haute qualité et de grade de production.","de":"Ideal für visuelle KI-Agents, die über hochwertige, produktionsreife Frontend-Schnittstellen-Designfunktionen verfügen müssen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Visuais que exigem capacidades de design de interface de frontend de alta qualidade e produção.","ru":"Идеально для визуальных агентов ИИ, требующих высококачественного, промышленного дизайна интерфейса frontend.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الاستخبارات الاصطناعية البصرية التي تتطلب قدرات تصميم واجهة المستخدم الأمامية عالية الجودة و جاهزة للانتاج."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate creative, polished HTML/CSS layouts and React components, avoiding generic AI aesthetics by incorporating exceptional attention to aesthetic details and creative choices, utilizing real working code and UI design principles.","zh":"赋予代理生成创意、精致的HTML/CSS布局和React组件，通过融入异常的审美细节和创意选择，利用真正的工作代码和UI设计原则，避免通用的AI美学。","ja":"エージェントに創造的で磨かれたHTML/CSSレイアウトとReactコンポーネントを生成させ、特異的な美的細部と創造的選択を取り入れることで、一般的なAIの美的感覚を避け、実際の動作コードとUI設計原則を利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 창의적이고 정교한 HTML/CSS 레이아웃 및 React 컴포넌트를 생성할 수 있도록 해 주며, 예외적인 미적細節와 창의적인 선택을 통합하여 일반적인 AI 미학을 피하고, 실제 작동 코드와 UI 설계 원리를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar diseños de layouts HTML/CSS creativos y pulidos, y componentes de React, evitando estéticas de IA genéricas al incorporar una atención excepcional a los detalles estéticos y las elecciones creativas, utilizando código de trabajo real y principios de diseño de interfaz de usuario.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des dispositions de layout HTML/CSS créatives et polies, et des composants React, en évitant les esthétiques d''IA génériques en incorporant une attention exceptionnelle aux détails esthétiques et aux choix créatifs, en utilisant du code de travail réel et des principes de conception d''interface utilisateur.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, kreative, polierte HTML/CSS-Layouts und React-Komponenten zu generieren, indem sie generische KI-Ästhetik vermeiden, indem sie außergewöhnliche Aufmerksamkeit für ästhetische Details und kreative Entscheidungen aufbringen, unter Verwendung von echtem Arbeitscode und Benutzeroberflächen-Designprinzipien.","pt":"Habilita agentes a gerar layouts HTML/CSS criativos e componentes polidos do React, evitando estética de IA genérica incorporando atenção excepcional aos detalhes estéticos e escolhas criativas, utilizando código de trabalho real e princípios de design de UI.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать творческие, отполированные макеты HTML/CSS и компоненты React, избегая общей эстетики ИИ путем включения исключительного внимания к деталям и творческим решениям, используя рабочий код и принципы дизайна пользовательского интерфейса.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من توليد تخطيطات HTML/CSS مبتكرة ومكونات React مطفية، وتجنب جماليات الإي أي العامة من خلال دمج اهتمام استثنائي بالتفاصيل الجمالية والخيارات الإبداعية، باستخدام رمز العمل الحقيقي ومبادئ تصميم واجهة المستخدم."},"useCases":{"en":["Building distinctive web components","Creating custom landing pages with high design quality","Designing and styling dashboards with unique aesthetics"],"zh":["构建独特的Web组件","创建高设计质量的自定义着陆页","设计和样式化具有独特美学的仪表板"],"ja":["独自のWebコンポーネントを構築する","高品質のカスタムランディングページを作成する","ユニークな美的感覚を持つダッシュボードを設計およびスタイル化する"],"ko":["독특한 웹 컴포넌트 구축","고품질의 커스텀 랜딩 페이지 생성","독특한 미적 감각을 갖춘 대시보드 설계 및 스타일링"],"es":["Construir componentes web distintivos","Crear páginas de destino personalizadas con alta calidad de diseño","Diseñar y dar estilo a paneles de control con estéticas únicas"],"fr":["Construire des composants web distinctifs","Créer des pages de destination personnalisées avec une haute qualité de conception","Concevoir et styliser des tableaux de bord avec des esthétiques uniques"],"de":["Unterscheidbare Webkomponenten erstellen","Benutzerdefinierte Landingpages mit hoher Designqualität erstellen","Dashboards mit einzigartigen Ästhetiken entwerfen und stylen"],"pt":["Construir componentes web distintos","Criar páginas de destino personalizadas com alta qualidade de design","Projetar e estilizar dashboards com estética única"],"ru":["Создание отличительных веб-компонентов","Создание пользовательских посадочных страниц с высоким качеством дизайна","Проектирование и стилизация панелей управления с уникальной эстетикой"],"ar":["بناء مكونات الويب المميزة","إنشاء صفحات هبوط مخصصة ذات جودة تصميم عالية","تصميم وتنسيق لوحات التحكم بأسلوب جمالي فريد"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user-provided frontend requirements and context","May need additional technical constraints for optimal results"],"zh":["需要用户提供前端需求和上下文","可能需要额外的技术约束以获得最佳结果"],"ja":["前端要件とコンテキストをユーザーが提供する必要がある","最適な結果を得るために追加の技術的制約が必要になる可能性がある"],"ko":["사용자가 프론트엔드 요구 사항과 컨텍스트를 제공해야 함","최적의 결과를 얻기 위해 추가 기술 제약이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere requisitos y contexto de frontend proporcionados por el usuario","Puede necesitar restricciones técnicas adicionales para obtener resultados óptimos"],"fr":["Nécessite des exigences et un contexte de frontend fournis par l''utilisateur","Peut nécessiter des contraintes techniques supplémentaires pour obtenir des résultats optimaux"],"de":["Benötigt von Benutzern bereitgestellte Anforderungen und Kontext für Frontend","Kann zusätzliche technische Einschränkungen für optimale Ergebnisse benötigen"],"pt":["Exige requisitos e contexto de frontend fornecidos pelo usuário","Pode precisar de restrições técnicas adicionais para resultados ótimos"],"ru":["Требует предоставления требований и контекста frontend пользователем","Может потребовать дополнительных технических ограничений для оптимальных результатов"],"ar":["يتطلب متطلبات وسياق واجهة المستخدم الأمامية المقدمة من قبل المستخدم","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى قيود تقنية إضافية للحصول على نتائج أمثلية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"b81e2ff87ed8fa4d6c377ccb127a7254c9e6a77e3ae94f21e6b514f7bb2945a0","repoEtag":"W/\"5456759f24524b9171780a611a3970c1ae87a3d09576f2945661ad98ce4c37da\"","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('anthropics/skills/brand-guidelines', 'official', 'anthropics', 'skills', 'anthropics/skills', 'brand-guidelines', 71980, 7353, 50, '2026-02-20T01:38:00Z', '2026-02-20T01:44:18.610Z', '1120b3769e2985cefb3d25be981b1f914abeba57ae079b83c20c666c164fa9fe', '{"id":"anthropics/skills/brand-guidelines","name":"brand-guidelines","description":{"zh":"Anthropic品牌样式指南提供了官方品牌颜色和字体样式的应用方法","ja":"Anthoricブランドスタイリングガイドでは、公式ブランドカラーと字体スタイルの適用方法を提供","ko":"Anthropic 브랜드 스타일링 가이드에서는 공식 브랜드 색상과 글꼴 스타일을 적용하는 방법을 제공","es":"Este skill aplica los colores y la tipografía oficiales de Anthropics a cualquier artefacto. Proporciona acceso a los recursos de identidad y estilo de la marca.","fr":"Ce skill applique les couleurs et la typographie officielles d''Anthropics à tout type d''artefact. Il fournit un accès aux ressources d''identité et de style de la marque.","de":"Dieses Skill wendet die offiziellen Markenfarben und -typografie von Anthropics auf jedes Artefakt an. Es bietet Zugriff auf die Markenidentitäts- und Stilressourcen.","pt":"Aprenda a aplicar as diretrizes de marca da Anthropic em seus projetos, incluindo cores e tipografia oficiais","ru":"Примените руководство по бренду Anthropic к вашим проектам, включая официальные цвета и типографику","ar":"تعلم كيفية تطبيق إرشادات العلامة التجارية للأنثروبك في مشاريعك، بما في ذلك الألوان والتنسيق الرسمي","en":"Applies Anthropics official brand colors and typography to any sort of artifact that may benefit from having Anthropics look-and-feel. Use it when brand colors or style guidelines, visual formatting, or company design standards apply."},"owner":"anthropics","repo":"skills","repoPath":"anthropics/skills","stars":71980,"forks":7353,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:38:00Z","topics":["agent-skills"],"skillMd":{"name":"brand-guidelines","description":"Applies Anthropics official brand colors and typography to any sort of artifact that may benefit from having Anthropics look-and-feel. Use it when brand colors or style guidelines, visual formatting, or company design standards apply.","bodyPreview":"# Anthropic Brand Styling\n\n## Overview\n\nTo access Anthropic''s official brand identity and style resources, use this skill.\n\n**Keywords**: branding, corporate identity, visual identity, post-processing, styling, brand colors, typography, Anthropic brand, visual formatting, visual design\n\n## Brand Guidelines\n\n### Colors\n\n**Main Colors:**\n\n- Dark: `#141413` - Primary text and dark backgrounds\n- Light: `#faf9f5` - Light backgrounds and text on dark\n- Mid Gray: `#b0aea5` - Secondary elements\n- Light","body":"# Anthropic Brand Styling\n\n## Overview\n\nTo access Anthropic''s official brand identity and style resources, use this skill.\n\n**Keywords**: branding, corporate identity, visual identity, post-processing, styling, brand colors, typography, Anthropic brand, visual formatting, visual design\n\n## Brand Guidelines\n\n### Colors\n\n**Main Colors:**\n\n- Dark: `#141413` - Primary text and dark backgrounds\n- Light: `#faf9f5` - Light backgrounds and text on dark\n- Mid Gray: `#b0aea5` - Secondary elements\n- Light Gray: `#e8e6dc` - Subtle backgrounds\n\n**Accent Colors:**\n\n- Orange: `#d97757` - Primary accent\n- Blue: `#6a9bcc` - Secondary accent\n- Green: `#788c5d` - Tertiary accent\n\n### Typography\n\n- **Headings**: Poppins (with Arial fallback)\n- **Body Text**: Lora (with Georgia fallback)\n- **Note**: Fonts should be pre-installed in your environment for best results\n\n## Features\n\n### Smart Font Application\n\n- Applies Poppins font to headings (24pt and larger)\n- Applies Lora font to body text\n- Automatically falls back to Arial/Georgia if custom fonts unavailable\n- Preserves readability across all systems\n\n### Text Styling\n\n- Headings (24pt+): Poppins font\n- Body text: Lora font\n- Smart color selection based on background\n- Preserves text hierarchy and formatting\n\n### Shape and Accent Colors\n\n- Non-text shapes use accent colors\n- Cycles through orange, blue, and green accents\n- Maintains visual interest while staying on-brand\n\n## Technical Details\n\n### Font Management\n\n- Uses system-installed Poppins and Lora fonts when available\n- Provides automatic fallback to Arial (headings) and Georgia (body)\n- No font installation required - works with existing system fonts\n- For best results, pre-install Poppins and Lora fonts in your environment\n\n### Color Application\n\n- Uses RGB color values for precise brand matching\n- Applied via python-pptx''s RGBColor class\n- Maintains color fidelity across different systems\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T01:44:18.610Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"Anthropic品牌样式指南","ja":"Anthropicブランドスタイリングガイド","ko":"Anthropic 브랜드 스타일링 가이드","es":"Guías de marca Anthropics","fr":"Directives de marque Anthropics","de":"Anthropic Markenrichtlinien","pt":"Diretrizes de Marca Anthropic","ru":"Руководство по бренду Anthropic","ar":"إرشادات العلامة التجارية للأنثروبك","en":"brand-guidelines"},"description":{"zh":"Anthropic品牌样式指南提供了官方品牌颜色和字体样式的应用方法","ja":"Anthoricブランドスタイリングガイドでは、公式ブランドカラーと字体スタイルの適用方法を提供","ko":"Anthropic 브랜드 스타일링 가이드에서는 공식 브랜드 색상과 글꼴 스타일을 적용하는 방법을 제공","es":"Este skill aplica los colores y la tipografía oficiales de Anthropics a cualquier artefacto. Proporciona acceso a los recursos de identidad y estilo de la ma...","fr":"Ce skill applique les couleurs et la typographie officielles d''Anthropics à tout type d''artefact. Il fournit un accès aux ressources d''identité et de style d...","de":"Dieses Skill wendet die offiziellen Markenfarben und -typografie von Anthropics auf jedes Artefakt an. Es bietet Zugriff auf die Markenidentitäts- und Stilre...","pt":"Aprenda a aplicar as diretrizes de marca da Anthropic em seus projetos, incluindo cores e tipografia oficiais","ru":"Примените руководство по бренду Anthropic к вашим проектам, включая официальные цвета и типографику","ar":"تعلم كيفية تطبيق إرشادات العلامة التجارية للأنثروبك في مشاريعك، بما في ذلك الألوان والتنسيق الرسمي","en":"Applies Anthropics official brand colors and typography to any sort of artifact that may benefit from having Anthropics look-and-feel. Use it when brand colo..."},"definition":{"en":"Applies Anthropics official brand colors and typography to any sort of artifact that may benefit from having Anthropics look-and-feel. Use it when brand colors or style guidelines, visual formatting, or company design standards apply."},"features":{"zh":["应用Anthropic官方品牌颜色","应用Anthropic官方字体样式","支持多种设计元素","提供品牌样式指南","帮助开发者保持一致的品牌风格"],"ja":["公式ブランドカラーの適用","公式字体スタイルの適用","複数のデザイン要素のサポート","ブランドスタイリングガイドの提供","開発者による一貫したブランドスタイルの保持"],"ko":["공식 브랜드 색상의 적용","공식 글꼴 스타일의 적용","다양한 디자인 요소의 지원","브랜드 스타일링 가이드의 제공","개발자에 의한 일관된 브랜드 스타일의 유지"],"es":["Colores de marca oficiales","Tipografía personalizada","Estilos de formato visual","Acceso a recursos de identidad de la marca","Aplicación de la identidad visual de Anthropics"],"fr":["Couleurs de marque officielles","Typographie personnalisée","Styles de formatage visuel","Accès aux ressources d''identité de la marque","Application de l''identité visuelle d''Anthropics"],"de":["Offizielle Markenfarben","Maßgeschneiderte Typografie","Visuelle Formatierungsstile","Zugriff auf Markenidentitätsressourcen","Anwendung der visuellen Identität von Anthropics"],"pt":["Cores oficiais da Anthropic","Tipografia oficial da Anthropic","Padrões de design visual","Formatação de texto","Estilos de fundo","Elementos secundários"],"ru":["Официальные цвета Anthropic","Официальная типография Anthropic","Визуальные стандарты дизайна","Форматирование текста","Стили фона","Второстепенные элементы"],"ar":["الألوان الرسمية للأنثروبك","التنسيق الرسمي للأنثروبك","معايير التصميم البصري","تنسيق النص","أسلوب الخلفية","عناصر ثانوية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Anthropic品牌样式","品牌颜色","字体样式","设计元素","品牌风格","开发者工具"],"ja":["Anthoricブランドスタイリング","ブランドカラー","字体スタイル","デザイン要素","ブランドスタイル","開発者ツール"],"ko":["Anthropic 브랜드 스타일링","브랜드 색상","글꼴 스타일","디자인 요소","브랜드 스타일","개발자 도구"],"es":["guías de marca","identidad visual","colores de marca","tipografía","estilos de formato visual","recursos de identidad de la marca","Anthropic","marca","diseño visual"],"fr":["directives de marque","identité visuelle","couleurs de marque","typographie","styles de formatage visuel","ressources d''identité de la marque","Anthropics","marque","conception visuelle"],"de":["Markenrichtlinien","visuelle Identität","Markenfarben","Typografie","visuelle Formatierungsstile","Markenidentitätsressourcen","Anthropic","Marke","visuelles Design"],"pt":["diretrizes de marca","cores oficiais","tipografia oficial","design visual","formatação de texto","estilos de fundo","elementos secundários","branding","identidade corporativa"],"ru":["руководство по бренду","официальные цвета","официальная типография","визуальный дизайн","форматирование текста","стили фона","второстепенные элементы","брендинг","корпоративная идентичность"],"ar":["إرشادات العلامة التجارية","الألوان الرسمية","التنسيق الرسمي","التصميم البصري","تنسيق النص","أسلوب الخلفية","عناصر ثانوية","ブランド","الهوية الشركة"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Visual Design Agents requiring consistent application of Anthropic''s brand identity and style resources","zh":"适用于需要一致应用Anthropic品牌身份和风格资源的视觉设计代理","ja":"Anthropicのブランドアイデンティティとスタイルリソースを一貫して適用する必要があるビジュアルデザインエージェントに最適","ko":"Anthropic의 브랜드 정체성과 스타일 리소스를 일관되게 적용해야 하는 비주얼 디자인 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Diseño Visual que requieren una aplicación consistente de la identidad y los recursos de estilo de la marca Anthropic","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de conception visuelle nécessitant une application cohérente de l''identité de marque et des ressources de style d''Anthropic","de":"Ideal für visuelle Designagenten, die eine konsistente Anwendung der Markenidentität und Stilressourcen von Anthropic erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Design Visual que exigem aplicação consistente da identidade e recursos de estilo da marca Anthropic","ru":"Идеально для Визуальных Дизайн-агентов, требующих последовательного применения идентичности бренда и ресурсов стиля Anthropic","ar":"مثالية لوسائط التصميم البصري التي تتطلب تطبيقًا متسقًا للهوية والعلامة التجارية لموارد Anthropic"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply Anthropic''s official brand colors and typography, ensuring consistent visual formatting and styling across various artifacts, utilizing specific brand guidelines such as main colors, typography, and visual design standards","zh":"赋予代理应用Anthropic的官方品牌颜色和字体，确保各种文档中的一致视觉格式和样式，利用特定的品牌指南，例如主要颜色、字体和视觉设计标准","ja":"エージェントにAnthropicの公式ブランドカラーとタイポグラフィを適用することを可能にし、さまざまなアーティファクト全体で一貫した視覚的なフォーマットとスタイリングを保証する、具体的にはメインカラー、タイポグラフィ、視覚デザイン標準などのブランドガイドラインを利用","ko":"에이전트가 Anthropic의 공식 브랜드 색상과 타이포그래피를 적용할 수 있도록 해주어, 다양한 아티팩트에서 일관된 시각적 형식과 스타일링을 보장하며, 주요 색상, 타이포그래피, 시각적 디자인 표준 등을 포함한 특정 브랜드 가이드라인을 사용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar los colores oficiales de la marca Anthropic y la tipografía, garantizando un formato y estilo visual coherente en varios artefactos, utilizando pautas de marca específicas como colores principales, tipografía y normas de diseño visual","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer les couleurs de marque officielles d''Anthropic et la typographie, garantissant un formatage et un style visuel cohérents dans divers artefacts, en utilisant des directives de marque spécifiques telles que les couleurs principales, la typographie et les normes de conception visuelle","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die offiziellen Markenfarben und die Typografie von Anthropic anzuwenden, um ein konsistentes visuelles Format und Styling über verschiedene Artefakte hinweg sicherzustellen, unter Verwendung spezifischer Markenrichtlinien wie Hauptfarben, Typografie und visuelle Designstandards","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicarem as cores oficiais da marca Anthropic e a tipografia, garantindo um formato e estilo visual consistentes em vários artefatos, utilizando diretrizes de marca específicas, como cores principais, tipografia e padrões de design visual","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять официальные цвета бренда и типографику Anthropic, обеспечивая последовательное визуальное форматирование и стилизацию различных артефактов, используя конкретные руководства по бренду, такие как основные цвета, типография и стандарты визуального дизайна","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تطبيق ألوان العلامة التجارية الرسمية وطباعة Anthropic، مما يضمن تنسيقًا وتصميمًا بصريًا متسقين عبر各种 إصدارات، باستخدام إرشادات العلامة التجارية المحددة، مثل الألوان الرئيسية وطباعة وتصميم بیان"},"useCases":{"en":["Applying Anthropic''s brand colors to marketing materials","Generating visually consistent reports using Anthropic''s typography","Enforcing company design standards across digital platforms"],"zh":["将Anthropic的品牌颜色应用于营销材料","使用Anthropic的字体生成视觉一致的报告","在数字平台上执行公司设计标准"],"ja":["マーケティング資料にAnthropicのブランドカラーを適用する","Anthropicのタイポグラフィを使用して視覚的一貫したレポートを生成する","デジタルプラットフォーム全体で会社のデザイン標準を実施する"],"ko":["Anthropic의 브랜드 색상을 마케팅 자료에 적용하는 것","Anthropic의 타이포그래피를 사용하여 시각적으로 일관된 보고서를 생성하는 것","디지털 플랫폼에서 회사 디자인 표준을 적용하는 것"],"es":["Aplicar los colores de la marca Anthropic a materiales de marketing","Generar informes visualmente coherentes utilizando la tipografía de Anthropic","Hacer cumplir los estándares de diseño de la empresa en plataformas digitales"],"fr":["Appliquer les couleurs de la marque Anthropic à des matériaux de marketing","Générer des rapports visuellement cohérents en utilisant la typographie d''Anthropic","Faire respecter les normes de conception de l''entreprise sur les plateformes numériques"],"de":["Anwenden der Markenfarben von Anthropic auf Marketingmaterialien","Erzeugen visuell konsistenter Berichte unter Verwendung der Typografie von Anthropic","Durchsetzen der Designstandards des Unternehmens auf digitalen Plattformen"],"pt":["Aplicar as cores da marca Anthropic em materiais de marketing","Gerar relatórios visualmente consistentes usando a tipografia da Anthropic","Impor os padrões de design da empresa em plataformas digitais"],"ru":["Применение цветов бренда Anthropic к маркетинговым материалам","Генерация визуально последовательных отчетов с использованием типографики Anthropic","Внедрение стандартов дизайна компании на цифровых платформах"],"ar":["تطبيق ألوان العلامة التجارية من Anthropic على مواد التسويق","توليد تقارير متسقة بصريًا باستخدام طباعة Anthropic","فرض معايير تصميم الشركة عبر منصات رقمية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to Anthropic''s brand identity and style resources","Limited to Anthropic''s official brand guidelines and style"],"zh":["需要访问Anthropic的品牌身份和风格资源","仅限于Anthropic的官方品牌指南和风格"],"ja":["Anthropicのブランドアイデンティティとスタイルリソースへのアクセスが必要","Anthropicの公式ブランドガイドラインとスタイルに限定"],"ko":["Anthropic의 브랜드 정체성과 스타일 리소스에 접근할 수 있어야 함","Anthropic의 공식 브랜드 가이드라인과 스타일만 사용 가능"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la identidad y los recursos de estilo de la marca Anthropic","Limitado a las pautas oficiales de marca y estilo de Anthropic"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''identité de marque et aux ressources de style d''Anthropic","Limité aux directives de marque et de style officielles d''Anthropic"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Markenidentität und Stilressourcen von Anthropic","Begrenzt auf die offiziellen Markenrichtlinien und Stile von Anthropic"],"pt":["Exige acesso aos recursos de identidade e estilo da marca Anthropic","Limitado às diretrizes oficiais de marca e estilo da Anthropic"],"ru":["Требует доступа к ресурсам идентичности и стиля бренда Anthropic","Ограничен официальными руководствами по бренду и стилю Anthropic"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى موارد الهوية والتصميم للعلامة التجارية من Anthropic","محدود bằng إرشادات العلامة التجارية الرسمية والأسلوب من Anthropic"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"1120b3769e2985cefb3d25be981b1f914abeba57ae079b83c20c666c164fa9fe","repoEtag":"W/\"76d69a3a3bb3abe2a601cefe1745ab33d5b89bce596aefbe206b5cf70e5967b9\"","qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('vercel-labs/skills/find-skills', 'official', 'vercel-labs', 'skills', 'vercel-labs/skills', 'find-skills', 6326, 534, 100, '2026-02-20T01:53:15Z', '2026-02-20T02:03:08.239Z', '54b44dc9539df865fbb060f62fb062e8232e765852a0cf14c38301fe0c1eb264', '{"id":"vercel-labs/skills/find-skills","name":"find-skills","description":{"zh":"发现技能功能帮助您从开放代理技能生态系统中搜索和安装所需的技能，扩展代理功能","ja":"スキルを探す機能は、オープンエージェントスキルエコシステムから必要なスキルを検索してインストールし、エージェントの機能を拡張","ko":"스킬 찾기 기능은开放 에이전트 스킬 생태계에서 필요한 스킬을 검색하고 설치하여 에이전트 기능을 확장","es":"Find-skills te ayuda a descubrir e instalar habilidades de agente desde el ecosistema de habilidades de agente abierto","fr":"Find-skills vous aide à découvrir et à installer des compétences d''agent à partir de l''écosystème de compétences d''agent ouvert","de":"Find-skills hilft Ihnen, Agentenfähigkeiten aus dem offenen Agentenfähigkeits-Ökosystem zu entdecken und zu installieren","pt":"O find-skills ajuda a descobrir e instalar habilidades de agente da ecossistema de habilidades de agente aberto.","ru":"Find-skills помогает обнаружить и установить навыки агента из открытого экосистемы навыков агента.","ar":"يحصل find-skills على العثور على وتثبيت مهارات الوكيل من النظام البيئي المفتوح لمهارات الوكيل.","en":"Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like how do I do X, find a skill for X, is there a skill that can..., or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill."},"owner":"vercel-labs","repo":"skills","repoPath":"vercel-labs/skills","stars":6326,"forks":534,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:53:15Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"find-skills","description":"Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like how do I do X, find a skill for X, is there a skill that can..., or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill.","bodyPreview":"# Find Skills\n\nThis skill helps you discover and install skills from the open agent skills ecosystem.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user:\n\n- Asks \"how do I do X\" where X might be a common task with an existing skill\n- Says \"find a skill for X\" or \"is there a skill for X\"\n- Asks \"can you do X\" where X is a specialized capability\n- Expresses interest in extending agent capabilities\n- Wants to search for tools, templates, or workflows\n- Mentions they wish they had help with a","body":"# Find Skills\n\nThis skill helps you discover and install skills from the open agent skills ecosystem.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user:\n\n- Asks \"how do I do X\" where X might be a common task with an existing skill\n- Says \"find a skill for X\" or \"is there a skill for X\"\n- Asks \"can you do X\" where X is a specialized capability\n- Expresses interest in extending agent capabilities\n- Wants to search for tools, templates, or workflows\n- Mentions they wish they had help with a specific domain (design, testing, deployment, etc.)\n\n## What is the Skills CLI?\n\nThe Skills CLI (`npx skills`) is the package manager for the open agent skills ecosystem. Skills are modular packages that extend agent capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools.\n\n**Key commands:**\n\n- `npx skills find [query]` - Search for skills interactively or by keyword\n- `npx skills add <package>` - Install a skill from GitHub or other sources\n- `npx skills check` - Check for skill updates\n- `npx skills update` - Update all installed skills\n\n**Browse skills at:** https://skills.sh/\n\n## How to Help Users Find Skills\n\n### Step 1: Understand What They Need\n\nWhen a user asks for help with something, identify:\n\n1. The domain (e.g., React, testing, design, deployment)\n2. The specific task (e.g., writing tests, creating animations, reviewing PRs)\n3. Whether this is a common enough task that a skill likely exists\n\n### Step 2: Search for Skills\n\nRun the find command with a relevant query:\n\n```bash\nnpx skills find [query]\n```\n\nFor example:\n\n- User asks \"how do I make my React app faster?\" → `npx skills find react performance`\n- User asks \"can you help me with PR reviews?\" → `npx skills find pr review`\n- User asks \"I need to create a changelog\" → `npx skills find changelog`\n\nThe command will return results like:\n\n```\nInstall with npx skills add <owner/repo@skill>\n\nvercel-labs/agent-skills@vercel-react-best-practices\n└ https://skills.sh/vercel-labs/agent-skills/vercel-react-best-practices\n```\n\n### Step 3: Present Options to the User\n\nWhen you find relevant skills, present them to the user with:\n\n1. The skill name and what it does\n2. The install command they can run\n3. A link to learn more at skills.sh\n\nExample response:\n\n```\nI found a skill that might help! The \"vercel-react-best-practices\" skill provides\nReact and Next.js performance optimization guidelines from Vercel Engineering.\n\nTo install it:\nnpx skills add vercel-labs/agent-skills@vercel-react-best-practices\n\nLearn more: https://skills.sh/vercel-labs/agent-skills/vercel-react-best-practices\n```\n\n### Step 4: Offer to Install\n\nIf the user wants to proceed, you can install the skill for them:\n\n```bash\nnpx skills add <owner/repo@skill> -g -y\n```\n\nThe `-g` flag installs globally (user-level) and `-y` skips confirmation prompts.\n\n## Common Skill Categories\n\nWhen searching, consider these common categories:\n\n| Category        | Example Queries                          |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Web Development | react, nextjs, typescript, css, tailwind |\n| Testing         | testing, jest, playwright, e2e           |\n| DevOps          | deploy, docker, kubernetes, ci-cd        |\n| Documentation   | docs, readme, changelog, api-docs        |\n| Code Quality    | review, lint, refactor, best-practices   |\n| Design          | ui, ux, design-system, accessibility     |\n| Productivity    | workflow, automation, git                |\n\n## Tips for Effective Searches\n\n1. **Use specific keywords**: \"react testing\" is better than just \"testing\"\n2. **Try alternative terms**: If \"deploy\" doesn''t work, try \"deployment\" or \"ci-cd\"\n3. **Check popular sources**: Many skills come from `vercel-labs/agent-skills` or `ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills`\n\n## When No Skills Are Found\n\nIf no relevant skills exist:\n\n1. Acknowledge that no existing skill was found\n2. Offer to help with the task directly using your general capabilities\n3. Suggest the user could create their own skill with `npx skills init`\n\nExample:\n\n```\nI searched for skills related to \"xyz\" but didn''t find any matches.\nI can still help you with this task directly! Would you like me to proceed?\n\nIf this is something you do often, you could create your own skill:\nnpx skills init my-xyz-skill\n```\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:03:08.239Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"发现技能 - 找到并安装所需的代理技能","ja":"スキルを探す - 必要なエージェントスキルを検索してインストール","ko":"스킬 찾기 - 필요한 에이전트 스킬을 검색하고 설치","es":"Descubre habilidades de agente con find-skills","fr":"Découvrez les compétences d''agent avec find-skills","de":"Entdecken Sie Agentenfähigkeiten mit find-skills","pt":"Descubra Habilidades de Agente com find-skills","ru":"Найти навыки агента с помощью find-skills","ar":"اكتشف مهارات الوكيل مع find-skills","en":"find-skills"},"description":{"zh":"发现技能功能帮助您从开放代理技能生态系统中搜索和安装所需的技能，扩展代理功能","ja":"スキルを探す機能は、オープンエージェントスキルエコシステムから必要なスキルを検索してインストールし、エージェントの機能を拡張","ko":"스킬 찾기 기능은开放 에이전트 스킬 생태계에서 필요한 스킬을 검색하고 설치하여 에이전트 기능을 확장","es":"Find-skills te ayuda a descubrir e instalar habilidades de agente desde el ecosistema de habilidades de agente abierto","fr":"Find-skills vous aide à découvrir et à installer des compétences d''agent à partir de l''écosystème de compétences d''agent ouvert","de":"Find-skills hilft Ihnen, Agentenfähigkeiten aus dem offenen Agentenfähigkeits-Ökosystem zu entdecken und zu installieren","pt":"O find-skills ajuda a descobrir e instalar habilidades de agente da ecossistema de habilidades de agente aberto.","ru":"Find-skills помогает обнаружить и установить навыки агента из открытого экосистемы навыков агента.","ar":"يحصل find-skills على العثور على وتثبيت مهارات الوكيل من النظام البيئي المفتوح لمهارات الوكيل.","en":"Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like how do I do X, find a skill for X, is there a skill that can..., or express intere..."},"definition":{"en":"Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like how do I do X, find a skill for X, is there a skill that can..., or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill."},"features":{"zh":["搜索开放代理技能生态系统中的技能","安装所需的技能以扩展代理功能","支持用户询问如何执行特定任务","支持用户搜索工具、模板或工作流","帮助用户发现新的代理功能"],"ja":["オープンエージェントスキルエコシステムからスキルを検索","必要なスキルをインストールしてエージェントの機能を拡張","ユーザーが特定のタスクを実行する方法を尋ねる際のサポート","ユーザーがツール、テンプレート、またはワークフローを検索する際のサポート","ユーザーが新しいエージェント機能を発見するのを支援"],"ko":["开放 에이전트 스킬 생태계에서 스킬을 검색","必要한 스킬을 설치하여 에이전트 기능을 확장","사용자가 특정 작업을 수행하는 방법을 묻는 경우 지원","사용자가 도구, 템플릿 또는 워크플로우를 검색하는 경우 지원","사용자가 새로운 에이전트 기능을 발견하는 것을 지원"],"es":["Descubre habilidades de agente","Instala habilidades de agente","Amplía las capacidades de tu agente","Busca herramientas y plantillas","Extiende las funcionalidades de tu agente"],"fr":["Découvrez des compétences d''agent","Installez des compétences d''agent","Étendez les capacités de votre agent","Recherchez des outils et des modèles","Étendez les fonctionnalités de votre agent"],"de":["Entdecken Sie Agentenfähigkeiten","Installieren Sie Agentenfähigkeiten","Erweitern Sie die Fähigkeiten Ihres Agenten","Suchen Sie nach Tools und Vorlagen","Erweitern Sie die Funktionalitäten Ihres Agenten"],"pt":["Descubra habilidades de agente","Instale habilidades de agente","Estenda as capacidades do seu agente","Encontre ferramentas e workflows","Melhore a eficiência do seu agente","Acesse a ecossistema de habilidades de agente aberto"],"ru":["Обнаружите навыки агента","Установите навыки агента","Расширьте возможности своего агента","Найдите инструменты и workflows","Улучшите эффективность своего агента","Доступ к открытому экосистеме навыков агента"],"ar":["اكتشف مهارات الوكيل","ثبت مهارات الوكيل","وسع إمكانيات وكيلك","ابحث عن أدوات ورسومات","حسن كفاءة وكيلك","الوصول إلى النظام البيئي المفتوح لمهارات الوكيل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["发现技能","代理技能","开放代理技能生态系统","技能搜索","技能安装","代理功能扩展","开发者工具"],"ja":["スキルを探す","エージェントスキル","オープンエージェントスキルエコシステム","スキル検索","スキルインストール","エージェント機能拡張","開発者ツール"],"ko":["스킬 찾기","에이전트 스킬","开放 에이전트 스킬 생태계","스킬 검색","스킬 설치","에이전트 기능 확장","개발자 도구"],"es":["habilidades de agente","find-skills","ecosistema de habilidades de agente","ampliar capacidades","instalar habilidades","descubrir habilidades"],"fr":["compétences d''agent","find-skills","écosystème de compétences d''agent","étendre les capacités","installer des compétences","découvrir des compétences"],"de":["Agentenfähigkeiten","find-skills","Agentenfähigkeits-Ökosystem","Fähigkeiten erweitern","Fähigkeiten installieren","Fähigkeiten entdecken"],"pt":["habilidades de agente","find-skills","ecossistema de habilidades de agente","descobrir habilidades","instalar habilidades","estender capacidades","ferramentas de agente","workflows de agente","eficiência do agente"],"ru":["навыки агента","find-skills","экосистема навыков агента","обнаружить навыки","установить навыки","расширить возможности","инструменты агента","workflows агента","эффективность агента"],"ar":["مهارات الوكيل","find-skills","نظام بيئي لمهارات الوكيل","اكتشف مهارات","ثبت مهارات","وسع إمكانيات","أدوات الوكيل","رسومات الوكيل","كفاءة الوكيل"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for curious AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code seeking to expand their capabilities through discoverable and installable skills","zh":"適合像Cursor、Windsurf或Claude Code等好奇的AI代理，尋求通過可發現和可安裝的技能來擴展其功能的代理","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、またはClaude Codeのような好奇心旺盛なAIエージェントに適しており、新しい機能を拡張するために検出可能でインストール可能なスキルを探すエージェントに適している","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf 또는 Claude Code와 같은 호기심이 많은 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 검색 가능하고 설치 가능한 기능을 통해 기능을 확장하려는 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA curiosos como Cursor, Windsurf o Claude Code que buscan expandir sus capacidades a través de habilidades descubribles e instalables","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de l''IA curieux comme Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code cherchant à étendre leurs capacités grâce à des compétences découvrables et installables","de":"Ideal für neugierige KI-Agenten wie Cursor, Windsurf oder Claude Code, die ihre Fähigkeiten durch entdeckbare und installierbare Fähigkeiten erweitern möchten","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA curiosos como Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code que buscam expandir suas capacidades por meio de habilidades descobríveis e instaláveis","ru":"Идеально для любопытных агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf или Claude Code, стремящихся расширить свои возможности посредством обнаруживаемых и устанавливаемых навыков","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المحبين للتعلم مثل Cursor و Windsurf أو Claude Code الذين يبحثون عن توسيع قدراتهم من خلال مهارات يمكن اكتشافها وتثبيتها"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to search and install new skills from the open agent skills ecosystem, leveraging keywords, task-based queries, and capability-driven searches, all while utilizing natural language processing to understand user requests for functionality like ''how do I do X'' or ''find a skill for X''","zh":"啟用代理搜索和安裝新的技能從開放代理技能生態系統，利用關鍵詞、基於任務的查詢和基於能力的搜索，同時利用自然語言處理來理解用戶對功能的請求，例如''我如何做X''或''為X找到一個技能''","ja":"エージェントがオープンエージェントスキルエコシステムから新しいスキルを検索してインストールできるようにし、キーワード、タスクベースのクエリ、能力駆動の検索を活用し、同時に自然言語処理を使用してユーザーの機能に対するリクエストを理解する、たとえば''Xをする方法は？''または''X用のスキルを見つけてください''","ko":"에이전트가 오픈 에이전트 스킬 생태계에서 새로운 스킬을 검색하고 설치할 수 있도록 하며, 키워드, 작업 기반 쿼리 및 능력 기반 검색을 활용하고,同時に 자연어 처리를 사용하여 사용자의 기능에 대한 요청을 이해합니다. 예를 들어 ''X를 어떻게 합니까?'' 또는 ''X를 위한 스킬을 찾으십시오''","es":"Habilita a los agentes a buscar e instalar nuevas habilidades desde el ecosistema de habilidades de agentes abiertas, aprovechando palabras clave, consultas basadas en tareas y búsquedas impulsadas por capacidades, todo mientras utiliza el procesamiento de lenguaje natural para comprender las solicitudes de los usuarios para funcionalidades como ''¿cómo hago X'' o ''encuentra una habilidad para X''","fr":"Permet aux agents de rechercher et d''installer de nouvelles compétences à partir de l''écosystème de compétences d''agents ouvert, en exploitant les mots-clés, les requêtes basées sur les tâches et les recherches axées sur les capacités, le tout en utilisant le traitement automatique des langues pour comprendre les demandes des utilisateurs pour des fonctionnalités comme ''comment faire X'' ou ''trouver une compétence pour X''","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, neue Fähigkeiten aus dem offenen Agenten-Fähigkeits-Ökosystem zu suchen und zu installieren, indem es Schlüsselwörter, aufgabenbasierte Abfragen und fähigkeitsgetriebene Suchanfragen nutzt, und zwar unter Verwendung der natürlichen Sprachverarbeitung, um Benutzeranfragen für Funktionalitäten wie ''wie mache ich X'' oder ''finde eine Fähigkeit für X'' zu verstehen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a pesquisar e instalar novas habilidades do ecossistema de habilidades de agentes abertos, utilizando palavras-chave, consultas baseadas em tarefas e pesquisas orientadas por capacidades, tudo isso utilizando o processamento de linguagem natural para entender as solicitações do usuário para funcionalidades como ''como faço X'' ou ''encontre uma habilidade para X''","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью искать и устанавливать новые навыки из открытого экосистемы навыков агентов, используя ключевые слова, запросы на основе задач и возможности поиска, все это при использовании обработки естественного языка для понимания запросов пользователей для функциональности типа ''как я делаю X'' или ''найдите навык для X''","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من البحث وتثبيت مهارات جديدة من نظام البيئة المفتوح للوكلاء، باستخدام الكلمات الرئيسية والاستفسارات القائمة على المهام والبحث الموجه بالقدرات، وكل ذلك باستخدام معالجة اللغة الطبيعية لفهم طلبات المستخدم لتوظيف مثل ''كيف أفعل X'' أو ''ابحث عن مهارة لـ X''"},"useCases":{"en":["Discovering skills for specialized tasks through natural language queries","Installing new skills based on user requests for extended capabilities","Searching the open agent skills ecosystem for tools, templates, or workflows"],"zh":["通过自然语言查询發現專門任務的技能","基於用戶請求安裝新的技能以擴展功能","搜索開放代理技能生態系統中的工具、模板或工作流"],"ja":["自然言語クエリを使用して専門タスクのスキルを発見する","ユーザーのリクエストに基づいて新しいスキルをインストールして機能を拡張する","オープンエージェントスキルエコシステム内のツール、テンプレート、またはワークフローを検索する"],"ko":["자연어 질의를 통해 전문 작업의 스킬을 발견하는こと","사용자의 요청에 따라 새로운 스킬을 설치하여 기능을 확장하는 것","오픈 에이전트 스킬 생태계 내의 도구, 템플릿 또는 워크플로우를 검색하는こと"],"es":["Descubrir habilidades para tareas especializadas a través de consultas de lenguaje natural","Instalar nuevas habilidades en función de las solicitudes de los usuarios para capacidades extendidas","Buscar en el ecosistema de habilidades de agentes abiertas herramientas, plantillas o flujos de trabajo"],"fr":["Découvrir des compétences pour des tâches spécialisées via des requêtes en langage naturel","Installer de nouvelles compétences en fonction des demandes des utilisateurs pour des capacités étendues","Rechercher dans l''écosystème de compétences d''agents ouvert des outils, des modèles ou des flux de travail"],"de":["Entdecken von Fähigkeiten für spezialisierte Aufgaben durch natürliche Sprachabfragen","Installieren neuer Fähigkeiten basierend auf den Anfragen der Benutzer für erweiterte Fähigkeiten","Suchen im offenen Agenten-Fähigkeits-Ökosystem nach Tools, Vorlagen oder Workflows"],"pt":["Descobrir habilidades para tarefas especializadas por meio de consultas de linguagem natural","Instalar novas habilidades com base em solicitações de usuários para capacidades estendidas","Pesquisar o ecossistema de habilidades de agentes abertos por ferramentas, modelos ou fluxos de trabalho"],"ru":["Обнаружение навыков для специализированных задач посредством запросов естественного языка","Установка новых навыков на основе запросов пользователей для расширенных возможностей","Поиск в открытой экосистеме навыков агентов по инструментам, шаблонам или рабочим процессам"],"ar":["اكتشاف المهارات لمهام متخصصة من خلال استفسارات لغة طبيعية","تثبيت مهارات جديدة بناءً على طلبات المستخدمين لقدرات موسعة","البحث في نظام البيئة المفتوح للوكلاء عن أدوات أو قوالب أو تدفقات عمل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to the open agent skills ecosystem","Dependent on user''s ability to articulate needs through specific queries or requests"],"zh":["需要訪問開放代理技能生態系統","依賴用戶通過具體查詢或請求來闡明其需求"],"ja":["オープンエージェントスキルエコシステムへのアクセスが必要","ユーザーのニーズを特定のクエリまたはリクエストを通じて明確にする能力に依存する"],"ko":["오픈 에이전트 스킬 생태계에 대한 액세스가 필요함","사용자가 구체적인 쿼리 또는 요청을 통해 자신의需求을 설명하는 능력에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso al ecosistema de habilidades de agentes abiertas","Depende de la capacidad del usuario para articular necesidades a través de consultas o solicitudes específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''écosystème de compétences d''agents ouvert","Dépend de la capacité de l''utilisateur à formuler des besoins à travers des requêtes ou des demandes spécifiques"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf das offene Agenten-Fähigkeits-Ökosystem","Hängt von der Fähigkeit des Benutzers ab, Bedürfnisse durch spezifische Abfragen oder Anfragen zu artikulieren"],"pt":["Exige acesso ao ecossistema de habilidades de agentes abertos","Depende da capacidade do usuário de articular necessidades por meio de consultas ou solicitações específicas"],"ru":["Требует доступа к открытой экосистеме навыков агентов","Зависит от способности пользователя формулировать потребности посредством конкретных запросов или просьб"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى نظام البيئة المفتوح للوكلاء","يعتمد على قدرة المستخدم على صياغة الاحتياجات من خلال استفسارات أو طلبات محددة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"54b44dc9539df865fbb060f62fb062e8232e765852a0cf14c38301fe0c1eb264","repoEtag":"W/\"b07ea64c9777634c78ab67a865c1986211205b14682e11f92295ed3e43ad5876\"","qualityScore":100}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/brainstorming', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'brainstorming', 55427, 4195, 60, '2026-02-20T02:00:37Z', '2026-02-20T02:04:23.055Z', '7a238df1ebf0656c1da199aafafcc78c42f47bf4e56dd4e007a67afbb10af455', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/brainstorming","name":"brainstorming","description":{"zh":"脑力激荡技能帮助您将想法转化为全面的设计和规格，通过自然的协作对话实现","ja":"ブレーンストーミングスキルは、アイデアを完全な設計と仕様に変換するのに役立ちます","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬은 아이디어를 완전한 디자인과 사양으로 변환하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El brainstorming es una técnica para desarrollar ideas en diseños y especificaciones. Ayuda a entender el contexto del proyecto y a refinar las ideas a través del diálogo.","fr":"Le brainstorming est une technique pour développer des idées en conceptions et spécifications. Il aide à comprendre le contexte du projet et à affiner les idées via le dialogue.","de":"Das Brainstorming ist eine Technik, um Ideen in Designs und Spezifikationen zu entwickeln. Es hilft, den Projektinhalt zu verstehen und die Ideen durch das Gespräch zu verfeinern.","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica de criação de designs e especificações através do diálogo colaborativo natural","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это техника создания дизайнов и спецификаций через естественный коллаборативный диалог","ar":"تمطر الأفكار هو تقنية لإنشاء التصاميم و المواصفات من خلال الحوار التعاوني الطبيعي","en":"You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requirements and design before implementation."},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55427,"forks":4195,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T02:00:37Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"brainstorming","description":"You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requirements and design before implementation.","bodyPreview":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design and get user approval.\n\n<HARD-GATE>\nDo NOT invoke any implementation skill, write any code, scaffold any project, or take any implementation action until you have presented a design and the us","body":"# Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs\n\n## Overview\n\nHelp turn ideas into fully formed designs and specs through natural collaborative dialogue.\n\nStart by understanding the current project context, then ask questions one at a time to refine the idea. Once you understand what you''re building, present the design and get user approval.\n\n<HARD-GATE>\nDo NOT invoke any implementation skill, write any code, scaffold any project, or take any implementation action until you have presented a design and the user has approved it. This applies to EVERY project regardless of perceived simplicity.\n</HARD-GATE>\n\n## Anti-Pattern: \"This Is Too Simple To Need A Design\"\n\nEvery project goes through this process. A todo list, a single-function utility, a config change — all of them. \"Simple\" projects are where unexamined assumptions cause the most wasted work. The design can be short (a few sentences for truly simple projects), but you MUST present it and get approval.\n\n## Checklist\n\nYou MUST create a task for each of these items and complete them in order:\n\n1. **Explore project context** — check files, docs, recent commits\n2. **Ask clarifying questions** — one at a time, understand purpose/constraints/success criteria\n3. **Propose 2-3 approaches** — with trade-offs and your recommendation\n4. **Present design** — in sections scaled to their complexity, get user approval after each section\n5. **Write design doc** — save to `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md` and commit\n6. **Transition to implementation** — invoke writing-plans skill to create implementation plan\n\n## Process Flow\n\n```dot\ndigraph brainstorming {\n    \"Explore project context\" [shape=box];\n    \"Ask clarifying questions\" [shape=box];\n    \"Propose 2-3 approaches\" [shape=box];\n    \"Present design sections\" [shape=box];\n    \"User approves design?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Write design doc\" [shape=box];\n    \"Invoke writing-plans skill\" [shape=doublecircle];\n\n    \"Explore project context\" -> \"Ask clarifying questions\";\n    \"Ask clarifying questions\" -> \"Propose 2-3 approaches\";\n    \"Propose 2-3 approaches\" -> \"Present design sections\";\n    \"Present design sections\" -> \"User approves design?\";\n    \"User approves design?\" -> \"Present design sections\" [label=\"no, revise\"];\n    \"User approves design?\" -> \"Write design doc\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Write design doc\" -> \"Invoke writing-plans skill\";\n}\n```\n\n**The terminal state is invoking writing-plans.** Do NOT invoke frontend-design, mcp-builder, or any other implementation skill. The ONLY skill you invoke after brainstorming is writing-plans.\n\n## The Process\n\n**Understanding the idea:**\n- Check out the current project state first (files, docs, recent commits)\n- Ask questions one at a time to refine the idea\n- Prefer multiple choice questions when possible, but open-ended is fine too\n- Only one question per message - if a topic needs more exploration, break it into multiple questions\n- Focus on understanding: purpose, constraints, success criteria\n\n**Exploring approaches:**\n- Propose 2-3 different approaches with trade-offs\n- Present options conversationally with your recommendation and reasoning\n- Lead with your recommended option and explain why\n\n**Presenting the design:**\n- Once you believe you understand what you''re building, present the design\n- Scale each section to its complexity: a few sentences if straightforward, up to 200-300 words if nuanced\n- Ask after each section whether it looks right so far\n- Cover: architecture, components, data flow, error handling, testing\n- Be ready to go back and clarify if something doesn''t make sense\n\n## After the Design\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Write the validated design to `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md`\n- Use elements-of-style:writing-clearly-and-concisely skill if available\n- Commit the design document to git\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Invoke the writing-plans skill to create a detailed implementation plan\n- Do NOT invoke any other skill. writing-plans is the next step.\n\n## Key Principles\n\n- **One question at a time** - Don''t overwhelm with multiple questions\n- **Multiple choice preferred** - Easier to answer than open-ended when possible\n- **YAGNI ruthlessly** - Remove unnecessary features from all designs\n- **Explore alternatives** - Always propose 2-3 approaches before settling\n- **Incremental validation** - Present design, get approval before moving on\n- **Be flexible** - Go back and clarify when something doesn''t make sense\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:04:23.055Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"脑力激荡：将想法转化为设计","ja":"ブレーンストーミング：アイデアを設計に","ko":"브레인스토밍: 아이디어를 디자인으로","es":"Brainstorming: Desarrolla Ideas en Diseños","fr":"Brainstorming: Développez des Idées en Conceptions","de":"Brainstorming: Entwickeln Sie Ideen in Designs","pt":"Brainstorming: Transforme Ideias em Design","ru":"Мозговой штурм: превращение идей в дизайн","ar":"تمطر الأفكار: تحويل الأفكار إلى تصميم","en":"brainstorming"},"description":{"zh":"脑力激荡技能帮助您将想法转化为全面的设计和规格，通过自然的协作对话实现","ja":"ブレーンストーミングスキルは、アイデアを完全な設計と仕様に変換するのに役立ちます","ko":"브레인스토밍 스킬은 아이디어를 완전한 디자인과 사양으로 변환하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El brainstorming es una técnica para desarrollar ideas en diseños y especificaciones. Ayuda a entender el contexto del proyecto y a refinar las ideas a travé...","fr":"Le brainstorming est une technique pour développer des idées en conceptions et spécifications. Il aide à comprendre le contexte du projet et à affiner les id...","de":"Das Brainstorming ist eine Technik, um Ideen in Designs und Spezifikationen zu entwickeln. Es hilft, den Projektinhalt zu verstehen und die Ideen durch das G...","pt":"O brainstorming é uma técnica de criação de designs e especificações através do diálogo colaborativo natural","ru":"Мозговой штурм - это техника создания дизайнов и спецификаций через естественный коллаборативный диалог","ar":"تمطر الأفكار هو تقنية لإنشاء التصاميم و المواصفات من خلال الحوار التعاوني الطبيعي","en":"You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requi..."},"definition":{"en":"You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requirements and design before implementation."},"features":{"zh":["协作对话","设计和规格生成","自然语言处理","项目背景理解","用户意图分析"],"ja":["コラボレーションディアログ","設計と仕様の生成","自然言語処理","プロジェクトコンテキストの理解","ユーザー意図の分析"],"ko":["협력 대화","디자인 및 사양 생성","자연어 처리","프로젝트 컨텍스트 이해","사용자 의도 분석"],"es":["Desarrollo de ideas en diseños y especificaciones","Diálogo colaborativo para refinar ideas","Comprensión del contexto del proyecto","Presentación de diseños y aprobación del usuario","Iteración y mejora continua"],"fr":["Développement d''idées en conceptions et spécifications","Dialogue collaboratif pour affiner les idées","Compréhension du contexte du projet","Présentation de conceptions et approbation de l''utilisateur","Itération et amélioration continue"],"de":["Entwicklung von Ideen in Designs und Spezifikationen","Kollaboratives Gespräch zur Verfeinerung von Ideen","Verständnis des Projektinhalts","Präsentation von Designs und Benutzerzustimmung","Iteration und kontinuierliche Verbesserung"],"pt":["Criação de designs e especificações","Diálogo colaborativo natural","Refinamento de ideias","Apresentação de designs","Aprovação de usuários"],"ru":["Создание дизайнов и спецификаций","Естественный коллаборативный диалог","Уточнение идей","Представление дизайнов","Одобрение пользователей"],"ar":["إنشاء التصاميم و المواصفات","حوار تعاوني طبيعي","تحسين الأفكار","عرض التصاميم","موافقة المستخدمين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["脑力激荡","设计","开发","协作","自然语言处理","项目管理","用户体验","软件开发"],"ja":["ブレーンストーミング","設計","開発","コラボレーション","自然言語処理","プロジェクトマネジメント","ユーザーエクスペリエンス","ソフトウェア開発"],"ko":["브레인스토밍","디자인","개발","협력","자연어 처리","프로젝트 관리","사용자 경험","소프트웨어 개발"],"es":["brainstorming","desarrollo de ideas","diseño de software","colaboración en equipo","desarrollo de proyectos","innovación tecnológica"],"fr":["brainstorming","développement d''idées","conception de logiciels","collaboration d''équipe","développement de projets","innovation technologique"],"de":["brainstorming","ideenentwicklung","software-design","teamkollaboration","projektentwicklung","technologische innovation"],"pt":["brainstorming","criação de designs","diálogo colaborativo","refinamento de ideias","apresentação de designs","desenvolvimento de software","técnica de design"],"ru":["мозговой штурм","создание дизайнов","коллаборативный диалог","уточнение идей","представление дизайнов","разработка программного обеспечения","техника дизайна"],"ar":["تمطر الأفكار","إنشاء التصاميم","حوار تعاوني","تحسين الأفكار","عرض التصاميم","تطوير البرمجيات","تقنية التصميم"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Creative Agents requiring collaborative design dialogue and natural language processing for project ideation.","zh":"适合需要协作设计对话和自然语言处理来进行项目构想的创意代理","ja":"創造的なエージェントが共同のデザイン対話と自然言語処理をプロジェクトのアイデアを生み出すために必要とする場合に最適","ko":"공동 디자인 대화와 프로젝트 아이디어를 위해 자연어 처리가 필요한 창의적 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes creativos que requieren un diálogo de diseño colaborativo y procesamiento de lenguaje natural para la ideación de proyectos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents créatifs nécessitant un dialogue de conception collaborative et un traitement du langage naturel pour l''idéation de projet.","de":"Ideal für kreative Agenten, die ein kollaboratives Design-Dialog und eine natürliche Sprachverarbeitung für die Projektidee benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Criativos que requerem diálogo de design colaborativo e processamento de linguagem natural para ideias de projeto.","ru":"Идеально для творческих агентов, требующих совместного диалога дизайна и обработки естественного языка для идеи проекта.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الإبداع الذي يتطلب حوار تصميم تعاوني ومعالجة لغة طبيعية لفكرة المشروع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to refine user intent through iterative questioning, presenting fully formed designs and specs for approval, utilizing natural collaborative dialogue and leveraging context understanding to inform the design process.","zh":"赋予代理通过迭代提问来完善用户意图的能力，提出完整的设计和规范供批准，并利用自然的协作对话和上下文理解来指导设计过程","ja":"エージェントに、ユーザーの意図を反復的な質問を通じて洗練し、完全に形成されたデザインと仕様を承認のために提示し、自然な共同の対話を利用してコンテキストの理解を設計プロセスに役立てることを可能にする","ko":"에이전트가 반복적인 질문을 통해 사용자의 의도를 정제하고 완전히 형성된 디자인과 사양을 승인하기 위해 제시하며 자연적인 협업 대화를 활용하여 컨텍스트 이해를 디자인 프로세스에 활용할 수 있도록 한다","es":"Permite a los agentes perfeccionar la intención del usuario a través de preguntas iterativas, presentando diseños y especificaciones completamente formados para su aprobación, utilizando un diálogo colaborativo natural y aprovechando la comprensión del contexto para informar el proceso de diseño.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''affiner l''intention de l''utilisateur à travers des questions itératives, en présentant des conceptions et des spécifications entièrement formées pour approbation, en utilisant un dialogue collaboratif naturel et en exploitant la compréhension du contexte pour éclairer le processus de conception.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Benutzerabsicht durch iterative Fragen zu verfeinern, präsentiert vollständig ausgebildete Designs und Spezifikationen für die Genehmigung, unter Verwendung natürlicher kollaborativer Dialoge und Nutzung des Kontextverständnisses, um den Designprozess zu informieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a refinar a intenção do usuário por meio de questionamento iterativo, apresentando designs e especificações totalmente formados para aprovação, utilizando diálogo colaborativo natural e aproveitando a compreensão do contexto para informar o processo de design.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью усовершенствовать намерения пользователя путем итеративного вопроса, представляя полностью сформированные конструкции и характеристики для одобрения, используя естественный совместный диалог и используя понимание контекста для информирования процесса проектирования.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تحسين نية المستخدم من خلال الاستجواب المتكرر، وطرح التصاميم والمواصفات المكتملة بشكل كامل للموافقة، باستخدام الحوار التعاوني الطبيعي وتسخير فهم السياق لإبلاغ عملية التصميم."},"useCases":{"en":["Refining project requirements through iterative questioning","Generating fully formed design specs for user approval","Exploring user intent and project context before implementation"],"zh":["通过迭代提问来完善项目需求","生成供用户批准的完整设计规范","在实施之前探索用户意图和项目上下文"],"ja":["反復的な質問を通じてプロジェクトの要件を洗練する","ユーザーの承認のために完全に形成されたデザイン仕様を生成する","実装前にユーザーの意図とプロジェクトのコンテキストを探索する"],"ko":["반복적인 질문을 통해 프로젝트 요구 사항을 정제","사용자 승인에 대한 완전히 형성된 디자인 사양 생성","구현 전에 사용자 의도 및 프로젝트 컨텍스트 탐색"],"es":["Refinar los requisitos del proyecto a través de preguntas iterativas","Generar especificaciones de diseño completamente formadas para la aprobación del usuario","Explorar la intención del usuario y el contexto del proyecto antes de la implementación"],"fr":["Affiner les exigences du projet à travers des questions itératives","Générer des spécifications de conception entièrement formées pour l''approbation de l''utilisateur","Explorer l''intention de l''utilisateur et le contexte du projet avant la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Die Projektanforderungen durch iterative Fragen verfeinern","Vollständig ausgebildete Designspezifikationen für die Benutzerfreigabe generieren","Die Benutzerabsicht und den Projektzusammenhang vor der Implementierung erkunden"],"pt":["Refinamento dos requisitos do projeto por meio de questionamento iterativo","Geração de especificações de design totalmente formadas para aprovação do usuário","Exploração da intenção do usuário e do contexto do projeto antes da implementação"],"ru":["Уточнение требований проекта путем итеративного вопроса","Генерация полностью сформированных технических характеристик конструкции для одобрения пользователя","Изучение намерений пользователя и контекста проекта до реализации"],"ar":["تحسين متطلبات المشروع من خلال الاستجواب المتكرر","توليد مواصفات التصميم المكتملة بشكل كامل للموافقة المستخدم","استكشاف نية المستخدم وسياق المشروع قبل التنفيذ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires explicit user approval before proceeding to implementation","Does not invoke implementation skills or write code"],"zh":["需要用户明确批准后才能继续实施","不调用实施技能或编写代码"],"ja":["実装を続行する前にユーザーの明示的な承認が必要","実装スキルを呼び出さず、コードを記述しない"],"ko":["구현을 계속하기 전에 사용자의 명시적인 승인을 필요로 함","구현 기술을 호출하지 않으며 코드를 작성하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere una aprobación explícita del usuario antes de proceder a la implementación","No invoca habilidades de implementación ni escribe código"],"fr":["Nécessite une approbation explicite de l''utilisateur avant de procéder à la mise en œuvre","Ne pas invoquer les compétences de mise en œuvre ou écrire du code"],"de":["Benötigt eine explizite Benutzerfreigabe, bevor es zur Implementierung fortschreitet","Ruft keine Implementierungsfähigkeiten auf und schreibt keinen Code"],"pt":["Exige aprovação explícita do usuário antes de proceder à implementação","Não invoca habilidades de implementação ou escreve código"],"ru":["Требует явного одобрения пользователя до перехода к реализации","Не вызывает навыки реализации или пишет код"],"ar":["يتطلب موافقة مستخدم صريحة قبل المضي في التنفيذ","لا يستدعي مهارات التنفيذ أو يكتب الشفرة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"7a238df1ebf0656c1da199aafafcc78c42f47bf4e56dd4e007a67afbb10af455","repoEtag":"W/\"29bf55250b8f240dcbe9ab5b26295b46f9245d08f7c3ef5107c7cf22c3e2ed5f\"","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/dispatching-parallel-agents', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'dispatching-parallel-agents', 55427, 4195, 90, '2026-02-20T02:00:37Z', '2026-02-20T02:05:27.276Z', 'c628917689ccc12ce9991615db6824d44c4fe71f8427cd959560aebe6a1a6476', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/dispatching-parallel-agents","name":"dispatching-parallel-agents","description":{"zh":"并行代理调度是一种高效的任务处理技术，适用于多个独立任务","ja":"並列エージェントのdispatchは、複数の独立したタスクを効率的に処理する技術です","ko":"병렬 에이전트 디스패치는 다중 독립 태스크를 효율적으로 처리하는 기술입니다","es":"Los agentes paralelos permiten trabajar en tareas independientes de manera concurrente, ahorrando tiempo","fr":"Les agents parallèles permettent de travailler sur des tâches indépendantes de manière concurrente, ce qui permet de gagner du temps","de":"Parallele Agenten ermöglichen die Bearbeitung unabhängiger Aufgaben gleichzeitig, was Zeit spart","pt":"O dispatching de agentes paralelos é uma técnica para trabalhar em tarefas independentes sem estado compartilhado ou dependências sequenciais","ru":"Диспетчеризация параллельных агентов - это техника для работы над независимыми задачами без общего состояния или последовательных зависимостей","ar":"توجيه وكلاء متوازي هو تقنية للعمل على المهام المستقلة بدون حالة مشتركة أو зависимости متسلسلة","en":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55427,"forks":4195,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T02:00:37Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"dispatching-parallel-agents","description":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies","bodyPreview":"# Dispatching Parallel Agents\n\n## Overview\n\nWhen you have multiple unrelated failures (different test files, different subsystems, different bugs), investigating them sequentially wastes time. Each investigation is independent and can happen in parallel.\n\n**Core principle:** Dispatch one agent per independent problem domain. Let them work concurrently.\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Multiple failures?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Are they independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Single","body":"# Dispatching Parallel Agents\n\n## Overview\n\nWhen you have multiple unrelated failures (different test files, different subsystems, different bugs), investigating them sequentially wastes time. Each investigation is independent and can happen in parallel.\n\n**Core principle:** Dispatch one agent per independent problem domain. Let them work concurrently.\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Multiple failures?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Are they independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Single agent investigates all\" [shape=box];\n    \"One agent per problem domain\" [shape=box];\n    \"Can they work in parallel?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Sequential agents\" [shape=box];\n    \"Parallel dispatch\" [shape=box];\n\n    \"Multiple failures?\" -> \"Are they independent?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Are they independent?\" -> \"Single agent investigates all\" [label=\"no - related\"];\n    \"Are they independent?\" -> \"Can they work in parallel?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Can they work in parallel?\" -> \"Parallel dispatch\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Can they work in parallel?\" -> \"Sequential agents\" [label=\"no - shared state\"];\n}\n```\n\n**Use when:**\n- 3+ test files failing with different root causes\n- Multiple subsystems broken independently\n- Each problem can be understood without context from others\n- No shared state between investigations\n\n**Don''t use when:**\n- Failures are related (fix one might fix others)\n- Need to understand full system state\n- Agents would interfere with each other\n\n## The Pattern\n\n### 1. Identify Independent Domains\n\nGroup failures by what''s broken:\n- File A tests: Tool approval flow\n- File B tests: Batch completion behavior\n- File C tests: Abort functionality\n\nEach domain is independent - fixing tool approval doesn''t affect abort tests.\n\n### 2. Create Focused Agent Tasks\n\nEach agent gets:\n- **Specific scope:** One test file or subsystem\n- **Clear goal:** Make these tests pass\n- **Constraints:** Don''t change other code\n- **Expected output:** Summary of what you found and fixed\n\n### 3. Dispatch in Parallel\n\n```typescript\n// In Claude Code / AI environment\nTask(\"Fix agent-tool-abort.test.ts failures\")\nTask(\"Fix batch-completion-behavior.test.ts failures\")\nTask(\"Fix tool-approval-race-conditions.test.ts failures\")\n// All three run concurrently\n```\n\n### 4. Review and Integrate\n\nWhen agents return:\n- Read each summary\n- Verify fixes don''t conflict\n- Run full test suite\n- Integrate all changes\n\n## Agent Prompt Structure\n\nGood agent prompts are:\n1. **Focused** - One clear problem domain\n2. **Self-contained** - All context needed to understand the problem\n3. **Specific about output** - What should the agent return?\n\n```markdown\nFix the 3 failing tests in src/agents/agent-tool-abort.test.ts:\n\n1. \"should abort tool with partial output capture\" - expects ''interrupted at'' in message\n2. \"should handle mixed completed and aborted tools\" - fast tool aborted instead of completed\n3. \"should properly track pendingToolCount\" - expects 3 results but gets 0\n\nThese are timing/race condition issues. Your task:\n\n1. Read the test file and understand what each test verifies\n2. Identify root cause - timing issues or actual bugs?\n3. Fix by:\n   - Replacing arbitrary timeouts with event-based waiting\n   - Fixing bugs in abort implementation if found\n   - Adjusting test expectations if testing changed behavior\n\nDo NOT just increase timeouts - find the real issue.\n\nReturn: Summary of what you found and what you fixed.\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**❌ Too broad:** \"Fix all the tests\" - agent gets lost\n**✅ Specific:** \"Fix agent-tool-abort.test.ts\" - focused scope\n\n**❌ No context:** \"Fix the race condition\" - agent doesn''t know where\n**✅ Context:** Paste the error messages and test names\n\n**❌ No constraints:** Agent might refactor everything\n**✅ Constraints:** \"Do NOT change production code\" or \"Fix tests only\"\n\n**❌ Vague output:** \"Fix it\" - you don''t know what changed\n**✅ Specific:** \"Return summary of root cause and changes\"\n\n## When NOT to Use\n\n**Related failures:** Fixing one might fix others - investigate together first\n**Need full context:** Understanding requires seeing entire system\n**Exploratory debugging:** You don''t know what''s broken yet\n**Shared state:** Agents would interfere (editing same files, using same resources)\n\n## Real Example from Session\n\n**Scenario:** 6 test failures across 3 files after major refactoring\n\n**Failures:**\n- agent-tool-abort.test.ts: 3 failures (timing issues)\n- batch-completion-behavior.test.ts: 2 failures (tools not executing)\n- tool-approval-race-conditions.test.ts: 1 failure (execution count = 0)\n\n**Decision:** Independent domains - abort logic separate from batch completion separate from race conditions\n\n**Dispatch:**\n```\nAgent 1 → Fix agent-tool-abort.test.ts\nAgent 2 → Fix batch-completion-behavior.test.ts\nAgent 3 → Fix tool-approval-race-conditions.test.ts\n```\n\n**Results:**\n- Agent 1: Replaced timeouts with event-based waiting\n- Agent 2: Fixed event structure bug (threadId in wrong place)\n- Agent 3: Added wait for async tool execution to complete\n\n**Integration:** All fixes independent, no conflicts, full suite green\n\n**Time saved:** 3 problems solved in parallel vs sequentially\n\n## Key Benefits\n\n1. **Parallelization** - Multiple investigations happen simultaneously\n2. **Focus** - Each agent has narrow scope, less context to track\n3. **Independence** - Agents don''t interfere with each other\n4. **Speed** - 3 problems solved in time of 1\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter agents return:\n1. **Review each summary** - Understand what changed\n2. **Check for conflicts** - Did agents edit same code?\n3. **Run full suite** - Verify all fixes work together\n4. **Spot check** - Agents can make systematic errors\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging session (2025-10-03):\n- 6 failures across 3 files\n- 3 agents dispatched in parallel\n- All investigations completed concurrently\n- All fixes integrated successfully\n- Zero conflicts between agent changes\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:05:27.276Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"并行代理调度技术","ja":"並列エージェントの.dispatch","ko":"병렬 에이전트 디스패치","es":"Agentes Paralelos: Mejora la Eficiencia","fr":"Agents Parallèles: Améliorez l''Efficacité","de":"Parallele Agenten: Effizienz Steigern","pt":"Dispatching de Agentes Paralelos","ru":"Диспетчер параллельных агентов","ar":"توجيه وكلاء متوازي","en":"dispatching-parallel-agents"},"description":{"zh":"并行代理调度是一种高效的任务处理技术，适用于多个独立任务","ja":"並列エージェントのdispatchは、複数の独立したタスクを効率的に処理する技術です","ko":"병렬 에이전트 디스패치는 다중 독립 태스크를 효율적으로 처리하는 기술입니다","es":"Los agentes paralelos permiten trabajar en tareas independientes de manera concurrente, ahorrando tiempo","fr":"Les agents parallèles permettent de travailler sur des tâches indépendantes de manière concurrente, ce qui permet de gagner du temps","de":"Parallele Agenten ermöglichen die Bearbeitung unabhängiger Aufgaben gleichzeitig, was Zeit spart","pt":"O dispatching de agentes paralelos é uma técnica para trabalhar em tarefas independentes sem estado compartilhado ou dependências sequenciais","ru":"Диспетчеризация параллельных агентов - это техника для работы над независимыми задачами без общего состояния или последовательных зависимостей","ar":"توجيه وكلاء متوازي هو تقنية للعمل على المهام المستقلة بدون حالة مشتركة أو зависимости متسلسلة","en":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies"},"definition":{"en":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies"},"features":{"zh":["提高多任务处理效率","减少时间浪费","适用于多个独立任务","并行处理多个任务","提高系统吞吐量"],"ja":["複数タスクの処理を効率化","時間の浪費を減らす","複数の独立したタスクに適する","並列に複数のタスクを処理","システムのスループットを向上"],"ko":["다중 태스크 처리 효율성을 높임","시간浪費를 줄임","다중 독립 태스크에 적합","병렬로 다중 태스크를 처리","시스템의 처리량을 향상"],"es":["Trabajar en tareas independientes","Mejora la eficiencia","Reduce el tiempo de investigación","Permite la ejecución concurrente","Se utiliza en entornos de prueba","Optimiza el uso de recursos"],"fr":["Travailler sur des tâches indépendantes","Améliore l''efficacité","Réduit le temps d''investigation","Permet l''exécution concurrente","Est utilisé dans les environnements de test","Optimise l''utilisation des ressources"],"de":["Arbeiten an unabhängigen Aufgaben","Verbesserung der Effizienz","Reduziert die Untersuchungszeit","Ermöglicht die gleichzeitige Ausführung","Wird in Testumgebungen verwendet","Optimiert den Ressourceneinsatz"],"pt":["Trabalho em tarefas independentes","Sem estado compartilhado ou dependências sequenciais","Investigação paralela para múltiplas falhas","Otimização do tempo de investigação","Aumento da produtividade"],"ru":["Работа над независимыми задачами","Без общего состояния или последовательных зависимостей","Параллельное расследование для нескольких неисправностей","Оптимизация времени расследования","Повышение производительности"],"ar":["العمل على المهام المستقلة","بدون حالة مشتركة أو зависимости متسلسلة","التحقيق المتوازي لمشاكل متعددة","تحسين وقت التحقيق","زيادة الإنتاجية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["并行代理调度","多任务处理","任务处理效率","独立任务","并行处理"],"ja":["並列エージェントのdispatch","複数タスクの処理","タスク処理の効率化","独立したタスク","並列処理"],"ko":["병렬 에이전트 디스패치","다중 태스크 처리","태스크 처리 효율성","독립 태스크","병렬 처리"],"es":["agentes paralelos","tareas independientes","eficiencia","concurrente","investigación","pruebas","recursos","optimización"],"fr":["agents parallèles","tâches indépendantes","efficacité","concurrent","investigation","tests","ressources","optimisation"],"de":["parallele Agenten","unabhängige Aufgaben","Effizienz","gleichzeitig","Untersuchung","Tests","Ressourcen","Optimierung"],"pt":["dispatching de agentes paralelos","tarefas independentes","trabalho concorrente","investigação paralela","otimização do tempo","produtividade","desenvolvimento de software","técnica de programação"],"ru":["диспетчеризация параллельных агентов","независимые задачи","параллельная работа","параллельное расследование","оптимизация времени","производительность","разработка программного обеспечения","техника программирования"],"ar":["توجيه وكلاء متوازي","مهام مستقلة","عمل متوازي","تحقيق متوازي","تحسين الوقت","إنتاجية","تطوير البرمجيات","تقنية البرمجة"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Multi-Tasking Agents needing concurrent execution of independent tasks without shared state or sequential dependencies","zh":"适用于需要同时执行独立任务且无共享状态或顺序依赖的多任务代理","ja":"独立したタスクを同時に実行し、共有状態や順序依存関係がないマルチタスクエージェントに最適","ko":"공유 상태나 순차적 종속성 없이 독립적인 작업을 동시에 실행해야 하는 다중 작업 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de multitarea que necesitan ejecución concurrente de tareas independientes sin estado compartido o dependencias secuenciales","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de multitâche nécessitant une exécution concurrente de tâches indépendantes sans état partagé ou dépendances séquentielles","de":"Ideal für Multi-Tasking-Agents, die eine gleichzeitige Ausführung unabhängiger Aufgaben ohne gemeinsamen Zustand oder sequenzielle Abhängigkeiten benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Multi-Tarefa que necessitam de execução concorrente de tarefas independentes sem estado compartilhado ou dependências sequenciais","ru":"Идеально для Мультизадачных Агентов, требующих параллельного выполнения независимых задач без общего состояния или последовательных зависимостей","ar":"مثالي لعميل متعدد المهام الذي يحتاج إلى تنفيذ متزامن لمهام مستقلة بدون حالة مشتركة أو зависимости متسلسلة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to dispatch parallel tasks using independent problem domains, leveraging core principles of concurrent execution and enabling them to work on multiple unrelated failures simultaneously, such as investigating different test files, subsystems, or bugs, utilizing dot graph analysis for decision-making","zh":"使代理能够使用独立的问题域派发并行任务，利用并发执行的核心原理，使其能够同时处理多个无关的故障，如调查不同的测试文件、子系统或错误，利用点图分析进行决策","ja":"エージェントが独立した問題ドメインを使用して並列タスクを送信できるようにし、並行実行の基本原則を利用して、異なるテストファイル、サブシステム、またはバグなどの複数の無関係な障害を同時に処理できるようにし、ドットグラフ分析を使用した意思決定を可能にします","ko":"에이전트가 독립된 문제 도메인을 사용하여 병렬 작업을.dispatch 할 수 있도록 하여, 동시 실행의 핵심 원리를 활용하여, 서로 다른 테스트 파일, 서브시스템 또는 버그와 같은 여러 개의 관련이 없는 오류를 동시에 처리할 수 있도록 하며, 점 그래프 분석을 사용한 의사 결정","es":"Habilita a los agentes a enviar tareas paralelas utilizando dominios de problemas independientes, aprovechando los principios básicos de la ejecución concurrente y permitiéndoles trabajar en múltiples fallos no relacionados simultáneamente, como investigar diferentes archivos de prueba, subsistemas o errores, utilizando el análisis de gráficos de puntos para la toma de decisiones","fr":"Permet aux agents d''envoyer des tâches parallèles en utilisant des domaines de problèmes indépendants, en exploitant les principes fondamentaux de l''exécution concurrente et en leur permettant de travailler sur plusieurs défaillances non liées simultanément, comme investiguer différents fichiers de test, sous-systèmes ou bogues, en utilisant l''analyse de graphiques de points pour la prise de décision","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, parallele Aufgaben mithilfe unabhängiger Problemdomänen zu versenden, die Kernprinzipien der gleichzeitigen Ausführung nutzt und es ihnen ermöglicht, an mehreren nicht verwandten Fehlern gleichzeitig zu arbeiten, wie z. B. die Untersuchung verschiedener Testdateien, Subsysteme oder Fehler, unter Verwendung der Punktdiagrammanalyse für die Entscheidungsfindung","pt":"Habilita os agentes a despachar tarefas paralelas usando domínios de problemas independentes, aproveitando princípios básicos de execução concorrente e permitindo que eles trabalhem em várias falhas não relacionadas simultaneamente, como investigar diferentes arquivos de teste, subsistemas ou bugs, utilizando análise de gráficos de pontos para tomada de decisões","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью отправлять параллельные задачи, используя независимые области задач, используя основные принципы параллельного выполнения и позволяя им работать над несколькими несвязанными сбоями одновременно, такие как расследование различных тестовых файлов, подсистем или ошибок, используя анализ графика точек для принятия решений","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إرسال مهام متوازية باستخدام مجالات مشكلات مستقلة، وتحقيق المبادئ الأساسية للتنفيذ المتزامن، وتمكنهم من العمل على عدة فشل غير مرتبط في نفس الوقت، مثل التحقيق في ملفات اختبار مختلفة، أو أنظمة فرعية أو أخطاء، باستخدام تحليل الرسم البياني للنقاط لاتخاذ القرارات"},"useCases":{"en":["Investigating multiple unrelated failures in parallel","Concurrently executing independent tasks without shared state","Optimizing task execution by avoiding sequential dependencies"],"zh":["并行调查多个无关的故障","同时执行独立任务且无共享状态","通过避免顺序依赖关系优化任务执行"],"ja":["無関係な複数の障害を並行して調査する","共有状態がない独立したタスクを同時に実行する","順序依存関係を回避してタスクの実行を最適化する"],"ko":["관련이 없는 여러 개의 오류를 동시에 조사","공유 상태가 없는 독립적인 작업을 동시에 실행","순차적 종속성을 피하여 작업 실행을 최적화"],"es":["Investigar múltiples fallos no relacionados en paralelo","Ejecutar tareas independientes de forma concurrente sin estado compartido","Optimizar la ejecución de tareas evitando dependencias secuenciales"],"fr":["Investiguer plusieurs défaillances non liées en parallèle","Exécuter des tâches indépendantes de manière concurrente sans état partagé","Optimiser l''exécution des tâches en évitant les dépendances séquentielles"],"de":["Mehrere nicht verwandte Fehler gleichzeitig untersuchen","Unabhängige Aufgaben ohne gemeinsamen Zustand gleichzeitig ausführen","Die Ausführung von Aufgaben optimieren, indem sequenzielle Abhängigkeiten vermieden werden"],"pt":["Investigar várias falhas não relacionadas em paralelo","Executar tarefas independentes concorrentemente sem estado compartilhado","Otimizar a execução de tarefas evitando dependências sequenciais"],"ru":["Расследование нескольких несвязанных сбоев параллельно","Параллельное выполнение независимых задач без общего состояния","Оптимизация выполнения задач, избегая последовательных зависимостей"],"ar":["التحقيق في عدة فشل غير مرتبط في وقت واحد","تنفيذ مهام مستقلة متوازية بدون حالة مشتركة","تحسين تنفيذ المهام بالتخلص من الاعتماد المتسلسل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires independent tasks without shared state or sequential dependencies","No support for tasks with interdependent workflows"],"zh":["需要独立任务且无共享状态或顺序依赖关系","不支持具有相互依存工作流的任务"],"ja":["共有状態や順序依存関係がない独立したタスクが必要","相互に依存するワークフローを持つタスクはサポートされません"],"ko":["공유 상태나 순차적 종속성이 없는 독립적인 작업이 필요","서로 종속된 워크플로를 갖는 작업은 지원되지 않음"],"es":["Requiere tareas independientes sin estado compartido o dependencias secuenciales","No admite tareas con flujos de trabajo interdependientes"],"fr":["Nécessite des tâches indépendantes sans état partagé ou dépendances séquentielles","Ne prend pas en charge les tâches avec des flux de travail interdépendants"],"de":["Benötigt unabhängige Aufgaben ohne gemeinsamen Zustand oder sequenzielle Abhängigkeiten","Unterstützt keine Aufgaben mit interdependenten Workflows"],"pt":["Requer tarefas independentes sem estado compartilhado ou dependências sequenciais","Não suporta tarefas com fluxos de trabalho interdependentes"],"ru":["Требует независимых задач без общего состояния или последовательных зависимостей","Не поддерживает задачи с взаимозависимыми рабочими процессами"],"ar":["يتطلب مهام مستقلة بدون حالة مشتركة أو зависимости متسلسلة","لا يدعم المهام التي لديها سير عمل مت phụ thuộc"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c628917689ccc12ce9991615db6824d44c4fe71f8427cd959560aebe6a1a6476","repoEtag":"W/\"29bf55250b8f240dcbe9ab5b26295b46f9245d08f7c3ef5107c7cf22c3e2ed5f\"","qualityScore":90}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/executing-plans', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'executing-plans', 55427, 4195, 55, '2026-02-20T02:00:37Z', '2026-02-20T02:06:39.409Z', 'd099fa42fd7518f4dafa9f2d51c1c08fce970490d57682b6acd3e7a57bb55b52', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/executing-plans","name":"executing-plans","description":{"zh":"执行计划技能用于批量执行任务并在批次之间进行审查","ja":"実行計画スキルはバッチ実行とレビューを実現する","ko":"실행 계획 스킬은 배치 실행 및 리뷰를 수행","es":"El skill de ejecución de planes permite cargar, revisar y ejecutar tareas en lotes con puntos de revisión","fr":"Le skill d''exécution de plans permet de charger, de réviser et d''exécuter des tâches par lots avec des points de contrôle","de":"Das Skill zum Ausführen von Plänen ermöglicht das Laden, Überprüfen und Ausführen von Aufgaben in Batches mit Überprüfungspunkten","pt":"Executando planos de implementação com revisão crítica e checkpoints para garantir a entrega de qualidade","ru":"Выполнение планов реализации с критической проверкой и контрольными точками для обеспечения высококачественной доставки","ar":"تنفيذ خطط التنفيذ مع المراجعة النقدية والنقاط المرجعية لضمان تسليم عالي الجودة","en":"Use when you have a written implementation plan to execute in a separate session with review checkpoints"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55427,"forks":4195,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T02:00:37Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"executing-plans","description":"Use when you have a written implementation plan to execute in a separate session with review checkpoints","bodyPreview":"# Executing Plans\n\n## Overview\n\nLoad plan, review critically, execute tasks in batches, report for review between batches.\n\n**Core principle:** Batch execution with checkpoints for architect review.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the executing-plans skill to implement this plan.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Load and Review Plan\n1. Read plan file\n2. Review critically - identify any questions or concerns about the plan\n3. If concerns: Raise them with your human partner before starting\n4. If n","body":"# Executing Plans\n\n## Overview\n\nLoad plan, review critically, execute tasks in batches, report for review between batches.\n\n**Core principle:** Batch execution with checkpoints for architect review.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the executing-plans skill to implement this plan.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Load and Review Plan\n1. Read plan file\n2. Review critically - identify any questions or concerns about the plan\n3. If concerns: Raise them with your human partner before starting\n4. If no concerns: Create TodoWrite and proceed\n\n### Step 2: Execute Batch\n**Default: First 3 tasks**\n\nFor each task:\n1. Mark as in_progress\n2. Follow each step exactly (plan has bite-sized steps)\n3. Run verifications as specified\n4. Mark as completed\n\n### Step 3: Report\nWhen batch complete:\n- Show what was implemented\n- Show verification output\n- Say: \"Ready for feedback.\"\n\n### Step 4: Continue\nBased on feedback:\n- Apply changes if needed\n- Execute next batch\n- Repeat until complete\n\n### Step 5: Complete Development\n\nAfter all tasks complete and verified:\n- Announce: \"I''m using the finishing-a-development-branch skill to complete this work.\"\n- **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch\n- Follow that skill to verify tests, present options, execute choice\n\n## When to Stop and Ask for Help\n\n**STOP executing immediately when:**\n- Hit a blocker mid-batch (missing dependency, test fails, instruction unclear)\n- Plan has critical gaps preventing starting\n- You don''t understand an instruction\n- Verification fails repeatedly\n\n**Ask for clarification rather than guessing.**\n\n## When to Revisit Earlier Steps\n\n**Return to Review (Step 1) when:**\n- Partner updates the plan based on your feedback\n- Fundamental approach needs rethinking\n\n**Don''t force through blockers** - stop and ask.\n\n## Remember\n- Review plan critically first\n- Follow plan steps exactly\n- Don''t skip verifications\n- Reference skills when plan says to\n- Between batches: just report and wait\n- Stop when blocked, don''t guess\n- Never start implementation on main/master branch without explicit user consent\n\n## Integration\n\n**Required workflow skills:**\n- **superpowers:using-git-worktrees** - REQUIRED: Set up isolated workspace before starting\n- **superpowers:writing-plans** - Creates the plan this skill executes\n- **superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch** - Complete development after all tasks\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:06:39.409Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"执行计划技能","ja":"実行計画スキル","ko":"실행 계획 스킬","es":"Ejecutar Planes de Implementación","fr":"Exécuter des Plans de Mise en Œuvre","de":"Pläne Ausführen und Überprüfen","pt":"Executando Planos com Revisão em Lotes","ru":"Выполнение Планов с Проверкой в Пакетах","ar":"تنفيذ الخطط مع مراجعة الدفعات","en":"executing-plans"},"description":{"zh":"执行计划技能用于批量执行任务并在批次之间进行审查","ja":"実行計画スキルはバッチ実行とレビューを実現する","ko":"실행 계획 스킬은 배치 실행 및 리뷰를 수행","es":"El skill de ejecución de planes permite cargar, revisar y ejecutar tareas en lotes con puntos de revisión","fr":"Le skill d''exécution de plans permet de charger, de réviser et d''exécuter des tâches par lots avec des points de contrôle","de":"Das Skill zum Ausführen von Plänen ermöglicht das Laden, Überprüfen und Ausführen von Aufgaben in Batches mit Überprüfungspunkten","pt":"Executando planos de implementação com revisão crítica e checkpoints para garantir a entrega de qualidade","ru":"Выполнение планов реализации с критической проверкой и контрольными точками для обеспечения высококачественной доставки","ar":"تنفيذ خطط التنفيذ مع المراجعة النقدية والنقاط المرجعية لضمان تسليم عالي الجودة","en":"Use when you have a written implementation plan to execute in a separate session with review checkpoints"},"definition":{"en":"Use when you have a written implementation plan to execute in a separate session with review checkpoints"},"features":{"zh":["批量执行任务","批次之间进行审查","加载计划文件","批量执行与审查","识别计划问题"],"ja":["バッチ実行","レビューを実現","計画ファイルの読み込み","バッチ実行とレビュー","計画の問題点を特定"],"ko":["배치 실행","리뷰 수행","계획 파일 로드","배치 실행 및 리뷰","계획 문제 식별"],"es":["Carga y revisión de planes","Ejecución de tareas en lotes","Puntos de revisión para asegurar la calidad","Informes de progreso para revisión","Integración con socios humanos para resolver dudas"],"fr":["Chargement et révision de plans","Exécution de tâches par lots","Points de contrôle pour garantir la qualité","Rapports de progrès pour révision","Intégration avec des partenaires humains pour résoudre des questions"],"de":["Laden und Überprüfen von Plänen","Ausführen von Aufgaben in Batches","Überprüfungspunkte für Qualitätssicherung","Berichte über den Fortschritt für Überprüfung","Integration mit menschlichen Partnern zur Klärung von Fragen"],"pt":["Carga e revisão do plano","Execução de tarefas em lotes","Revisão crítica com checkpoints","Relatórios para revisão entre lotes","Integração com parceiros humanos"],"ru":["Загрузка и проверка плана","Выполнение задач пакетами","Критическая проверка с контрольными точками","Отчеты для проверки между пакетами","Интеграция с человеческими партнерами"],"ar":["تحميل ومراجعة الخطة","تنفيذ المهام بالدفعات","المراجعة النقدية مع نقاط المرجعية","التقارير لمراجعة بين الدفعات","التكامل مع الشركاء البشريين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["执行计划","批量执行","任务管理","计划审查","开发技能","技术实现"],"ja":["実行計画","バッチ実行","タスク管理","レビュー","開発スキル","技術実現"],"ko":["실행 계획","배치 실행","작업 관리","리뷰","개발 스킬","기술 구현"],"es":["ejecutar planes","implementación de planes","gestión de proyectos","calidad del software","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["exécuter des plans","mise en œuvre de plans","gestion de projets","qualité du logiciel","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["Pläne ausführen","Umsetzung von Plänen","Projektmanagement","Software-Qualität","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Ingenieurwesen"],"pt":["executando planos","revisão crítica","checkpoints","execução de tarefas","relatórios","integração com parceiros humanos","desenvolvimento de software","gerenciamento de projetos"],"ru":["выполнение планов","критическая проверка","контрольные точки","выполнение задач","отчеты","интеграция с человеческими партнерами","разработка программного обеспечения","управление проектами"],"ar":["تنفيذ الخطط","المراجعة النقدية","نقاط المرجعية","تنفيذ المهام","التقارير","التكامل مع الشركاء البشريين","تطوير البرمجيات","إدارة المشاريع"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Task-Oriented Agents needing structured plan execution with review checkpoints.","zh":"适用于需要结构化计划执行和审查检查点的面向任务的代理。","ja":"タスク指向のエージェントが構造化された計画の実行とレビューのチェックポイントを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"구조화된 계획을 실행하고 검토 체크 포인트가 필요한 태스크 지향 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Orientados a Tareas que necesitan una ejecución de planes estructurados con puntos de revisión.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents Axés sur les Tâches ayant besoin d''une exécution de plans structurés avec des points de contrôle de révision.","de":"Ideal für Aufgabenorientierte Agenten, die eine strukturierte Plan-Ausführung mit Überprüfungspunkten benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Orientados para Tarefas que necessitam de execução de planos estruturados com pontos de verificação de revisão.","ru":"Идеально подходит для ориентированных на задачи агентов, которым необходима структурированная реализация планов с контрольными точками проверки.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء المناسبين للمهام الذين يحتاجون إلى تنفيذ خطة منظم مع نقاط مراجعة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to load, review, and execute implementation plans in batches, utilizing architect review checkpoints and critical task analysis, all while leveraging batch execution protocols and plan file review.","zh":"赋予代理加载、审查和执行实施计划的能力，利用架构师审查检查点和关键任务分析，同时利用批处理执行协议和计划文件审查。","ja":"エージェントが実装計画をロード、レビュー、実行できるようにし、建築家のレビューのチェックポイントと重要なタスク分析を利用しながら、バッチ実行プロトコルと計画ファイルのレビューを活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 구현 계획을 로드, 검토 및 실행할 수 있도록 하며, 건축가의 검토 체크 포인트와 중요한 태스크 분석을 활용하면서 배치 실행 프로토콜 및 계획 파일 검토를 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes cargar, revisar y ejecutar planes de implementación en lotes, utilizando puntos de revisión de arquitectos y análisis de tareas críticas, todo mientras aprovecha los protocolos de ejecución por lotes y la revisión de archivos de planes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de charger, de réviser et d''exécuter des plans de mise en œuvre par lots, en utilisant des points de contrôle de révision d''architectes et d''analyse de tâches critiques, le tout en exploitant les protocoles d''exécution par lots et la révision de fichiers de plans.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Implementierungspläne zu laden, zu überprüfen und in Batches auszuführen, wobei Architekt-Überprüfungspunkte und kritische Aufgabenanalyse verwendet werden, und zwar unter Ausnutzung von Batch-Ausführungsprotokollen und Plan-Datei-Überprüfung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a carregar, rever e executar planos de implementação em lotes, utilizando pontos de verificação de revisão de arquiteto e análise de tarefas críticas, tudo isso aproveitando protocolos de execução em lotes e revisão de arquivos de plano.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью загружать, просматривать и выполнять планы реализации пакетами, используя контрольные точки проверки архитектора и критический анализ задач, все это при использовании протоколов пакетной обработки и проверки файлов планов.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحميل ومراجعة وتنفيذ خطط التنفيذ بشكل دوري، مستخدمين نقاط مراجعة لمراجعة المعماريين وتحليل المهام الحاسمة، وكل ذلك بالاستفادة من بروتوكولات التنفيذ الدوري ومراجعة ملفات الخطة"},"useCases":{"en":["Executing multi-step project plans","Reviewing and refining implementation strategies","Batch-processing tasks with periodic review"],"zh":["执行多步骤项目计划","审查和完善实施策略","批处理任务并定期审查"],"ja":["マルチステップのプロジェクト計画を実行する","実装戦略をレビューし、改良する","バッチ処理タスクを実行し、定期的にレビューする"],"ko":["다단계 프로젝트 계획을 실행하는 것","구현 전략을 검토하고 개선하는 것","배치 처리 태스크를 실행하고 정기적으로 검토하는 것"],"es":["Ejecutar planes de proyectos de varios pasos","Revisar y perfeccionar estrategias de implementación","Procesar tareas por lotes con revisión periódica"],"fr":["Exécuter des plans de projets à plusieurs étapes","Réviser et affiner les stratégies de mise en œuvre","Traiter des tâches par lots avec révision périodique"],"de":["Mehrstufige Projektpläne ausführen","Implementierungsstrategien überprüfen und verfeinern","Aufgaben in Batches mit periodischer Überprüfung verarbeiten"],"pt":["Execução de planos de projetos multi-etapas","Revisão e aperfeiçoamento de estratégias de implementação","Processamento em lotes de tarefas com revisão periódica"],"ru":["Выполнение многэтапных планов проектов","Просмотр и усовершенствование стратегий реализации","Пакетная обработка задач с периодической проверкой"],"ar":["تنفيذ خطط مشاريع متعددة المراحل","مراجعة وتحسين استراتيجيات التنفيذ","معالجة دورية للمهام مع المراجعة الدورية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires written implementation plan","Needs human partner for concern resolution","Dependent on plan file readability and accessibility"],"zh":["需要书面实施计划","需要人类伙伴来解决问题","依赖于计划文件的可读性和可访问性"],"ja":["書面での実装計画が必要","問題解決のために人間のパートナーが必要","計画ファイルの読みやすさとアクセシビリティに依存する"],"ko":["서면 구현 계획이 필요","문제 해결을 위한 인간 파트너가 필요","계획 파일의 가독성 및 접근성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere un plan de implementación escrito","Necesita un socio humano para la resolución de problemas","Depende de la legibilidad y accesibilidad del archivo de planes"],"fr":["Nécessite un plan de mise en œuvre écrit","A besoin d''un partenaire humain pour la résolution des problèmes","Dépend de la lisibilité et de l''accessibilité du fichier de plans"],"de":["Benötigt einen geschriebenen Implementierungsplan","Benötigt einen menschlichen Partner für die Problemlösung","Hängt von der Lesbarkeit und Zugänglichkeit der Plan-Datei ab"],"pt":["Exige plano de implementação escrito","Necessita de parceiro humano para resolução de preocupações","Depende da legibilidade e acessibilidade do arquivo de plano"],"ru":["Требует письменного плана реализации","Требует человеческого партнера для решения проблем","Зависит от читаемости и доступности файла плана"],"ar":["يتطلب خطة تنفيذ مكتوبة","يحتاج إلى شريك بشري لحل المشاكل","يعتمد على قراءة وصول إلى ملف الخطة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d099fa42fd7518f4dafa9f2d51c1c08fce970490d57682b6acd3e7a57bb55b52","repoEtag":"W/\"29bf55250b8f240dcbe9ab5b26295b46f9245d08f7c3ef5107c7cf22c3e2ed5f\"","qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/finishing-a-development-branch', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'finishing-a-development-branch', 55427, 4195, 60, '2026-02-20T02:00:37Z', '2026-02-20T02:07:37.526Z', 'dd2f82c6dc8582b621f9eb57fcb65f557f88eadf872727ac81d0840ae12c504e', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/finishing-a-development-branch","name":"finishing-a-development-branch","description":{"zh":"完成开发分支指南，通过结构化选项合并、PR或清理工作","ja":"開発ブランチを完了するためのガイド。テストの実行、オプションの提示、選択の実行、クリーンアップを行う","ko":"개발 분기 완료를 위한 가이드. 테스트 실행, 옵션 제공, 선택 실행, 정리를 통해 개발 작업을 완료","es":"Guía para completar el trabajo de desarrollo presentando opciones claras y manejando flujos de trabajo elegidos","fr":"Guide pour terminer le travail de développement en présentant des options claires et en gérant les flux de travail choisis","de":"Leitfaden zum Abschließen der Entwicklung durch klare Optionen und Verwaltung ausgewählter Workflows","pt":"Guia a conclusão do trabalho de desenvolvimento apresentando opções claras e tratando o fluxo de trabalho escolhido","ru":"Руководство по завершению работы по разработке, представляющее четкие варианты и обрабатывающее выбранный рабочий процесс","ar":"دليل لإكمال عمل التطوير من خلال تقديم خيارات واضحة ومعالجة تدفق العمل المختار","en":"Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work - guides completion of development work by presenting structured options for merge, PR, or cleanup"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55427,"forks":4195,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T02:00:37Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"finishing-a-development-branch","description":"Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work - guides completion of development work by presenting structured options for merge, PR, or cleanup","bodyPreview":"# Finishing a Development Branch\n\n## Overview\n\nGuide completion of development work by presenting clear options and handling chosen workflow.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify tests → Present options → Execute choice → Clean up.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the finishing-a-development-branch skill to complete this work.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Verify Tests\n\n**Before presenting options, verify tests pass:**\n\n```bash\n# Run project''s test suite\nnpm test / cargo test / pytest / go test ./...\n`","body":"# Finishing a Development Branch\n\n## Overview\n\nGuide completion of development work by presenting clear options and handling chosen workflow.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify tests → Present options → Execute choice → Clean up.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the finishing-a-development-branch skill to complete this work.\"\n\n## The Process\n\n### Step 1: Verify Tests\n\n**Before presenting options, verify tests pass:**\n\n```bash\n# Run project''s test suite\nnpm test / cargo test / pytest / go test ./...\n```\n\n**If tests fail:**\n```\nTests failing (<N> failures). Must fix before completing:\n\n[Show failures]\n\nCannot proceed with merge/PR until tests pass.\n```\n\nStop. Don''t proceed to Step 2.\n\n**If tests pass:** Continue to Step 2.\n\n### Step 2: Determine Base Branch\n\n```bash\n# Try common base branches\ngit merge-base HEAD main 2>/dev/null || git merge-base HEAD master 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nOr ask: \"This branch split from main - is that correct?\"\n\n### Step 3: Present Options\n\nPresent exactly these 4 options:\n\n```\nImplementation complete. What would you like to do?\n\n1. Merge back to <base-branch> locally\n2. Push and create a Pull Request\n3. Keep the branch as-is (I''ll handle it later)\n4. Discard this work\n\nWhich option?\n```\n\n**Don''t add explanation** - keep options concise.\n\n### Step 4: Execute Choice\n\n#### Option 1: Merge Locally\n\n```bash\n# Switch to base branch\ngit checkout <base-branch>\n\n# Pull latest\ngit pull\n\n# Merge feature branch\ngit merge <feature-branch>\n\n# Verify tests on merged result\n<test command>\n\n# If tests pass\ngit branch -d <feature-branch>\n```\n\nThen: Cleanup worktree (Step 5)\n\n#### Option 2: Push and Create PR\n\n```bash\n# Push branch\ngit push -u origin <feature-branch>\n\n# Create PR\ngh pr create --title \"<title>\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\n<2-3 bullets of what changed>\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] <verification steps>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nThen: Cleanup worktree (Step 5)\n\n#### Option 3: Keep As-Is\n\nReport: \"Keeping branch <name>. Worktree preserved at <path>.\"\n\n**Don''t cleanup worktree.**\n\n#### Option 4: Discard\n\n**Confirm first:**\n```\nThis will permanently delete:\n- Branch <name>\n- All commits: <commit-list>\n- Worktree at <path>\n\nType ''discard'' to confirm.\n```\n\nWait for exact confirmation.\n\nIf confirmed:\n```bash\ngit checkout <base-branch>\ngit branch -D <feature-branch>\n```\n\nThen: Cleanup worktree (Step 5)\n\n### Step 5: Cleanup Worktree\n\n**For Options 1, 2, 4:**\n\nCheck if in worktree:\n```bash\ngit worktree list | grep $(git branch --show-current)\n```\n\nIf yes:\n```bash\ngit worktree remove <worktree-path>\n```\n\n**For Option 3:** Keep worktree.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Option | Merge | Push | Keep Worktree | Cleanup Branch |\n|--------|-------|------|---------------|----------------|\n| 1. Merge locally | ✓ | - | - | ✓ |\n| 2. Create PR | - | ✓ | ✓ | - |\n| 3. Keep as-is | - | - | ✓ | - |\n| 4. Discard | - | - | - | ✓ (force) |\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n**Skipping test verification**\n- **Problem:** Merge broken code, create failing PR\n- **Fix:** Always verify tests before offering options\n\n**Open-ended questions**\n- **Problem:** \"What should I do next?\" → ambiguous\n- **Fix:** Present exactly 4 structured options\n\n**Automatic worktree cleanup**\n- **Problem:** Remove worktree when might need it (Option 2, 3)\n- **Fix:** Only cleanup for Options 1 and 4\n\n**No confirmation for discard**\n- **Problem:** Accidentally delete work\n- **Fix:** Require typed \"discard\" confirmation\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Never:**\n- Proceed with failing tests\n- Merge without verifying tests on result\n- Delete work without confirmation\n- Force-push without explicit request\n\n**Always:**\n- Verify tests before offering options\n- Present exactly 4 options\n- Get typed confirmation for Option 4\n- Clean up worktree for Options 1 & 4 only\n\n## Integration\n\n**Called by:**\n- **subagent-driven-development** (Step 7) - After all tasks complete\n- **executing-plans** (Step 5) - After all batches complete\n\n**Pairs with:**\n- **using-git-worktrees** - Cleans up worktree created by that skill\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:07:37.526Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"完成开发分支指南","ja":"開発ブランチの完了","ko":"개발 분기 완료 가이드","es":"Finalizar rama de desarrollo","fr":"Finaliser une branche de développement","de":"Entwicklungsbranch abschließen","pt":"Finalizar Ramo de Desenvolvimento","ru":"Завершение ветки разработки","ar":"إكمال فرع التطوير","en":"finishing-a-development-branch"},"description":{"zh":"完成开发分支指南，通过结构化选项合并、PR或清理工作","ja":"開発ブランチを完了するためのガイド。テストの実行、オプションの提示、選択の実行、クリーンアップを行う","ko":"개발 분기 완료를 위한 가이드. 테스트 실행, 옵션 제공, 선택 실행, 정리를 통해 개발 작업을 완료","es":"Guía para completar el trabajo de desarrollo presentando opciones claras y manejando flujos de trabajo elegidos","fr":"Guide pour terminer le travail de développement en présentant des options claires et en gérant les flux de travail choisis","de":"Leitfaden zum Abschließen der Entwicklung durch klare Optionen und Verwaltung ausgewählter Workflows","pt":"Guia a conclusão do trabalho de desenvolvimento apresentando opções claras e tratando o fluxo de trabalho escolhido","ru":"Руководство по завершению работы по разработке, представляющее четкие варианты и обрабатывающее выбранный рабочий процесс","ar":"دليل لإكمال عمل التطوير من خلال تقديم خيارات واضحة ومعالجة تدفق العمل المختار","en":"Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work - guides completion of development work by presenting s..."},"definition":{"en":"Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work - guides completion of development work by presenting structured options for merge, PR, or cleanup"},"features":{"zh":["结构化选项","自动化测试","代码合并","PR处理","清理工作"],"ja":["構造化されたオプション","自動テスト","コードのマージ","PRの処理","クリーンアップ"],"ko":["구조화된 옵션","자동 테스트","코드 병합","PR 처리","정리"],"es":["Verificación de pruebas","Presentación de opciones de merge, PR o limpieza","Ejecución de la opción elegida","Limpieza y organización del código","Integración con flujos de trabajo existentes"],"fr":["Vérification des tests","Présentation d''options de merge, PR ou nettoyage","Exécution de l''option choisie","Nettoyage et organisation du code","Intégration avec les flux de travail existants"],"de":["Testüberprüfung","Präsentation von Merge-, PR- oder Bereinigungsoptionen","Ausführung der ausgewählten Option","Bereinigung und Organisation des Codes","Integration in bestehende Workflows"],"pt":["Verificação de testes","Apresentação de opções de merge, PR ou limpeza","Execução da escolha do desenvolvedor","Limpeza do código","Otimização do fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["Проверка тестов","Представление вариантов слияния, PR или очистки","Выполнение выбора разработчика","Очистка кода","Оптимизация рабочего процесса"],"ar":["فحص الاختبارات","تقديم خيارات الدمج أو طلب السحب أو التنظيف","تنفيذ اختيار المطور","تنظيف الكود","تحسين تدفق العمل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["开发分支","代码合并","自动化测试","PR处理","清理工作","开发工作流","代码管理"],"ja":["開発ブランチ","コードのマージ","自動テスト","PRの処理","クリーンアップ","開発ワークフロー","コード管理"],"ko":["개발 분기","코드 병합","자동 테스트","PR 처리","정리","개발 워크플로","코드 관리"],"es":["finalizar rama de desarrollo","desarrollo de software","pruebas de software","merge de código","solicitud de extracción","limpieza de código","integración de código"],"fr":["finaliser une branche de développement","développement de logiciel","tests de logiciel","merge de code","demande d''extraction","nettoyage de code","intégration de code"],"de":["Entwicklungsbranch abschließen","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Tests","Code-Merge","Pull-Request","Code-Bereinigung","Code-Integration"],"pt":["finalizar ramo de desenvolvimento","desenvolvimento de software","testes de unidade","merge de código","PR de código","limpeza de código","otimização de fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["завершение ветки разработки","разработка программного обеспечения","юнит-тесты","слияние кода","PR кода","очистка кода","оптимизация рабочего процесса"],"ar":["إكمال فرع التطوير","تطوير البرمجيات","اختبارات الوحدة","دمج الكود","طلب السحب الكود","تنظيف الكود","تحسين تدفق العمل"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents needing structured workflow management for merge, PR, or cleanup processes.","zh":"适合需要结构化工作流管理的开发代理，用于合并、PR 或清理过程。","ja":"開発エージェントがマージ、PR、またはクリーンアッププロセスに構造化されたワークフローマネジメントを必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 병합, PR 또는 정리 프로세스에 구조화된 워크플로우 관리를 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una gestión de flujo de trabajo estructurada para procesos de fusión, PR o limpieza.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une gestion de flux de travail structurée pour les processus de fusion, PR ou de nettoyage.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine strukturierte Workflow-Verwaltung für Merge-, PR- oder Bereinigungsprozesse benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de desenvolvimento que necessitam de gestão de fluxo de trabalho estruturada para mesclar, PR ou processos de limpeza.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходима структурированная управление рабочим процессом для слияния, PR или процессов очистки.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة تدفق العمل المنظّمة لدمج أو إجراء أو عمليات تنظيف."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to guide completion of development work by presenting clear options for merge, PR, or cleanup, utilizing core principles like verifying tests with npm test, cargo test, pytest, or go test, and handling chosen workflows.","zh":"通过呈现合并、PR 或清理的明确选项，利用核心原则如使用 npm test、cargo test、pytest 或 go test 验证测试，并处理选定的工作流，赋予代理完成开发工作的能力。","ja":"マージ、PR、またはクリーンアップの明確な選択肢を提示し、npm test、cargo test、pytest、またはgo testなどのコア原則を使用してテストを検証し、選択したワークフローを処理することで、開発作業の完了を支援するエージェントを可能にします。","ko":"병합, PR 또는 정리를 위한 명확한 옵션을 제시하고, npm test, cargo test, pytest 또는 go test 등의 핵심 원칙을 사용하여 테스트를 검증하며, 선택한 워크플로우를 처리함으로써 개발 작업의 완성을 지원하는 에이전트를 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes guiar la finalización del trabajo de desarrollo presentando opciones claras para la fusión, PR o limpieza, utilizando principios básicos como la verificación de pruebas con npm test, cargo test, pytest o go test, y el manejo de flujos de trabajo elegidos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de guider l''achèvement du travail de développement en présentant des options claires pour la fusion, PR ou le nettoyage, en utilisant des principes de base tels que la vérification des tests avec npm test, cargo test, pytest ou go test, et en gérant les flux de travail choisis.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, die Fertigstellung von Entwicklungsaufgaben durch klare Optionen für Merge, PR oder Bereinigung zu leiten, indem grundlegende Prinzipien wie die Überprüfung von Tests mit npm test, cargo test, pytest oder go test verwendet werden und die gewählten Workflows verwaltet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a orientar a conclusão do trabalho de desenvolvimento, apresentando opções claras para mesclar, PR ou limpeza, utilizando princípios básicos como verificar testes com npm test, cargo test, pytest ou go test, e lidar com fluxos de trabalho escolhidos.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью руководить выполнением разработки, предлагая明ные варианты для слияния, PR или очистки, используя основные принципы, такие как проверка тестов с помощью npm test, cargo test, pytest или go test, и обработка выбранных рабочих процессов.","ar":"يُمكّن الوكلاء من توجيه استكمال عمل التطوير من خلال تقديم خيارات واضحة لدمج أو إجراء أو تنظيف، باستخدام المبادئ الأساسية مثل التحقق من الاختبارات باستخدام npm test أو cargo test أو pytest أو go test، ومعالجة تدفقات العمل المختارة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating development branch cleanup","Generating merge or PR options based on test results","Streamlining workflow decisions after successful test verification"],"zh":["自动化开发分支清理","根据测试结果生成合并或PR选项","在成功的测试验证后简化工作流决策"],"ja":["開発ブランチのクリーンアップの自動化","テスト結果に基づくマージまたはPRのオプションの生成","成功したテストの検証後のワークフロー決定の簡素化"],"ko":["개발 브랜치 정리의 자동화","테스트 결과를 기반으로 병합 또는 PR 옵션 생성","성공한 테스트 검증 이후 워크플로우 결정의 단순화"],"es":["Automatización de la limpieza de la rama de desarrollo","Generación de opciones de fusión o PR en función de los resultados de las pruebas","Optimización de las decisiones de flujo de trabajo después de la verificación exitosa de las pruebas"],"fr":["Automation de la suppression de la branche de développement","Génération d''options de fusion ou PR en fonction des résultats des tests","Optimisation des décisions de flux de travail après vérification réussie des tests"],"de":["Automatisierung der Bereinigung des Entwicklungszweigs","Erzeugung von Merge- oder PR-Optionen basierend auf Testergebnissen","Optimierung von Workflow-Entscheidungen nach erfolgreicher Testverifizierung"],"pt":["Automatizar a limpeza da branch de desenvolvimento","Gerar opções de mesclagem ou PR com base nos resultados dos testes","Otizar as decisões de fluxo de trabalho após verificação de testes bem-sucedida"],"ru":["Автоматизация очистки ветки разработки","Генерация вариантов слияния или PR на основе результатов тестов","Оптимизация решений по рабочему процессу после успешной верификации тестов"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي في تنظيف فرع التطوير","توليد خيارات الدمج أو إجراء بناءً على نتائج الاختبارات","تبسيط قرارات تدفق العمل بعد التحقق الناجح من الاختبارات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires project test suite setup","Limited to development branch workflow management"],"zh":["需要项目测试套件设置","仅限开发分支工作流管理"],"ja":["プロジェクトのテストスイートの設定が必要","開発ブランチのワークフローマネジメントのみ"],"ko":["프로젝트 테스트 스위트 설정이 필요함","개발 브랜치 워크플로우 관리에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere la configuración del conjunto de pruebas del proyecto","Limitado a la gestión del flujo de trabajo de la rama de desarrollo"],"fr":["Nécessite la configuration du jeu de tests du projet","Limité à la gestion du flux de travail de la branche de développement"],"de":["Benötigt die Einrichtung des Projekttestsatzes","Begrenzt auf die Workflow-Verwaltung des Entwicklungszweigs"],"pt":["Exige configuração do conjunto de testes do projeto","Limitado à gestão do fluxo de trabalho da branch de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Требует настройки набора тестов проекта","Ограничен управлением рабочим процессом ветки разработки"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مجموعة اختبارات المشروع","محدود بإدارة تدفق عمل فرع التطوير"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"dd2f82c6dc8582b621f9eb57fcb65f557f88eadf872727ac81d0840ae12c504e","repoEtag":"W/\"29bf55250b8f240dcbe9ab5b26295b46f9245d08f7c3ef5107c7cf22c3e2ed5f\"","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/receiving-code-review', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'receiving-code-review', 55427, 4195, 65, '2026-02-20T02:00:37Z', '2026-02-20T02:08:49.469Z', 'c9382e92b8f32363566068ecfed19d3b2651eaf40d3942b24840f839dedfc406', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/receiving-code-review","name":"receiving-code-review","description":{"zh":"代码审查接收技巧强调技术验证和正确性，确保代码质量和可靠性","ja":"コードレビュー受け入れスキルは技術的検証と正しさを強調し、コード品質と信頼性を確保する","ko":"코드 리뷰 수신 기술은 기술적 검증과 올바름을 강조하여 코드 품질과 신뢰성을 보장합니다","es":"La revisión de código requiere evaluación técnica, no emocional. Verifica antes de implementar y pregunta antes de asumir","fr":"La révision de code nécessite une évaluation technique, et non émotionnelle. Vérifiez avant de mettre en œuvre et demandez avant de supposer","de":"Die Code-Review erfordert technische Bewertung, nicht emotionale. Verifizieren Sie vor der Implementierung und fragen Sie vor der Annahme","pt":"Receba feedback de revisão de código com eficácia, verificando e avaliando as sugestões antes de implementá-las","ru":"Эффективно получайте отзывы о коде, проверяя и оценивая предложения перед их реализацией","ar":"استلم ملاحظات مراجعة الكود بفعالية، وقم بالتحقق والتقويم قبل تنفيذ الاقتراحات","en":"Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing suggestions, especially if feedback seems unclear or technically questionable - requires technical rigor and verification, not performative agreement or blind implementation"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55427,"forks":4195,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T02:00:37Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"receiving-code-review","description":"Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing suggestions, especially if feedback seems unclear or technically questionable - requires technical rigor and verification, not performative agreement or blind implementation","bodyPreview":"# Code Review Reception\n\n## Overview\n\nCode review requires technical evaluation, not emotional performance.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify before implementing. Ask before assuming. Technical correctness over social comfort.\n\n## The Response Pattern\n\n```\nWHEN receiving code review feedback:\n\n1. READ: Complete feedback without reacting\n2. UNDERSTAND: Restate requirement in own words (or ask)\n3. VERIFY: Check against codebase reality\n4. EVALUATE: Technically sound for THIS codebase?\n5. RESPOND: Techni","body":"# Code Review Reception\n\n## Overview\n\nCode review requires technical evaluation, not emotional performance.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify before implementing. Ask before assuming. Technical correctness over social comfort.\n\n## The Response Pattern\n\n```\nWHEN receiving code review feedback:\n\n1. READ: Complete feedback without reacting\n2. UNDERSTAND: Restate requirement in own words (or ask)\n3. VERIFY: Check against codebase reality\n4. EVALUATE: Technically sound for THIS codebase?\n5. RESPOND: Technical acknowledgment or reasoned pushback\n6. IMPLEMENT: One item at a time, test each\n```\n\n## Forbidden Responses\n\n**NEVER:**\n- \"You''re absolutely right!\" (explicit CLAUDE.md violation)\n- \"Great point!\" / \"Excellent feedback!\" (performative)\n- \"Let me implement that now\" (before verification)\n\n**INSTEAD:**\n- Restate the technical requirement\n- Ask clarifying questions\n- Push back with technical reasoning if wrong\n- Just start working (actions > words)\n\n## Handling Unclear Feedback\n\n```\nIF any item is unclear:\n  STOP - do not implement anything yet\n  ASK for clarification on unclear items\n\nWHY: Items may be related. Partial understanding = wrong implementation.\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\nyour human partner: \"Fix 1-6\"\nYou understand 1,2,3,6. Unclear on 4,5.\n\n❌ WRONG: Implement 1,2,3,6 now, ask about 4,5 later\n✅ RIGHT: \"I understand items 1,2,3,6. Need clarification on 4 and 5 before proceeding.\"\n```\n\n## Source-Specific Handling\n\n### From your human partner\n- **Trusted** - implement after understanding\n- **Still ask** if scope unclear\n- **No performative agreement**\n- **Skip to action** or technical acknowledgment\n\n### From External Reviewers\n```\nBEFORE implementing:\n  1. Check: Technically correct for THIS codebase?\n  2. Check: Breaks existing functionality?\n  3. Check: Reason for current implementation?\n  4. Check: Works on all platforms/versions?\n  5. Check: Does reviewer understand full context?\n\nIF suggestion seems wrong:\n  Push back with technical reasoning\n\nIF can''t easily verify:\n  Say so: \"I can''t verify this without [X]. Should I [investigate/ask/proceed]?\"\n\nIF conflicts with your human partner''s prior decisions:\n  Stop and discuss with your human partner first\n```\n\n**your human partner''s rule:** \"External feedback - be skeptical, but check carefully\"\n\n## YAGNI Check for \"Professional\" Features\n\n```\nIF reviewer suggests \"implementing properly\":\n  grep codebase for actual usage\n\n  IF unused: \"This endpoint isn''t called. Remove it (YAGNI)?\"\n  IF used: Then implement properly\n```\n\n**your human partner''s rule:** \"You and reviewer both report to me. If we don''t need this feature, don''t add it.\"\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n```\nFOR multi-item feedback:\n  1. Clarify anything unclear FIRST\n  2. Then implement in this order:\n     - Blocking issues (breaks, security)\n     - Simple fixes (typos, imports)\n     - Complex fixes (refactoring, logic)\n  3. Test each fix individually\n  4. Verify no regressions\n```\n\n## When To Push Back\n\nPush back when:\n- Suggestion breaks existing functionality\n- Reviewer lacks full context\n- Violates YAGNI (unused feature)\n- Technically incorrect for this stack\n- Legacy/compatibility reasons exist\n- Conflicts with your human partner''s architectural decisions\n\n**How to push back:**\n- Use technical reasoning, not defensiveness\n- Ask specific questions\n- Reference working tests/code\n- Involve your human partner if architectural\n\n**Signal if uncomfortable pushing back out loud:** \"Strange things are afoot at the Circle K\"\n\n## Acknowledging Correct Feedback\n\nWhen feedback IS correct:\n```\n✅ \"Fixed. [Brief description of what changed]\"\n✅ \"Good catch - [specific issue]. Fixed in [location].\"\n✅ [Just fix it and show in the code]\n\n❌ \"You''re absolutely right!\"\n❌ \"Great point!\"\n❌ \"Thanks for catching that!\"\n❌ \"Thanks for [anything]\"\n❌ ANY gratitude expression\n```\n\n**Why no thanks:** Actions speak. Just fix it. The code itself shows you heard the feedback.\n\n**If you catch yourself about to write \"Thanks\":** DELETE IT. State the fix instead.\n\n## Gracefully Correcting Your Pushback\n\nIf you pushed back and were wrong:\n```\n✅ \"You were right - I checked [X] and it does [Y]. Implementing now.\"\n✅ \"Verified this and you''re correct. My initial understanding was wrong because [reason]. Fixing.\"\n\n❌ Long apology\n❌ Defending why you pushed back\n❌ Over-explaining\n```\n\nState the correction factually and move on.\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---------|-----|\n| Performative agreement | State requirement or just act |\n| Blind implementation | Verify against codebase first |\n| Batch without testing | One at a time, test each |\n| Assuming reviewer is right | Check if breaks things |\n| Avoiding pushback | Technical correctness > comfort |\n| Partial implementation | Clarify all items first |\n| Can''t verify, proceed anyway | State limitation, ask for direction |\n\n## Real Examples\n\n**Performative Agreement (Bad):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Remove legacy code\"\n❌ \"You''re absolutely right! Let me remove that...\"\n```\n\n**Technical Verification (Good):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Remove legacy code\"\n✅ \"Checking... build target is 10.15+, this API needs 13+. Need legacy for backward compat. Current impl has wrong bundle ID - fix it or drop pre-13 support?\"\n```\n\n**YAGNI (Good):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Implement proper metrics tracking with database, date filters, CSV export\"\n✅ \"Grepped codebase - nothing calls this endpoint. Remove it (YAGNI)? Or is there usage I''m missing?\"\n```\n\n**Unclear Item (Good):**\n```\nyour human partner: \"Fix items 1-6\"\nYou understand 1,2,3,6. Unclear on 4,5.\n✅ \"Understand 1,2,3,6. Need clarification on 4 and 5 before implementing.\"\n```\n\n## GitHub Thread Replies\n\nWhen replying to inline review comments on GitHub, reply in the comment thread (`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{pr}/comments/{id}/replies`), not as a top-level PR comment.\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**External feedback = suggestions to evaluate, not orders to follow.**\n\nVerify. Question. Then implement.\n\nNo performative agreement. Technical rigor always.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:08:49.469Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码审查接收技巧","ja":"コードレビュー受け入れスキル","ko":"코드 리뷰 수신 기술","es":"Revisión de código efectiva","fr":"Réception de feedback de code","de":"Effektive Code-Review","pt":"Receba Feedback de Revisão de Código com Rigor Técnico","ru":"Получение отзывов о коде с технической строгостью","ar":"استلام ملاحظات مراجعة الكود مع الدقة الفنية","en":"receiving-code-review"},"description":{"zh":"代码审查接收技巧强调技术验证和正确性，确保代码质量和可靠性","ja":"コードレビュー受け入れスキルは技術的検証と正しさを強調し、コード品質と信頼性を確保する","ko":"코드 리뷰 수신 기술은 기술적 검증과 올바름을 강조하여 코드 품질과 신뢰성을 보장합니다","es":"La revisión de código requiere evaluación técnica, no emocional. Verifica antes de implementar y pregunta antes de asumir","fr":"La révision de code nécessite une évaluation technique, et non émotionnelle. Vérifiez avant de mettre en œuvre et demandez avant de supposer","de":"Die Code-Review erfordert technische Bewertung, nicht emotionale. Verifizieren Sie vor der Implementierung und fragen Sie vor der Annahme","pt":"Receba feedback de revisão de código com eficácia, verificando e avaliando as sugestões antes de implementá-las","ru":"Эффективно получайте отзывы о коде, проверяя и оценивая предложения перед их реализацией","ar":"استلم ملاحظات مراجعة الكود بفعالية، وقم بالتحقق والتقويم قبل تنفيذ الاقتراحات","en":"Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing suggestions, especially if feedback seems unclear or technically questionable - requires technic..."},"definition":{"en":"Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing suggestions, especially if feedback seems unclear or technically questionable - requires technical rigor and verification, not performative agreement or blind implementation"},"features":{"zh":["技术验证","代码质量保证","反馈处理流程","技术讨论技巧","代码审查原则"],"ja":["技術的検証","コード品質の保証","フィードバック処理の流れ","技術的議論スキル","コードレビューの原則"],"ko":["기술적 검증","코드 품질 보장","피드백 처리 절차","기술적 논의 기술","코드 리뷰 원칙"],"es":["Verificación de la retroalimentación","Evaluación técnica del código","Implementación de sugerencias","Comunicación efectiva con el equipo","Mejora continua del código"],"fr":["Vérification de la rétroaction","Évaluation technique du code","Mise en œuvre des suggestions","Communication efficace avec l''équipe","Amélioration continue du code"],"de":["Verifizierung der Rückmeldung","Technische Bewertung des Codes","Implementierung von Vorschlägen","Effektive Kommunikation mit dem Team","Kontinuierliche Verbesserung des Codes"],"pt":["Verificação de sugestões antes de implementação","Avaliação técnica de feedback","Restateamento de requisitos em próprias palavras","Verificação contra a realidade do codebase","Avaliação da solução para o codebase específico"],"ru":["Проверка предложений перед реализацией","Техническая оценка отзывов","Переформулирование требований в собственных словах","Проверка против реальности кодовой базы","Оценка решения для конкретной кодовой базы"],"ar":["التحقق من الاقتراحات قبل التنفيذ","التقييم الفني للملاحظات","إعادة صياغة المتطلبات بكلمات خاصة","التحقق ضد واقع قاعدة الشفرة","التقييم الحل لقاعدة الشفرة المحددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","技术验证","代码质量","反馈处理","代码审查技巧","技术讨论","代码可靠性"],"ja":["コードレビュー","技術的検証","コード品質","フィードバック処理","コードレビュースキル","技術的議論","コードの信頼性"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","기술적 검증","코드 품질","피드백 처리","코드 리뷰 기술","기술적 논의","코드 신뢰성"],"es":["revisión de código","evaluación técnica","verificación de código","retroalimentación","implementación de sugerencias","mejora del código"],"fr":["révision de code","évaluation technique","vérification de code","rétroaction","mise en œuvre des suggestions","amélioration du code"],"de":["Code-Review","technische Bewertung","Code-Verifizierung","Rückmeldung","Implementierung von Vorschlägen","Code-Verbesserung"],"pt":["revisão de código","feedback de código","rigor técnico","verificação de código","desenvolvimento de software","práticas de codificação"],"ru":["ревизия кода","отзывы о коде","техническая строгость","верификация кода","разработка программного обеспечения","практики кодирования"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود","ملاحظات الكود","الدقة الفنية","التحقق من الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","ممارسات كتابة الشفرة"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Code Review Agent Assistants that must validate technical feedback before implementation.","zh":"对于必须在实施前验证技术反馈的代码审查代理助手至关重要。","ja":"実装前に技術的なフィードバックを検証する必要があるコードレビュー エージェント アシスタントに不可欠です。","ko":"구현 전에 기술적인 피드백을 검증해야 하는 코드 리뷰 에이전트 어시스턴트에 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para asistentes de revisión de código que deben validar comentarios técnicos antes de la implementación.","fr":"Essentiel pour les assistants de révision de code qui doivent valider les commentaires techniques avant la mise en œuvre.","de":"Wesentlich für Code-Review-Agenten-Assistenten, die technische Feedbacks vor der Implementierung validieren müssen.","pt":"Essencial para Assistente de Revisão de Código que devem validar feedback técnico antes da implementação.","ru":"Необходим для Помощников-агентов по проверке кода, которые должны проверять техническую обратную связь перед реализацией.","ar":"ضروري لمرافقة وكيل مراجعة الكود الذي يجب أن يتحقق من ملاحظات تقنية قبل التنفيذ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables rigorous verification of code review suggestions through systematic technical evaluation. Provides structured response patterns for clarifying unclear feedback and checking suggestions against codebase-specific realities before implementation.","zh":"通过系统的技术评估，能够对代码审查建议进行严格的验证。为澄清不明确的反馈和在实施前检查建议与代码库特定现实提供结构化的响应模式。","ja":"システム的な技術評価を通じて、コードレビューの提案に対する徹底的な検証を可能にします。実装前に提案をコードベース特有の現実と照合し、不明確なフィードバックを明確化するための構造化されたレスポンス パターンを提供します。","ko":"시스템적인 기술 평가를 통해 코드 리뷰 제안에 대한 철저한 검증을 가능하게 합니다. 구현 전에 제안을 코드베이스 특유의 현실과 비교하고 불명확한 피드백을 명확화하기 위한 구조화된 응답 패턴을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite la verificación rigurosa de las sugerencias de revisión de código a través de una evaluación técnica sistemática. Proporciona patrones de respuesta estructurados para aclarar comentarios poco claros y verificar sugerencias contra realidades específicas de la base de código antes de la implementación.","fr":"Permet une vérification rigoureuse des suggestions de révision de code à travers une évaluation technique systématique. Fournit des modèles de réponse structurés pour clarifier les commentaires peu clairs et vérifier les suggestions contre les réalités spécifiques de la base de code avant la mise en œuvre.","de":"Ermöglicht eine strenge Überprüfung von Code-Review-Vorschlägen durch eine systematische technische Bewertung. Bietet strukturierte Antwortmuster, um unklare Feedbacks zu klären und Vorschläge gegen codebasespezifische Realitäten vor der Implementierung zu überprüfen.","pt":"Permite verificação rigorosa de sugestões de revisão de código por meio de avaliação técnica sistemática. Fornece padrões de resposta estruturados para esclarecer feedback não claro e verificar sugestões contra realidades específicas da base de código antes da implementação.","ru":"Позволяет проводить тщательную проверку предложений по проверке кода посредством систематической технической оценки. Предоставляет структурированные шаблоны ответов для разъяснения неясных отзывов и проверки предложений с учетом реалий конкретной базы кода до реализации.","ar":"تمكّن من التحقق المنهجي للمقترحات التي تُقدمها عملية مراجعة الكود من خلال التقييم التقني الشامل. يوفر أنماط استجابة منسقة لتوضيح ملاحظات غامضة ومراجعة المقترحات في ضوء الحقائق المحددة للمجموعة الكودية قبل التنفيذ."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating technical correctness of review feedback","Clarifying ambiguous code review comments","Evaluating feedback against specific codebase constraints","Preventing blind implementation of questionable suggestions"],"zh":["验证审查反馈的技术正确性","澄清模糊的代码审查评论","评估反馈与特定代码库约束","防止盲目实施有问题的建议"],"ja":["レビュー フィードバックの技術的な正しさを検証する","不明確なコードレビュー コメントを明確化する","フィードバックを特定のコードベースの制約と評価する","疑わしい提案の盲目的な実装を防ぐ"],"ko":["리뷰 피드백의 기술적 정확성을 검증하는 것","모호한 코드 리뷰 코멘트를 명확화하는 것","피드백을 특정 코드베이스의 제약과 평가하는 것","의심스러운 제안의 무작위적인 구현을 방지하는 것"],"es":["Validar la corrección técnica de los comentarios de revisión","Aclarar comentarios de revisión de código ambiguos","Evaluar comentarios en función de restricciones específicas de la base de código","Prevenir la implementación ciega de sugerencias cuestionables"],"fr":["Valider la correction technique des commentaires de révision","Clarifier les commentaires de révision de code ambigus","Évaluer les commentaires en fonction de contraintes spécifiques de la base de code","Prévenir la mise en œuvre aveugle de suggestions discutables"],"de":["Die technische Richtigkeit von Review-Feedbacks überprüfen","Mehrdeutige Code-Review-Kommentare klären","Feedbacks anhand spezifischer Codebase-Einschränkungen bewerten","Verhindern eine blinden Implementierung von fragwürdigen Vorschlägen"],"pt":["Validar a correção técnica de feedback de revisão","Esclarecer comentários ambíguos de revisão de código","Avaliar feedback contra restrições específicas da base de código","Prevenir a implementação cega de sugestões questionáveis"],"ru":["Проверка технической правильности обратной связи при проверке","Разъяснение неоднозначных комментариев при проверке кода","Оценка обратной связи с учетом конкретных ограничений базы кода","Предотвращение слепой реализации сомнительных предложений"],"ar":["التحقق من صحة الملاحظات التقنية لمراجعة الكود","إزالة غموض تعليقات مراجعة الكود","تقييم الملاحظات في ضوء القيود المحددة للمجموعة الكودية","منع التنفيذ الأعمى للمقترحات المثيرة للشك"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires full codebase access for verification","Needs technical understanding of codebase context","Depends on clear communication channels with reviewers"],"zh":["需要完全的代码库访问权限以进行验证","需要对代码库上下文有技术上的理解","依赖于与审查者的清晰通信渠道"],"ja":["検証のために完全なコードベースへのアクセスが必要","コードベースのコンテキストに対する技術的な理解が必要","レビューアーとの明確なコミュニケーション チャネルに依存"],"ko":["검증을 위해 완전한 코드베이스에 대한 접근 권한이 필요","코드베이스의 문맥에 대한 기술적인 이해가 필요","리뷰어와의 명확한 의사소통 채널에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso completo a la base de código para la verificación","Necesita comprensión técnica del contexto de la base de código","Depende de canales de comunicación claros con los revisores"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès complet à la base de code pour la vérification","Nécessite une compréhension technique du contexte de la base de code","Dépend de canaux de communication clairs avec les réviseurs"],"de":["Benötigt vollen Zugriff auf die Codebase für die Überprüfung","Benötigt technisches Verständnis des Codebase-Kontexts","Hängt von klaren Kommunikationskanälen mit den Reviewern ab"],"pt":["Requer acesso completo à base de código para verificação","Necessita de compreensão técnica do contexto da base de código","Depende de canais de comunicação claros com revisores"],"ru":["Требует полного доступа к базе кода для проверки","Требует технического понимания контекста базы кода","Зависит от четких каналов связи с рецензентами"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول الكامل إلى مجموعة الكود للتحقق","يحتاج إلى فهم تقني لسياق مجموعة الكود","يعتمد على قنوات اتصال واضحة مع المراجعين"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c9382e92b8f32363566068ecfed19d3b2651eaf40d3942b24840f839dedfc406","repoEtag":"W/\"29bf55250b8f240dcbe9ab5b26295b46f9245d08f7c3ef5107c7cf22c3e2ed5f\"","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/requesting-code-review', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'requesting-code-review', 55427, 4195, 60, '2026-02-20T02:00:37Z', '2026-02-20T02:09:57.710Z', '2da31af22a58938ab78f3ee6d5b4687fcca062b923b646459eb52ba72117ef97', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/requesting-code-review","name":"requesting-code-review","description":{"zh":"请求代码审查是确保代码符合要求的重要步骤，通过早期和频繁的审查来发现问题","ja":"コードレビューのリクエストはコードが要件を満たすことを保証するための重要なステップであり、早期に頻繁に問題を発見する","ko":"코드 리뷰 요청은 코드가 요구 사항을 충족하는지 확인하는 중요한 단계로, 초기에 빈번하게 문제를 발견합니다","es":"La revisión de código es crucial para garantizar la calidad y cumplimiento de los requisitos. Aprende cuándo y cómo solicitar una revisión","fr":"La revue de code est cruciale pour garantir la qualité et le respect des exigences. Découvrez quand et comment demander une revue","de":"Die Code-Review ist entscheidend für die Qualität und Einhaltung der Anforderungen. Erfahren Sie, wann und wie Sie eine Überprüfung anfordern","pt":"A revisão de código é uma prática essencial para garantir a qualidade do seu trabalho. Saiba quando e como solicitar revisões para evitar erros e melhorar a colaboração.","ru":"Код-ревью является необходимой практикой для обеспечения качества своей работы. Узнайте, когда и как запрашивать код-ревью, чтобы избежать ошибок и улучшить сотрудничество.","ar":"مراجعة الكود هي ممارسة أساسية لضمان جودة عملك. تعلم متى وكيفية استدعاء المراجعات لتجنب الأخطاء وتحسين التعاون.","en":"Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55427,"forks":4195,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T02:00:37Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"requesting-code-review","description":"Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements","bodyPreview":"# Requesting Code Review\n\nDispatch superpowers:code-reviewer subagent to catch issues before they cascade.\n\n**Core principle:** Review early, review often.\n\n## When to Request Review\n\n**Mandatory:**\n- After each task in subagent-driven development\n- After completing major feature\n- Before merge to main\n\n**Optional but valuable:**\n- When stuck (fresh perspective)\n- Before refactoring (baseline check)\n- After fixing complex bug\n\n## How to Request\n\n**1. Get git SHAs:**\n```bash\nBASE_SHA=$(git rev-pa","body":"# Requesting Code Review\n\nDispatch superpowers:code-reviewer subagent to catch issues before they cascade.\n\n**Core principle:** Review early, review often.\n\n## When to Request Review\n\n**Mandatory:**\n- After each task in subagent-driven development\n- After completing major feature\n- Before merge to main\n\n**Optional but valuable:**\n- When stuck (fresh perspective)\n- Before refactoring (baseline check)\n- After fixing complex bug\n\n## How to Request\n\n**1. Get git SHAs:**\n```bash\nBASE_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD~1)  # or origin/main\nHEAD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)\n```\n\n**2. Dispatch code-reviewer subagent:**\n\nUse Task tool with superpowers:code-reviewer type, fill template at `code-reviewer.md`\n\n**Placeholders:**\n- `{WHAT_WAS_IMPLEMENTED}` - What you just built\n- `{PLAN_OR_REQUIREMENTS}` - What it should do\n- `{BASE_SHA}` - Starting commit\n- `{HEAD_SHA}` - Ending commit\n- `{DESCRIPTION}` - Brief summary\n\n**3. Act on feedback:**\n- Fix Critical issues immediately\n- Fix Important issues before proceeding\n- Note Minor issues for later\n- Push back if reviewer is wrong (with reasoning)\n\n## Example\n\n```\n[Just completed Task 2: Add verification function]\n\nYou: Let me request code review before proceeding.\n\nBASE_SHA=$(git log --oneline | grep \"Task 1\" | head -1 | awk ''{print $1}'')\nHEAD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)\n\n[Dispatch superpowers:code-reviewer subagent]\n  WHAT_WAS_IMPLEMENTED: Verification and repair functions for conversation index\n  PLAN_OR_REQUIREMENTS: Task 2 from docs/plans/deployment-plan.md\n  BASE_SHA: a7981ec\n  HEAD_SHA: 3df7661\n  DESCRIPTION: Added verifyIndex() and repairIndex() with 4 issue types\n\n[Subagent returns]:\n  Strengths: Clean architecture, real tests\n  Issues:\n    Important: Missing progress indicators\n    Minor: Magic number (100) for reporting interval\n  Assessment: Ready to proceed\n\nYou: [Fix progress indicators]\n[Continue to Task 3]\n```\n\n## Integration with Workflows\n\n**Subagent-Driven Development:**\n- Review after EACH task\n- Catch issues before they compound\n- Fix before moving to next task\n\n**Executing Plans:**\n- Review after each batch (3 tasks)\n- Get feedback, apply, continue\n\n**Ad-Hoc Development:**\n- Review before merge\n- Review when stuck\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Never:**\n- Skip review because \"it''s simple\"\n- Ignore Critical issues\n- Proceed with unfixed Important issues\n- Argue with valid technical feedback\n\n**If reviewer wrong:**\n- Push back with technical reasoning\n- Show code/tests that prove it works\n- Request clarification\n\nSee template at: requesting-code-review/code-reviewer.md\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:09:57.710Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码审查请求","ja":"コードレビューのリクエスト","ko":"코드 리뷰 요청","es":"Revisión de código: Mejora la calidad del código","fr":"Demande de revue de code: Améliorez la qualité du code","de":"Code-Review: Verbessern Sie die Code-Qualität","pt":"Revisão de Código: O Poder do Controle de Qualidade","ru":"Запрос код-ревью: Надежный контроль качества","ar":"استدعاء مراجعة الكود: القوة في ضمان الجودة","en":"requesting-code-review"},"description":{"zh":"请求代码审查是确保代码符合要求的重要步骤，通过早期和频繁的审查来发现问题","ja":"コードレビューのリクエストはコードが要件を満たすことを保証するための重要なステップであり、早期に頻繁に問題を発見する","ko":"코드 리뷰 요청은 코드가 요구 사항을 충족하는지 확인하는 중요한 단계로, 초기에 빈번하게 문제를 발견합니다","es":"La revisión de código es crucial para garantizar la calidad y cumplimiento de los requisitos. Aprende cuándo y cómo solicitar una revisión","fr":"La revue de code est cruciale pour garantir la qualité et le respect des exigences. Découvrez quand et comment demander une revue","de":"Die Code-Review ist entscheidend für die Qualität und Einhaltung der Anforderungen. Erfahren Sie, wann und wie Sie eine Überprüfung anfordern","pt":"A revisão de código é uma prática essencial para garantir a qualidade do seu trabalho. Saiba quando e como solicitar revisões para evitar erros e melhorar a ...","ru":"Код-ревью является необходимой практикой для обеспечения качества своей работы. Узнайте, когда и как запрашивать код-ревью, чтобы избежать ошибок и улучшить ...","ar":"مراجعة الكود هي ممارسة أساسية لضمان جودة عملك. تعلم متى وكيفية استدعاء المراجعات لتجنب الأخطاء وتحسين التعاون.","en":"Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements"},"definition":{"en":"Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements"},"features":{"zh":["早期和频繁的审查","减少错误和缺陷","提高代码质量","确保工作符合要求","增强团队合作和沟通"],"ja":["早期に頻繁にレビュー","エラーと欠陥の削減","コードの品質の向上","要件を満たすことを保証","チームワークとコミュニケーションの強化"],"ko":["초기와 빈번한 검토","오류와 결함의 감소","코드 품질의 향상","요구 사항을 충족하는 것을 보장","팀 협업과 의사 소통의 강화"],"es":["Revisión temprana y frecuente","Detección de errores antes de la implementación","Mejora de la calidad del código","Cumplimiento de los requisitos","Colaboración en equipo"],"fr":["Revue précoce et fréquente","Détection des erreurs avant la mise en œuvre","Amélioration de la qualité du code","Respect des exigences","Collaboration d''équipe"],"de":["Frühe und häufige Überprüfung","Fehlererkennung vor der Implementierung","Qualitätsverbesserung des Codes","Einhaltung der Anforderungen","Teamzusammenarbeit"],"pt":["Detecção de erros e bugs","Melhoria da legibilidade e manutenção do código","Garantia de conformidade com os padrões","Colaboração e feedback entre desenvolvedores","Otimização do processo de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Обнаружение ошибок и багов","Улучшение читаемости и поддержки кода","Обеспечение соответствия стандартам","Сотрудничество и обратная связь между разработчиками","Оптимизация процесса разработки"],"ar":["اكتشاف الأخطاء والعيوب","تحسين القراءة وضمان صيانة الكود","ضمان المطابقة للمعايير","التعاون والتعليقات بين المطورين","تحسين عملية التطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码质量","代码检查","开发流程","团队合作","代码管理","软件开发","代码优化"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード品質","コードチェック","開発プロセス","チームワーク","コード管理","ソフトウェア開発","コード最適化"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 품질","코드 검토","개발 프로세스","팀 협업","코드 관리","소프트웨어 개발","코드 최적화"],"es":["revisión de código","calidad del código","cumplimiento de requisitos","desarrollo de software","colaboración en equipo","mejora de la calidad"],"fr":["revue de code","qualité du code","respect des exigences","développement de logiciels","collaboration d''équipe","amélioration de la qualité"],"de":["Code-Review","Code-Qualität","Einhaltung der Anforderungen","Software-Entwicklung","Teamzusammenarbeit","Qualitätsverbesserung"],"pt":["revisão de código","controle de qualidade","desenvolvimento de software","colaboração em equipe","melhoria da legibilidade","detecção de erros"],"ru":["код-ревью","контроль качества","разработка программного обеспечения","командное сотрудничество","улучшение читаемости","обнаружение ошибок"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود","ضبط الجودة","تطوير البرمجيات","التعاون الفريق","تحسين القراءة","اكتشاف الأخطاء"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents needing to verify work meets requirements through git SHA comparisons and subagent-driven development","zh":"适用于需要通过git SHA比较和子代理驱动开发来验证工作是否符合要求的代码审查代理的理想选择","ja":"コードレビュー代理が要件を満たしていることを確認するためにgit SHAの比較とサブエージェント駆動開発を必要とするコードレビュー代理に最適","ko":"코드 리뷰 에이전트가 작업이 요구 사항을 충족하는지 확인하기 위해 git SHA 비교 및 하위 에이전트 주도 개발을 필요로 할 때 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan verificar que el trabajo cumple con los requisitos a través de comparaciones de SHA de git y desarrollo impulsado por subagentes","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de révision de code ayant besoin de vérifier que le travail répond aux exigences via des comparaisons de SHA Git et un développement piloté par des sous-agents","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agenten, die prüfen müssen, ob die Arbeit die Anforderungen durch Git-SHA-Vergleiche und subagentengetriebene Entwicklung erfüllt","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que precisam verificar se o trabalho atende aos requisitos por meio de comparações de SHA do git e desenvolvimento impulsionado por subagentes","ru":"Идеально для агентов проверки кода, которым необходимо проверить, соответствует ли работа требованиям через сравнения SHA git и разработку, управляемую субагентами","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى التحقق من أن العمل يلبي المتطلبات من خلال مقارنات SHA git و التطوير المدفوع بالعميل الفرعي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to catch issues before they cascade by dispatching a code-reviewer subagent, utilizing git rev-parse for SHA retrieval and ensuring compliance with core principles like reviewing early and often","zh":"使代理能够在问题扩散之前捕获问题，方法是调度代码审查子代理，利用git rev-parse检索SHA并确保遵守像早期和经常审查这样的核心原则","ja":"エージェントが問題を早期に検知できるようにすることで、コードレビューサブエージェントを派遣し、git rev-parseを使用してSHAを取得し、早くて頻繁にレビューするなどのコアプリンシプルに準拠する","ko":"에이전트가 코드를 검토하는 서브 에이전트를派遣하고 git rev-parse를 사용하여 SHA를 가져오고 早期에 그리고 자주 검토하는 것과 같은 핵심 원칙을 준수하여 문제가 확산되기 전에 문제를 捕获 할 수 있도록 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a detectar problemas antes de que se produzcan cascadas, mediante el envío de un subagente de revisión de código, utilizando git rev-parse para la recuperación de SHA y garantizando el cumplimiento de principios básicos como la revisión temprana y frecuente","fr":"Permet aux agents de détecter les problèmes avant qu''ils ne se propagent en dépêchant un sous-agent de révision de code, en utilisant git rev-parse pour la récupération de SHA et en garantissant le respect de principes fondamentaux tels que la révision précoce et fréquente","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Probleme zu erkennen, bevor sie sich ausbreiten, indem sie einen Code-Reviewer-Subagenten entsenden, git rev-parse zur SHA-Abrufung verwenden und die Einhaltung von Grundprinzipien wie früher und häufiger Überprüfung sicherstellen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a capturar problemas antes que eles se propaguem, enviando um subagente revisor de código, utilizando git rev-parse para recuperação de SHA e garantindo o cumprimento de princípios básicos como revisar cedo e frequentemente","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обнаруживать проблемы до их распространения, отправляя субагент-ревьювер кода, используя git rev-parse для извлечения SHA и обеспечивая соблюдение основных принципов, таких как ранний и частый обзор","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التقاط المشاكل قبل انتشارها من خلال إرسال عميل فرعي لمراجعة الكود، باستخدام git rev-parse لاسترجاع SHA وضمان الامتثال للمبادئ الأساسية مثل المراجعة المبكرة والمكررة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code review requests after completing tasks","Debugging complex bugs before merging to main","Validating major feature implementations"],"zh":["任务完成后自动执行代码审查请求","调试合并到主分支之前的复杂错误","验证主要功能实现"],"ja":["タスクの完了後にコードレビューのリクエストを自動化する","メインブランチにマージする前に複雑なバグをデバッグする","主要な機能の実装を検証する"],"ko":["작업을 완료한 후 코드 리뷰 요청을 자동화","메인 브랜치로 병합하기 전에 복잡한 버그를 디버깅","주요 기능 구현을 검증"],"es":["Automatizar solicitudes de revisión de código después de completar tareas","Depurar errores complejos antes de fusionarlos con la rama principal","Validar implementaciones de características principales"],"fr":["Automatiser les demandes de révision de code après avoir terminé les tâches","Déboguer des bogues complexes avant de les fusionner avec la branche principale","Valider les mises en œuvre de fonctionnalités principales"],"de":["Automatisieren von Code-Review-Anfragen nach Abschluss von Aufgaben","Komplexe Fehler beheben, bevor sie mit dem Hauptzweig zusammengeführt werden","Validieren von Implementierungen wichtiger Funktionen"],"pt":["Automatizar solicitações de revisão de código após concluir tarefas","Depurar bugs complexos antes de mesclar com o principal","Validar implementações de recursos principais"],"ru":["Автоматизировать запросы на проверку кода после выполнения задач","Отладить сложные ошибки перед слиянием с основным","Проверить реализацию основных функций"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي في طلبات مراجعة الكود بعد إكمال المهام","تصحيح الأخطاء المعقدة قبل الدمج مع الرئيسي","التحقق من تنفيذ الميزات الرئيسية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git access","Subagent-driven development environment needed","Limited to code review use cases"],"zh":["需要git访问权限","需要子代理驱动的开发环境","仅限代码审查用例"],"ja":["gitへのアクセスが必要","サブエージェント駆動の開発環境が必要","コードレビューのユースケースに限定"],"ko":["git에 접근해야 함","하위 에이전트 주도 개발 환경이 필요","코드 리뷰 유즈 케이스에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere acceso a git","Se necesita un entorno de desarrollo impulsado por subagentes","Limitado a casos de uso de revisión de código"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à Git","Un environnement de développement piloté par des sous-agents est nécessaire","Limité aux cas d''utilisation de la révision de code"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Zugriff","Ein subagentengetriebenes Entwicklungsumfeld ist erforderlich","Begrenzt auf Code-Review-Use-Cases"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao git","Ambiente de desenvolvimento impulsionado por subagente necessário","Limitado a casos de uso de revisão de código"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к git","Необходимо окружение разработки, управляемое субагентом","Ограничен для случаев использования проверки кода"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى جيت","بيئة التطوير المدفوعة بالعميل الفرعي ضرورية","محدود لケース استخدام مراجعة الكود"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"2da31af22a58938ab78f3ee6d5b4687fcca062b923b646459eb52ba72117ef97","repoEtag":"W/\"29bf55250b8f240dcbe9ab5b26295b46f9245d08f7c3ef5107c7cf22c3e2ed5f\"","qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/subagent-driven-development', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'subagent-driven-development', 55427, 4195, 95, '2026-02-20T02:00:37Z', '2026-02-20T02:11:07.688Z', '994b89a5d294eadd6a1611edb51377bac748d5f5fb7f4139d3c736b616b3a46a', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/subagent-driven-development","name":"subagent-driven-development","description":{"zh":"子代理驱动开发是一种高效的开发方法，通过分配独立任务和两阶段审查来实现快速迭代","ja":"サブエージェント駆動開発は、独立したタスクと二段階のレビューを通じて高速イテレーションを実現する開発方法です","ko":"서브 에이전트 주도 개발은 독립적인 태스크와 2단계 리뷰를 통해 빠른 반복을实现하는 개발 방법입니다","es":"El desarrollo impulsado por subagentes es una técnica para ejecutar planes de implementación de manera eficiente","fr":"Le développement piloté par sous-agents est une technique pour exécuter des plans d''implémentation de manière efficace","de":"Die subagenten-getriebene Entwicklung ist eine Technik, um Implementierungspläne effizient auszuführen","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por subagentes é uma abordagem para executar planos de implementação com tarefas independentes","ru":"Разработка на основе субагентов - это подход к выполнению планов реализации с независимыми задачами","ar":"التطوير الموجه بواسطة وكلاء فرعيين هو نهج لتنفيذ خطط التنفيذ بالمهام المستقلة","en":"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55427,"forks":4195,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T02:00:37Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"subagent-driven-development","description":"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session","bodyPreview":"# Subagent-Driven Development\n\nExecute plan by dispatching fresh subagent per task, with two-stage review after each: spec compliance review first, then code quality review.\n\n**Core principle:** Fresh subagent per task + two-stage review (spec then quality) = high quality, fast iteration\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Have implementation plan?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Tasks mostly independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Stay in this session?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"subagent-driven-d","body":"# Subagent-Driven Development\n\nExecute plan by dispatching fresh subagent per task, with two-stage review after each: spec compliance review first, then code quality review.\n\n**Core principle:** Fresh subagent per task + two-stage review (spec then quality) = high quality, fast iteration\n\n## When to Use\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_to_use {\n    \"Have implementation plan?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Tasks mostly independent?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Stay in this session?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"subagent-driven-development\" [shape=box];\n    \"executing-plans\" [shape=box];\n    \"Manual execution or brainstorm first\" [shape=box];\n\n    \"Have implementation plan?\" -> \"Tasks mostly independent?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Have implementation plan?\" -> \"Manual execution or brainstorm first\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Tasks mostly independent?\" -> \"Stay in this session?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Tasks mostly independent?\" -> \"Manual execution or brainstorm first\" [label=\"no - tightly coupled\"];\n    \"Stay in this session?\" -> \"subagent-driven-development\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Stay in this session?\" -> \"executing-plans\" [label=\"no - parallel session\"];\n}\n```\n\n**vs. Executing Plans (parallel session):**\n- Same session (no context switch)\n- Fresh subagent per task (no context pollution)\n- Two-stage review after each task: spec compliance first, then code quality\n- Faster iteration (no human-in-loop between tasks)\n\n## The Process\n\n```dot\ndigraph process {\n    rankdir=TB;\n\n    subgraph cluster_per_task {\n        label=\"Per Task\";\n        \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\" [shape=box];\n        \"Implementer subagent asks questions?\" [shape=diamond];\n        \"Answer questions, provide context\" [shape=box];\n        \"Implementer subagent implements, tests, commits, self-reviews\" [shape=box];\n        \"Dispatch spec reviewer subagent (./spec-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [shape=box];\n        \"Spec reviewer subagent confirms code matches spec?\" [shape=diamond];\n        \"Implementer subagent fixes spec gaps\" [shape=box];\n        \"Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent (./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [shape=box];\n        \"Code quality reviewer subagent approves?\" [shape=diamond];\n        \"Implementer subagent fixes quality issues\" [shape=box];\n        \"Mark task complete in TodoWrite\" [shape=box];\n    }\n\n    \"Read plan, extract all tasks with full text, note context, create TodoWrite\" [shape=box];\n    \"More tasks remain?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Dispatch final code reviewer subagent for entire implementation\" [shape=box];\n    \"Use superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch\" [shape=box style=filled fillcolor=lightgreen];\n\n    \"Read plan, extract all tasks with full text, note context, create TodoWrite\" -> \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\";\n    \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\" -> \"Implementer subagent asks questions?\";\n    \"Implementer subagent asks questions?\" -> \"Answer questions, provide context\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Answer questions, provide context\" -> \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\";\n    \"Implementer subagent asks questions?\" -> \"Implementer subagent implements, tests, commits, self-reviews\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Implementer subagent implements, tests, commits, self-reviews\" -> \"Dispatch spec reviewer subagent (./spec-reviewer-prompt.md)\";\n    \"Dispatch spec reviewer subagent (./spec-reviewer-prompt.md)\" -> \"Spec reviewer subagent confirms code matches spec?\";\n    \"Spec reviewer subagent confirms code matches spec?\" -> \"Implementer subagent fixes spec gaps\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Implementer subagent fixes spec gaps\" -> \"Dispatch spec reviewer subagent (./spec-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [label=\"re-review\"];\n    \"Spec reviewer subagent confirms code matches spec?\" -> \"Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent (./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent (./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md)\" -> \"Code quality reviewer subagent approves?\";\n    \"Code quality reviewer subagent approves?\" -> \"Implementer subagent fixes quality issues\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Implementer subagent fixes quality issues\" -> \"Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent (./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md)\" [label=\"re-review\"];\n    \"Code quality reviewer subagent approves?\" -> \"Mark task complete in TodoWrite\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Mark task complete in TodoWrite\" -> \"More tasks remain?\";\n    \"More tasks remain?\" -> \"Dispatch implementer subagent (./implementer-prompt.md)\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"More tasks remain?\" -> \"Dispatch final code reviewer subagent for entire implementation\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Dispatch final code reviewer subagent for entire implementation\" -> \"Use superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch\";\n}\n```\n\n## Prompt Templates\n\n- `./implementer-prompt.md` - Dispatch implementer subagent\n- `./spec-reviewer-prompt.md` - Dispatch spec compliance reviewer subagent\n- `./code-quality-reviewer-prompt.md` - Dispatch code quality reviewer subagent\n\n## Example Workflow\n\n```\nYou: I''m using Subagent-Driven Development to execute this plan.\n\n[Read plan file once: docs/plans/feature-plan.md]\n[Extract all 5 tasks with full text and context]\n[Create TodoWrite with all tasks]\n\nTask 1: Hook installation script\n\n[Get Task 1 text and context (already extracted)]\n[Dispatch implementation subagent with full task text + context]\n\nImplementer: \"Before I begin - should the hook be installed at user or system level?\"\n\nYou: \"User level (~/.config/superpowers/hooks/)\"\n\nImplementer: \"Got it. Implementing now...\"\n[Later] Implementer:\n  - Implemented install-hook command\n  - Added tests, 5/5 passing\n  - Self-review: Found I missed --force flag, added it\n  - Committed\n\n[Dispatch spec compliance reviewer]\nSpec reviewer: ✅ Spec compliant - all requirements met, nothing extra\n\n[Get git SHAs, dispatch code quality reviewer]\nCode reviewer: Strengths: Good test coverage, clean. Issues: None. Approved.\n\n[Mark Task 1 complete]\n\nTask 2: Recovery modes\n\n[Get Task 2 text and context (already extracted)]\n[Dispatch implementation subagent with full task text + context]\n\nImplementer: [No questions, proceeds]\nImplementer:\n  - Added verify/repair modes\n  - 8/8 tests passing\n  - Self-review: All good\n  - Committed\n\n[Dispatch spec compliance reviewer]\nSpec reviewer: ❌ Issues:\n  - Missing: Progress reporting (spec says \"report every 100 items\")\n  - Extra: Added --json flag (not requested)\n\n[Implementer fixes issues]\nImplementer: Removed --json flag, added progress reporting\n\n[Spec reviewer reviews again]\nSpec reviewer: ✅ Spec compliant now\n\n[Dispatch code quality reviewer]\nCode reviewer: Strengths: Solid. Issues (Important): Magic number (100)\n\n[Implementer fixes]\nImplementer: Extracted PROGRESS_INTERVAL constant\n\n[Code reviewer reviews again]\nCode reviewer: ✅ Approved\n\n[Mark Task 2 complete]\n\n...\n\n[After all tasks]\n[Dispatch final code-reviewer]\nFinal reviewer: All requirements met, ready to merge\n\nDone!\n```\n\n## Advantages\n\n**vs. Manual execution:**\n- Subagents follow TDD naturally\n- Fresh context per task (no confusion)\n- Parallel-safe (subagents don''t interfere)\n- Subagent can ask questions (before AND during work)\n\n**vs. Executing Plans:**\n- Same session (no handoff)\n- Continuous progress (no waiting)\n- Review checkpoints automatic\n\n**Efficiency gains:**\n- No file reading overhead (controller provides full text)\n- Controller curates exactly what context is needed\n- Subagent gets complete information upfront\n- Questions surfaced before work begins (not after)\n\n**Quality gates:**\n- Self-review catches issues before handoff\n- Two-stage review: spec compliance, then code quality\n- Review loops ensure fixes actually work\n- Spec compliance prevents over/under-building\n- Code quality ensures implementation is well-built\n\n**Cost:**\n- More subagent invocations (implementer + 2 reviewers per task)\n- Controller does more prep work (extracting all tasks upfront)\n- Review loops add iterations\n- But catches issues early (cheaper than debugging later)\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Never:**\n- Start implementation on main/master branch without explicit user consent\n- Skip reviews (spec compliance OR code quality)\n- Proceed with unfixed issues\n- Dispatch multiple implementation subagents in parallel (conflicts)\n- Make subagent read plan file (provide full text instead)\n- Skip scene-setting context (subagent needs to understand where task fits)\n- Ignore subagent questions (answer before letting them proceed)\n- Accept \"close enough\" on spec compliance (spec reviewer found issues = not done)\n- Skip review loops (reviewer found issues = implementer fixes = review again)\n- Let implementer self-review replace actual review (both are needed)\n- **Start code quality review before spec compliance is ✅** (wrong order)\n- Move to next task while either review has open issues\n\n**If subagent asks questions:**\n- Answer clearly and completely\n- Provide additional context if needed\n- Don''t rush them into implementation\n\n**If reviewer finds issues:**\n- Implementer (same subagent) fixes them\n- Reviewer reviews again\n- Repeat until approved\n- Don''t skip the re-review\n\n**If subagent fails task:**\n- Dispatch fix subagent with specific instructions\n- Don''t try to fix manually (context pollution)\n\n## Integration\n\n**Required workflow skills:**\n- **superpowers:using-git-worktrees** - REQUIRED: Set up isolated workspace before starting\n- **superpowers:writing-plans** - Creates the plan this skill executes\n- **superpowers:requesting-code-review** - Code review template for reviewer subagents\n- **superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch** - Complete development after all tasks\n\n**Subagents should use:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - Subagents follow TDD for each task\n\n**Alternative workflow:**\n- **superpowers:executing-plans** - Use for parallel session instead of same-session execution\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:11:07.688Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"子代理驱动开发 - 高效迭代开发方法","ja":"サブエージェント駆動開発 - 高速イテレーション開発方法","ko":"서브 에이전트 주도 개발 - 효율적인 반복 개발 방법","es":"Desarrollo impulsado por subagentes","fr":"Développement piloté par sous-agents","de":"Subagenten-getriebene Entwicklung","pt":"Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Subagentes","ru":"Разработка на основе субагентов","ar":"التطوير الموجه بواسطة وكلاء فرعيين","en":"subagent-driven-development"},"description":{"zh":"子代理驱动开发是一种高效的开发方法，通过分配独立任务和两阶段审查来实现快速迭代","ja":"サブエージェント駆動開発は、独立したタスクと二段階のレビューを通じて高速イテレーションを実現する開発方法です","ko":"서브 에이전트 주도 개발은 독립적인 태스크와 2단계 리뷰를 통해 빠른 반복을实现하는 개발 방법입니다","es":"El desarrollo impulsado por subagentes es una técnica para ejecutar planes de implementación de manera eficiente","fr":"Le développement piloté par sous-agents est une technique pour exécuter des plans d''implémentation de manière efficace","de":"Die subagenten-getriebene Entwicklung ist eine Technik, um Implementierungspläne effizient auszuführen","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por subagentes é uma abordagem para executar planos de implementação com tarefas independentes","ru":"Разработка на основе субагентов - это подход к выполнению планов реализации с независимыми задачами","ar":"التطوير الموجه بواسطة وكلاء فرعيين هو نهج لتنفيذ خطط التنفيذ بالمهام المستقلة","en":"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session"},"definition":{"en":"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session"},"features":{"zh":["独立任务分配","两阶段审查","快速迭代","高效开发","代码质量保证"],"ja":["独立したタスクの割り当て","二段階のレビュー","高速イテレーション","効率的な開発","コード品質の保証"],"ko":["독립적인 태스크 할당","2단계 리뷰","빠른 반복","효율적인 개발","코드 품질 보장"],"es":["Ejecución de planes de implementación","Tareas independientes","Revisión de dos etapas","Subagentes frescos por tarea","Iteración rápida y de alta calidad"],"fr":["Exécution de plans d''implémentation","Tâches indépendantes","Revue en deux étapes","Sous-agents frais par tâche","Itération rapide et de haute qualité"],"de":["Ausführung von Implementierungsplänen","Unabhängige Aufgaben","Zweistufige Überprüfung","Frische Subagenten pro Aufgabe","Schnelle und hochwertige Iteration"],"pt":["Execução de planos de implementação com tarefas independentes","Utilização de subagentes para executar tarefas","Revisão em duas etapas: conformidade com especificações e qualidade do código","Iteração rápida e de alta qualidade","Desenvolvimento de software eficiente"],"ru":["Выполнение планов реализации с независимыми задачами","Использование субагентов для выполнения задач","Проверка в два этапа: соответствие спецификациям и качество кода","Быстрая и качественная итерация","Эффективное развитие программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تنفيذ خطط التنفيذ بالمهام المستقلة","استخدام وكلاء فرعيين لتنفيذ المهام","استعراض في مرحلتين: مطابقة للمواصفات وجودة الشفرة","تكرار سريع وذو جودة عالية","تطوير برمجيات فعال"]},"keywords":{"zh":["子代理驱动开发","高效开发","快速迭代","代码质量","独立任务","两阶段审查"],"ja":["サブエージェント駆動開発","効率的な開発","高速イテレーション","コード品質","独立したタスク","二段階のレビュー"],"ko":["서브 에이전트 주도 개발","효율적인 개발","빠른 반복","코드 품질","독립적인 태스크","2단계 리뷰"],"es":["desarrollo de software","implementación de planes","tareas independientes","revisión de dos etapas","subagentes","iteración rápida","calidad del código"],"fr":["développement de logiciels","implémentation de plans","tâches indépendantes","revue en deux étapes","sous-agents","itération rapide","qualité du code"],"de":["Software-Entwicklung","Implementierung von Plänen","unabhängige Aufgaben","zweistufige Überprüfung","Subagenten","schnelle Iteration","Code-Qualität"],"pt":["desenvolvimento dirigido por subagentes","subagentes","tarefas independentes","plano de implementação","revisão em duas etapas","qualidade do código","iteração rápida","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["разработка на основе субагентов","субагенты","независимые задачи","план реализации","проверка в два этапа","качество кода","быстрая итерация","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["التطوير الموجه بواسطة وكلاء فرعيين","وكلاء فرعيين","مهام مستقلة","خطة التنفيذ","استعراض في مرحلتين","جودة الشفرة","تكرار سريع","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Autonomous Agents requiring efficient task execution and review processes, such as those utilizing subagent-driven development for independent task management.","zh":"适用于需要高效任务执行和审查流程的自治代理，例如使用子代理驱动的开发来进行独立任务管理。","ja":"タスクの実行とレビューのプロセスを効率的に行う必要がある自律エージェントに適しています。たとえば、独立したタスク管理のためにサブエージェント駆動開発を使用する場合などです。","ko":"효율적인 작업 실행 및 검토 프로세스가 필요한 자율 에이전트에 적합합니다. 예를 들어 독립적인 작업 관리를 위해 하위 에이전트 주도 개발을 사용하는 경우와 같은 경우입니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Autónomos que requieren una ejecución de tareas y procesos de revisión eficientes, como aquellos que utilizan el desarrollo impulsado por subagentes para la gestión de tareas independientes.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents Autonomes nécessitant une exécution de tâches et des processus de révision efficaces, tels que ceux utilisant le développement piloté par des sous-agents pour la gestion de tâches indépendantes.","de":"Ideal für autonome Agenten, die eine effiziente Aufgabenausführung und Überprüfungsprozesse erfordern, wie z.B. solche, die die subagentengetriebene Entwicklung für die unabhängige Aufgabenverwaltung nutzen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Autônomos que requerem execução e processos de revisão de tarefas eficientes, como aqueles que utilizam desenvolvimento impulsionado por subagentes para gerenciamento de tarefas independentes.","ru":"Идеально для автономных агентов, требующих эффективного выполнения задач и процессов проверки, таких как те, которые используют разработку, управляемую субагентами, для независимого управления задачами.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأوتوماتيكيين الذين يتطلبون تنفيذًا وعمليات مراجعة فعالة لل任务، مثل أولئك الذين يستخدمون تطويرًا مدفوعًا بالوكيل الفرعي لتدبير المهام المستقلة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute implementation plans with fresh subagents per task, leveraging two-stage review processes for spec compliance and code quality, ensuring high-quality and fast iteration cycles through dispatching and reviewing tasks efficiently.","zh":"赋予代理执行实现计划的能力，每个任务都使用新的子代理，并利用两阶段审查流程来确保规格合规性和代码质量，从而通过高效地调度和审查任务来实现高质量和快速的迭代周期。","ja":"エージェントに実装計画を実行する能力を与え、各タスクに新しいサブエージェントを使用し、仕様の準拠性とコード品質の向上を目的とした2段階のレビュー処理を利用することで、高品質で迅速なイテレーションサイクルを実現します。","ko":"에이전트에 구현 계획을 실행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며 각 작업에 새로운 하위 에이전트를 사용하고 규격 준수 및 코드 품질을 위한 2단계 검토 프로세스를 활용하여 높은 품질과 빠른 반복 주기를 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar planes de implementación con subagentes frescos por tarea, aprovechando procesos de revisión de dos etapas para el cumplimiento de especificaciones y la calidad del código, garantizando así ciclos de iteración de alta calidad y rápida ejecución mediante la asignación y revisión eficientes de tareas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des plans de mise en œuvre avec des sous-agents frais par tâche, en exploitant des processus de révision en deux étapes pour la conformité aux spécifications et la qualité du code, assurant ainsi des cycles d''itération de haute qualité et une exécution rapide grâce à l''envoi et à la révision efficaces des tâches.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Umsetzungspläne mit frischen Subagenten pro Aufgabe auszuführen, indem sie zweistufige Überprüfungsprozesse für Spezifikationskonformität und Codequalität nutzen, und so hochwertige und schnelle Iterationszyklen durch effizientes Dispatching und Überprüfen von Aufgaben gewährleisten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar planos de implementação com subagentes frescos por tarefa, aproveitando processos de revisão em duas etapas para conformidade com especificações e qualidade de código, garantindo ciclos de iteração de alta qualidade e rápidos por meio do despacho e revisão eficientes de tarefas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять планы реализации с свежими субагентами для каждой задачи, используя двухэтапные процессы проверки для соблюдения спецификаций и качества кода, обеспечивая высококачественные и быстрые циклы итерации за счет эффективного распределения и проверки задач.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تنفيذ خطط التنفيذ مع وكلاء فرعيين جدد لكل مهمة، مستفيدًا من عمليات المراجعة على مرحلتين للامتثال للمواصفات وجودة الشفرة، مما يضمن دورات التكرار عالية الجودة والسرعة من خلال إرسال ومراجعة المهام بفعالية."},"useCases":{"en":["Executing multi-task implementation plans within a single session","Dispatching independent tasks to fresh subagents for parallel processing","Implementing two-stage review processes for enhanced spec compliance and code quality"],"zh":["在单一会话中执行多任务实现计划","将独立任务分派给新的子代理进行并行处理","实施两阶段审查流程以增强规格合规性和代码质量"],"ja":["単一セッション内で多タスクの実装計画を実行する","独立したタスクを新しいサブエージェントに割り当てて並列処理を行う","仕様の準拠性とコード品質の向上を目的とした2段階のレビュー処理を実施する"],"ko":["단일 세션 내에서 다중 작업 구현 계획을 실행하는 것","독립적인 작업을 새로운 하위 에이전트에 할당하여 병렬 처리를 수행하는 것","규격 준수 및 코드 품질을 향상시키기 위한 2단계 검토 프로세스를 구현하는 것"],"es":["Ejecutar planes de implementación de varias tareas dentro de una sola sesión","Enviar tareas independientes a subagentes frescos para el procesamiento paralelo","Implementar procesos de revisión de dos etapas para una mayor conformidad con las especificaciones y la calidad del código"],"fr":["Exécuter des plans de mise en œuvre de plusieurs tâches au sein d''une seule session","Envoyer des tâches indépendantes à des sous-agents frais pour un traitement parallèle","Mettre en œuvre des processus de révision en deux étapes pour une meilleure conformité aux spécifications et à la qualité du code"],"de":["Ausführen von Umsetzungsplänen für mehrere Aufgaben innerhalb einer einzigen Sitzung","Unabhängige Aufgaben an frische Subagenten für paralleles Verarbeiten senden","Implementieren von zweistufigen Überprüfungsprozessen für eine verbesserte Spezifikationskonformität und Codequalität"],"pt":["Executando planos de implementação multi-tarefa dentro de uma única sessão","Envio de tarefas independentes para subagentes frescos para processamento paralelo","Implementação de processos de revisão em duas etapas para conformidade melhorada com especificações e qualidade de código"],"ru":["Выполнение планов реализации с несколькими задачами в рамках одной сессии","Распределение независимых задач между свежими субагентами для параллельной обработки","Реализация двухэтапных процессов проверки для повышения соблюдения спецификаций и качества кода"],"ar":["تنفيذ خطط التنفيذ متعددة المهام داخل جلسة واحدة","إرسال مهام مستقلة إلى وكلاء فرعيين جدد لمعالجة متوازية","تنفيذ عمليات المراجعة على مرحلتين لتحسين الامتثال للمواصفات وجودة الشفرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires ability to dispatch and manage subagents","Limited to tasks that can be executed independently within a single session"],"zh":["需要能够调度和管理子代理","仅限于可以在单一会话中独立执行的任务"],"ja":["サブエージェントを割り当てて管理する能力が必要","単一セッション内で独立して実行可能なタスクに限定される"],"ko":["하위 에이전트를 할당하고 관리할 수 있는 능력이 필요","단일 세션 내에서 독립적으로 실행할 수 있는 작업으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere la capacidad de enviar y gestionar subagentes","Limitado a tareas que se pueden ejecutar de forma independiente dentro de una sola sesión"],"fr":["Nécessite la capacité d''envoyer et de gérer des sous-agents","Limité aux tâches qui peuvent être exécutées de manière indépendante au sein d''une seule session"],"de":["Erfordert die Fähigkeit, Subagenten zu senden und zu verwalten","Begrenzt auf Aufgaben, die unabhängig innerhalb einer einzigen Sitzung ausgeführt werden können"],"pt":["Requer capacidade de despachar e gerenciar subagentes","Limitado a tarefas que podem ser executadas independentemente dentro de uma única sessão"],"ru":["Требует способности распределять и управлять субагентами","Ограничен задачами, которые могут быть выполнены независимо в рамках одной сессии"],"ar":["يتطلب القدرة على إرسال وإدارة الوكلاء الفرعيين","محدود بالمهام التي يمكن تنفيذها بشكل مستقل داخل جلسة واحدة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"994b89a5d294eadd6a1611edb51377bac748d5f5fb7f4139d3c736b616b3a46a","repoEtag":"W/\"29bf55250b8f240dcbe9ab5b26295b46f9245d08f7c3ef5107c7cf22c3e2ed5f\"","qualityScore":95}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/systematic-debugging', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'systematic-debugging', 55427, 4195, 90, '2026-02-20T02:00:37Z', '2026-02-20T02:12:07.939Z', '4999cb851360485eca5074e727bbdd62ef20549c5d5b01216fcbf5831badb473', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种科学的调试方法，强调找到根因在提出解决方案之前","ja":"体系的デバッグは、根本原因を特定する前に解決策を提案しないという科学的デバッグ方法です","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 찾은 후에 해결 방안을 제안하는 科学的な 디버깅 방법입니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque metódico para identificar y solucionar errores. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones.","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche méthodique pour identifier et résoudre les erreurs. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions.","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein methodischer Ansatz, um Fehler zu identifizieren und zu beheben. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen vorschlagen.","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem metódica para identificar e resolver problemas, garantindo que as soluções sejam eficazes e duradouras.","ru":"Систематическая отладка - это методический подход к выявлению и решению проблем, гарантирующий, что решения будут эффективными и долговечными.","ar":"حلل بطرق系统ية هو نهج منهجي لتحديد ومعالجة المشاكل، يضمن أن الحلول تكون فعالة ومستدامة.","en":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55427,"forks":4195,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T02:00:37Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:12:07.939Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"系统调试方法","ja":"体系的デバッグ","ko":"시스템 디버깅","es":"Depuración Sistemática: Encuentra la Causa Raíz","fr":"Débogage Systématique: Trouver la Cause Profonde","de":"Systematische Fehlersuche: Finde die Ursache","pt":"Depuração Sistemática: Encontre a Causa Raiz","ru":"Систематическая отладка: найдите корневую причину","ar":"حلل بطرق系统ية: اكتشف السبب الجذري","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种科学的调试方法，强调找到根因在提出解决方案之前","ja":"体系的デバッグは、根本原因を特定する前に解決策を提案しないという科学的デバッグ方法です","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 찾은 후에 해결 방안을 제안하는 科学的な 디버깅 방법입니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque metódico para identificar y solucionar errores. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones.","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche méthodique pour identifier et résoudre les erreurs. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant de proposer des soluti...","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein methodischer Ansatz, um Fehler zu identifizieren und zu beheben. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen vorsc...","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem metódica para identificar e resolver problemas, garantindo que as soluções sejam eficazes e duradouras.","ru":"Систематическая отладка - это методический подход к выявлению и решению проблем, гарантирующий, что решения будут эффективными и долговечными.","ar":"حلل بطرق系统ية هو نهج منهجي لتحديد ومعالجة المشاكل، يضمن أن الحلول تكون فعالة ومستدامة.","en":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes"},"definition":{"en":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes"},"features":{"zh":["找到根因","提高调试效率","减少新bug的产生","遵循铁律","适用于任何技术问题"],"ja":["根本原因を特定する","デバッグの効率を高める","新しいバグの発生を減らす","鉄則に従う","すべての技術的な問題に適用可能"],"ko":["근본 원인을 찾기","디버깅 효율을 높이기","새로운 버그 발생을 줄이기","철칙을 준수하기","모든 기술적인 문제에 적용 가능"],"es":["Identifica la causa raíz de los errores","Evita soluciones temporales","Mejora la eficiencia del proceso de desarrollo","Reduce el tiempo de depuración","Garantiza soluciones efectivas"],"fr":["Identifie la cause profonde des erreurs","Évite les solutions temporaires","Améliore l''efficacité du processus de développement","Réduit le temps de débogage","Garantit des solutions efficaces"],"de":["Identifiziert die Ursache von Fehlern","Vermeidet temporäre Lösungen","Verbessert die Effizienz des Entwicklungsprozesses","Reduziert die Fehlerbehebungszeit","Garantiert effektive Lösungen"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz","Abordagem metódica","Resolução eficaz de problemas","Prevenção de novos bugs","Melhoria da qualidade do código"],"ru":["Выявление корневой причины","Методический подход","Эффективное решение проблем","Предотвращение новых ошибок","Улучшение качества кода"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري","نهج منهجي","معالجة فعالة للمشاكل","منع أخطاء جديدة","تحسين جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统调试","调试方法","根因分析","技术问题解决","软件开发","质量保证","测试和调试"],"ja":["体系的デバッグ","デバッグ方法","根本原因分析","技術的な問題の解決","ソフトウェア開発","品質保証","テストとデバッグ"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","디버깅 방법","근본 원인 분석","기술적인 문제 해결","소프트웨어 개발","품질 보증","테스트와 디버깅"],"es":["depuración sistemática","causa raíz","errores","fallos","desarrollo de software","eficiencia"],"fr":["débogage systématique","cause profonde","erreurs","défaillances","développement de logiciels","efficacité"],"de":["systematische Fehlersuche","Ursache","Fehler","Ausfälle","Software-Entwicklung","Effizienz"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","causa raiz","resolução de problemas","qualidade do código","desenvolvimento de software","testes de software"],"ru":["систематическая отладка","корневая причина","решение проблем","качество кода","разработка программного обеспечения","тестирование программного обеспечения"],"ar":["حلل بطرق системية","السبب الجذري","معالجة المشاكل","جودة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","اختبار البرمجيات"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents like AutoGPT and LangChain needing rigorous systematic-debugging for root cause analysis in complex technical issues","zh":"适合像 AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的高级 AI 代理，需要严格的系统调试来分析复杂技术问题的根因","ja":"AutoGPT や LangChain などの高度な AI エージェントに適しており、複雑な技術的な問題の根本原因分析のための厳格なシステムデバッグが必要","ko":"AutoGPT와 LangChain 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 복잡한 기술 문제의 근본 원인 분석을 위한 엄격한 시스템 디버깅이 필요","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA avanzados como AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan un depuración sistemática rigurosa para el análisis de causa raíz en problemas técnicos complejos","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA avancés comme AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant un débogage systématique rigoureux pour l''analyse de cause racine dans des problèmes techniques complexes","de":"Perfekt für erweiterte KI-Agenten wie AutoGPT und LangChain, die eine streng systematische Fehlersuche für die Ursachenanalyse bei komplexen technischen Problemen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Avançados como AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de depuração sistemática rigorosa para análise de causa raiz em problemas técnicos complexos","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как AutoGPT и LangChain, которым требуется тщательная системная отладка для анализа коренной причины в сложных технических проблемах","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمة مثل AutoGPT و LangChain التي تحتاج إلى تصحيح نظامي صارم لتحليل السبب الأصلي في المشكلات الفنية المعقدة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to root out bugs and test failures by enforcing a strict NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST policy, utilizing the Iron Law of systematic debugging to prevent symptom fixes and ensure thorough investigation of technical issues","zh":"赋予代理能力以消除错误和测试失败，通过执行严格的先进行根本原因调查的政策，利用系统调试的铁律防止症状修复，确保技术问题的彻底调查","ja":"エージェントにバグやテストの失敗を根本原因から排除する能力を与え、根本原因の調査を行わない修復は行わないという厳格なポリシーを実施し、システムデバッグの鉄則を利用して症状の修復を防ぎ、技術的な問題の徹底的な調査を保証","ko":"에이전트에 버그와 테스트 실패를 근본 원인에서 제거하는 능력을 부여하며, 근본 원인 조사를 먼저 수행하는 엄격한 정책을 시행하고, 시스템 디버깅의 철칙을 활용하여 증상 수정을 방지하며, 기술적인 문제의 철저한 조사를 보장","es":"Habilita a los agentes a eliminar errores y fallos de prueba al aplicar una política estricta de NO REPARACIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, utilizando la Ley de Hierro del depuración sistemática para prevenir arreglos de síntomas y garantizar una investigación exhaustiva de los problemas técnicos","fr":"Permet aux agents d''éliminer les bogues et les échecs de test en appliquant une politique stricte de PAS DE CORRECTIONS SANS ENQUÊTE DE CAUSE RACINE D''ABORD, en utilisant la Loi de Fer du débogage systématique pour prévenir les corrections de symptômes et assurer une investigation approfondie des problèmes techniques","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Fehler und Testfehler zu beseitigen, indem sie eine strikte Richtlinie von KEINE REPARIERUNGEN OHNE URSACHENANALYSE ERST durchsetzen, unter Nutzung des Eisernen Gesetzes der systematischen Fehlersuche, um Symptome zu vermeiden und eine gründliche Untersuchung der technischen Probleme sicherzustellen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a erradicar bugs e falhas de teste, aplicando uma política estrita de NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, utilizando a Lei de Ferro da depuração sistemática para prevenir correções de sintomas e garantir uma investigação minuciosa de problemas técnicos","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью искоренить ошибки и тестовые сбои, реализуя строгую политику НИКАКИХ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, используя Железный Закон системной отладки для предотвращения исправления симптомов и обеспечения тщательного расследования технических проблем","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على القضاء على الأعطال وفشل الاختبار من خلال فرض سياسة صارمة لا يوجد إصلاح بدون تحقيق في السبب الأصلي أولا، باستخدام قانون الحديد لتصحيح النظام لمنع إصلاح الأعراض وضمان التحقيق الشامل للمشكلات الفنية"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging unexpected behavior in code","Investigating test failures for underlying causes","Analyzing bugs to identify root causes before proposing fixes"],"zh":["调试代码中的意外行为","调查测试失败的潜在原因","分析错误以确定根因，然后提出修复方案"],"ja":["コード内の予期しない動作のデバッグ","テストの失敗の潜在的な原因の調査","バグを分析して根本原因を特定し、修復を提案する"],"ko":["코드 내의 예상치 못한 동작의 디버깅","테스트 실패의 근본 원인 조사","버그를 분석하여 근본 원인을 확인하고, 수정을 제안"],"es":["Depuración de comportamiento inesperado en el código","Investigación de fallos de prueba para causas subyacentes","Análisis de errores para identificar causas raíz antes de proponer soluciones"],"fr":["Débogage d''un comportement inattendu dans le code","Enquête sur les échecs de test pour les causes sous-jacentes","Analyse des bogues pour identifier les causes racines avant de proposer des correctifs"],"de":["Fehlersuche bei unerwartetem Verhalten im Code","Untersuchung von Testfehlern auf zugrunde liegende Ursachen","Analyse von Fehlern, um Ursachen zu identifizieren, bevor Lösungen vorgeschlagen werden"],"pt":["Depuração de comportamento inesperado no código","Investigação de falhas de teste para causas subjacentes","Análise de bugs para identificar causas raiz antes de propor correções"],"ru":["Отладка неожиданного поведения кода","Расследование тестовых сбоев для выявления основных причин","Анализ ошибок для выявления коренной причины до предложения исправлений"],"ar":["تصحيح السلوك غير المتوقع في الكود","تحقيق فشل الاختبار لأسباب خفية","تحليل الأعطال لتحديد السبب الأصلي قبل اقتراح الإصلاحات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the Iron Law of systematic debugging","Violating the letter of the process is considered violating the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要遵守系统调试的铁律","违反流程的字母被认为是违反调试的精神"],"ja":["システムデバッグの鉄則を遵守する必要がある","プロセスの文字を違反することはデバッグの精神を違反することとみなされる"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅의 철칙을 준수해야 함","프로세스의 문자를 위반하는 것은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것으로 간주"],"es":["Requiere adherencia a la Ley de Hierro de la depuración sistemática","Violación de la letra del proceso se considera violación del espíritu de la depuración"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion à la Loi de Fer du débogage systématique","La violation de la lettre du processus est considérée comme une violation de l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des Eisernen Gesetzes der systematischen Fehlersuche","Verletzung des Buchstabens des Prozesses gilt als Verletzung des Geistes der Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Exige adesão à Lei de Ferro da depuração sistemática","Violar a letra do processo é considerado violar o espírito da depuração"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения Железного Закона системной отладки","Нарушение буквы процесса считается нарушением духа отладки"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بقانون الحديد لتصحيح النظام","مخالفة حرفية العملية تعتبر مخالفة لروح التصحيح"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"4999cb851360485eca5074e727bbdd62ef20549c5d5b01216fcbf5831badb473","repoEtag":"W/\"29bf55250b8f240dcbe9ab5b26295b46f9245d08f7c3ef5107c7cf22c3e2ed5f\"","qualityScore":90}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/test-driven-development', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'test-driven-development', 55419, 4194, 90, '2026-02-20T01:50:39Z', '2026-02-20T02:01:36.325Z', '7dee67b4af6bdccc7a914ca34533184d64592d0f5b23aeae631538168db14994', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/test-driven-development","name":"test-driven-development","description":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）是一种软件开发过程，通过编写自动化测试来驱动代码的开发","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）は、自動テストを書くことでコードの開発を促進するソフトウェア開発プロセスです","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD)은 자동화된 테스트를 작성하여 코드 개발을 주도하는 소프트웨어 개발 프로세스입니다","es":"TDD es una práctica de desarrollo que implica escribir las pruebas antes de implementar el código, mejorando la calidad y reduciendo errores.","fr":"Le TDD est une pratique de développement qui consiste à écrire les tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code, améliorant ainsi la qualité et réduisant les erreurs.","de":"TDD ist eine Entwicklungsmethode, bei der die Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes geschrieben werden, um die Qualität zu verbessern und Fehler zu reduzieren.","pt":"O TDD é uma prática de desenvolvimento que envolve escrever testes antes de implementar o código, garantindo assim a qualidade e confiabilidade do software","ru":"TDD - это практика разработки, которая включает в себя написание тестов до реализации кода, обеспечивая тем самым качество и надежность программного обеспечения","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار هو ممارسة تطويرية تتضمن كتابة الاختبارات قبل تنفيذ الكود، مما يضمن جودة وثبات البرمجيات","en":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55419,"forks":4194,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:50:39Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"test-driven-development","description":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code","bodyPreview":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD","body":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD just this once\"? Stop. That''s rationalization.\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don''t look at it\n- Delete means delete\n\nImplement fresh from tests. Period.\n\n## Red-Green-Refactor\n\n```dot\ndigraph tdd_cycle {\n    rankdir=LR;\n    red [label=\"RED\\nWrite failing test\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffcccc\"];\n    verify_red [label=\"Verify fails\\ncorrectly\", shape=diamond];\n    green [label=\"GREEN\\nMinimal code\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccffcc\"];\n    verify_green [label=\"Verify passes\\nAll green\", shape=diamond];\n    refactor [label=\"REFACTOR\\nClean up\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccccff\"];\n    next [label=\"Next\", shape=ellipse];\n\n    red -> verify_red;\n    verify_red -> green [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_red -> red [label=\"wrong\\nfailure\"];\n    green -> verify_green;\n    verify_green -> refactor [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_green -> green [label=\"no\"];\n    refactor -> verify_green [label=\"stay\\ngreen\"];\n    verify_green -> next;\n    next -> red;\n}\n```\n\n### RED - Write Failing Test\n\nWrite one minimal test showing what should happen.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\ntest(''retries failed operations 3 times'', async () => {\n  let attempts = 0;\n  const operation = () => {\n    attempts++;\n    if (attempts < 3) throw new Error(''fail'');\n    return ''success'';\n  };\n\n  const result = await retryOperation(operation);\n\n  expect(result).toBe(''success'');\n  expect(attempts).toBe(3);\n});\n```\nClear name, tests real behavior, one thing\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\ntest(''retry works'', async () => {\n  const mock = jest.fn()\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockResolvedValueOnce(''success'');\n  await retryOperation(mock);\n  expect(mock).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(3);\n});\n```\nVague name, tests mock not code\n</Bad>\n\n**Requirements:**\n- One behavior\n- Clear name\n- Real code (no mocks unless unavoidable)\n\n### Verify RED - Watch It Fail\n\n**MANDATORY. Never skip.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test fails (not errors)\n- Failure message is expected\n- Fails because feature missing (not typos)\n\n**Test passes?** You''re testing existing behavior. Fix test.\n\n**Test errors?** Fix error, re-run until it fails correctly.\n\n### GREEN - Minimal Code\n\nWrite simplest code to pass the test.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn();\n    } catch (e) {\n      if (i === 2) throw e;\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(''unreachable'');\n}\n```\nJust enough to pass\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(\n  fn: () => Promise<T>,\n  options?: {\n    maxRetries?: number;\n    backoff?: ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n    onRetry?: (attempt: number) => void;\n  }\n): Promise<T> {\n  // YAGNI\n}\n```\nOver-engineered\n</Bad>\n\nDon''t add features, refactor other code, or \"improve\" beyond the test.\n\n### Verify GREEN - Watch It Pass\n\n**MANDATORY.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test passes\n- Other tests still pass\n- Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n\n**Test fails?** Fix code, not test.\n\n**Other tests fail?** Fix now.\n\n### REFACTOR - Clean Up\n\nAfter green only:\n- Remove duplication\n- Improve names\n- Extract helpers\n\nKeep tests green. Don''t add behavior.\n\n### Repeat\n\nNext failing test for next feature.\n\n## Good Tests\n\n| Quality | Good | Bad |\n|---------|------|-----|\n| **Minimal** | One thing. \"and\" in name? Split it. | `test(''validates email and domain and whitespace'')` |\n| **Clear** | Name describes behavior | `test(''test1'')` |\n| **Shows intent** | Demonstrates desired API | Obscures what code should do |\n\n## Why Order Matters\n\n**\"I''ll write tests after to verify it works\"**\n\nTests written after code pass immediately. Passing immediately proves nothing:\n- Might test wrong thing\n- Might test implementation, not behavior\n- Might miss edge cases you forgot\n- You never saw it catch the bug\n\nTest-first forces you to see the test fail, proving it actually tests something.\n\n**\"I already manually tested all the edge cases\"**\n\nManual testing is ad-hoc. You think you tested everything but:\n- No record of what you tested\n- Can''t re-run when code changes\n- Easy to forget cases under pressure\n- \"It worked when I tried it\" ≠ comprehensive\n\nAutomated tests are systematic. They run the same way every time.\n\n**\"Deleting X hours of work is wasteful\"**\n\nSunk cost fallacy. The time is already gone. Your choice now:\n- Delete and rewrite with TDD (X more hours, high confidence)\n- Keep it and add tests after (30 min, low confidence, likely bugs)\n\nThe \"waste\" is keeping code you can''t trust. Working code without real tests is technical debt.\n\n**\"TDD is dogmatic, being pragmatic means adapting\"**\n\nTDD IS pragmatic:\n- Finds bugs before commit (faster than debugging after)\n- Prevents regressions (tests catch breaks immediately)\n- Documents behavior (tests show how to use code)\n- Enables refactoring (change freely, tests catch breaks)\n\n\"Pragmatic\" shortcuts = debugging in production = slower.\n\n**\"Tests after achieve the same goals - it''s spirit not ritual\"**\n\nNo. Tests-after answer \"What does this do?\" Tests-first answer \"What should this do?\"\n\nTests-after are biased by your implementation. You test what you built, not what''s required. You verify remembered edge cases, not discovered ones.\n\nTests-first force edge case discovery before implementing. Tests-after verify you remembered everything (you didn''t).\n\n30 minutes of tests after ≠ TDD. You get coverage, lose proof tests work.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Too simple to test\" | Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n| \"Already manually tested\" | Ad-hoc ≠ systematic. No record, can''t re-run. |\n| \"Deleting X hours is wasteful\" | Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt. |\n| \"Keep as reference, write tests first\" | You''ll adapt it. That''s testing after. Delete means delete. |\n| \"Need to explore first\" | Fine. Throw away exploration, start with TDD. |\n| \"Test hard = design unclear\" | Listen to test. Hard to test = hard to use. |\n| \"TDD will slow me down\" | TDD faster than debugging. Pragmatic = test-first. |\n| \"Manual test faster\" | Manual doesn''t prove edge cases. You''ll re-test every change. |\n| \"Existing code has no tests\" | You''re improving it. Add tests for existing code. |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Start Over\n\n- Code before test\n- Test after implementation\n- Test passes immediately\n- Can''t explain why test failed\n- Tests added \"later\"\n- Rationalizing \"just this once\"\n- \"I already manually tested it\"\n- \"Tests after achieve the same purpose\"\n- \"It''s about spirit not ritual\"\n- \"Keep as reference\" or \"adapt existing code\"\n- \"Already spent X hours, deleting is wasteful\"\n- \"TDD is dogmatic, I''m being pragmatic\"\n- \"This is different because...\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n\n## Example: Bug Fix\n\n**Bug:** Empty email accepted\n\n**RED**\n```typescript\ntest(''rejects empty email'', async () => {\n  const result = await submitForm({ email: '''' });\n  expect(result.error).toBe(''Email required'');\n});\n```\n\n**Verify RED**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nFAIL: expected ''Email required'', got undefined\n```\n\n**GREEN**\n```typescript\nfunction submitForm(data: FormData) {\n  if (!data.email?.trim()) {\n    return { error: ''Email required'' };\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Verify GREEN**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nPASS\n```\n\n**REFACTOR**\nExtract validation for multiple fields if needed.\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\nBefore marking work complete:\n\n- [ ] Every new function/method has a test\n- [ ] Watched each test fail before implementing\n- [ ] Each test failed for expected reason (feature missing, not typo)\n- [ ] Wrote minimal code to pass each test\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n- [ ] Tests use real code (mocks only if unavoidable)\n- [ ] Edge cases and errors covered\n\nCan''t check all boxes? You skipped TDD. Start over.\n\n## When Stuck\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| Don''t know how to test | Write wished-for API. Write assertion first. Ask your human partner. |\n| Test too complicated | Design too complicated. Simplify interface. |\n| Must mock everything | Code too coupled. Use dependency injection. |\n| Test setup huge | Extract helpers. Still complex? Simplify design. |\n\n## Debugging Integration\n\nBug found? Write failing test reproducing it. Follow TDD cycle. Test proves fix and prevents regression.\n\nNever fix bugs without a test.\n\n## Testing Anti-Patterns\n\nWhen adding mocks or test utilities, read @testing-anti-patterns.md to avoid common pitfalls:\n- Testing mock behavior instead of real behavior\n- Adding test-only methods to production classes\n- Mocking without understanding dependencies\n\n## Final Rule\n\n```\nProduction code → test exists and failed first\nOtherwise → not TDD\n```\n\nNo exceptions without your human partner''s permission.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:01:36.325Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD)","es":"Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD) - Mejora la calidad...","fr":"Développement Dirigé par les Tests (TDD) - Améliorez la q...","de":"Testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) - Verbessern Sie die Cod...","pt":"Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD) - Melhores Prát...","ru":"Разработка через тестирование (TDD) - Лучшие практики","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) - أفضل الممارسات","en":"test-driven-development"},"description":{"zh":"测试驱动开发（TDD）是一种软件开发过程，通过编写自动化测试来驱动代码的开发","ja":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）は、自動テストを書くことでコードの開発を促進するソフトウェア開発プロセスです","ko":"테스트 주도 개발(TDD)은 자동화된 테스트를 작성하여 코드 개발을 주도하는 소프트웨어 개발 프로세스입니다","es":"TDD es una práctica de desarrollo que implica escribir las pruebas antes de implementar el código, mejorando la calidad y reduciendo errores.","fr":"Le TDD est une pratique de développement qui consiste à écrire les tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code, améliorant ainsi la qualité et réduisant les erreurs.","de":"TDD ist eine Entwicklungsmethode, bei der die Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes geschrieben werden, um die Qualität zu verbessern und Fehler zu reduzie...","pt":"O TDD é uma prática de desenvolvimento que envolve escrever testes antes de implementar o código, garantindo assim a qualidade e confiabilidade do software","ru":"TDD - это практика разработки, которая включает в себя написание тестов до реализации кода, обеспечивая тем самым качество и надежность программного обеспечения","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار هو ممارسة تطويرية تتضمن كتابة الاختبارات قبل تنفيذ الكود، مما يضمن جودة وثبات البرمجيات","en":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code"},"definition":{"en":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code"},"features":{"zh":["编写自动化测试","驱动代码开发","提高代码质量","减少 bug","提高开发效率"],"ja":["自動テストの作成","コード開発の促進","コード品質の向上","バグの削減","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["자동화된 테스트 작성","코드 개발 주도","코드 品質 향상","버그 감소","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Escribe las pruebas antes de implementar el código","Mejora la calidad del código y reduce errores","Se aplica a nuevas características, correcciones de errores y refactorización","Excepto para prototipos desechables, código generado y archivos de configuración","Ayuda a garantizar que el código sea correcto y funcione como se espera"],"fr":["Écrivez les tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code","Améliorez la qualité du code et réduisez les erreurs","S''applique à de nouvelles fonctionnalités, à la correction de bogues et à la refactoring","À l''exception des prototypes jetables, du code généré et des fichiers de configuration","Aide à garantir que le code soit correct et fonctionne comme prévu"],"de":["Schreiben Sie die Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes","Verbessern Sie die Qualität des Codes und reduzieren Sie Fehler","Wird auf neue Funktionen, Fehlerkorrekturen und Refactoring angewendet","Außer für verworfene Prototypen, generierten Code und Konfigurationsdateien","Hilft dabei, sicherzustellen, dass der Code korrekt ist und wie erwartet funktioniert"],"pt":["Escrever testes antes de implementar o código","Garantir a qualidade e confiabilidade do software","Reduzir erros e bugs","Melhorar a manutenção e atualização do código","Aumentar a produtividade e eficiência do desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Написание тестов до реализации кода","Обеспечение качества и надежности программного обеспечения","Снижение ошибок и багов","Улучшение обслуживания и обновления кода","Повышение производительности и эффективности разработки"],"ar":["كتابة الاختبارات قبل تنفيذ الكود","ضمان جودة وثبات البرمجيات","تقليل الأخطاء والخروقات","تحسين صيانة وتحديث الكود","زيادة الإنتاجية وفعالية التطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["测试驱动开发","TDD","自动化测试","软件开发","代码质量","开发效率"],"ja":["テスト駆動開発","TDD","自動テスト","ソフトウェア開発","コード品質","開発効率"],"ko":["테스트 주도 개발","TDD","자동화된 테스트","소프트웨어 개발","코드 品質","개발 효율성"],"es":["Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas","TDD","Pruebas unitarias","Calidad del código","Reducir errores","Mejorar la calidad del software","Desarrollo de software","Prácticas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Développement Dirigé par les Tests","TDD","Tests unitaires","Qualité du code","Réduire les erreurs","Améliorer la qualité du logiciel","Développement de logiciels","Pratiques de développement"],"de":["Testgetriebene Entwicklung","TDD","Einheitliche Tests","Codequalität","Fehler reduzieren","Software-Qualität verbessern","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungspraktiken"],"pt":["TDD","Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes","Testes Automatizados","Qualidade de Software","Confiabilidade de Software","Melhores Práticas de Desenvolvimento"],"ru":["TDD","Разработка через тестирование","Автоматизированные тесты","Качество программного обеспечения","Надежность программного обеспечения","Лучшие практики разработки"],"ar":["TDD","التطوير الموجه بالاختبار","الاختبارات الآلية","جودة البرمجيات","ثبات البرمجيات","أفضل الممارسات التطويرية"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Code Generation Agents implementing features or fixing bugs with verified correctness.","zh":"对于实现特性或修复 bug 的代码生成代理来说是必不可少的，需要经过验证的正确性。","ja":"コード生成エージェントが機能を実装したりバグを修正したりする際に検証された正しさを実現するために不可欠です。","ko":"검증된 올바름을 구현하는 코드 생성 에이전트에게 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para los agentes de generación de código que implementan características o corrigen errores con corrección verificada.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents de génération de code qui mettent en œuvre des fonctionnalités ou corrigent des bogues avec une correction vérifiée.","de":"Wesentlich für Code-Generierungsagenten, die Funktionen implementieren oder Fehler mit überprüfter Korrektheit beheben.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Geração de Código que implementam recursos ou consertam bugs com correção verificada.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов генерации кода, реализующих функции или исправляющих ошибки с верифицированной корректностью.","ar":"ضروري لعميل إгенرатор الكود الذي ينفذ الميزات أو يصلح الأخطاء بالصحة المُثبتة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enforces writing failing tests first before implementation, ensuring code meets specifications and prevents regressions. This methodology guarantees test validity by requiring observed failure before writing minimal passing code.","zh":"强制先编写失败的测试，然后再进行实现，确保代码符合规范并防止回归。这一方法通过要求在编写最小的通过代码之前观察到失败来保证测试的有效性。","ja":"実装前に失敗テストを書くことを強制し、コードが仕様を満たして回帰を防ぐことを保証します。この方法は、最小の通過コードを書く前に失敗が観察されることを要求することで、テストの有効性を保証します。","ko":"구현 전에 실패하는 테스트를 작성하도록 강제하여 코드가 사양을 충족하고 회귀를 방지하도록 합니다. 이 방법은 최소한의 통과 코드를 작성하기 전에 실패를 관찰함으로써 테스트의 유효성을 보장합니다.","es":"Hace cumplir la escritura de pruebas fallidas antes de la implementación, asegurando que el código cumpla con las especificaciones y evite las regresiones. Esta metodología garantiza la validez de las pruebas al requerir un fallo observado antes de escribir el código mínimo que pasa.","fr":"Impose l''écriture de tests qui échouent avant la mise en œuvre, en garantissant que le code répond aux spécifications et prévient les régressions. Cette méthodologie garantit la validité des tests en exigeant un échec observé avant d''écrire le code minimal qui passe.","de":"Zwingt die Erstellung von fehlgeschlagenen Tests vor der Implementierung, um sicherzustellen, dass der Code den Spezifikationen entspricht und Regressionsfehler vermeidet. Diese Methodik gewährleistet die Testgültigkeit, indem sie vor der Erstellung des minimalen passierenden Codes einen beobachteten Fehler erfordert.","pt":"Exige a escrita de testes com falha antes da implementação, garantindo que o código atenda às especificações e previna regressões. Esta metodologia garante a validade do teste, exigindo falha observada antes de escrever código mínimo passível.","ru":"Запрашивает написание неудачных тестов перед реализацией, гарантируя, что код соответствует спецификациям и предотвращает регрессию. Этот метод гарантирует действительность теста, требуя наблюдаемой неудачи перед написанием минимального проходящего кода.","ar":"يشترط كتابة اختبارات فاشلة قبل التنفيذ، مما يضمن أن ي滿ى البرنامج للمواصفات و يمنع الرجوع. تضمن هذه المنهجية صحة الاختبار بالطلب فشل ملاحظ قبل كتابة رمز عابر أدنى."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing new features with validated behavior","Fixing bugs with regression tests","Refactoring code with safety nets","Verifying behavior changes don''t break existing functionality"],"zh":["实现具有验证行为的新功能","使用回归测试修复 bug","使用安全网重构代码","验证行为更改不会破坏现有功能"],"ja":["検証された動作を備えた新しい機能の実装","回帰テストを使用したバグの修正","安全ネットを使用したコードのリファクタリング","動作の変更が既存の機能を破壊しないことを検証"],"ko":["검증된 동작을 갖춘 새로운 기능의 구현","회귀 테스트를 사용한 버그 수정","안전網을 사용한 코드의 리팩토링","동작의 변경이 기존의 기능을 破壊하지 않는 것을 검증"],"es":["Implementación de nuevas características con comportamiento validado","Corrección de errores con pruebas de regresión","Reestructuración de código con redes de seguridad","Verificación de que los cambios de comportamiento no rompen la funcionalidad existente"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de nouvelles fonctionnalités avec un comportement validé","Correction de bogues avec des tests de régression","Réorganisation de code avec des filets de sécurité","Vérification que les changements de comportement n''brisent pas la fonctionnalité existante"],"de":["Implementierung neuer Funktionen mit validiertem Verhalten","Behebung von Fehlern mit Regressions-tests","Umstrukturierung von Code mit Sicherheitsnetzen","Überprüfung, dass Verhaltensänderungen die bestehende Funktionalität nicht brechen"],"pt":["Implementação de novos recursos com comportamento validado","Conserto de bugs com testes de regressão","Reestruturação de código com redes de segurança","Verificação de que mudanças de comportamento não quebram funcionalidades existentes"],"ru":["Реализация новых функций с проверенным поведением","Исправление ошибок с тестами регрессии","Переструктуризация кода с гарантиями безопасности","Проверка того, что изменения поведения не нарушают существующую функциональность"],"ar":["تنفيذ ميزات جديدة السلوك المُثبت","إصلاح الأخطاء بالاختبارات الانعكاسية","إعادة هيكلة الكود بشبكات الأمان","التحقق من أن التغييرات في السلوك لا تكسر الوظائف الحالية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires human consultation for throwaway prototypes","Not applicable to generated code or configuration files","Demands discipline to maintain red-green-refactor cycle"],"zh":["需要人类咨询来处理一次性原型","不适用于生成的代码或配置文件","需要纪律来维护红绿重构周期"],"ja":["使い捨てのプロトタイプに人間のコンサルティングが必要","生成されたコードや設定ファイルには適用できない","赤緑リファクタリングサイクルを維持するための規律が必要"],"ko":["一次성 프로토타입을 처리하기 위해 인간의 상담이 필요","생성된 코드나 설정 파일에는 적용할 수 없음","적그린 리팩토링 주기를 유지하기 위한 규율이 필요"],"es":["Requiere consulta humana para prototipos desechables","No es aplicable al código generado o a los archivos de configuración","Exige disciplina para mantener el ciclo rojo-verde-reestructuración"],"fr":["Nécessite une consultation humaine pour les prototypes jetables","N''est pas applicable au code généré ou aux fichiers de configuration","Exige de la discipline pour maintenir le cycle rouge-vert-réorganisation"],"de":["Erfordert menschliche Konsultation für Wegwerf-Prototypen","Ist nicht auf generierten Code oder Konfigurationsdateien anwendbar","Erfordert Disziplin, um den rote-grüne-Refaktorisierungszyklus aufrechtzuerhalten"],"pt":["Exige consulta humana para protótipos descartáveis","Não se aplica a código gerado ou arquivos de configuração","Exige disciplina para manter o ciclo vermelho-verde-reestruturação"],"ru":["Требует человеческой консультации для одноразовых прототипов","Не применимо к сгенерированному коду или файлам конфигурации","Требует дисциплины для поддержания цикла красный-зеленый-рефакторинг"],"ar":["يشترط استشارة بشرية للأنموذجيات القابلة للرمي","لا ينطبق على الكود المُولّد أو ملفات التهيئة","يشترط الانضباط للحفاظ على دورة الحمر-الأخضر-إعادة الهيكلة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"7dee67b4af6bdccc7a914ca34533184d64592d0f5b23aeae631538168db14994","repoEtag":"W/\"0e7bd5c7950d5eac1d4957d49c8fa41c08258bb488461e66f172588c15374b72\"","qualityScore":90}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/using-git-worktrees', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'using-git-worktrees', 55419, 4194, 100, '2026-02-20T01:50:39Z', '2026-02-20T02:02:39.098Z', 'de9dcde34840eee074047ec327d4ea6ca4954c5a73a6d874dc48f25fe46c9e7c', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/using-git-worktrees","name":"using-git-worktrees","description":{"zh":"Git Worktrees允许您创建隔离的工作空间，支持同时处理多个分支，提高开发效率","ja":"Git Worktreesは分離されたワークスペースを作成し、複数のブランチを同時に処理することができます","ko":"Git Worktrees를 사용하여 격리된 작업 공간을 생성하고 여러 분기를 동시에 처리하여 개발 효율성을 높일 수 있습니다","es":"Git Worktrees permite crear espacios de trabajo aislados para desarrollar características de forma independiente","fr":"Les worktrees Git vous permettent de créer des environnements de développement isolés pour travailler sur plusieurs branches simultanément","de":"Git Worktrees ermöglicht die Erstellung von isolierten Arbeitsbereichen für die unabhängige Entwicklung von Funktionen","pt":"Git Worktrees permite criar ambientes de trabalho isolados para desenvolver recursos sem afetar o workspace atual. Isso aumenta a produtividade e reduz erros","ru":"Git Worktrees позволяет создавать изолированные рабочие пространства для разработки функций без влияния на текущее рабочее пространство. Это увеличивает производительность и снижает ошибки","ar":"Git Worktrees يسمح بإنشاء بيئات عمل معزولة لتطوير الميزات دون التأثير على مساحة العمل الحالية. هذا يزيد من الإنتاجية ويقلل من الأخطاء","en":"Use when starting feature work that needs isolation from current workspace or before executing implementation plans - creates isolated git worktrees with smart directory selection and safety verification"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55419,"forks":4194,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:50:39Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"using-git-worktrees","description":"Use when starting feature work that needs isolation from current workspace or before executing implementation plans - creates isolated git worktrees with smart directory selection and safety verification","bodyPreview":"# Using Git Worktrees\n\n## Overview\n\nGit worktrees create isolated workspaces sharing the same repository, allowing work on multiple branches simultaneously without switching.\n\n**Core principle:** Systematic directory selection + safety verification = reliable isolation.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the using-git-worktrees skill to set up an isolated workspace.\"\n\n## Directory Selection Process\n\nFollow this priority order:\n\n### 1. Check Existing Directories\n\n```bash\n# Check in priority order","body":"# Using Git Worktrees\n\n## Overview\n\nGit worktrees create isolated workspaces sharing the same repository, allowing work on multiple branches simultaneously without switching.\n\n**Core principle:** Systematic directory selection + safety verification = reliable isolation.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the using-git-worktrees skill to set up an isolated workspace.\"\n\n## Directory Selection Process\n\nFollow this priority order:\n\n### 1. Check Existing Directories\n\n```bash\n# Check in priority order\nls -d .worktrees 2>/dev/null     # Preferred (hidden)\nls -d worktrees 2>/dev/null      # Alternative\n```\n\n**If found:** Use that directory. If both exist, `.worktrees` wins.\n\n### 2. Check CLAUDE.md\n\n```bash\ngrep -i \"worktree.*director\" CLAUDE.md 2>/dev/null\n```\n\n**If preference specified:** Use it without asking.\n\n### 3. Ask User\n\nIf no directory exists and no CLAUDE.md preference:\n\n```\nNo worktree directory found. Where should I create worktrees?\n\n1. .worktrees/ (project-local, hidden)\n2. ~/.config/superpowers/worktrees/<project-name>/ (global location)\n\nWhich would you prefer?\n```\n\n## Safety Verification\n\n### For Project-Local Directories (.worktrees or worktrees)\n\n**MUST verify directory is ignored before creating worktree:**\n\n```bash\n# Check if directory is ignored (respects local, global, and system gitignore)\ngit check-ignore -q .worktrees 2>/dev/null || git check-ignore -q worktrees 2>/dev/null\n```\n\n**If NOT ignored:**\n\nPer Jesse''s rule \"Fix broken things immediately\":\n1. Add appropriate line to .gitignore\n2. Commit the change\n3. Proceed with worktree creation\n\n**Why critical:** Prevents accidentally committing worktree contents to repository.\n\n### For Global Directory (~/.config/superpowers/worktrees)\n\nNo .gitignore verification needed - outside project entirely.\n\n## Creation Steps\n\n### 1. Detect Project Name\n\n```bash\nproject=$(basename \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\")\n```\n\n### 2. Create Worktree\n\n```bash\n# Determine full path\ncase $LOCATION in\n  .worktrees|worktrees)\n    path=\"$LOCATION/$BRANCH_NAME\"\n    ;;\n  ~/.config/superpowers/worktrees/*)\n    path=\"~/.config/superpowers/worktrees/$project/$BRANCH_NAME\"\n    ;;\nesac\n\n# Create worktree with new branch\ngit worktree add \"$path\" -b \"$BRANCH_NAME\"\ncd \"$path\"\n```\n\n### 3. Run Project Setup\n\nAuto-detect and run appropriate setup:\n\n```bash\n# Node.js\nif [ -f package.json ]; then npm install; fi\n\n# Rust\nif [ -f Cargo.toml ]; then cargo build; fi\n\n# Python\nif [ -f requirements.txt ]; then pip install -r requirements.txt; fi\nif [ -f pyproject.toml ]; then poetry install; fi\n\n# Go\nif [ -f go.mod ]; then go mod download; fi\n```\n\n### 4. Verify Clean Baseline\n\nRun tests to ensure worktree starts clean:\n\n```bash\n# Examples - use project-appropriate command\nnpm test\ncargo test\npytest\ngo test ./...\n```\n\n**If tests fail:** Report failures, ask whether to proceed or investigate.\n\n**If tests pass:** Report ready.\n\n### 5. Report Location\n\n```\nWorktree ready at <full-path>\nTests passing (<N> tests, 0 failures)\nReady to implement <feature-name>\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Situation | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| `.worktrees/` exists | Use it (verify ignored) |\n| `worktrees/` exists | Use it (verify ignored) |\n| Both exist | Use `.worktrees/` |\n| Neither exists | Check CLAUDE.md → Ask user |\n| Directory not ignored | Add to .gitignore + commit |\n| Tests fail during baseline | Report failures + ask |\n| No package.json/Cargo.toml | Skip dependency install |\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n### Skipping ignore verification\n\n- **Problem:** Worktree contents get tracked, pollute git status\n- **Fix:** Always use `git check-ignore` before creating project-local worktree\n\n### Assuming directory location\n\n- **Problem:** Creates inconsistency, violates project conventions\n- **Fix:** Follow priority: existing > CLAUDE.md > ask\n\n### Proceeding with failing tests\n\n- **Problem:** Can''t distinguish new bugs from pre-existing issues\n- **Fix:** Report failures, get explicit permission to proceed\n\n### Hardcoding setup commands\n\n- **Problem:** Breaks on projects using different tools\n- **Fix:** Auto-detect from project files (package.json, etc.)\n\n## Example Workflow\n\n```\nYou: I''m using the using-git-worktrees skill to set up an isolated workspace.\n\n[Check .worktrees/ - exists]\n[Verify ignored - git check-ignore confirms .worktrees/ is ignored]\n[Create worktree: git worktree add .worktrees/auth -b feature/auth]\n[Run npm install]\n[Run npm test - 47 passing]\n\nWorktree ready at /Users/jesse/myproject/.worktrees/auth\nTests passing (47 tests, 0 failures)\nReady to implement auth feature\n```\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Never:**\n- Create worktree without verifying it''s ignored (project-local)\n- Skip baseline test verification\n- Proceed with failing tests without asking\n- Assume directory location when ambiguous\n- Skip CLAUDE.md check\n\n**Always:**\n- Follow directory priority: existing > CLAUDE.md > ask\n- Verify directory is ignored for project-local\n- Auto-detect and run project setup\n- Verify clean test baseline\n\n## Integration\n\n**Called by:**\n- **brainstorming** (Phase 4) - REQUIRED when design is approved and implementation follows\n- **subagent-driven-development** - REQUIRED before executing any tasks\n- **executing-plans** - REQUIRED before executing any tasks\n- Any skill needing isolated workspace\n\n**Pairs with:**\n- **finishing-a-development-branch** - REQUIRED for cleanup after work complete\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:02:39.098Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"Git Worktrees 使用指南","ja":"Git Worktreesの使い方","ko":"Git Worktrees 사용법","es":"Trabajos aislados con Git Worktrees","fr":"Utiliser les worktrees Git pour un développement isolé","de":"Isolierte Arbeitsbereiche mit Git Worktrees","pt":"Usando Git Worktrees para Desenvolvimento Isolado","ru":"Использование Git Worktrees для Изолированного Разработки","ar":"استخدام Git Worktrees للتنمية المعزولة","en":"using-git-worktrees"},"description":{"zh":"Git Worktrees允许您创建隔离的工作空间，支持同时处理多个分支，提高开发效率","ja":"Git Worktreesは分離されたワークスペースを作成し、複数のブランチを同時に処理することができます","ko":"Git Worktrees를 사용하여 격리된 작업 공간을 생성하고 여러 분기를 동시에 처리하여 개발 효율성을 높일 수 있습니다","es":"Git Worktrees permite crear espacios de trabajo aislados para desarrollar características de forma independiente","fr":"Les worktrees Git vous permettent de créer des environnements de développement isolés pour travailler sur plusieurs branches simultanément","de":"Git Worktrees ermöglicht die Erstellung von isolierten Arbeitsbereichen für die unabhängige Entwicklung von Funktionen","pt":"Git Worktrees permite criar ambientes de trabalho isolados para desenvolver recursos sem afetar o workspace atual. Isso aumenta a produtividade e reduz erros","ru":"Git Worktrees позволяет создавать изолированные рабочие пространства для разработки функций без влияния на текущее рабочее пространство. Это увеличивает прои...","ar":"Git Worktrees يسمح بإنشاء بيئات عمل معزولة لتطوير الميزات دون التأثير على مساحة العمل الحالية. هذا يزيد من الإنتاجية ويقلل من الأخطاء","en":"Use when starting feature work that needs isolation from current workspace or before executing implementation plans - creates isolated git worktrees with sma..."},"definition":{"en":"Use when starting feature work that needs isolation from current workspace or before executing implementation plans - creates isolated git worktrees with smart directory selection and safety verification"},"features":{"zh":["创建隔离工作空间","支持同时处理多个分支","提高开发效率","智能目录选择","安全性验证"],"ja":["分離されたワークスペースの作成","複数のブランチの同時処理","開発効率の向上","スマートなディレクトリ選択","安全性の検証"],"ko":["격리된 작업 공간 생성","여러 분기의 동시 처리","개발 효율성 향상","스마트 디렉토리 선택","안전성 검증"],"es":["Creación de espacios de trabajo aislados","Trabajo en varias ramas simultáneamente","Selección de directorios inteligente","Verificación de seguridad"],"fr":["Création d''environnements de développement isolés","Travail sur plusieurs branches en même temps","Sélection de répertoires intelligente","Vérification de sécurité"],"de":["Erstellung von isolierten Arbeitsbereichen","Arbeit an mehreren Branches gleichzeitig","Intelligente Verzeichnisauswahl","Sicherheitsüberprüfung"],"pt":["Criação de ambientes de trabalho isolados","Desenvolvimento de recursos sem afetar o workspace atual","Prioridade de seleção de diretórios","Verificação de segurança para evitar erros"],"ru":["Создание изолированных рабочих пространств","Разработка функций без влияния на текущее рабочее пространство","Приоритет выбора директорий","Проверка безопасности для предотвращения ошибок"],"ar":["إنشاء بيئات عمل معزولة","تطوير الميزات دون التأثير على مساحة العمل الحالية","أولوية اختيار الدلائل","فحص الأمان لتجنب الأخطاء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git Worktrees","隔离工作空间","多分支处理","开发效率","Git开发工具"],"ja":["Git Worktrees","分離されたワークスペース","複数ブランチ処理","開発効率","Git開発ツール"],"ko":["Git Worktrees","격리된 작업 공간","여러 분기 처리","개발 효율성","Git 개발 도구"],"es":["Git Worktrees","desarrollo de software","espacios de trabajo aislados","ramas de desarrollo","control de versiones"],"fr":["worktrees Git","développement de logiciels","environnements de développement isolés","branches de développement","contrôle de version"],"de":["Git Worktrees","Software-Entwicklung","isolierte Arbeitsbereiche","Entwicklungsbranchen","Versionskontrolle"],"pt":["git worktrees","desenvolvimento isolado","ambientes de trabalho","produtividade","redução de erros","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["git worktrees","изолированное разработка","рабочие пространства","производительность","снижение ошибок","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["git worktrees","تطوير معزول","بيئات عمل","إنتاجية","تقليل الأخطاء","أدوات التطوير"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing isolated workspace management and simultaneous branch work","zh":"适合需要隔离工作空间管理和同时分支工作的开发代理","ja":"開発エージェントが隔離されたワークスペース管理と同時にブランチ作業を行う必要がある場合に最適","ko":"분리된 작업 공간 관리와 동시에 분기 작업이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan gestión de espacio de trabajo aislado y trabajo de rama simultáneo","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant une gestion d''espace de travail isolé et un travail de branche simultané","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine isolierte Arbeitsbereichsverwaltung und simultane Branch-Arbeit benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de gerenciamento de espaço de trabalho isolado e trabalho de branch simultâneo","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходимы изолированное управление рабочим пространством и одновременная работа с ветками","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التطويين الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة مساحة عمل معزولة وعملهم الفرعي المتزامن"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create isolated git worktrees with systematic directory selection and safety verification, allowing for reliable isolation and simultaneous work on multiple branches using git protocols","zh":"赋予代理创建隔离的git工作树的能力，具有系统的目录选择和安全性验证，使得可靠的隔离和同时使用git协议在多个分支上工作成为可能","ja":"エージェントがシステムのディレクトリ選択と安全性の検証を備えた隔離されたgitワークツリーを作成できるようにし、gitプロトコルを使用して複数のブランチで同時に作業できるようにする","ko":"에이전트가 시스템의 디렉토리 선택과 안전성 검증을 갖춘 격리된 git 작업 트리를 생성할 수 있도록 하여 git 프로토콜을 사용하여 여러 분기에서 동시에 작업할 수 있도록 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear worktrees de git aislados con selección de directorio sistemática y verificación de seguridad, lo que permite una aislación confiable y un trabajo simultáneo en varias ramas utilizando protocolos git","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des worktrees git isolés avec une sélection de répertoire systématique et une vérification de sécurité, permettant ainsi une isolation fiable et un travail simultané sur plusieurs branches en utilisant les protocoles git","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, isolierte Git-Arbeitsbereiche mit systematischer Verzeichnisauswahl und Sicherheitsüberprüfung zu erstellen, was eine zuverlässige Isolation und simultane Arbeit an mehreren Zweigen unter Verwendung von Git-Protokollen ermöglicht","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem worktrees git isolados com seleção sistemática de diretórios e verificação de segurança, permitindo isolamento confiável e trabalho simultâneo em várias branches usando protocolos git","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать изолированные рабочие деревья git с систематическим выбором директорий и проверкой безопасности, что позволяет обеспечить надежное изоляцию и одновременную работу над несколькими ветками с использованием протоколов git","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء من خلاله إنشاء أشجار عمل معزولة مع تحديد المديرين بشكل منهجي وتأكيد السلامة، مما يسمح بالعزل الموثوق والعمل المتزامن على عدة فروع باستخدام بروتوكولات جيت"},"useCases":{"en":["Isolating feature work from the main workspace","Simultaneously working on multiple branches","Executing implementation plans in a safe environment"],"zh":["从主工作空间中隔离功能工作","同时在多个分支上工作","在安全环境中执行实现计划"],"ja":["メインワークスペースから機能作業を分離する","複数のブランチで同時に作業する","安全な環境で実装計画を実行する"],"ko":["메인 작업 공간에서 기능 작업을 분리","여러 분기에서 동시에 작업","안전한 환경에서 구현 계획을 실행"],"es":["Aislar el trabajo de características del espacio de trabajo principal","Trabajar simultáneamente en varias ramas","Ejecutar planes de implementación en un entorno seguro"],"fr":["Isoler le travail de fonctionnalités de l''espace de travail principal","Travailler simultanément sur plusieurs branches","Exécuter des plans d''implémentation dans un environnement sécurisé"],"de":["Isolieren der Funktionsarbeiten vom primären Arbeitsbereich","Simultane Arbeit an mehreren Zweigen","Ausführen von Implementierungsplänen in einer sicheren Umgebung"],"pt":["Isolar o trabalho de recursos do espaço de trabalho principal","Trabalhar simultaneamente em várias branches","Executar planos de implementação em um ambiente seguro"],"ru":["Изолировать работу над функциями от основного рабочего пространства","Одновременно работать над несколькими ветками","Выполнять планы реализации в безопасной среде"],"ar":["عزل عمل الميزات عن مساحة العمل الرئيسية","العمل المتزامن على عدة فروع","تنفيذ خطط التنفيذ في بيئة آمنة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git installation","Limited to git-based version control systems"],"zh":["需要git安装","仅限于基于git的版本控制系统"],"ja":["gitのインストールが必要","gitベースのバージョン管理システムのみ"],"ko":["git 설치가 필요","git 기반 버전 관리 시스템만"],"es":["Requiere instalación de git","Limitado a sistemas de control de versiones basados en git"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de git","Limité aux systèmes de contrôle de version basés sur git"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Installation","Begrenzt auf Git-basierte Versionskontrollsysteme"],"pt":["Requer instalação do git","Limitado a sistemas de controle de versão baseados em git"],"ru":["Требуется установка git","Ограничен для систем контроля версий на основе git"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت جيت","محدود لأنظمة التحكم في الإصدارات التي تعتمد على جيت"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"de9dcde34840eee074047ec327d4ea6ca4954c5a73a6d874dc48f25fe46c9e7c","repoEtag":"W/\"0e7bd5c7950d5eac1d4957d49c8fa41c08258bb488461e66f172588c15374b72\"","qualityScore":100}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/using-superpowers', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'using-superpowers', 55419, 4194, 70, '2026-02-20T01:50:39Z', '2026-02-20T02:03:47.894Z', '07d73726944e38fac59b9c90d876e0f714e395308b357973ae77b1321fc75067', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/using-superpowers","name":"using-superpowers","description":{"zh":"使用超级技能可以显著提升开发效率，通过正确的技能调用来简化开发过程","ja":"スーパーパワーを使用することで開発効率を大幅に向上させることができます","ko":"슈퍼 파워를 사용하면 개발 효율을 크게 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"La habilidad ''using-superpowers'' permite a los desarrolladores invocar habilidades para mejorar sus tareas","fr":"La compétence ''using-superpowers'' permet aux développeurs d''invoquer des compétences pour améliorer leurs tâches","de":"Die Fähigkeit ''using-superpowers'' ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Fähigkeiten zu verwenden, um ihre Aufgaben zu verbessern","pt":"O skill using-superpowers é essencial para desenvolvedores, fornecendo acesso a habilidades avançadas.","ru":"Навык using-superpowers необходим для разработчиков, предоставляя доступ к продвинутым способностям.","ar":"المهارة using-superpowers ضرورية للمطورين، مما يوفر الوصول إلى القدرات المتقدمة.","en":"Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55419,"forks":4194,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:50:39Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"using-superpowers","description":"Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions","bodyPreview":"<EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\nIf you think there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to what you are doing, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke the skill.\n\nIF A SKILL APPLIES TO YOUR TASK, YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE. YOU MUST USE IT.\n\nThis is not negotiable. This is not optional. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\n</EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\n\n## How to Access Skills\n\n**In Claude Code:** Use the `Skill` tool. When you invoke a skill, its content is loaded and presented to you—follow it directly. Never use","body":"<EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\nIf you think there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to what you are doing, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke the skill.\n\nIF A SKILL APPLIES TO YOUR TASK, YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE. YOU MUST USE IT.\n\nThis is not negotiable. This is not optional. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\n</EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\n\n## How to Access Skills\n\n**In Claude Code:** Use the `Skill` tool. When you invoke a skill, its content is loaded and presented to you—follow it directly. Never use the Read tool on skill files.\n\n**In other environments:** Check your platform''s documentation for how skills are loaded.\n\n# Using Skills\n\n## The Rule\n\n**Invoke relevant or requested skills BEFORE any response or action.** Even a 1% chance a skill might apply means that you should invoke the skill to check. If an invoked skill turns out to be wrong for the situation, you don''t need to use it.\n\n```dot\ndigraph skill_flow {\n    \"User message received\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [shape=box];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" [shape=box];\n    \"Announce: ''Using [skill] to [purpose]''\" [shape=box];\n    \"Has checklist?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [shape=box];\n    \"Follow skill exactly\" [shape=box];\n    \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [shape=doublecircle];\n\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" -> \"Already brainstormed?\";\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n\n    \"User message received\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Invoke Skill tool\" [label=\"yes, even 1%\"];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [label=\"definitely not\"];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" -> \"Announce: ''Using [skill] to [purpose]''\";\n    \"Announce: ''Using [skill] to [purpose]''\" -> \"Has checklist?\";\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\";\n}\n```\n\n## Red Flags\n\nThese thoughts mean STOP—you''re rationalizing:\n\n| Thought | Reality |\n|---------|---------|\n| \"This is just a simple question\" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |\n| \"I need more context first\" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |\n| \"Let me explore the codebase first\" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |\n| \"I can check git/files quickly\" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |\n| \"Let me gather information first\" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |\n| \"This doesn''t need a formal skill\" | If a skill exists, use it. |\n| \"I remember this skill\" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |\n| \"This doesn''t count as a task\" | Action = task. Check for skills. |\n| \"The skill is overkill\" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |\n| \"I''ll just do this one thing first\" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |\n| \"This feels productive\" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |\n| \"I know what that means\" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |\n\n## Skill Priority\n\nWhen multiple skills could apply, use this order:\n\n1. **Process skills first** (brainstorming, debugging) - these determine HOW to approach the task\n2. **Implementation skills second** (frontend-design, mcp-builder) - these guide execution\n\n\"Let''s build X\" → brainstorming first, then implementation skills.\n\"Fix this bug\" → debugging first, then domain-specific skills.\n\n## Skill Types\n\n**Rigid** (TDD, debugging): Follow exactly. Don''t adapt away discipline.\n\n**Flexible** (patterns): Adapt principles to context.\n\nThe skill itself tells you which.\n\n## User Instructions\n\nInstructions say WHAT, not HOW. \"Add X\" or \"Fix Y\" doesn''t mean skip workflows.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:03:47.894Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"使用超级技能","ja":"スーパーパワーの使用","ko":"슈퍼 파워 사용","es":"Invocar habilidades con superpoderes","fr":"Utiliser des superpouvoirs pour invoquer des compétences","de":"Superkräfte nutzen, um Fähigkeiten zu verwenden","pt":"Usando Superpoderes: Guia de Desenvolvedores","ru":"Использование Суперспособностей: Руководство для Разработ...","ar":"استخدام القوى الخارقة: دليل للمطورين","en":"using-superpowers"},"description":{"zh":"使用超级技能可以显著提升开发效率，通过正确的技能调用来简化开发过程","ja":"スーパーパワーを使用することで開発効率を大幅に向上させることができます","ko":"슈퍼 파워를 사용하면 개발 효율을 크게 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"La habilidad ''using-superpowers'' permite a los desarrolladores invocar habilidades para mejorar sus tareas","fr":"La compétence ''using-superpowers'' permet aux développeurs d''invoquer des compétences pour améliorer leurs tâches","de":"Die Fähigkeit ''using-superpowers'' ermöglicht es Entwicklern, Fähigkeiten zu verwenden, um ihre Aufgaben zu verbessern","pt":"O skill using-superpowers é essencial para desenvolvedores, fornecendo acesso a habilidades avançadas.","ru":"Навык using-superpowers необходим для разработчиков, предоставляя доступ к продвинутым способностям.","ar":"المهارة using-superpowers ضرورية للمطورين، مما يوفر الوصول إلى القدرات المتقدمة.","en":"Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions"},"definition":{"en":"Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions"},"features":{"zh":["简化开发过程","提升开发效率","正确的技能调用","开发工具集成","增强开发体验","提高代码质量"],"ja":["開発プロセスの簡素化","開発効率の向上","スキルの正しい呼び出し","開発ツールの統合","開発体験の強化","コード品質の向上"],"ko":["개발 프로세스 간소화","개발 효율성 향상","스킬 호출","개발 도구 통합","개발 경험 강화","코드 품질 향상"],"es":["Invocación de habilidades con superpoderes","Mejora de tareas con habilidades","Requerimiento de invocación de habilidades antes de cualquier respuesta","Uso de la herramienta ''Skill'' en Claude Code","Presentación de contenido de habilidades después de la invocación"],"fr":["Invocation de compétences avec des superpouvoirs","Amélioration de tâches avec des compétences","Exigence d''invocation de compétences avant toute réponse","Utilisation de l''outil ''Skill'' en Claude Code","Présentation de contenu de compétences après l''invocation"],"de":["Verwendung von Superkräften, um Fähigkeiten zu verwenden","Verbesserung von Aufgaben mit Fähigkeiten","Erfordernis der Verwendung von Fähigkeiten vor jeder Antwort","Verwendung des ''Skill''-Tools in Claude Code","Präsentation von Fähigkeitsinhalten nach der Verwendung"],"pt":["Acesso a habilidades avançadas","Invocação de ferramentas de skill","Uso de código Claude","Implementação de superpoderes","Desenvolvimento de soluções personalizadas"],"ru":["Доступ к продвинутым способностям","Вызов инструментов навыка","Использование кода Claude","Реализация суперспособностей","Разработка индивидуальных решений"],"ar":["الوصول إلى القدرات المتقدمة","استدعاء أدوات المهارة","استخدام كود كلود","تنفيذ القوى الخارقة","تطوير حلول مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["开发效率","超级技能","开发工具","代码质量","开发体验","开发者工具","技能调用"],"ja":["開発効率","スーパーパワー","開発ツール","コード品質","開発体験","開発者ツール","スキルの呼び出し"],"ko":["개발 효율성","슈퍼 파워","개발 도구","코드 품질","개발 경험","개발자 도구","스킬 호출"],"es":["invocar habilidades","superpoderes para desarrolladores","mejora de tareas","herramienta Skill","Claude Code","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["invoquer des compétences","superpouvoirs pour développeurs","amélioration de tâches","outil Skill","Claude Code","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Fähigkeiten verwenden","Superkräfte für Entwickler","Aufgabenverbesserung","Skill-Tool","Claude Code","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["using-superpowers","desenvolvimento de software","habilidades avançadas","ferramentas de skill","código Claude","superpoderes","soluções personalizadas"],"ru":["using-superpowers","разработка программного обеспечения","продвинутые способности","инструменты навыка","код Claude","суперспособности","индивидуальные решения"],"ar":["using-superpowers","تطوير البرمجيات","القدرات المتقدمة","أدوات المهارة","كود كلود","القوى الخارقة","حلول مخصصة"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents needing strict skill invocation protocols for efficient task management.","zh":"适合需要严格技能调用协议的高级 AI 代理以实现高效任务管理。","ja":"高度な AI エージェントが効率的なタスク管理のために厳格なスキル呼び出しプロトコルを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"효율적인 작업 관리를 위해 엄격한 스킬 호출 프로토콜이 필요한 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de IA Avanzados que necesitan protocolos de invocación de habilidades estrictos para una gestión de tareas eficiente.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''IA Avancés nécessitant des protocoles d''invocation de compétences stricts pour une gestion de tâches efficace.","de":"Perfekt für fortgeschrittene KI-Agents, die strenge Fähigkeitsaufrufprotokolle für eine effiziente Aufgabenverwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA Avançados que necessitam de protocolos estritos de invocação de habilidades para gerenciamento de tarefas eficiente.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, которым необходимы строгие протоколы вызова навыков для эффективного управления задачами.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمة التي تحتاج إلى بروتوكولات صارمة لاستدعاء المهارات من أجل إدارة المهام الفعالة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to mandatorily invoke skills using the `Skill` tool, ensuring adherence to critical task protocols via direct content loading and presentation, leveraging tools like Claude Code for seamless skill integration.","zh":"赋予代理使用 `Skill` 工具强制调用技能，通过直接内容加载和呈现确保遵守关键任务协议，并利用 Claude Code 等工具实现无缝的技能集成。","ja":"エージェントに `Skill` ツールを使用してスキルを強制的に呼び出し、直接のコンテンツの読み込みと提示を介して重要なタスクのプロトコルに従うことを保証し、Claude Code などのツールを使用してスキルのシームレスな統合を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 `Skill` 툴을 사용하여 강제로 스킬을 호출하도록 하여 직접 콘텐츠 로딩 및 프레젠테이션을 통해 중요한 작업 프로토콜을 준수하도록 하고 Claude Code 등의 툴을 사용하여 스킬의 무결한 통합을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a invocar obligatoriamente habilidades utilizando la herramienta `Skill`, garantizando el cumplimiento de protocolos de tareas críticas a través de la carga y presentación directa de contenido, aprovechando herramientas como Claude Code para una integración de habilidades sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''invoker obligatoirement des compétences en utilisant l''outil `Skill`, en garantissant le respect des protocoles de tâches critiques via le chargement et la présentation directe de contenu, en exploitant des outils comme Claude Code pour une intégration de compétences sans accroc.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, Fähigkeiten verpflichtend mit dem `Skill`-Werkzeug aufzurufen, wodurch die Einhaltung kritischer Aufgabenprotokolle durch direktes Laden und Präsentieren von Inhalten sichergestellt wird, indem Werkzeuge wie Claude Code für eine nahtlose Fähigkeitsintegration genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a invocar habilidades obrigatoriamente usando a ferramenta `Skill`, garantindo a adesão a protocolos de tarefas críticas por meio do carregamento e apresentação direta de conteúdo, aproveitando ferramentas como Claude Code para integração de habilidades sem interrupções.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обязательного вызова навыков с помощью инструмента `Skill`, обеспечивая соблюдение критических протоколов задач посредством прямой загрузки и представления контента, используя инструменты типа Claude Code для бесшовной интеграции навыков.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من استدعاء المهارات بالضرورة باستخدام أداة `Skill` ، مما يضمن الالتزام ببروتوكولات المهام الحرجة من خلال تحميل المحتوى وتقديمه مباشرة ، واستخدام أدوات مثل Claude Code لتكامل المهارات بسلاسة."},"useCases":{"en":["Invoking skills for task clarification","Ensuring protocol adherence in complex tasks","Mandating skill usage for critical operations"],"zh":["调用技能以澄清任务","确保复杂任务中的协议遵守","强制使用技能进行关键操作"],"ja":["タスクの明確化ためにスキルを呼び出す","複雑なタスクにおけるプロトコルの遵守を確保する","重要な操作のためにスキルの使用を強制する"],"ko":["작업 명확화를 위해 스킬 호출하기","복잡한 작업에서 프로토콜 준수 보장하기","임계 작동을 위한 스킬 사용 강제하기"],"es":["Invocar habilidades para la clarificación de tareas","Garantizar el cumplimiento de protocolos en tareas complejas","Exigir el uso de habilidades para operaciones críticas"],"fr":["Invocquer des compétences pour la clarification de tâches","Assurer le respect des protocoles dans les tâches complexes","Exiger l''utilisation de compétences pour les opérations critiques"],"de":["Fähigkeiten aufrufen, um Aufgaben zu klären","Die Einhaltung von Protokollen in komplexen Aufgaben sicherstellen","Die Verwendung von Fähigkeiten für kritische Operationen vorschreiben"],"pt":["Invocar habilidades para esclarecimento de tarefas","Garantir a adesão ao protocolo em tarefas complexas","Exigir uso de habilidades para operações críticas"],"ru":["Вызов навыков для уточнения задач","Обеспечение соблюдения протокола в сложных задачах","Требование использования навыков для критических операций"],"ar":["استدعاء المهارات لتوضيح المهام","ضمان الالتزام بالبروتوكول في المهام المعقدة","إلزام استخدام المهارات للعمليات الحرجة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Skill tool invocation","Compatible with Claude Code and similar AI agent ecosystems"],"zh":["需要 Skill 工具的调用","仅兼容 Claude Code 和类似的 AI 代理生态系统"],"ja":["Skill ツールの呼び出しが必要","Claude Code と同等の AI エージェントのエコシステムとのみ互換性がある"],"ko":["스킬 툴 호출 필요","클라우드 코드와 유사한 AI 에이전트 생태계만과 호환"],"es":["Requiere la invocación de la herramienta Skill","Compatible con Claude Code y ecosistemas de agentes de IA similares"],"fr":["Nécessite l''invocation de l''outil Skill","Compatible avec Claude Code et des écosystèmes d''agents d''IA similaires"],"de":["Benötigt die Aufruf der Skill-Tools","Kompatibel mit Claude Code und ähnlichen KI-Agenten-Ökosystemen"],"pt":["Requer invocação da ferramenta Skill","Compatível com Claude Code e ecossistemas de agentes de IA semelhantes"],"ru":["Требует вызова инструмента Skill","Совместим с Claude Code и аналогичными экосистемами агентов ИИ"],"ar":["يتطلب استدعاء أداة Skill","متوافق مع Claude Code وبيئات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي المماثلة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"07d73726944e38fac59b9c90d876e0f714e395308b357973ae77b1321fc75067","repoEtag":"W/\"0e7bd5c7950d5eac1d4957d49c8fa41c08258bb488461e66f172588c15374b72\"","qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/verification-before-completion', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'verification-before-completion', 55419, 4194, 70, '2026-02-20T01:50:39Z', '2026-02-20T02:05:06.918Z', 'ea52d15aabaf72bc6b558efe2c126f161b53961090ddcd712000273bfe8c7b6c', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/verification-before-completion","name":"verification-before-completion","description":{"zh":"验证前完成技能是一种确保代码质量和可靠性的方法，通过在提交代码前运行验证命令来确认输出","ja":"完了前に検証するスキルは、コードの品質と信頼性を高めるための方法で、コードを提出する前に検証コマンドを実行して出力を確認する","ko":"완료 전 검증 스킬은 코드 품질과 신뢰성을 높이는 방법으로, 코드를 제출하기 전에 검증 명령을 실행하여 출력을 확인하는 것을 의미","es":"La verificación antes de completar es un principio fundamental que garantiza la calidad y precisión en el desarrollo de software","fr":"La vérification avant achèvement est un principe clé qui assure la qualité et la précision dans le développement de logiciels","de":"Die Verifizierung vor Abschluss ist ein Grundprinzip, das die Qualität und Genauigkeit in der Softwareentwicklung gewährleistet","pt":"A verificação antes da conclusão é uma prática essencial que assegura a qualidade e a honestidade no desenvolvimento de software, evitando reclamações infundadas.","ru":"Верификация перед завершением является необходимой практикой, обеспечивающей качество и честность в разработке программного обеспечения, избегая необоснованных заявлений.","ar":"التحقق قبل الاستكمال هو ممارسة أساسية تضمن الجودة والصدق في تطوير البرمجيات، وتجنب المطالبات غير المبررة.","en":"Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55419,"forks":4194,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:50:39Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"verification-before-completion","description":"Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always","bodyPreview":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing sati","body":"# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\nClaiming work is complete without verification is dishonesty, not efficiency.\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven''t run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing satisfaction:\n\n1. IDENTIFY: What command proves this claim?\n2. RUN: Execute the FULL command (fresh, complete)\n3. READ: Full output, check exit code, count failures\n4. VERIFY: Does output confirm the claim?\n   - If NO: State actual status with evidence\n   - If YES: State claim WITH evidence\n5. ONLY THEN: Make the claim\n\nSkip any step = lying, not verifying\n```\n\n## Common Failures\n\n| Claim | Requires | Not Sufficient |\n|-------|----------|----------------|\n| Tests pass | Test command output: 0 failures | Previous run, \"should pass\" |\n| Linter clean | Linter output: 0 errors | Partial check, extrapolation |\n| Build succeeds | Build command: exit 0 | Linter passing, logs look good |\n| Bug fixed | Test original symptom: passes | Code changed, assumed fixed |\n| Regression test works | Red-green cycle verified | Test passes once |\n| Agent completed | VCS diff shows changes | Agent reports \"success\" |\n| Requirements met | Line-by-line checklist | Tests passing |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP\n\n- Using \"should\", \"probably\", \"seems to\"\n- Expressing satisfaction before verification (\"Great!\", \"Perfect!\", \"Done!\", etc.)\n- About to commit/push/PR without verification\n- Trusting agent success reports\n- Relying on partial verification\n- Thinking \"just this once\"\n- Tired and wanting work over\n- **ANY wording implying success without having run verification**\n\n## Rationalization Prevention\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Should work now\" | RUN the verification |\n| \"I''m confident\" | Confidence ≠ evidence |\n| \"Just this once\" | No exceptions |\n| \"Linter passed\" | Linter ≠ compiler |\n| \"Agent said success\" | Verify independently |\n| \"I''m tired\" | Exhaustion ≠ excuse |\n| \"Partial check is enough\" | Partial proves nothing |\n| \"Different words so rule doesn''t apply\" | Spirit over letter |\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n**Tests:**\n```\n✅ [Run test command] [See: 34/34 pass] \"All tests pass\"\n❌ \"Should pass now\" / \"Looks correct\"\n```\n\n**Regression tests (TDD Red-Green):**\n```\n✅ Write → Run (pass) → Revert fix → Run (MUST FAIL) → Restore → Run (pass)\n❌ \"I''ve written a regression test\" (without red-green verification)\n```\n\n**Build:**\n```\n✅ [Run build] [See: exit 0] \"Build passes\"\n❌ \"Linter passed\" (linter doesn''t check compilation)\n```\n\n**Requirements:**\n```\n✅ Re-read plan → Create checklist → Verify each → Report gaps or completion\n❌ \"Tests pass, phase complete\"\n```\n\n**Agent delegation:**\n```\n✅ Agent reports success → Check VCS diff → Verify changes → Report actual state\n❌ Trust agent report\n```\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nFrom 24 failure memories:\n- your human partner said \"I don''t believe you\" - trust broken\n- Undefined functions shipped - would crash\n- Missing requirements shipped - incomplete features\n- Time wasted on false completion → redirect → rework\n- Violates: \"Honesty is a core value. If you lie, you''ll be replaced.\"\n\n## When To Apply\n\n**ALWAYS before:**\n- ANY variation of success/completion claims\n- ANY expression of satisfaction\n- ANY positive statement about work state\n- Committing, PR creation, task completion\n- Moving to next task\n- Delegating to agents\n\n**Rule applies to:**\n- Exact phrases\n- Paraphrases and synonyms\n- Implications of success\n- ANY communication suggesting completion/correctness\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**No shortcuts for verification.**\n\nRun the command. Read the output. THEN claim the result.\n\nThis is non-negotiable.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:05:06.918Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"验证前完成技能","ja":"完了前に検証するスキル","ko":"완료 전 검증 스킬","es":"Verificación antes de completar: principio fundamental","fr":"Vérification avant achèvement : principe clé","de":"Verifizierung vor Abschluss: Grundprinzip","pt":"Verificação Antes da Conclusão","ru":"Верификация Перед Завершением","ar":"التحقق قبل الاستكمال","en":"verification-before-completion"},"description":{"zh":"验证前完成技能是一种确保代码质量和可靠性的方法，通过在提交代码前运行验证命令来确认输出","ja":"完了前に検証するスキルは、コードの品質と信頼性を高めるための方法で、コードを提出する前に検証コマンドを実行して出力を確認する","ko":"완료 전 검증 스킬은 코드 품질과 신뢰성을 높이는 방법으로, 코드를 제출하기 전에 검증 명령을 실행하여 출력을 확인하는 것을 의미","es":"La verificación antes de completar es un principio fundamental que garantiza la calidad y precisión en el desarrollo de software","fr":"La vérification avant achèvement est un principe clé qui assure la qualité et la précision dans le développement de logiciels","de":"Die Verifizierung vor Abschluss ist ein Grundprinzip, das die Qualität und Genauigkeit in der Softwareentwicklung gewährleistet","pt":"A verificação antes da conclusão é uma prática essencial que assegura a qualidade e a honestidade no desenvolvimento de software, evitando reclamações infund...","ru":"Верификация перед завершением является необходимой практикой, обеспечивающей качество и честность в разработке программного обеспечения, избегая необоснованн...","ar":"التحقق قبل الاستكمال هو ممارسة أساسية تضمن الجودة والصدق في تطوير البرمجيات، وتجنب المطالبات غير المبررة.","en":"Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output..."},"definition":{"en":"Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always"},"features":{"zh":["确保代码质量和可靠性","在提交代码前运行验证命令","确认输出以避免错误","提高代码的可维护性和可扩展性","减少错误和 bug 的数量"],"ja":["コードの品質と信頼性を高める","コードを提出する前に検証コマンドを実行","出力を確認してエラーを避ける","コードのメンテナンス性と拡張性を高める","エラーとバグの数を減らす"],"ko":["코드 품질과 신뢰성을 높인다","코드를 제출하기 전에 검증 명령을 실행","출력을 확인하여 오류를 방지","코드의 유지 보수성과 확장성을 높인다","오류와 버그의 수를 줄인다"],"es":["Garantiza la calidad y precisión del trabajo","Requiere la ejecución de comandos de verificación","Exige evidencia antes de reclamar la finalización","Es fundamental para el desarrollo de software de alta calidad","Ayuda a prevenir errores y bugs","Mejora la confiabilidad y estabilidad del código"],"fr":["Assure la qualité et la précision du travail","Exige l''exécution de commandes de vérification","Requiert des preuves avant de réclamer l''achèvement","Est fondamental pour le développement de logiciels de haute qualité","Aide à prévenir les erreurs et les bogues","Améliore la fiabilité et la stabilité du code"],"de":["Gewährleistet die Qualität und Genauigkeit der Arbeit","Erfordert die Ausführung von Verifizierungsbefehlen","Fordert Beweise vor der Behauptung der Fertigstellung","Ist grundlegend für die Entwicklung von hochwertiger Software","Hilft, Fehler und Bugs zu vermeiden","Verbessert die Zuverlässigkeit und Stabilität des Codes"],"pt":["Garantia de qualidade","Evita reclamações infundadas","Melhora a confiabilidade","Otimiza o processo de desenvolvimento","Reduz erros e bugs"],"ru":["Гарантия качества","Избегает необоснованных заявлений","Улучшает надежность","Оптимизирует процесс разработки","Снижает количество ошибок и багов"],"ar":["ضمان الجودة","تجنب المطالبات غير المبررة","تحسين الموثوقية","تحسين عملية التطوير","تقليل الأخطاء والعيوب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["验证前完成技能","软件开发方法","代码质量","可靠性","验证命令","输出确认","错误避免","代码可维护性"],"ja":["完了前に検証するスキル","ソフトウェア開発方法","コード品質","信頼性","検証コマンド","出力確認","エラー避け","コードメンテナンス性"],"ko":["완료 전 검증 스킬","소프트웨어 개발 방법","코드 품질","신뢰성","검증 명령","출력 확인","오류 방지","코드 유지 보수성"],"es":["verificación antes de completar","principio fundamental","desarrollo de software","calidad y precisión","comandos de verificación","evidencia antes de reclamar","alta calidad","prevención de errores","confiabilidad y estabilidad"],"fr":["vérification avant achèvement","principe clé","développement de logiciels","qualité et précision","commandes de vérification","preuves avant de réclamer","haute qualité","prévention des erreurs","fiabilité et stabilité"],"de":["Verifizierung vor Abschluss","Grundprinzip","Softwareentwicklung","Qualität und Genauigkeit","Verifizierungsbefehle","Beweise vor der Behauptung","hochwertig","Fehlervermeidung","Zuverlässigkeit und Stabilität"],"pt":["verificação antes da conclusão","desenvolvimento de software","garantia de qualidade","evitar reclamações infundadas","melhorar a confiabilidade","otimizar o processo de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["верификация перед завершением","разработка программного обеспечения","гарантия качества","избегать необоснованных заявлений","улучшать надежность","оптимизировать процесс разработки"],"ar":["التحقق قبل الاستكمال","تطوير البرمجيات","ضمان الجودة","تجنب المطالبات غير المبررة","تحسين الموثوقية","تحسين عملية التطوير"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents requiring rigorous testing and verification protocols before claiming completion or success.","zh":"非常适合需要在声称完成或成功之前进行严格测试和验证协议的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが完了または成功を主張する前に、厳格なテストと検証プロトコルを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"완성을 주장하기 전에 엄격한 테스트 및 확인 프로토콜이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que requieren protocolos de prueba y verificación rigurosos antes de afirmar la finalización o el éxito.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant des protocoles de test et de vérification rigoureux avant de prétendre à l''achèvement ou à la réussite.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungssagenten, die strenge Test- und Verifizierungsprotokolle benötigen, bevor sie den Abschluss oder Erfolg beanspruchen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que exigem protocolos rigorosos de teste e verificação antes de reivindicar conclusão ou sucesso.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих строгого тестирования и протоколов верификации перед заявлением о завершении или успехе.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النموزجيين الذين يتطلبون بروتوكولات اختبار وตรวจ صارمة قبل المطالبة بالاستكمال أو النجاح."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to ensure accuracy and reliability by running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims, utilizing protocols like fresh verification evidence and gate functions to prevent premature completion claims.","zh":"通过运行验证命令并在提出任何成功主张之前确认输出，利用新鲜的验证证据和门函数等协议，赋予代理确保准确性和可靠性的能力，以防止过早的完成主张。","ja":"検証コマンドを実行し、成功を主張する前に出力を確認することで、精度と信頼性を確保するエージェントの能力を付与し、新鮮な検証証拠やゲート関数などのプロトコルを利用して、早期の完了主張を防ぐ。","ko":"검증 명령을 실행하고 성공을 주장하기 전에 출력을 확인하여 정확성과 신뢰성을 보장하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하고, 신선한 검증 증거 및 게이트 함수 등과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 조기 완료 주장을 방지합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a garantizar la precisión y la confiabilidad al ejecutar comandos de verificación y confirmar la salida antes de hacer cualquier reclamación de éxito, utilizando protocolos como pruebas de verificación frescas y funciones de puerta para prevenir reclamaciones de finalización prematura.","fr":"Permet aux agents de s''assurer de l''exactitude et de la fiabilité en exécutant des commandes de vérification et en confirmant la sortie avant de faire des déclarations de réussite, en utilisant des protocoles tels que des preuves de vérification fraîches et des fonctions de portail pour prévenir les déclarations de fin prématurée.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Genauigkeit und Zuverlässigkeit sicherzustellen, indem sie Überprüfungsbefehle ausführen und die Ausgabe bestätigen, bevor sie Erfolgsansprüche geltend machen, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie frischer Überprüfungsbeweis und Schrankenfunktionen, um vorzeitige Abschlussansprüche zu verhindern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a garantir a precisão e a confiabilidade ao executar comandos de verificação e confirmar a saída antes de fazer qualquer reivindicação de sucesso, utilizando protocolos como evidências de verificação frescas e funções de portão para evitar reivindicações de conclusão prematura.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечить точность и надежность путем выполнения команд верификации и подтверждения вывода перед любыми заявлениями об успехе, используя протоколы, такие как свежие доказательства верификации и функции шлюза, чтобы предотвратить преждевременные заявления о завершении.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من ضمان الدقة والموثوقية من خلال تشغيل أوامر التحقق والتأكد من الإخراج قبل تقديم أي مطالبات بنجاح، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل أدلة التحقق الطازجة ووظائف البوابة لمنع مطالبات الانتهاء المسبق."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating pre-commit checks to prevent broken code submissions","Generating verification reports to confirm output before claiming success","Debugging failed verification attempts to identify and fix issues"],"zh":["自动执行预提交检查以防止提交有缺陷的代码","生成验证报告以确认输出然后声称成功","调试失败的验证尝试以识别和修复问题"],"ja":["プレコミットチェックを自動化して壊れたコードの提出を防ぐ","出力を確認してから成功を主張するための検証レポートを生成する","失敗した検証試行をデバッグして問題を特定して修正する"],"ko":["완성을 주장하기 전에 출력을 확인하기 위한 검증 보고서를 생성하는 자동화된 전반 확인","broken 코드 제출을 방지하기 위한 자동화된 전반 확인","실패한 검증 시도를 디버깅하여 문제를 식별하고 수정하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar comprobaciones previas al compromiso para prevenir la presentación de código roto","Generar informes de verificación para confirmar la salida antes de afirmar el éxito","Depurar intentos de verificación fallidos para identificar y solucionar problemas"],"fr":["Automatiser les vérifications préalables à l''engagement pour prévenir les soumissions de code cassé","Générer des rapports de vérification pour confirmer la sortie avant de prétendre à la réussite","Déboguer les tentatives de vérification échouées pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes"],"de":["Automatisieren von Vorab-Prüfungen, um die Einreichung von fehlerhaftem Code zu verhindern","Generieren von Überprüfungsberichten, um die Ausgabe zu bestätigen, bevor der Erfolg behauptet wird","Fehlschläge bei der Überprüfung debuggen, um Probleme zu identifizieren und zu beheben"],"pt":["Automatizar verificações pré-envio para evitar envio de código quebrado","Gerar relatórios de verificação para confirmar a saída antes de reivindicar sucesso","Depurar tentativas de verificação com falha para identificar e corrigir problemas"],"ru":["Автоматизация проверок перед коммитом для предотвращения отправки сломанного кода","Генерация отчетов верификации для подтверждения вывода перед заявлением об успехе","Отладка неудачных попыток верификации для выявления и исправления проблем"],"ar":["تأتمتة فحص ما قبل الالتزام لمنع إرسال رمز معطوب","توليد تقارير التحقق ل確認 الإخراج قبل المطالبة بالنجاح","تصحيح محاولات التحقق الفاشلة لتحديد ومعالجة المشاكل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires implementation of verification commands and protocols","Must be used in conjunction with a testing framework or verification tool","Violations of the core principle may result in inaccurate or dishonest claims"],"zh":["需要实现验证命令和协议","必须与测试框架或验证工具一起使用","核心原则的违反可能导致不准确或不诚实的主张"],"ja":["検証コマンドとプロトコルの実装が必要","テストフレームワークまたは検証ツールと併用する必要がある","コア原則の違反により不正確または不誠実な主張が生じる可能性がある"],"ko":["검증 명령 및 프로토콜의 구현이 필요함","테스트 프레임워크 또는 검증 도구와 함께 사용해야 함","핵심 원칙의 위반으로 인해 부정확하거나 부정직한 주장이 발생할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere la implementación de comandos y protocolos de verificación","Debe utilizarse en conjunto con un marco de prueba o herramienta de verificación","Violaciones del principio fundamental pueden resultar en reclamaciones inexactas o deshonestas"],"fr":["Nécessite la mise en œuvre de commandes et de protocoles de vérification","Doit être utilisé en conjonction avec un cadre de test ou un outil de vérification","Les violations du principe fondamental peuvent entraîner des déclarations inexactes ou malhonnêtes"],"de":["Erfordert die Implementierung von Überprüfungsbefehlen und -protokollen","Muss in Verbindung mit einem Testframework oder einer Überprüfungswerkzeug verwendet werden","Verletzungen des Grundprinzips können zu ungenauen oder unehrlichen Ansprüchen führen"],"pt":["Exige a implementação de comandos de verificação e protocolos","Deve ser usado em conjunto com um quadro de teste ou ferramenta de verificação","Violações do princípio central podem resultar em reivindicações imprecisas ou desonestas"],"ru":["Требует реализации команд верификации и протоколов","Должно использоваться в сочетании с тестовым каркасом или инструментом верификации","Нарушения основного принципа могут привести к неточным или нечестным заявлениям"],"ar":["يتطلب تنفيذ أوامر التحقق والبروتوكولات","يجب استخدامه بالاشتراك مع إطار اختبار أو أداة تحقق","انتهاكات المبدأ الأساسي قد تؤدي إلى مطالبات غير دقيقة أو غير صادقة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"ea52d15aabaf72bc6b558efe2c126f161b53961090ddcd712000273bfe8c7b6c","repoEtag":"W/\"0e7bd5c7950d5eac1d4957d49c8fa41c08258bb488461e66f172588c15374b72\"","qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/writing-plans', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'writing-plans', 55419, 4194, 75, '2026-02-20T01:50:39Z', '2026-02-20T02:06:22.280Z', '8a9198d4d9efbcad6e019b17c422c182113062c864b6154ec2a3ba2ed0b6b9d0', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/writing-plans","name":"writing-plans","description":{"zh":"编写计划是开发前的多步骤任务规划，帮助开发人员高效地完成任务","ja":"プランの作成は開発前の多段階タスク計画であり、開発者がタスクを効率的に完了するのに役立ちます","ko":"개발 전 계획 수립은 개발자에게 작업을 효율적으로 완료하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"La planificación de escritura es un proceso que implica la creación de planes de implementación detallados para tareas complejas","fr":"La planification d''écriture est un processus qui consiste à créer des plans d''implémentation détaillés pour les tâches complexes","de":"Die Schreibplanung ist ein Prozess, der die Erstellung detaillierter Implementierungspläne für komplexe Aufgaben beinhaltet","pt":"O plano de implementação é uma ferramenta essencial para desenvolvedores, permitindo que eles criem planos detalhados para tarefas complexas","ru":"План реализации является необходимым инструментом для разработчиков, позволяющим им создавать подробные планы для сложных задач","ar":"خطة التنفيذ هي أداة أساسية للمطورين، مما يسمح لهم بإنشاء خطط مفصلة للمهام المعقدة","en":"Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55419,"forks":4194,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:50:39Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"writing-plans","description":"Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code","bodyPreview":"# Writing Plans\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite comprehensive implementation plans assuming the engineer has zero context for our codebase and questionable taste. Document everything they need to know: which files to touch for each task, code, testing, docs they might need to check, how to test it. Give them the whole plan as bite-sized tasks. DRY. YAGNI. TDD. Frequent commits.\n\nAssume they are a skilled developer, but know almost nothing about our toolset or problem domain. Assume they don''t know good test","body":"# Writing Plans\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite comprehensive implementation plans assuming the engineer has zero context for our codebase and questionable taste. Document everything they need to know: which files to touch for each task, code, testing, docs they might need to check, how to test it. Give them the whole plan as bite-sized tasks. DRY. YAGNI. TDD. Frequent commits.\n\nAssume they are a skilled developer, but know almost nothing about our toolset or problem domain. Assume they don''t know good test design very well.\n\n**Announce at start:** \"I''m using the writing-plans skill to create the implementation plan.\"\n\n**Context:** This should be run in a dedicated worktree (created by brainstorming skill).\n\n**Save plans to:** `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<feature-name>.md`\n\n## Bite-Sized Task Granularity\n\n**Each step is one action (2-5 minutes):**\n- \"Write the failing test\" - step\n- \"Run it to make sure it fails\" - step\n- \"Implement the minimal code to make the test pass\" - step\n- \"Run the tests and make sure they pass\" - step\n- \"Commit\" - step\n\n## Plan Document Header\n\n**Every plan MUST start with this header:**\n\n```markdown\n# [Feature Name] Implementation Plan\n\n> **For Claude:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.\n\n**Goal:** [One sentence describing what this builds]\n\n**Architecture:** [2-3 sentences about approach]\n\n**Tech Stack:** [Key technologies/libraries]\n\n---\n```\n\n## Task Structure\n\n````markdown\n### Task N: [Component Name]\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `exact/path/to/file.py`\n- Modify: `exact/path/to/existing.py:123-145`\n- Test: `tests/exact/path/to/test.py`\n\n**Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n```python\ndef test_specific_behavior():\n    result = function(input)\n    assert result == expected\n```\n\n**Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `pytest tests/path/test.py::test_name -v`\nExpected: FAIL with \"function not defined\"\n\n**Step 3: Write minimal implementation**\n\n```python\ndef function(input):\n    return expected\n```\n\n**Step 4: Run test to verify it passes**\n\nRun: `pytest tests/path/test.py::test_name -v`\nExpected: PASS\n\n**Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add tests/path/test.py src/path/file.py\ngit commit -m \"feat: add specific feature\"\n```\n````\n\n## Remember\n- Exact file paths always\n- Complete code in plan (not \"add validation\")\n- Exact commands with expected output\n- Reference relevant skills with @ syntax\n- DRY, YAGNI, TDD, frequent commits\n\n## Execution Handoff\n\nAfter saving the plan, offer execution choice:\n\n**\"Plan complete and saved to `docs/plans/<filename>.md`. Two execution options:**\n\n**1. Subagent-Driven (this session)** - I dispatch fresh subagent per task, review between tasks, fast iteration\n\n**2. Parallel Session (separate)** - Open new session with executing-plans, batch execution with checkpoints\n\n**Which approach?\"**\n\n**If Subagent-Driven chosen:**\n- **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development\n- Stay in this session\n- Fresh subagent per task + code review\n\n**If Parallel Session chosen:**\n- Guide them to open new session in worktree\n- **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** New session uses superpowers:executing-plans\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:06:22.280Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"编写计划：开发前的多步骤任务规划","ja":"プランの作成：開発前の多段階タスク計画","ko":"개발 전 多단계 작업 계획 수립","es":"Planificación de escritura: Guía para desarrolladores","fr":"Plans d''écriture: Guide pour les développeurs","de":"Schreibpläne: Leitfaden für Entwickler","pt":"Planejamento de Implementação","ru":"Планы реализации","ar":"خطط التنفيذ","en":"writing-plans"},"description":{"zh":"编写计划是开发前的多步骤任务规划，帮助开发人员高效地完成任务","ja":"プランの作成は開発前の多段階タスク計画であり、開発者がタスクを効率的に完了するのに役立ちます","ko":"개발 전 계획 수립은 개발자에게 작업을 효율적으로 완료하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"La planificación de escritura es un proceso que implica la creación de planes de implementación detallados para tareas complejas","fr":"La planification d''écriture est un processus qui consiste à créer des plans d''implémentation détaillés pour les tâches complexes","de":"Die Schreibplanung ist ein Prozess, der die Erstellung detaillierter Implementierungspläne für komplexe Aufgaben beinhaltet","pt":"O plano de implementação é uma ferramenta essencial para desenvolvedores, permitindo que eles criem planos detalhados para tarefas complexas","ru":"План реализации является необходимым инструментом для разработчиков, позволяющим им создавать подробные планы для сложных задач","ar":"خطة التنفيذ هي أداة أساسية للمطورين، مما يسمح لهم بإنشاء خطط مفصلة للمهام المعقدة","en":"Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code"},"definition":{"en":"Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code"},"features":{"zh":["任务分解","代码规划","测试策略","文档管理","频繁提交"],"ja":["タスクの分解","コードの計画","テスト戦略","ドキュメント管理","頻繁なコミット"],"ko":["작업 분할","코드 계획","테스트 전략","문서 관리","頻繁한 커밋"],"es":["Creación de planes de implementación detallados","Asunción de cero contexto para el código base","Documentación de todos los pasos necesarios","Uso de principios de DRY, YAGNI y TDD","Commits frecuentes"],"fr":["Création de plans d''implémentation détaillés","Hypothèse de zéro contexte pour la base de code","Documentation de toutes les étapes nécessaires","Utilisation des principes de DRY, YAGNI et TDD","Commits fréquents"],"de":["Erstellung detaillierter Implementierungspläne","Annahme von null Kontext für den Code-Stamm","Dokumentation aller notwendigen Schritte","Verwendung der Prinzipien von DRY, YAGNI und TDD","Häufige Commits"],"pt":["Criação de planos de implementação detalhados","Inclusão de código, testes e documentação","Divisão de tarefas em etapas menores","Uso de princípios de DRY, YAGNI e TDD","Commits frequentes para controle de versão"],"ru":["Создание подробных планов реализации","Включение кода, тестов и документации","Разделение задач на меньшие этапы","Использование принципов DRY, YAGNI и TDD","Частые коммиты для контроля версий"],"ar":["إنشاء خطط تنفيذ مفصلة","إدراج الكود والاختبارات والتوثيق","تقسيم المهام إلى مراحل أصغر","استخدام مبادئ DRY و YAGNI و TDD","الالتزامات المتكررة للسيطرة على الإصدار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["开发计划","任务规划","代码设计","测试驱动开发","文档管理","频繁提交","开发效率"],"ja":["開発計画","タスク計画","コード設計","テスト駆動開発","ドキュメント管理","頻繁なコミット","開発効率"],"ko":["개발 계획","작업 계획","코드 설계","테스트 주도 개발","문서 관리","頻繁한 커밋","개발 효율"],"es":["planificación de escritura","desarrollo de software","implementación de tareas","principios de DRY","principios de YAGNI","principios de TDD","commits frecuentes","documentación de código"],"fr":["planification d''écriture","développement de logiciels","implémentation de tâches","principes de DRY","principes de YAGNI","principes de TDD","commits fréquents","documentation de code"],"de":["Schreibplanung","Software-Entwicklung","Implementierung von Aufgaben","Prinzipien von DRY","Prinzipien von YAGNI","Prinzipien von TDD","häufige Commits","Code-Dokumentation"],"pt":["plano de implementação","desenvolvimento de software"," gerenciamento de projeto","testes de unidade","documentação de código","princípios de DRY","princípios de YAGNI","princípios de TDD"],"ru":["план реализации","разработка программного обеспечения","управление проектом","юнит-тесты","документация кода","принципы DRY","принципы YAGNI","принципы TDD"],"ar":["خطة التنفيذ","تطوير البرمجيات","إدارة المشروع","اختبارات الوحدة","توثيق الكود","مبادئ DRY","مبادئ YAGNI","مبادئ TDD"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Developer Agents requiring structured implementation planning with zero context for a codebase.","zh":"适用于需要结构化实现规划且代码库上下文为零的开发者代理。","ja":"コードベースのコンテキストがゼロの構造化された実装計画を必要とする開発者エージェントに最適です。","ko":"코드베이스에 대한 문맥이 전혀 없는 구조화된 구현 계획을 필요로 하는 개발자 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollador que requieren una planificación de implementación estructurada con cero contexto para una base de código.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une planification d''implémentation structurée avec zéro contexte pour une base de code.","de":"Ideal für Entwickleragenten, die eine strukturierte Implementierungsplanung mit keinem Kontext für eine Codebasis benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvedor que exigem planejamento de implementação estruturado com zero contexto para uma base de código.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработчиков, требующих структурированного планирования реализации с нулевым контекстом для базы кода.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المطورين الذين يتطلبون تخطيط تنفيذ منظم بدون سياق لمجموعة من التعليمات البرمجية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create comprehensive multi-step task plans, incorporating principles like DRY, YAGNI, and TDD, with frequent commits, and assuming the engineer has questionable taste and zero context for the codebase, utilizing testing and documentation checks.","zh":"赋予代理创建全面多步骤任务计划的能力，融入如 DRY、YAGNI 和 TDD 等原则，包括频繁提交，并假设工程师具有可疑的品味和代码库的零上下文，利用测试和文档检查。","ja":"エージェントが、DRY、YAGNI、TDD などの原則を取り入れ、頻繁なコミットを行い、エンジニアがツールセットや問題ドメインに関する知識が不足していることを前提として、包括的なマルチステップタスクプランを作成する能力を与え、コードベースのゼロコンテキストを利用し、テストとドキュメントのチェックを行う。","ko":"에이전트가 DRY, YAGNI, TDD와 같은 원칙을 포함하여 종합적인 다단계 작업 계획을 생성하고 빈번한 커밋을 수행하며, 엔지니어가 도구 세트나 문제 도메인에 대한 지식이 부족하다는 가정하에 코드베이스에 대한 영 문맥을 활용하여 테스트와 문서화를 체크하는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear planes de tareas multi-etapa integrales, incorporando principios como DRY, YAGNI y TDD, con confirmaciones frecuentes, y asumiendo que el ingeniero tiene un gusto cuestionable y cero contexto para la base de código, utilizando pruebas y controles de documentación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des plans de tâches multi-étapes complets, intégrant des principes tels que DRY, YAGNI et TDD, avec des validations fréquentes, et en supposant que l''ingénieur a un goût douteux et zéro contexte pour la base de code, en utilisant des tests et des contrôles de documentation.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, umfassende, mehrschrittige Aufgabenpläne zu erstellen, die Prinzipien wie DRY, YAGNI und TDD einbeziehen, mit häufigen Commits und unter der Annahme, dass der Ingenieur einen zweifelhaften Geschmack und keinen Kontext für die Codebasis hat, unter Verwendung von Tests und Dokumentationsprüfungen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar planos de tarefas abrangentes e multietapas, incorporando princípios como DRY, YAGNI e TDD, com commits frequentes, e supondo que o engenheiro tenha gosto questionável e zero contexto para a base de código, utilizando verificações de teste e documentação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать комплексные многоступенчатые планы задач, включающие принципы như DRY, YAGNI и TDD, с частыми коммитами, и предполагая, что инженер имеет сомнительный вкус и нулевой контекст для базы кода, используя проверки тестирования и документации.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء خطط شاملة متعددة الخطوات للمهام، متضمنة مبادئ مثل DRY و YAGNI و TDD، مع التزامات متكررة، وافتراض أن مهندس البرمجيات لديه ذوق مشكوك فيه وعدم وجود سياق لمجموعة من التعليمات البرمجية، باستخدام فحص الاختبار والتوثيق."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating step-by-step implementation guides","Creating test plans for multi-step tasks","Documenting codebase interactions for new engineers"],"zh":["生成步骤式实现指南","创建多步骤任务的测试计划","为新工程师记录代码库交互"],"ja":["ステップバイステップの実装ガイドを生成する","マルチステップタスクのテストプランを作成する","新しいエンジニアのためにコードベースの相互作用を文書化する"],"ko":["단계별 구현 가이드 생성","다단계 작업에 대한 테스트 계획 생성","신규 엔지니어를 위한 코드베이스 상호작용 문서화"],"es":["Generación de guías de implementación paso a paso","Creación de planes de prueba para tareas multi-etapa","Documentación de interacciones de base de código para nuevos ingenieros"],"fr":["Génération de guides d''implémentation étape par étape","Création de plans de test pour des tâches multi-étapes","Documentation des interactions de base de code pour les nouveaux ingénieurs"],"de":["Erstellung von schrittweisen Implementierungsleitfäden","Erstellung von Testplänen für mehrschrittige Aufgaben","Dokumentation von Codebasis-Interaktionen für neue Ingenieure"],"pt":["Gerar guias de implementação passo a passo","Criar planos de teste para tarefas multietapas","Documentar interações da base de código para novos engenheiros"],"ru":["Генерировать пошаговые руководства по реализации","Создавать планы тестирования для многоступенчатых задач","Документировать взаимодействия базы кода для новых инженеров"],"ar":["генерировать دليلاً خطوة بخطوة لتنفيذ","إنشاء خطط اختبار للمهام متعددة الخطوات","توثيق تفاعلات مجموعة من التعليمات البرمجية لمهندسي البرمجيات الجدد"]},"limitations":{"en":["Assumes a skilled developer with little knowledge of the toolset or problem domain","Requires adherence to specific development principles like DRY and YAGNI"],"zh":["假设开发人员对工具集或问题域知之甚少","需要遵守特定的开发原则，如 DRY 和 YAGNI"],"ja":["ツールセットや問題ドメインに関する知識が不足している熟練した開発者を前提とする","DRY や YAGNI などの特定の開発原則に従う必要がある"],"ko":["도구 세트나 문제 도메인에 대한 지식이 거의 없는 숙련된 개발자를 가정","특정 개발 원칙인 DRY와 YAGNI를 준수해야 함"],"es":["Supone un desarrollador capacitado con poco conocimiento del conjunto de herramientas o del dominio del problema","Requiere la adhesión a principios de desarrollo específicos como DRY y YAGNI"],"fr":["Suppose un développeur compétent avec peu de connaissances de l''ensemble d''outils ou du domaine du problème","Exige l''adhésion à des principes de développement spécifiques comme DRY et YAGNI"],"de":["Geht von einem erfahrenen Entwickler mit wenig Kenntnissen des Werkzeugsets oder des Problemdomains aus","Erfordert die Einhaltung spezifischer Entwicklungsprinzipien wie DRY und YAGNI"],"pt":["Supõe um desenvolvedor habilidoso com pouco conhecimento do conjunto de ferramentas ou domínio do problema","Exige adesão a princípios de desenvolvimento específicos como DRY e YAGNI"],"ru":["Предполагает опытного разработчика с небольшим знанием набора инструментов или области проблемы","Требует соблюдения определенных принципов разработки, таких как DRY и YAGNI"],"ar":["يفترض وجود مطور ماهر مع قليل من المعرفة بمجموعة الأدوات أو مجال المشكلة","يتطلب اتباع مبادئ معينة لتطوير البرمجيات مثل DRY و YAGNI"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"8a9198d4d9efbcad6e019b17c422c182113062c864b6154ec2a3ba2ed0b6b9d0","repoEtag":"W/\"0e7bd5c7950d5eac1d4957d49c8fa41c08258bb488461e66f172588c15374b72\"","qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/writing-skills', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'writing-skills', 55419, 4194, 100, '2026-02-20T01:50:39Z', '2026-02-20T02:07:31.390Z', 'd83a09d6a1c6976f6cc2f40addeae653a4a6eb5903097ebc365d90242e00e379', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/writing-skills","name":"writing-skills","description":{"zh":"技能编写技巧是将测试驱动开发应用于过程文档，通过测试和重构提高代码质量","ja":"スキル作成テクニックはプロセス文書にテスト駆動開発を適用し、テストとリファクタリングによってコード品質を向上させる","ko":"스킬 작성 기술은 프로세스 문서에 테스트 주도 개발을 적용하여 테스트와 리팩토링을 통해 코드 품질을 높입니다","es":"Nuestro enfoque de habilidades de escritura aplica el desarrollo dirigido por pruebas a la documentación de procesos","fr":"Notre approche de compétences en rédaction applique le développement piloté par les tests à la documentation de processus","de":"Unser Schreibfähigkeiten-Ansatz wendet testgetriebene Entwicklung auf die Prozessdokumentation an","pt":"As habilidades de escrita aplicam o Test-Driven Development à documentação de processos, permitindo que os desenvolvedores criem testes e documentação de forma eficaz.","ru":"Навыки написания применяют Test-Driven Development к документации процессов, позволяя разработчикам создавать тесты и документацию эффективно.","ar":"مهارات الكتابة تطبق Test-Driven Development على توثيق العملية، مما يسمح للمطورين بإنشاء اختبارات وتوثيق بشكل فعال.","en":"Use when creating new skills, editing existing skills, or verifying skills work before deployment"},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":55419,"forks":4194,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T01:50:39Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"writing-skills","description":"Use when creating new skills, editing existing skills, or verifying skills work before deployment","bodyPreview":"# Writing Skills\n\n## Overview\n\n**Writing skills IS Test-Driven Development applied to process documentation.**\n\n**Personal skills live in agent-specific directories (`~/.claude/skills` for Claude Code, `~/.agents/skills/` for Codex)** \n\nYou write test cases (pressure scenarios with subagents), watch them fail (baseline behavior), write the skill (documentation), watch tests pass (agents comply), and refactor (close loopholes).\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch an agent fail without the sk","body":"# Writing Skills\n\n## Overview\n\n**Writing skills IS Test-Driven Development applied to process documentation.**\n\n**Personal skills live in agent-specific directories (`~/.claude/skills` for Claude Code, `~/.agents/skills/` for Codex)** \n\nYou write test cases (pressure scenarios with subagents), watch them fail (baseline behavior), write the skill (documentation), watch tests pass (agents comply), and refactor (close loopholes).\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch an agent fail without the skill, you don''t know if the skill teaches the right thing.\n\n**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** You MUST understand superpowers:test-driven-development before using this skill. That skill defines the fundamental RED-GREEN-REFACTOR cycle. This skill adapts TDD to documentation.\n\n**Official guidance:** For Anthropic''s official skill authoring best practices, see anthropic-best-practices.md. This document provides additional patterns and guidelines that complement the TDD-focused approach in this skill.\n\n## What is a Skill?\n\nA **skill** is a reference guide for proven techniques, patterns, or tools. Skills help future Claude instances find and apply effective approaches.\n\n**Skills are:** Reusable techniques, patterns, tools, reference guides\n\n**Skills are NOT:** Narratives about how you solved a problem once\n\n## TDD Mapping for Skills\n\n| TDD Concept | Skill Creation |\n|-------------|----------------|\n| **Test case** | Pressure scenario with subagent |\n| **Production code** | Skill document (SKILL.md) |\n| **Test fails (RED)** | Agent violates rule without skill (baseline) |\n| **Test passes (GREEN)** | Agent complies with skill present |\n| **Refactor** | Close loopholes while maintaining compliance |\n| **Write test first** | Run baseline scenario BEFORE writing skill |\n| **Watch it fail** | Document exact rationalizations agent uses |\n| **Minimal code** | Write skill addressing those specific violations |\n| **Watch it pass** | Verify agent now complies |\n| **Refactor cycle** | Find new rationalizations → plug → re-verify |\n\nThe entire skill creation process follows RED-GREEN-REFACTOR.\n\n## When to Create a Skill\n\n**Create when:**\n- Technique wasn''t intuitively obvious to you\n- You''d reference this again across projects\n- Pattern applies broadly (not project-specific)\n- Others would benefit\n\n**Don''t create for:**\n- One-off solutions\n- Standard practices well-documented elsewhere\n- Project-specific conventions (put in CLAUDE.md)\n- Mechanical constraints (if it''s enforceable with regex/validation, automate it—save documentation for judgment calls)\n\n## Skill Types\n\n### Technique\nConcrete method with steps to follow (condition-based-waiting, root-cause-tracing)\n\n### Pattern\nWay of thinking about problems (flatten-with-flags, test-invariants)\n\n### Reference\nAPI docs, syntax guides, tool documentation (office docs)\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n\n```\nskills/\n  skill-name/\n    SKILL.md              # Main reference (required)\n    supporting-file.*     # Only if needed\n```\n\n**Flat namespace** - all skills in one searchable namespace\n\n**Separate files for:**\n1. **Heavy reference** (100+ lines) - API docs, comprehensive syntax\n2. **Reusable tools** - Scripts, utilities, templates\n\n**Keep inline:**\n- Principles and concepts\n- Code patterns (< 50 lines)\n- Everything else\n\n## SKILL.md Structure\n\n**Frontmatter (YAML):**\n- Only two fields supported: `name` and `description`\n- Max 1024 characters total\n- `name`: Use letters, numbers, and hyphens only (no parentheses, special chars)\n- `description`: Third-person, describes ONLY when to use (NOT what it does)\n  - Start with \"Use when...\" to focus on triggering conditions\n  - Include specific symptoms, situations, and contexts\n  - **NEVER summarize the skill''s process or workflow** (see CSO section for why)\n  - Keep under 500 characters if possible\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: Skill-Name-With-Hyphens\ndescription: Use when [specific triggering conditions and symptoms]\n---\n\n# Skill Name\n\n## Overview\nWhat is this? Core principle in 1-2 sentences.\n\n## When to Use\n[Small inline flowchart IF decision non-obvious]\n\nBullet list with SYMPTOMS and use cases\nWhen NOT to use\n\n## Core Pattern (for techniques/patterns)\nBefore/after code comparison\n\n## Quick Reference\nTable or bullets for scanning common operations\n\n## Implementation\nInline code for simple patterns\nLink to file for heavy reference or reusable tools\n\n## Common Mistakes\nWhat goes wrong + fixes\n\n## Real-World Impact (optional)\nConcrete results\n```\n\n\n## Claude Search Optimization (CSO)\n\n**Critical for discovery:** Future Claude needs to FIND your skill\n\n### 1. Rich Description Field\n\n**Purpose:** Claude reads description to decide which skills to load for a given task. Make it answer: \"Should I read this skill right now?\"\n\n**Format:** Start with \"Use when...\" to focus on triggering conditions\n\n**CRITICAL: Description = When to Use, NOT What the Skill Does**\n\nThe description should ONLY describe triggering conditions. Do NOT summarize the skill''s process or workflow in the description.\n\n**Why this matters:** Testing revealed that when a description summarizes the skill''s workflow, Claude may follow the description instead of reading the full skill content. A description saying \"code review between tasks\" caused Claude to do ONE review, even though the skill''s flowchart clearly showed TWO reviews (spec compliance then code quality).\n\nWhen the description was changed to just \"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks\" (no workflow summary), Claude correctly read the flowchart and followed the two-stage review process.\n\n**The trap:** Descriptions that summarize workflow create a shortcut Claude will take. The skill body becomes documentation Claude skips.\n\n```yaml\n# ❌ BAD: Summarizes workflow - Claude may follow this instead of reading skill\ndescription: Use when executing plans - dispatches subagent per task with code review between tasks\n\n# ❌ BAD: Too much process detail\ndescription: Use for TDD - write test first, watch it fail, write minimal code, refactor\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Just triggering conditions, no workflow summary\ndescription: Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Triggering conditions only\ndescription: Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code\n```\n\n**Content:**\n- Use concrete triggers, symptoms, and situations that signal this skill applies\n- Describe the *problem* (race conditions, inconsistent behavior) not *language-specific symptoms* (setTimeout, sleep)\n- Keep triggers technology-agnostic unless the skill itself is technology-specific\n- If skill is technology-specific, make that explicit in the trigger\n- Write in third person (injected into system prompt)\n- **NEVER summarize the skill''s process or workflow**\n\n```yaml\n# ❌ BAD: Too abstract, vague, doesn''t include when to use\ndescription: For async testing\n\n# ❌ BAD: First person\ndescription: I can help you with async tests when they''re flaky\n\n# ❌ BAD: Mentions technology but skill isn''t specific to it\ndescription: Use when tests use setTimeout/sleep and are flaky\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Starts with \"Use when\", describes problem, no workflow\ndescription: Use when tests have race conditions, timing dependencies, or pass/fail inconsistently\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Technology-specific skill with explicit trigger\ndescription: Use when using React Router and handling authentication redirects\n```\n\n### 2. Keyword Coverage\n\nUse words Claude would search for:\n- Error messages: \"Hook timed out\", \"ENOTEMPTY\", \"race condition\"\n- Symptoms: \"flaky\", \"hanging\", \"zombie\", \"pollution\"\n- Synonyms: \"timeout/hang/freeze\", \"cleanup/teardown/afterEach\"\n- Tools: Actual commands, library names, file types\n\n### 3. Descriptive Naming\n\n**Use active voice, verb-first:**\n- ✅ `creating-skills` not `skill-creation`\n- ✅ `condition-based-waiting` not `async-test-helpers`\n\n### 4. Token Efficiency (Critical)\n\n**Problem:** getting-started and frequently-referenced skills load into EVERY conversation. Every token counts.\n\n**Target word counts:**\n- getting-started workflows: <150 words each\n- Frequently-loaded skills: <200 words total\n- Other skills: <500 words (still be concise)\n\n**Techniques:**\n\n**Move details to tool help:**\n```bash\n# ❌ BAD: Document all flags in SKILL.md\nsearch-conversations supports --text, --both, --after DATE, --before DATE, --limit N\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Reference --help\nsearch-conversations supports multiple modes and filters. Run --help for details.\n```\n\n**Use cross-references:**\n```markdown\n# ❌ BAD: Repeat workflow details\nWhen searching, dispatch subagent with template...\n[20 lines of repeated instructions]\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Reference other skill\nAlways use subagents (50-100x context savings). REQUIRED: Use [other-skill-name] for workflow.\n```\n\n**Compress examples:**\n```markdown\n# ❌ BAD: Verbose example (42 words)\nyour human partner: \"How did we handle authentication errors in React Router before?\"\nYou: I''ll search past conversations for React Router authentication patterns.\n[Dispatch subagent with search query: \"React Router authentication error handling 401\"]\n\n# ✅ GOOD: Minimal example (20 words)\nPartner: \"How did we handle auth errors in React Router?\"\nYou: Searching...\n[Dispatch subagent → synthesis]\n```\n\n**Eliminate redundancy:**\n- Don''t repeat what''s in cross-referenced skills\n- Don''t explain what''s obvious from command\n- Don''t include multiple examples of same pattern\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\nwc -w skills/path/SKILL.md\n# getting-started workflows: aim for <150 each\n# Other frequently-loaded: aim for <200 total\n```\n\n**Name by what you DO or core insight:**\n- ✅ `condition-based-waiting` > `async-test-helpers`\n- ✅ `using-skills` not `skill-usage`\n- ✅ `flatten-with-flags` > `data-structure-refactoring`\n- ✅ `root-cause-tracing` > `debugging-techniques`\n\n**Gerunds (-ing) work well for processes:**\n- `creating-skills`, `testing-skills`, `debugging-with-logs`\n- Active, describes the action you''re taking\n\n### 4. Cross-Referencing Other Skills\n\n**When writing documentation that references other skills:**\n\nUse skill name only, with explicit requirement markers:\n- ✅ Good: `**REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:test-driven-development`\n- ✅ Good: `**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** You MUST understand superpowers:systematic-debugging`\n- ❌ Bad: `See skills/testing/test-driven-development` (unclear if required)\n- ❌ Bad: `@skills/testing/test-driven-development/SKILL.md` (force-loads, burns context)\n\n**Why no @ links:** `@` syntax force-loads files immediately, consuming 200k+ context before you need them.\n\n## Flowchart Usage\n\n```dot\ndigraph when_flowchart {\n    \"Need to show information?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Use markdown\" [shape=box];\n    \"Small inline flowchart\" [shape=box];\n\n    \"Need to show information?\" -> \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" -> \"Small inline flowchart\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Decision where I might go wrong?\" -> \"Use markdown\" [label=\"no\"];\n}\n```\n\n**Use flowcharts ONLY for:**\n- Non-obvious decision points\n- Process loops where you might stop too early\n- \"When to use A vs B\" decisions\n\n**Never use flowcharts for:**\n- Reference material → Tables, lists\n- Code examples → Markdown blocks\n- Linear instructions → Numbered lists\n- Labels without semantic meaning (step1, helper2)\n\nSee @graphviz-conventions.dot for graphviz style rules.\n\n**Visualizing for your human partner:** Use `render-graphs.js` in this directory to render a skill''s flowcharts to SVG:\n```bash\n./render-graphs.js ../some-skill           # Each diagram separately\n./render-graphs.js ../some-skill --combine # All diagrams in one SVG\n```\n\n## Code Examples\n\n**One excellent example beats many mediocre ones**\n\nChoose most relevant language:\n- Testing techniques → TypeScript/JavaScript\n- System debugging → Shell/Python\n- Data processing → Python\n\n**Good example:**\n- Complete and runnable\n- Well-commented explaining WHY\n- From real scenario\n- Shows pattern clearly\n- Ready to adapt (not generic template)\n\n**Don''t:**\n- Implement in 5+ languages\n- Create fill-in-the-blank templates\n- Write contrived examples\n\nYou''re good at porting - one great example is enough.\n\n## File Organization\n\n### Self-Contained Skill\n```\ndefense-in-depth/\n  SKILL.md    # Everything inline\n```\nWhen: All content fits, no heavy reference needed\n\n### Skill with Reusable Tool\n```\ncondition-based-waiting/\n  SKILL.md    # Overview + patterns\n  example.ts  # Working helpers to adapt\n```\nWhen: Tool is reusable code, not just narrative\n\n### Skill with Heavy Reference\n```\npptx/\n  SKILL.md       # Overview + workflows\n  pptxgenjs.md   # 600 lines API reference\n  ooxml.md       # 500 lines XML structure\n  scripts/       # Executable tools\n```\nWhen: Reference material too large for inline\n\n## The Iron Law (Same as TDD)\n\n```\nNO SKILL WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nThis applies to NEW skills AND EDITS to existing skills.\n\nWrite skill before testing? Delete it. Start over.\nEdit skill without testing? Same violation.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Not for \"simple additions\"\n- Not for \"just adding a section\"\n- Not for \"documentation updates\"\n- Don''t keep untested changes as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" while running tests\n- Delete means delete\n\n**REQUIRED BACKGROUND:** The superpowers:test-driven-development skill explains why this matters. Same principles apply to documentation.\n\n## Testing All Skill Types\n\nDifferent skill types need different test approaches:\n\n### Discipline-Enforcing Skills (rules/requirements)\n\n**Examples:** TDD, verification-before-completion, designing-before-coding\n\n**Test with:**\n- Academic questions: Do they understand the rules?\n- Pressure scenarios: Do they comply under stress?\n- Multiple pressures combined: time + sunk cost + exhaustion\n- Identify rationalizations and add explicit counters\n\n**Success criteria:** Agent follows rule under maximum pressure\n\n### Technique Skills (how-to guides)\n\n**Examples:** condition-based-waiting, root-cause-tracing, defensive-programming\n\n**Test with:**\n- Application scenarios: Can they apply the technique correctly?\n- Variation scenarios: Do they handle edge cases?\n- Missing information tests: Do instructions have gaps?\n\n**Success criteria:** Agent successfully applies technique to new scenario\n\n### Pattern Skills (mental models)\n\n**Examples:** reducing-complexity, information-hiding concepts\n\n**Test with:**\n- Recognition scenarios: Do they recognize when pattern applies?\n- Application scenarios: Can they use the mental model?\n- Counter-examples: Do they know when NOT to apply?\n\n**Success criteria:** Agent correctly identifies when/how to apply pattern\n\n### Reference Skills (documentation/APIs)\n\n**Examples:** API documentation, command references, library guides\n\n**Test with:**\n- Retrieval scenarios: Can they find the right information?\n- Application scenarios: Can they use what they found correctly?\n- Gap testing: Are common use cases covered?\n\n**Success criteria:** Agent finds and correctly applies reference information\n\n## Common Rationalizations for Skipping Testing\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Skill is obviously clear\" | Clear to you ≠ clear to other agents. Test it. |\n| \"It''s just a reference\" | References can have gaps, unclear sections. Test retrieval. |\n| \"Testing is overkill\" | Untested skills have issues. Always. 15 min testing saves hours. |\n| \"I''ll test if problems emerge\" | Problems = agents can''t use skill. Test BEFORE deploying. |\n| \"Too tedious to test\" | Testing is less tedious than debugging bad skill in production. |\n| \"I''m confident it''s good\" | Overconfidence guarantees issues. Test anyway. |\n| \"Academic review is enough\" | Reading ≠ using. Test application scenarios. |\n| \"No time to test\" | Deploying untested skill wastes more time fixing it later. |\n\n**All of these mean: Test before deploying. No exceptions.**\n\n## Bulletproofing Skills Against Rationalization\n\nSkills that enforce discipline (like TDD) need to resist rationalization. Agents are smart and will find loopholes when under pressure.\n\n**Psychology note:** Understanding WHY persuasion techniques work helps you apply them systematically. See persuasion-principles.md for research foundation (Cialdini, 2021; Meincke et al., 2025) on authority, commitment, scarcity, social proof, and unity principles.\n\n### Close Every Loophole Explicitly\n\nDon''t just state the rule - forbid specific workarounds:\n\n<Bad>\n```markdown\nWrite code before test? Delete it.\n```\n</Bad>\n\n<Good>\n```markdown\nWrite code before test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don''t look at it\n- Delete means delete\n```\n</Good>\n\n### Address \"Spirit vs Letter\" Arguments\n\nAdd foundational principle early:\n\n```markdown\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n```\n\nThis cuts off entire class of \"I''m following the spirit\" rationalizations.\n\n### Build Rationalization Table\n\nCapture rationalizations from baseline testing (see Testing section below). Every excuse agents make goes in the table:\n\n```markdown\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Too simple to test\" | Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n```\n\n### Create Red Flags List\n\nMake it easy for agents to self-check when rationalizing:\n\n```markdown\n## Red Flags - STOP and Start Over\n\n- Code before test\n- \"I already manually tested it\"\n- \"Tests after achieve the same purpose\"\n- \"It''s about spirit not ritual\"\n- \"This is different because...\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n```\n\n### Update CSO for Violation Symptoms\n\nAdd to description: symptoms of when you''re ABOUT to violate the rule:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code\n```\n\n## RED-GREEN-REFACTOR for Skills\n\nFollow the TDD cycle:\n\n### RED: Write Failing Test (Baseline)\n\nRun pressure scenario with subagent WITHOUT the skill. Document exact behavior:\n- What choices did they make?\n- What rationalizations did they use (verbatim)?\n- Which pressures triggered violations?\n\nThis is \"watch the test fail\" - you must see what agents naturally do before writing the skill.\n\n### GREEN: Write Minimal Skill\n\nWrite skill that addresses those specific rationalizations. Don''t add extra content for hypothetical cases.\n\nRun same scenarios WITH skill. Agent should now comply.\n\n### REFACTOR: Close Loopholes\n\nAgent found new rationalization? Add explicit counter. Re-test until bulletproof.\n\n**Testing methodology:** See @testing-skills-with-subagents.md for the complete testing methodology:\n- How to write pressure scenarios\n- Pressure types (time, sunk cost, authority, exhaustion)\n- Plugging holes systematically\n- Meta-testing techniques\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### ❌ Narrative Example\n\"In session 2025-10-03, we found empty projectDir caused...\"\n**Why bad:** Too specific, not reusable\n\n### ❌ Multi-Language Dilution\nexample-js.js, example-py.py, example-go.go\n**Why bad:** Mediocre quality, maintenance burden\n\n### ❌ Code in Flowcharts\n```dot\nstep1 [label=\"import fs\"];\nstep2 [label=\"read file\"];\n```\n**Why bad:** Can''t copy-paste, hard to read\n\n### ❌ Generic Labels\nhelper1, helper2, step3, pattern4\n**Why bad:** Labels should have semantic meaning\n\n## STOP: Before Moving to Next Skill\n\n**After writing ANY skill, you MUST STOP and complete the deployment process.**\n\n**Do NOT:**\n- Create multiple skills in batch without testing each\n- Move to next skill before current one is verified\n- Skip testing because \"batching is more efficient\"\n\n**The deployment checklist below is MANDATORY for EACH skill.**\n\nDeploying untested skills = deploying untested code. It''s a violation of quality standards.\n\n## Skill Creation Checklist (TDD Adapted)\n\n**IMPORTANT: Use TodoWrite to create todos for EACH checklist item below.**\n\n**RED Phase - Write Failing Test:**\n- [ ] Create pressure scenarios (3+ combined pressures for discipline skills)\n- [ ] Run scenarios WITHOUT skill - document baseline behavior verbatim\n- [ ] Identify patterns in rationalizations/failures\n\n**GREEN Phase - Write Minimal Skill:**\n- [ ] Name uses only letters, numbers, hyphens (no parentheses/special chars)\n- [ ] YAML frontmatter with only name and description (max 1024 chars)\n- [ ] Description starts with \"Use when...\" and includes specific triggers/symptoms\n- [ ] Description written in third person\n- [ ] Keywords throughout for search (errors, symptoms, tools)\n- [ ] Clear overview with core principle\n- [ ] Address specific baseline failures identified in RED\n- [ ] Code inline OR link to separate file\n- [ ] One excellent example (not multi-language)\n- [ ] Run scenarios WITH skill - verify agents now comply\n\n**REFACTOR Phase - Close Loopholes:**\n- [ ] Identify NEW rationalizations from testing\n- [ ] Add explicit counters (if discipline skill)\n- [ ] Build rationalization table from all test iterations\n- [ ] Create red flags list\n- [ ] Re-test until bulletproof\n\n**Quality Checks:**\n- [ ] Small flowchart only if decision non-obvious\n- [ ] Quick reference table\n- [ ] Common mistakes section\n- [ ] No narrative storytelling\n- [ ] Supporting files only for tools or heavy reference\n\n**Deployment:**\n- [ ] Commit skill to git and push to your fork (if configured)\n- [ ] Consider contributing back via PR (if broadly useful)\n\n## Discovery Workflow\n\nHow future Claude finds your skill:\n\n1. **Encounters problem** (\"tests are flaky\")\n3. **Finds SKILL** (description matches)\n4. **Scans overview** (is this relevant?)\n5. **Reads patterns** (quick reference table)\n6. **Loads example** (only when implementing)\n\n**Optimize for this flow** - put searchable terms early and often.\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**Creating skills IS TDD for process documentation.**\n\nSame Iron Law: No skill without failing test first.\nSame cycle: RED (baseline) → GREEN (write skill) → REFACTOR (close loopholes).\nSame benefits: Better quality, fewer surprises, bulletproof results.\n\nIf you follow TDD for code, follow it for skills. It''s the same discipline applied to documentation.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-02-20T02:07:31.390Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"技能编写技巧 - 测试驱动开发","ja":"スキル作成テクニック - テスト駆動開発","ko":"스킬 작성 기술 - 테스트 주도 개발","es":"Habilidades de escritura para desarrollo de habilidades","fr":"Compétences en rédaction pour le développement de compéte...","de":"Schreibfähigkeiten für die Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","pt":"Habilidades de Escrita para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Навыки Написания для Разработчиков","ar":"مهارات الكتابة لل مطورين","en":"writing-skills"},"description":{"zh":"技能编写技巧是将测试驱动开发应用